bioscript:
module viabilityDetection
module dropletReleaseDetection
module mCherryGFPDetection
module genomicCleavageDetection

manifest MCF7_Cells
manifest H1299_Cells
manifest PluronicF127
manifest PBS
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant
manifest CompleteMedia
manifest FDA_PI_Stain
manifest Cas9_eGFP_sgRNA_Plasmid
manifest Cas9_RAF1_sgRNA_Plasmid
manifest Lipofectamine3000
manifest TrypsinEDTA
manifest ConditionedMedia
manifest FC40_Oil

instructions:

// ============================================================
// One Cell, One Drop, One Click: Hybrid Microfluidics for
// Mammalian Single Cell Isolation
// Samlali, Ahmadi, Quach, Soffer, Shih - Small 2020, 16, 2002400
//
// Protocol: hydrodynamic single-cell trapping, in situ
// deterministic droplet encapsulation, on-demand droplet
// release/keep operations, cell viability assay, and a
// gene-editing pipeline (CRISPR knockout of eGFP in
// NCI-H1299 cells) with isoclone sorting, recovery, and
// expansion.
//
// NOTE ON BIOLOGICAL SCOPE: The paper performs two separate,
// independent knockout experiments -- eGFP KO and RAF1 KO --
// each transfected with a single plasmid and evaluated
// independently (Fig 6A/B, separate flow cytometry plots).
// This BioScript file encodes the eGFP knockout arm as the
// representative protocol. A separate .bs file should be
// used for the RAF1 knockout arm with Cas9_RAF1_sgRNA_Plasmid.
// Pooling both plasmids into one transfectionMix would imply
// co-transfection, which does not reflect the paper's design.
//
// NOTE ON TRAPPING ABSTRACTION: Steps 2 and 7 use `mix` to
// represent cell loading into the serpentine trapping channel.
// This is a BioScript abstraction for a flow-through
// hydrodynamic trapping event (cells loaded at 1-4 nL/s
// through 8 um constriction traps, ~88.3% efficiency).
// There is no reagent mixing in the DMF sense at these steps.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: device priming, cell trapping,
//                             phase change, in situ encapsulation,
//                             on-demand release characterisation
//   BB2  releasePass       -- releaseSignal > 0: droplet successfully
//                             released (characterisation run), dispose
//   BB3  releaseFail       -- releaseSignal <= 0: release failed, drain
//   BB4  releaseJoin       -- join: viability assay branch begins
//   BB5  viabilityPass     -- viabilitySignal > 0: cells viable (>80%), dispose
//   BB6  viabilityFail     -- viabilitySignal <= 0: low viability, drain
//   BB7  viabilityJoin     -- join: gene-editing branch begins
//   BB8  knockoutPass      -- knockoutSignal > 0: recover & expand isoclone
//   BB9  knockoutFail      -- knockoutSignal <= 0: drain sorted isoclone
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signal, experiment ends
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime device with 2% Pluronics F-127 in PBS for 5 min
//         to decrease cell adhesion to PDMS.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix      = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Load MCF-7 cells (1e5-1e6 cells/mL in PBS) into the
//         trapping device at 1-4 nL/s. Single cells are
//         hydrodynamically trapped (~88.3% efficiency) in
//         8 um constriction traps.
//         NOTE: `mix` here abstracts a channel flow-through
//         trapping event, not a DMF electrode mixing step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mcf7Cells    = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
trappedCells = mix mcf7Cells with primingMix for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Phase change - flow HFE7500 + 2% surfactant at
//         4 nL/s through the main channel while actuating
//         trap electrodes (15 kHz, 126 Vrms) to shear off
//         the aqueous phase and generate an in situ droplet
//         around the trapped single cell (deterministic
//         encapsulation, no Poisson statistics).
//         Average droplet volume: 150.3 +/- 5.6 pL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase         = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
encapsulatedCell = mix trappedCells with oilPhase for 4s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: On-demand droplet release characterisation.
//         Droplet released toward outlet under forward oil
//         flow (<1 nL/s gives >95% release probability) via
//         electrode actuation sequence (15 kHz, 126 Vrms).
//         NOTE: This block characterises release efficiency
//         (Fig 4A/B in paper) using a dedicated detection
//         module. This is separate from the sorting run in
//         STEP 7. The released droplet is disposed after
//         detection; it is not the isoclone being recovered.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// FIX #1 (was viabilityDetection): release characterisation
// uses dropletReleaseDetection, not the FDA/PI viability
// module. viabilityDetection is reserved for STEP 5.
releasedDroplet = mix encapsulatedCell with oilPhase for 1s
releaseSignal   = detect dropletReleaseDetection on releasedDroplet for 10s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Release characterisation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): releaseSignal > 0 -> droplet successfully
//             released; dispose (characterisation run only).
// Fail (BB3): releaseSignal <= 0 -> release failed
//             (droplet retained/lost); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (releaseJoin).
// ============================================================

if (releaseSignal > 0) {
    dispose releasedDroplet
} else {
    drain releasedDroplet
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: releaseJoin
// Dispose release QC signal droplet. Control falls into the
// viability assay branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose releaseSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5 (Viability assay): Trap fresh MCF-7 cells, actuate
//         electrodes for 30 s (15 kHz, 126 Vrms) to simulate
//         encapsulation conditions, then flow FDA/PI viability
//         stain and incubate for 10 min.
//         FDA labels live cells (ex 490 nm / em 526 nm).
//         PI labels dead cells (ex 488 nm / em 617 nm).
//         Result: no significant viability difference between
//         potentiated (82.5+/-8.1%) and control (87.5+/-7.2%)
//         cells (p=0.6687, N=3). (Fig 5, paper Section 2.3)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

viabilityCells  = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
viabilityPriming = dispense 1 units of PBS
viabilityTrapped = mix viabilityCells with viabilityPriming for 2s

// Electrode actuation (15 kHz, 126 Vrms for 30 s) modelled
// as a heat step at room temperature (25 C) for 30 s.
heat viabilityTrapped at 25c for 30s

fdaPiStain   = dispense 1 units of FDA_PI_Stain
stainedCells = mix viabilityTrapped with fdaPiStain for 10m

viabilitySignal = detect viabilityDetection on stainedCells for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Viability QC gate
// Pass (BB5): viabilitySignal > 0 -> cells viable (>80%), dispose
// Fail (BB6): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> low viability, drain
// Both branches converge at BB7 (viabilityJoin).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedCells
} else {
    drain stainedCells
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: viabilityJoin
// Dispose viability QC signal. Control falls into the
// gene-editing / isoclone sorting branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6 (Gene editing - eGFP KO arm): Transient lipid-
//         mediated transfection of NCI-H1299 cells with
//         Cas9/mCherry/sgRNA plasmid targeting eGFP (off-chip),
//         generating a heterozygous knockout population
//         (~25.3% transfection efficiency, ~4.95% KO efficiency
//         by genomic cleavage detection assay). Incubated
//         48 h at 37 C / 5% CO2 before on-chip sorting.
//
// FIX #2 (was: mix egfpPlasmid with raf1Plasmid): The paper
//         runs eGFP KO and RAF1 KO as two independent
//         experiments. Only the eGFP plasmid is used here.
//         48 h incubation = 2880 min.
// FIX #3 (was: heat ... for 48h): BioScript duration tokens
//         are s / m only. 48 h converted to 2880m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

h1299Cells      = dispense 1 units of H1299_Cells
egfpPlasmid     = dispense 1 units of Cas9_eGFP_sgRNA_Plasmid
lipofectamine   = dispense 1 units of Lipofectamine3000

transfectionMix  = mix egfpPlasmid with lipofectamine for 5s
transfectedCells = mix h1299Cells with transfectionMix for 1m

// 48 h post-transfection incubation at 37 C (= 2880 min).
heat transfectedCells at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Trap transfected H1299 cells on-chip and screen by
//         fluorescence for mCherry expression (transfection
//         reporter) and eGFP loss (knockout signal) using the
//         mCherryGFPDetection module.
//         Successful isoclones predicted in ~1 of 6 traps
//         (~16.7%). Successful clones are encapsulated in situ
//         and released on-demand toward the outlet (~45 min
//         total trap-to-recovery time).
//         NOTE: `mix` steps abstract channel-based hydrodynamic
//         trapping and oil-phase encapsulation events.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS2       = dispense 1 units of PBS
chipTrappedClones = mix transfectedCells with primingPBS2 for 2s

oilPhase2         = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
encapsulatedClone = mix chipTrappedClones with oilPhase2 for 4s
sortedIsoclone    = mix encapsulatedClone with oilPhase2 for 1s

// Fluorescence detection: mCherry+ / eGFP-loss identifies
// successfully transfected and knocked-out isoclones.
knockoutSignal = detect mCherryGFPDetection on sortedIsoclone for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Knockout sorting QC gate
// Pass (BB8): knockoutSignal > 0 -> successful eGFP knockout
//             isoclone detected (mCherry+ / GFP-loss);
//             carry forward into capillary recovery and
//             96-well expansion.
// Fail (BB9): knockoutSignal <= 0 -> no edited clone in trap;
//             drain sortedIsoclone and re-trap at higher
//             forward flow rate (off-chip iterative step).
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup). Only the
// pass branch produces a non-empty recoveredClone droplet.
// ============================================================

if (knockoutSignal > 0) {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    // Recovery and expansion (pass path only):
    // The isoclone-containing droplet is transferred via capillary
    // onto a hydrophobic PTFE membrane. FC-40 oil wash removes
    // HFE7500 and surfactant. The aqueous isoclone droplet is
    // released into conditioned media and transferred to a 96-well
    // plate at 37 C. Clonal expansion monitored at Day 5 and Day 7.
    // Media replaced with fresh complete growth media after Day 5.
    //
    // FIX #4 (was: heat ... for 168h): 7 days = 10080 min.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    conditionedMedia = dispense 1 units of ConditionedMedia
    fc40Wash         = dispense 1 units of FC40_Oil

    membraneWash   = mix sortedIsoclone with fc40Wash for 1m
    recoveredClone = mix membraneWash with conditionedMedia for 1m

    // 7-day clonal expansion at 37 C / 5% CO2 (= 10080 min).
    // Day 5: image eGFP-negative clones; Day 7: confirm expansion.
    // mCherry reporter lost by Day 2-3 (transient transfection).
    heat recoveredClone at 37c for 10080m

    dispose recoveredClone
} else {
    drain sortedIsoclone
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose the knockout QC signal droplet; experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose knockoutSignal

// [terminal -- no instructions; exit node for CFG]

module absorbanceDetection
module lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection
module rosFluorescenceDetection

manifest CyclotellaCryptica
manifest LipidTOX_Stock
manifest DCFDA_Kit
manifest AscorbicAcid
manifest FC_Medium
manifest FC_Medium_NoSilicon
manifest LED_BlueArray
manifest LED_YellowArray

// ============================================================
// A Droplet-Based Screen for Wavelength-Dependent Lipid
// Production in Algae.
// Shih, Mufti, Chamberlain, Kim, Wheeler
// Energy Environ. Sci., 2014, DOI: 10.1039/c4ee01123f
//
// Protocol: Digital microfluidic (DMF) long-term culture and
// multiplexed screening of Cyclotella cryptica for neutral
// lipid production under varying LED illumination wavelengths
// (multicolour screen then blue/yellow cycling screen), plus
// a reactive oxygen species (ROS) mechanistic assay.
//
// DEVICE OVERVIEW:
//   Two four-electrode active reservoirs (algae + LipidTOX),
//   8 bussed dye-dispensing electrodes, 8 algae culture zone
//   electrodes, 8 absorbance detection electrodes (L-shaped),
//   8 fluorescence detection electrodes, 8 waste reservoir
//   electrodes with 1 mm through-holes. Detection pitch: 9 mm,
//   compatible with standard 384-well multiwell plate reader.
//   Narrow dispenser electrodes (>=0.5:1 ratio to destination)
//   ensure reliable parallel dispensing on bussed electrodes.
//
// ALGAE CULTURE CONDITIONS:
//   C. cryptica (CCMP 332) in f/2 medium + biotin +
//   cyanocobalamin + 0.02% w/v Pluronic F68, 20 C,
//   12 h white light / 12 h dark alternating cycle.
//   Inoculation density: ~9.0e5 cells/mL (exponential phase).
//   Cell suspension: 1.5e6 cells/mL in complete media.
//   LipidTOX working solution: stock diluted 200x in media.
//
// SCREENING DESIGN:
//   PROTOCOL 1 (multicolour): 7 LED wavelengths (red, orange,
//     yellow, green, blue, purple, white) + dark control, at
//     low (50 umol/m2/s) and high (250 umol/m2/s) intensity,
//     all LEDs on for 24 h. This .bs file encodes the HIGH
//     intensity arm as the representative protocol (Fig. 3b,d,f).
//     A separate run is needed for low intensity (Fig. 3a,c,e).
//   PROTOCOL 2 (blue/yellow cycling): 8 timed blue/yellow
//     combinations at high intensity (250 umol/m2/s). Only the
//     optimal condition (15 h blue / 9 h yellow) is encoded here
//     as the representative arm (Fig. 4a,b). Other timing
//     variants follow identical structure with different heat
//     durations.
//   PROTOCOL 3 (ROS mechanistic assay): DCFDA fluorescence
//     to quantify reactive oxygen species under yellow vs. blue
//     vs. normal conditions, and with ascorbate antioxidant
//     (Fig. 5c). Encoded as a sequential three-condition assay.
//
// DETECTION:
//   Absorbance at 660 nm (cell density proxy), PHERAstar reader,
//   scan matrix 15x15, scan width 3 mm, focal height 8.7 mm.
//   Fluorescence: 488 nm excitation / 520 nm emission (LipidTOX),
//   scan matrix 20x20, scan width 3 mm, focal height 8.7 mm,
//   gain = 550. DCFDA: excitation 490 nm / emission 526 nm.
//
// KEY FINDINGS ENCODED:
//   Yellow LEDs (580 nm) cause >2x neutral lipid accumulation
//   vs. control; 15 h blue / 9 h yellow cycling produces ~4x
//   lipid increase (best hit). Yellow light correlates with
//   elevated ROS; ascorbate reverses the effect, consistent
//   with photooxidative stress mechanism.
//
// NOTE ON TIMING ABSTRACTION:
//   BioScript `heat` durations use s/m tokens only.
//   6 h = 360m, 9 h = 540m, 15 h = 900m, 18 h = 1080m,
//   24 h = 1440m. All conversions applied below.
//
// NOTE ON PARALLELISM ABSTRACTION:
//   The DMF device simultaneously cultures 8 droplets per
//   condition. BioScript encodes a single representative
//   droplet lineage per condition. The bussed electrode
//   architecture handles parallelism in hardware. Three
//   physical device replicates (n=3) are run separately.
//
// NOTE ON ACTIVE RESERVOIR:
//   Both reservoirs (algae suspension and LipidTOX) are
//   continuously circulated on their four active electrodes
//   to maintain homogeneous cell density before each
//   dispense step. This is abstracted as a `mix` loop on
//   the reservoir droplets prior to culture dispensing.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- device loading, active reservoir
//                             mixing, multicolour screen (P1)
//   BB2  colourPass        -- absorbSignal1 > 0: valid cell
//                             density; proceed to fluorescence
//   BB3  colourFail        -- absorbSignal1 <= 0: no cells; drain
//   BB4  colourJoin        -- join: blue/yellow screen (P2)
//   BB5  blueYellowPass    -- absorbSignal2 > 0: proceed to ROS
//   BB6  blueYellowFail    -- absorbSignal2 <= 0: drain
//   BB7  blueYellowJoin    -- join: ROS mechanistic assay (P3)
//   BB8  rosYellowPass     -- rosSignalYellow > 0: valid ROS
//                             signal; dispose
//   BB9  rosYellowFail     -- rosSignalYellow <= 0: drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// DEVICE LOADING (STEP 1):
// Load algae suspension (150 uL, 1.5e6 cells/mL) and LipidTOX
// working solution (120 uL, 200x diluted stock) into their
// respective active reservoirs. Each reservoir circulates
// continuously on four electrodes to prevent cell settling
// and maintain homogeneous density before dispensing.
// These are the only two manual pipette steps required for
// a full 24 h run generating 48 measurements.
// NOTE: `mix` abstracts active-reservoir continuous circulation
// (not a single mixing event); duration = pre-dispense hold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

algaeReservoir     = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
lipidTOXReservoir  = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock

// Active reservoir circulation to maintain cell homogeneity
// before culture droplets are dispensed (Step 2).
algaeCirculating   = mix algaeReservoir with algaeReservoir for 10s
lipidTOXCirculating = mix lipidTOXReservoir with lipidTOXReservoir for 10s

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: MULTICOLOUR LED SCREEN (HIGH INTENSITY)
// 7 wavelength conditions + dark control, 250 umol/m2/s,
// all LEDs on for 24 h. Encodes the yellow LED arm as the
// representative condition for lipid accumulation (best
// single-colour result, Fig. 3d/f).
// Full screen requires 8 separate device runs (one per colour).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Dispense 8 culture droplets (12 uL each) from algae
// active reservoir into 8 algae culture zone electrodes, in
// series. Bussed dispensing ensures all 8 dispense in one
// electrode actuation sequence.
// Representative: single culture droplet lineage encoded here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cultureDrop1       = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Dispense LipidTOX source droplet (~15 uL) from dye
// active reservoir onto dye dispensing bus, forming 8 label
// droplets (2 uL each) simultaneously via bussed electrodes.
// Representative: single label droplet encoded here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

labelDrop1         = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Dispense 8 daughter culture droplets (2 uL each)
// from culture zones to L-shaped absorbance detection
// electrodes. Device placed on transparent 384-well plate;
// PHERAstar reads absorbance at 660 nm (cell density).
// Time point 1: t = 0 h (baseline before illumination).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

daughterCulture1   = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// Absorbance measurement at t=0 (cell density baseline).
// Device positioned on transparent 384-well plate,
// PHERAstar plate reader, 660 nm, scan matrix 15x15,
// scan width 3 mm, focal height 8.7 mm.
absorbT0_colour    = detect absorbanceDetection on daughterCulture1 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Mix 8 daughter culture droplets with 8 label droplets
// (one-to-one merge); incubate 5 min for LipidTOX staining.
// Device placed on black 384-well plate; PHERAstar reads
// fluorescence at 488 nm ex / 520 nm em (LipidTOX/neutral lipid).
// Time point 1: t = 0 h (lipid baseline before illumination).
// After measurement, mixed droplets are driven to waste
// reservoirs; fluid wicks through 1 mm through-holes.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stainedDrop1       = mix daughterCulture1 with labelDrop1 for 5m
fluorT0_colour     = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stainedDrop1 for 30s

dispose stainedDrop1

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ILLUMINATION PHASE 1 (6 h, yellow LEDs, 250 umol/m2/s):
// Device placed under custom LED array (Fig. S2 in paper).
// Yellow LED array: peak ~580 nm.
// `heat` abstracts LED array incubation at ambient temp (20 C).
// After 6 h: repeat Steps 4-5 for time point 2 measurement.
// 6 h = 360m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop1 at 20c for 360m

// Time point 2 absorbance (t = 6 h).
daughterCulture2   = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
absorbT6_colour    = detect absorbanceDetection on daughterCulture2 for 30s

labelDrop2         = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
stainedDrop2       = mix daughterCulture2 with labelDrop2 for 5m
fluorT6_colour     = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stainedDrop2 for 30s

dispose stainedDrop2

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ILLUMINATION PHASE 2 (remaining 18 h, yellow LEDs):
// Device incubated a further 18 h under yellow illumination
// to complete the 24 h total exposure.
// After 24 h total: repeat Steps 4-5 for time point 3.
// 18 h = 1080m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop1 at 20c for 1080m

// Time point 3 absorbance (t = 24 h, primary endpoint).
daughterCulture3   = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// QC gate keyed on absorbance signal at t=24h.
absorbSignal1      = detect absorbanceDetection on daughterCulture3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Multicolour screen QC gate (absorbance at 24 h)
// Pass (BB2): absorbSignal1 > 0 -> valid cell density; proceed
//             to fluorescence measurement and lipid quantitation.
// Fail (BB3): absorbSignal1 <= 0 -> no cells (settling/dropout);
//             drain culture droplet.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (colourJoin).
// ============================================================

if (absorbSignal1 > 0) {
    labelDrop3         = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
    stainedDrop3       = mix daughterCulture3 with labelDrop3 for 5m
    fluorT24_colour    = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stainedDrop3 for 30s
    dispose stainedDrop3
    dispose fluorT24_colour
} else {
    drain daughterCulture3
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: colourJoin
// Dispose multicolour screen QC signals. Control falls into
// blue/yellow cycling screen (Protocol 2).
// ============================================================

dispose absorbSignal1
dispose absorbT0_colour
dispose fluorT0_colour
dispose absorbT6_colour
dispose fluorT6_colour

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: BLUE/YELLOW CYCLING SCREEN
// Optimal condition: 15 h blue (450 nm) / 9 h yellow (580 nm).
// High intensity: 250 umol/m2/s throughout.
// This condition produced ~4x lipid increase vs. control
// (Fig. 4b) and scaled to macroscale (200 mL flasks, Fig. 4d).
// Other 7 timing variants follow the same structure.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Fresh culture droplet for the blue/yellow cycling run.
// Active reservoir re-circulates to maintain homogeneity
// before dispensing for Protocol 2.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cultureDrop_BY     = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// Baseline measurement before cycling illumination (t = 0 h).
labelDrop_BY0      = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
daughter_BY0       = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

absorbBY_T0        = detect absorbanceDetection on daughter_BY0 for 30s

stained_BY0        = mix daughter_BY0 with labelDrop_BY0 for 5m
fluorBY_T0         = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stained_BY0 for 30s

dispose stained_BY0

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BLUE PHASE (15 h, LED array ~450 nm, 250 umol/m2/s):
// Blue illumination supports high algal growth rate
// (highest biomass accumulation, consistent with chlorophyll c
// absorbance maxima at blue wavelengths).
// 15 h = 900m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop_BY at 20c for 900m

// Mid-point measurement after 15 h blue (t = 15 h).
daughter_BY15      = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
labelDrop_BY15     = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock

absorbBY_T15       = detect absorbanceDetection on daughter_BY15 for 30s

stained_BY15       = mix daughter_BY15 with labelDrop_BY15 for 5m
fluorBY_T15        = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stained_BY15 for 30s

dispose stained_BY15

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// YELLOW PHASE (9 h, LED array ~580 nm, 250 umol/m2/s):
// Yellow phase drives neutral lipid accumulation via
// photooxidative stress while maintaining growth rates
// established during the preceding blue phase.
// 9 h = 540m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop_BY at 20c for 540m

// Final measurement after 9 h yellow / 24 h total (t = 24 h).
daughter_BY24      = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// QC gate keyed on absorbance at t=24h.
absorbSignal2      = detect absorbanceDetection on daughter_BY24 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Blue/yellow screen QC gate (absorbance at 24 h)
// Pass (BB5): absorbSignal2 > 0 -> valid cell density; proceed
//             to lipid fluorescence measurement at t=24h.
// Fail (BB6): absorbSignal2 <= 0 -> no cells; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (blueYellowJoin).
// ============================================================

if (absorbSignal2 > 0) {
    labelDrop_BY24     = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
    stained_BY24       = mix daughter_BY24 with labelDrop_BY24 for 5m
    fluorBY_T24        = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stained_BY24 for 30s
    dispose stained_BY24
    dispose fluorBY_T24
} else {
    drain daughter_BY24
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: blueYellowJoin
// Dispose blue/yellow screen QC signals. Control falls into
// ROS mechanistic assay (Protocol 3).
// ============================================================

dispose absorbSignal2
dispose absorbBY_T0
dispose fluorBY_T0
dispose absorbBY_T15
dispose fluorBY_T15

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 3: ROS MECHANISTIC ASSAY (DCFDA)
// Tests whether yellow illumination increases reactive oxygen
// species (ROS) production relative to blue and normal
// (12 h white/12 h dark) conditions, and whether ascorbate
// antioxidant reverses the effect (Fig. 5c).
//
// Conditions encoded (three sequential arms):
//   Arm A: Yellow 24 h (ROS positive)
//   Arm B: Blue 24 h (ROS negative control)
//   Arm C: Yellow 24 h + ascorbate (antioxidant rescue)
//   Arm D: Silicon deprivation (positive control, off-chip)
//     -- omitted here as it is an off-chip macroscale control
//        run in 200 mL Pyrex flasks, not on the DMF device.
//
// DCFDA PROTOCOL (macroscale, abstracted on-chip):
//   Algae grown at 5e6 cells/mL in 200 mL Pyrex flasks under
//   standard conditions (12 h light/dark) for >=1.5 weeks.
//   Cells centrifuged (3000 rpm, 5 min), resuspended in 50 mL
//   complete media or complete media without sodium silicate
//   or complete media + 50 ug/mL ascorbic acid.
//   Illuminated under assigned condition.
//   DCFDA kit: cells incubated at 37 C for 30 min in dark,
//   washed 1x, re-suspended; 150 uL aliquots read in
//   black-bottom 96-well plates.
//   `heat` at 37 C for 30 min abstracts DCFDA incubation.
//   `detect rosFluorescenceDetection` abstracts CLARIOStar/
//   PHERAstar readout (ex 490 nm / em 526 nm for DCFDA/MUF).
//
// NOTE: ROS assay was validated at macroscale (200 mL flasks);
// BioScript encodes the on-chip abstraction for consistency
// with the DMF screening context of the paper.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM A: YELLOW 24 h -- ROS positive arm
// Fresh algae in complete media, illuminated yellow 24 h.
// 24 h = 1440m (illumination); DCFDA incubation: 30m at 37C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rosAlgae_Yellow    = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// Yellow illumination (24 h = 1440m).
heat rosAlgae_Yellow at 20c for 1440m

// DCFDA staining incubation (37 C, 30 min, dark).
heat rosAlgae_Yellow at 37c for 30m

// Fluorescence detection: DCFDA ROS reporter (ex 490 / em 526).
// QC gate keyed on yellow arm (highest expected ROS signal).
rosSignalYellow    = detect rosFluorescenceDetection on rosAlgae_Yellow for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM B: BLUE 24 h -- ROS negative control
// Fresh algae in complete media, illuminated blue 24 h.
// Blue light supports high growth (chlorophyll c maxima)
// but does not drive photooxidative stress; expected low ROS.
// 24 h = 1440m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rosAlgae_Blue      = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

heat rosAlgae_Blue at 20c for 1440m
heat rosAlgae_Blue at 37c for 30m

rosSignalBlue      = detect rosFluorescenceDetection on rosAlgae_Blue for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM C: YELLOW 24 h + ASCORBATE -- antioxidant rescue
// Complete media supplemented with 50 ug/mL ascorbic acid.
// Ascorbate scavenges ROS; reversal of yellow-light ROS
// elevation confirms photooxidative stress mechanism (Fig. 5c).
// 24 h = 1440m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rosAlgae_Ascorbate = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
ascorbateDrop      = dispense 1 units of AscorbicAcid

rosAlgae_AscMix    = mix rosAlgae_Ascorbate with ascorbateDrop for 5s

heat rosAlgae_AscMix at 20c for 1440m
heat rosAlgae_AscMix at 37c for 30m

rosSignalAscorbate = detect rosFluorescenceDetection on rosAlgae_AscMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: ROS assay QC gate (keyed on yellow arm)
// Pass (BB8): rosSignalYellow > 0 -> valid DCFDA fluorescence
//             detected; dispose all three ROS arm droplets.
//             Expected: Yellow > Blue; Yellow+Ascorbate ~ Blue
//             (antioxidant rescue confirmed).
// Fail (BB9): rosSignalYellow <= 0 -> no ROS signal
//             (DCFDA failure or cell dropout); drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rosSignalYellow > 0) {
    dispose rosAlgae_Yellow
    dispose rosAlgae_Blue
    dispose rosAlgae_AscMix
} else {
    drain rosAlgae_Yellow
    drain rosAlgae_Blue
    drain rosAlgae_AscMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all ROS assay QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose rosSignalYellow
dispose rosSignalBlue
dispose rosSignalAscorbate

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module saAnalysis
module aminoAcidAnalysis

manifest MeOH
manifest HydrazineReagent
manifest AADerivatizationReagent
manifest AASolvent
manifest DBSPunch
manifest InternalStandard_13C5_SA

// ============================================================
// Dried Blood Spot Analysis by Digital Microfluidics Coupled
// to Nanoelectrospray Ionization Mass Spectrometry.
// Shih, Yang, Jebrail, Fobel, McIntosh, Al-Dirbashi,
// Chakraborty, Wheeler - Anal. Chem. 2012, 84, 3731-3738.
// DOI: 10.1021/ac300305s
//
// PROTOCOL OVERVIEW:
//   A 3.2 mm diameter dried blood spot (DBS) punch on Whatman
//   903 filter paper is loaded onto the DMF device bottom plate.
//   A nine-step automated protocol performs sequential solvent
//   extraction, derivatization, and nESI-MS/MS analysis of
//   succinylacetone (SA), a biomarker for hepatorenal tyrosinemia
//   (tyrosinemia type 1, HT).
//
//   Optionally, an extended protocol using a second nESI emitter
//   also enables parallel amino acid (AA) analysis from the
//   methanol pre-extractate (Fig. 6 in paper).
//
// KEY REAGENTS:
//   MeOH:               Neat methanol, pre-extraction solvent.
//   HydrazineReagent:   6.5 mM hydrazine + 15 uM 13C5-SA in
//                       80:20 acetonitrile:H2O + 0.1% v/v formic
//                       acid. SA extraction/derivatization/MS solvent.
//   AADerivatizationReagent: 3 N HCl in n-butanol, for amino acid
//                       butyl ester derivatization at 75 C.
//   AASolvent:          Acetonitrile:H2O 4:1 v/v, AA MS solvent.
//   InternalStandard_13C5_SA: 13C5-labeled succinylacetone (15 uM),
//                       co-dispensed in HydrazineReagent. Modelled
//                       as a separate manifest for clarity; in
//                       practice it is pre-mixed into HydrazineReagent.
//
// DROPLET VOLUMES: 15 uL per droplet for all steps.
//   Device gap: ~450 um (5x double-sided tape spacer).
//   Each 15 uL droplet spans approx. two 2.2 x 2.2 mm electrodes.
//
// ELECTRODE ACTUATION:
//   AC: 150-350 V_rms sine wave at 15 kHz (function generator +
//   amplifier). Automated impedance-based feedback control
//   (RBBB Arduino): if movement fails, voltage steps up 50 V_rms
//   (max 350 V_rms) until success. 100% movement success rate
//   achieved vs. 60% without feedback.
//
// nESI-MS INTERFACE:
//   Pulled-glass capillary emitter (360 um o.d., 50 um i.d.,
//   30 um tip i.d.) inserted between DMF plates. Droplet fills
//   capillary by capillary action (~100 nL capacity). DC 1.7-2.2 kV
//   applied to ITO top plate to generate stable nanoelectrospray
//   into LTQ mass spectrometer (Thermo Scientific).
//   Spray stable for >200 s, RSD = 7.3%, consumption ~800 nL/min.
//
// MS/MS DETECTION:
//   SA derivatized with hydrazine -> hydrazone derivative.
//   Parent ion -> 25% CID -> neutral loss of H2O (18 m/z).
//   SA: m/z 155 -> 137. 13C5-SA (IS): m/z 160 -> 142.
//   Spectra averaged over 50 acquisitions.
//   Calibration range: 5-80 uM SA in DBS punches.
//   R^2 = 0.9923. LOD: 4.95 uM (2.43 ng). Recovery: 85.2%.
//   HT clinical range: 16-150 uM.
//   Validated vs. NSO gold standard (paired t-test, p=0.05,
//   t=0.8177 -> no significant difference at 95% CI, Table 2).
//
// TEMPERATURE CONTROL:
//   Step 7 (SA extraction incubation): 37 C on hot-plate until
//   evaporation (~15 min). Modelled as heat at 37c for 15m.
//   AA derivatization step: 75 C until dryness (~15 min).
//   Modelled as heat at 75c for 15m.
//
// NOTE ON DBS ABSTRACTION:
//   The DBS punch is a solid-phase object placed on the DMF
//   device bottom plate. `mix` operations model the actuation
//   of a liquid droplet across and around the DBS punch (circular
//   5-electrode actuation pattern). The punch is not dispensed
//   from a reservoir; it is pre-loaded before the protocol begins.
//   DBSPunch is declared as a manifest to allow BioScript to
//   reference the punch location in mix steps.
//
// NOTE ON COMPILER CONSTRAINTS (lilott8/BioScript):
//   - Duration tokens: s (seconds) and m (minutes) only.
//   - `heat` models both hot-plate incubation and evaporation steps.
//   - No multi-unit dispense arrays are used; all droplets are
//     scalar 1-unit operations to avoid stranded array elements.
//   - Waste removal after each MeOH step modelled as `drain`.
//   - The nESI spray and MS detection are modelled as `detect`
//     calls using the saAnalysis / aminoAcidAnalysis modules.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- entry: pre-extraction (steps 1-6),
//                           SA extraction/derivatization (steps 7-8),
//                           nESI-MS analysis (step 9), AA branch
//   BB2  saPass           -- saSignal > 0: SA detected in range;
//                           dispose derivatized droplet
//   BB3  saFail           -- saSignal <= 0: signal below LOD or
//                           extraction failed; drain
//   BB4  saJoin           -- join: AA analysis branch begins
//   BB5  aaPass           -- aaSignal > 0: amino acids detected;
//                           dispose AA droplet
//   BB6  aaFail           -- aaSignal <= 0: AA signal invalid; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: MeOH pre-extraction #1 (15 min, room temperature).
//   A 15 uL droplet of neat methanol is loaded into the device
//   reservoir by pipetting at the plate edge and applying
//   driving potential to draw it in. The droplet is then
//   actuated to the DBS punch position and incubated for 15 min.
//   Methanol extracts amino acids, acylcarnitines, and other
//   small molecules that diffuse out of the blood matrix into
//   the solvent. SA remains in the residual blood spot at
//   this stage (it is extracted by hydrazine in step 7).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

meoh1        = dispense 1 units of MeOH
dbsPunch1    = dispense 1 units of DBSPunch
preExtract1  = mix meoh1 with dbsPunch1 for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Actuate MeOH pre-extractate #1 to waste reservoir.
//   After incubation, the methanol droplet (now containing
//   extracted amino acids and acylcarnitines) is actuated
//   away from the DBS punch to a waste reservoir electrode.
//   The DBS punch remains on the bottom plate.
//   In the extended AA-analysis protocol (Fig. 6), this
//   extractate is NOT wasted but instead isolated for
//   derivatization; see STEP 2a/2b branch below.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

drain preExtract1

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: MeOH pre-extraction #2 (15 min, room temperature).
//   A fresh 15 uL MeOH droplet is dispensed and actuated to
//   the residual DBS punch for a second pre-extraction cycle.
//   Three sequential methanol pre-extractions are performed
//   to maximise removal of compounds that would otherwise
//   interfere with the SA hydrazine derivatization step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

meoh2        = dispense 1 units of MeOH
preExtract2  = mix meoh2 with dbsPunch1 for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Actuate MeOH pre-extractate #2 to waste.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

drain preExtract2

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: MeOH pre-extraction #3 (15 min, room temperature).
//   Third and final methanol pre-extraction cycle.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

meoh3        = dispense 1 units of MeOH
preExtract3  = mix meoh3 with dbsPunch1 for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Actuate MeOH pre-extractate #3 to waste.
//   After three pre-extraction cycles, the DBS punch retains
//   succinylacetone (SA), which is not efficiently extracted
//   by methanol. The residual punch is now ready for SA
//   extraction with hydrazine reagent.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

drain preExtract3

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: SA extraction and derivatization - Part A (37 C,
//   15 min to evaporation).
//   A 15 uL droplet of the SA extraction/derivatization/MS
//   solvent (6.5 mM hydrazine + 15 uM 13C5-SA internal
//   standard in 80:20 acetonitrile:H2O + 0.1% formic acid)
//   is loaded and actuated to the residual DBS punch.
//   The device is placed on a hot-plate at 37 C. The droplet
//   incubates until evaporation (~15 min). Hydrazine reacts
//   with SA to form a stable hydrazone derivative. The
//   evaporation step concentrates the derivatized analyte.
//   Reaction mechanism: see Sander et al. Clin. Chem. 2006.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hydrazineReagent1 = dispense 1 units of HydrazineReagent
is1               = dispense 1 units of InternalStandard_13C5_SA
extractionMix1    = mix hydrazineReagent1 with is1 for 5s
saExtraction1     = mix extractionMix1 with dbsPunch1 for 15m

// Incubate at 37 C until evaporation (modelled as 15 min heat).
heat saExtraction1 at 37c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: SA extraction and derivatization - Part B (1 min,
//   room temperature, circular actuation).
//   A fresh 15 uL droplet of the same SA extraction/
//   derivatization/MS solvent is loaded and delivered to the
//   residual (now evaporated) blood spot. The droplet is
//   incubated for 1 min at room temperature. During this
//   minute, the feedback-controlled electrode system actuates
//   the droplet in a circular pattern around the five
//   electrodes adjacent to the DBS punch to maximise
//   re-dissolution and collection of derivatized SA hydrazone.
//   This two-step extraction (evaporate then re-dissolve)
//   is analogous to the conventional method (Allard et al.
//   Clin. Biochem. 2004) but miniaturised onto DMF.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hydrazineReagent2 = dispense 1 units of HydrazineReagent
is2               = dispense 1 units of InternalStandard_13C5_SA
extractionMix2    = mix hydrazineReagent2 with is2 for 5s

// Circular actuation around DBS punch for 1 min re-dissolution.
// `mix` abstracts the 5-electrode circular actuation sequence.
derivatizedSA     = mix extractionMix2 with saExtraction1 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Actuate derivatized SA droplet to nESI capillary
//   emitter inlet and acquire MS/MS data.
//   The droplet is driven to the edge of the pulled-glass
//   capillary emitter entrance orifice. The capillary fills
//   by capillary action (~100 nL capacity, seconds).
//   DC voltage (1.7-2.2 kV) is applied to the ITO top plate
//   to generate a stable nanoelectrospray. MS/MS spectra
//   are collected (50 acquisitions averaged) for SA
//   quantification via neutral loss (m/z 155->137 for SA,
//   160->142 for 13C5-SA). The saAnalysis module abstracts
//   the LTQ MS/MS acquisition and peak ratio calculation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

saSignal = detect saAnalysis on derivatizedSA for 200s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: SA quantification QC gate
// Pass (BB2): saSignal > 0 -> SA detected above LOD (4.95 uM);
//             ratio SA/13C5-SA used for calibration curve
//             quantification; dispose processed droplet.
// Fail (BB3): saSignal <= 0 -> SA below LOD or spray failed;
//             drain processed droplet.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (saJoin).
// ============================================================

if (saSignal > 0) {
    dispose derivatizedSA
} else {
    drain derivatizedSA
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: saJoin
// Dispose SA QC signal. Control falls into the extended
// amino acid (AA) analysis branch (BB5/BB6).
//
// NOTE ON AA BRANCH:
//   In the main protocol (SA-only), the methanol pre-extractates
//   (steps 1-6) are discarded. In the extended protocol (Fig. 6),
//   a 5 min (not 15 min) first MeOH incubation is used, and the
//   extractate is diverted for AA derivatization with n-butanol
//   HCl at 75 C before nESI-MS via a second capillary emitter.
//   This branch models the extended AA protocol using the same
//   DBS punch object as a second dispense to represent the
//   isolated MeOH extractate that would have been collected
//   in step 2 (rather than drained). In the BioScript model,
//   a fresh DBSPunch dispense represents the conceptual
//   isolation of this extractate for downstream AA processing.
// ============================================================

dispose saSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2a (AA extended protocol): Dry the MeOH pre-extractate.
//   The MeOH extractate from the first incubation is actuated
//   to a non-reservoir electrode and evaporated to dryness
//   at room temperature (~15 min). This concentrates the amino
//   acids extracted from the DBS punch prior to derivatization.
//   Modelled as heat at 25 C for 15 min (ambient evaporation).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

meoh_aa      = dispense 1 units of MeOH
dbsPunch2    = dispense 1 units of DBSPunch

// 5 min MeOH incubation for AA extraction (shorter than SA protocol).
aaExtract    = mix meoh_aa with dbsPunch2 for 5m

// Evaporate to dryness at room temperature.
heat aaExtract at 25c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2b (AA extended protocol): Derivatize amino acids.
//   A 15 uL droplet of AA derivatization reagent (3 N HCl
//   in n-butanol) is loaded and actuated to the dried MeOH
//   extractate. Incubated at 75 C on hot-plate until dryness.
//   This forms n-butyl ester derivatives of amino acids
//   compatible with ESI-MS/MS analysis (standard NBS method,
//   analogous to Turgeon et al. Clin. Chem. 2008).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aaDerivReagent   = dispense 1 units of AADerivatizationReagent
aaDerivMix       = mix aaDerivReagent with aaExtract for 5s

// Incubate at 75 C until dryness (butylation reaction).
heat aaDerivMix at 75c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2c (AA extended protocol): Re-dissolve derivatized AAs.
//   A 15 uL droplet of AA MS solvent (acetonitrile:H2O 4:1 v/v)
//   is loaded and driven to the dried butyl-ester derivative
//   to re-dissolve it, then actuated to the second nESI
//   capillary emitter (positioned at the opposite end of the
//   two-emitter device, Fig. 6a). nESI-MS data are collected
//   using the same 1.7-2.2 kV DC spray parameters.
//   AAs identified include: VAL, MET, TYR, HIS, GLN, PRO,
//   PHE, ASP (Fig. 6b, primary MS spectrum).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aaSolventDrop    = dispense 1 units of AASolvent
aaReadySample    = mix aaSolventDrop with aaDerivMix for 1m

aaSignal = detect aminoAcidAnalysis on aaReadySample for 200s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: AA analysis QC gate
// Pass (BB5): aaSignal > 0 -> amino acid peaks detected;
//             dispose AA droplet.
// Fail (BB6): aaSignal <= 0 -> no AA signal (derivatization
//             or spray failed); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (aaSignal > 0) {
    dispose aaReadySample
} else {
    drain aaReadySample
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all QC signal droplets. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose aaSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module impedanceSensing
module cellCountDetection

manifest HeLa_Cells
manifest CHO_K1_Cells
manifest NIH3T3_Cells
manifest CompleteMedia_DMEM
manifest CompleteMedia_F12DMEM
manifest SucroseBuffer
manifest FCS_Stock
manifest TrypsinEDTA
manifest PluronicF68

// ============================================================
// Digital Microfluidics with Impedance Sensing for
// Integrated Cell Culture and Analysis.
// Shih, Barbulovic-Nad, Yang, Fobel, Wheeler.
// Biosensors and Bioelectronics 42 (2013) 314-320.
// DOI: 10.1016/j.bios.2012.10.035
//
// DMF device: 66 bottom-plate electrodes, ITO top plate with
// 6 patterned 1 mm dia. hydrophilic cell-culture sites.
// Unit droplet: ~1 uL. Virtual microwell: ~0.2 uL.
// Cell media: DMEM + 10% FCS + pen/strep + 0.05% Pluronic F68.
// Impedance sensing voltage (Vsense): 100 Vrms AC, 15 kHz.
// Low-conductivity measurement medium: 500 mM aqueous sucrose
//   (10 mM HEPES, 0.05% Pluronic F68, pH 7.4).
// Passive dispensing (S1-S3): unit droplet translated across
//   hydrophilic site -> spontaneous virtual microwell formation.
// Reagent exchange (E1-E3): three-droplet sequential wash
//   sequence to replace microwell contents without disturbing
//   the cell monolayer.
// All cell suspensions supplemented with 0.05% Pluronic F68
//   (w/v) to prevent biofouling during DMF manipulation.
//
// THREE ASSAYS ENCODED IN SEQUENCE:
//   ASSAY 1: Calibration -- three cell lines (HeLa, CHO-K1,
//     NIH-3T3) seeded at three volumetric densities (0.5, 1.0,
//     2.0 x 10^6 cells/mL). Vsense measured at 15 kHz after
//     sucrose exchange. Regression: R2 >= 0.99 for all lines.
//     LOD: 20-25 cells/mm2.
//   ASSAY 2: Proliferation -- three cell lines seeded at
//     0.25 x 10^6 cells/mL; Vsense measured at 24h intervals
//     over 4 days. Vsense translated to surface density via
//     calibration regression curves.
//   ASSAY 3: Serum screening -- NIH-3T3 cells in dilution
//     series of FCS (0.63%, 1.25%, 2.5%, 5%, 10%) generated
//     on-chip; Vsense measured every 24h over 4 days.
//     At 5% and 10% FCS, sigmoidal growth profiles observed.
//
// NOTE ON VIRTUAL MICROWELL ABSTRACTION:
//   `mix` steps labelled "seeding" abstract the passive
//   dispensing event (S1-S3): a unit droplet is driven over
//   the hydrophilic ITO site, leaving a 0.2 uL virtual
//   microwell containing cells. This is not reagent mixing
//   in the DMF electrode sense.
//
// NOTE ON SUCROSE EXCHANGE ABSTRACTION:
//   `mix` steps labelled "exchange" abstract the E1-E3
//   three-droplet wash sequence. The sucrose buffer replaces
//   the cell media immediately before impedance measurement;
//   low-conductivity sucrose resolves density-dependent
//   impedance differences that are undetectable in full media.
//   Cells are exposed to sucrose for ~10 min (no viability
//   impact for any cell type tested).
//
// NOTE ON INCUBATION:
//   All cell culture incubations are at 37C / 5% CO2.
//   BioScript `heat` abstracts closed incubator conditions.
//   24h = 1440m; 6h = 360m.
//
// NOTE ON IMPEDANCE DETECTION:
//   `detect impedanceSensing` abstracts applying 100 Vrms
//   at 15 kHz to the cell-sensor electrode (bottom plate)
//   relative to the ITO top plate, and recording Vsense.
//   The feedback-control impedance circuit (Fig S1) is the
//   same hardware repurposed for cell density measurement.
//   `detect cellCountDetection` abstracts the microscopy-
//   based cell count used to validate Vsense regression
//   (ImageJ cell counting of surface density images).
//
// NOTE ON SERUM DILUTION (ASSAY 3):
//   Five FCS concentrations (0.63%, 1.25%, 2.5%, 5%, 10%)
//   are generated on-chip by the D1-D9 dilution program
//   using 20% FCS as "reagent" and serum-free DMEM as
//   "diluent". In BioScript, serial dilution is represented
//   as explicit dispense + mix chains (compiler does not
//   support parametric dilution loops). Each concentration
//   is a separate named droplet variable.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- entry: calibration assay
//                           (3 cell lines x 3 densities)
//   BB2  calibPass        -- calibSignal > 0: valid Vsense;
//                           dispose; proceed to proliferation
//   BB3  calibFail        -- calibSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  calibJoin        -- join: proliferation assay begins
//   BB5  prolifPass       -- prolifSignal > 0: growth detected;
//                           dispose; proceed to serum assay
//   BB6  prolifFail       -- prolifSignal <= 0: no growth; drain
//   BB7  prolifJoin       -- join: serum screening assay begins
//   BB8  serumPass        -- serumSignal > 0: valid growth curve;
//                           dispose all serum droplets
//   BB9  serumFail        -- serumSignal <= 0: no growth signal;
//                           drain all serum droplets
//   BB10 finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 (CALIBRATION) -- STEP 1: Seed HeLa cells (low
//   density, 0.5 x 10^6 cells/mL) onto virtual microwell 1.
//   Passive dispensing (S1-S3) modelled as `mix` of cell
//   suspension with complete DMEM over hydrophilic site.
//   24h incubation at 37C to allow cell attachment and spread.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

helaLow_Media    = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
helaLow_Cells    = dispense 1 units of HeLa_Cells
helaLow_Seeded   = mix helaLow_Cells with helaLow_Media for 5s

heat helaLow_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 2: Exchange HeLa low-density microwell
//   with sucrose buffer (E1-E3) prior to Vsense measurement.
//   Three-droplet sequential wash modelled as single mix step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sucrose_helaLow     = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
helaLow_Exchanged   = mix helaLow_Seeded with sucrose_helaLow for 10s

// Vsense at 15 kHz: 100 Vrms pulse, 1s duration.
helaLow_Vsense      = detect impedanceSensing on helaLow_Exchanged for 1s

// Microscopy QC: ImageJ cell count to validate surface density.
helaLow_Count       = detect cellCountDetection on helaLow_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 3: Seed HeLa cells (mid density,
//   1.0 x 10^6 cells/mL) onto virtual microwell 2.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

helaMid_Media    = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
helaMid_Cells    = dispense 1 units of HeLa_Cells
helaMid_Seeded   = mix helaMid_Cells with helaMid_Media for 5s

heat helaMid_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_helaMid     = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
helaMid_Exchanged   = mix helaMid_Seeded with sucrose_helaMid for 10s

helaMid_Vsense      = detect impedanceSensing on helaMid_Exchanged for 1s
helaMid_Count       = detect cellCountDetection on helaMid_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 4: Seed HeLa cells (high density,
//   2.0 x 10^6 cells/mL) onto virtual microwell 3.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

helaHigh_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
helaHigh_Cells   = dispense 1 units of HeLa_Cells
helaHigh_Seeded  = mix helaHigh_Cells with helaHigh_Media for 5s

heat helaHigh_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_helaHigh    = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
helaHigh_Exchanged  = mix helaHigh_Seeded with sucrose_helaHigh for 10s

helaHigh_Vsense     = detect impedanceSensing on helaHigh_Exchanged for 1s
helaHigh_Count      = detect cellCountDetection on helaHigh_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 5: Seed NIH-3T3 cells (low density,
//   0.5 x 10^6 cells/mL) onto virtual microwell 4.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nih3t3Low_Media  = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
nih3t3Low_Cells  = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_Cells
nih3t3Low_Seeded = mix nih3t3Low_Cells with nih3t3Low_Media for 5s

heat nih3t3Low_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_nih3t3Low     = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
nih3t3Low_Exchanged   = mix nih3t3Low_Seeded with sucrose_nih3t3Low for 10s

nih3t3Low_Vsense      = detect impedanceSensing on nih3t3Low_Exchanged for 1s
nih3t3Low_Count       = detect cellCountDetection on nih3t3Low_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 6: Seed NIH-3T3 cells (mid density,
//   1.0 x 10^6 cells/mL) onto virtual microwell 5.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nih3t3Mid_Media  = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
nih3t3Mid_Cells  = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_Cells
nih3t3Mid_Seeded = mix nih3t3Mid_Cells with nih3t3Mid_Media for 5s

heat nih3t3Mid_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_nih3t3Mid     = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
nih3t3Mid_Exchanged   = mix nih3t3Mid_Seeded with sucrose_nih3t3Mid for 10s

nih3t3Mid_Vsense      = detect impedanceSensing on nih3t3Mid_Exchanged for 1s
nih3t3Mid_Count       = detect cellCountDetection on nih3t3Mid_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 7: Seed NIH-3T3 cells (high density,
//   2.0 x 10^6 cells/mL) onto virtual microwell 6.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nih3t3High_Media  = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
nih3t3High_Cells  = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_Cells
nih3t3High_Seeded = mix nih3t3High_Cells with nih3t3High_Media for 5s

heat nih3t3High_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_nih3t3High    = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
nih3t3High_Exchanged  = mix nih3t3High_Seeded with sucrose_nih3t3High for 10s

nih3t3High_Vsense     = detect impedanceSensing on nih3t3High_Exchanged for 1s
nih3t3High_Count      = detect cellCountDetection on nih3t3High_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 8: Seed CHO-K1 cells (low density,
//   0.5 x 10^6 cells/mL). Media: 50/50 v/v F-12/DMEM + 10%
//   FCS + pen/strep + 0.05% Pluronic F68.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

choLow_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_F12DMEM
choLow_Cells   = dispense 1 units of CHO_K1_Cells
choLow_Seeded  = mix choLow_Cells with choLow_Media for 5s

heat choLow_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_choLow    = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
choLow_Exchanged  = mix choLow_Seeded with sucrose_choLow for 10s

choLow_Vsense     = detect impedanceSensing on choLow_Exchanged for 1s
choLow_Count      = detect cellCountDetection on choLow_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 9: Seed CHO-K1 cells (mid density,
//   1.0 x 10^6 cells/mL).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

choMid_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_F12DMEM
choMid_Cells   = dispense 1 units of CHO_K1_Cells
choMid_Seeded  = mix choMid_Cells with choMid_Media for 5s

heat choMid_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_choMid    = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
choMid_Exchanged  = mix choMid_Seeded with sucrose_choMid for 10s

choMid_Vsense     = detect impedanceSensing on choMid_Exchanged for 1s
choMid_Count      = detect cellCountDetection on choMid_Exchanged for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 1 -- STEP 10: Seed CHO-K1 cells (high density,
//   2.0 x 10^6 cells/mL).
//   QC gate uses NIH-3T3 high-density signal as representative
//   calibration signal (highest Vsense, clearest separation;
//   paper Fig. 4b regression R2=0.9935 for NIH-3T3).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

choHigh_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_F12DMEM
choHigh_Cells   = dispense 1 units of CHO_K1_Cells
choHigh_Seeded  = mix choHigh_Cells with choHigh_Media for 5s

heat choHigh_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

sucrose_choHigh    = dispense 1 units of SucroseBuffer
choHigh_Exchanged  = mix choHigh_Seeded with sucrose_choHigh for 10s

choHigh_Vsense     = detect impedanceSensing on choHigh_Exchanged for 1s
choHigh_Count      = detect cellCountDetection on choHigh_Exchanged for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Calibration QC gate
// Pass (BB2): nih3t3High_Vsense > 0 -> valid Vsense detected
//             (density-dependent impedance difference confirmed
//             in sucrose; p < 0.001 for high vs low density);
//             dispose all calibration droplets.
// Fail (BB3): nih3t3High_Vsense <= 0 -> no impedance signal
//             (possible: cell loss, electrode fouling, sucrose
//             exchange failure); drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (calibJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nih3t3High_Vsense > 0) {
    dispose helaLow_Exchanged
    dispose helaMid_Exchanged
    dispose helaHigh_Exchanged
    dispose nih3t3Low_Exchanged
    dispose nih3t3Mid_Exchanged
    dispose nih3t3High_Exchanged
    dispose choLow_Exchanged
    dispose choMid_Exchanged
    dispose choHigh_Exchanged
} else {
    drain helaLow_Exchanged
    drain helaMid_Exchanged
    drain helaHigh_Exchanged
    drain nih3t3Low_Exchanged
    drain nih3t3Mid_Exchanged
    drain nih3t3High_Exchanged
    drain choLow_Exchanged
    drain choMid_Exchanged
    drain choHigh_Exchanged
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: calibJoin
// Dispose all calibration Vsense and cell count signals.
// Control falls into proliferation assay (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose helaLow_Vsense
dispose helaMid_Vsense
dispose helaHigh_Vsense
dispose nih3t3Low_Vsense
dispose nih3t3Mid_Vsense
// nih3t3High_Vsense consumed by QC gate if-condition above; do not re-dispose
dispose choLow_Vsense
dispose choMid_Vsense
dispose choHigh_Vsense

dispose helaLow_Count
dispose helaMid_Count
dispose helaHigh_Count
dispose nih3t3Low_Count
dispose nih3t3Mid_Count
dispose nih3t3High_Count
dispose choLow_Count
dispose choMid_Count
dispose choHigh_Count

// ============================================================
// ASSAY 2 (PROLIFERATION)
// Three cell lines seeded at 0.25 x 10^6 cells/mL in virtual
// microwells. Vsense measured at 24h, 48h, 72h, 96h.
// Between each measurement: sucrose exchange -> measure ->
// fresh media exchange -> 24h culture.
// Paper result (Fig. 5a): NIH-3T3 and HeLa proliferate faster
// than CHO-K1; consistent with standard macroscale culture.
// Day 1: all cell lines below LOD (~20-25 cells/mm2).
// Days 2-4: measurable surface densities obtained.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSAY 2 -- DAY 0: Seed all three cell lines at
//   0.25 x 10^6 cells/mL. 24h incubation (1440m).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

prolif_HeLa_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
prolif_HeLa_Cells   = dispense 1 units of HeLa_Cells
prolif_HeLa_Seeded  = mix prolif_HeLa_Cells with prolif_HeLa_Media for 5s

heat prolif_HeLa_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

prolif_NIH_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_DMEM
prolif_NIH_Cells   = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_Cells
prolif_NIH_Seeded  = mix prolif_NIH_Cells with prolif_NIH_Media for 5s

heat prolif_NIH_Seeded at 37c for 1440m

prolif_CHO_Media   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia_F12DMEM
prolif_CHO_Cells   = dispense 1 units of CHO_K1_Cells
prolif_CHO_Seeded  = mix prolif_CHO_Cells with prolif_CHO_Media for 5s

