dispose multiPatQC

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module haptotaxisDetection
module chemotaxisDetection
module competingGradientDetection

manifest PBS
manifest Fibronectin
manifest PluronicF127
manifest B4F_BiotinFluorescein
manifest StreptavidinCy3
manifest CCL21_24_98_bio
manifest CCL19
manifest FITCDextran_10kDa
manifest DendriticCells
manifest CellCultureMedium_R10

// ============================================================
// A Microfluidic Device for Measuring Cell Migration Towards
// Substrate-Bound and Soluble Chemokine Gradients.
// Schwarz, Bierbaum, Merrin, Frank, Hauschild, Bollenbach,
// Tay, Sixt, Mehling - Scientific Reports 6:36440 (2016).
// DOI: 10.1038/srep36440
//
// Protocol: Two-layer PDMS microfluidic device for simultaneous
// generation of (i) surface-immobilized haptotactic chemokine
// gradients (CCL21) via LAPAP photo-patterning and (ii) diffusion-
// based soluble chemotactic gradients (CCL19) via flow-switching
// source-sink strategy. Dendritic cells (DCs) derived from
// C57BL/6J mouse bone marrow are tracked at single-cell
// resolution in combined and competing chemokine gradient fields.
//
// Device geometry: 6 migration chambers per chip
//   l = 1100 um, w = 200 um, h_max = 28 um
//   9 reagent inlets, 1 cell loading inlet, 3 waste outlets
//   Independently controllable PDMS membrane valves on all ports
//   Support channels connect reagent inlets to migration chambers
//   Chambers coated with fibronectin (250 ug/mL) for beta2-
//   integrin-mediated DC adhesion and 2D migration.
//
// LAPAP (Laser-Assisted Protein Adsorption by Photobleaching):
//   UV laser (355 nm, pulsed, 20x objective, galvanometric mirrors)
//   photobleaches B4F (biotin-4-fluorescein) covalently deposited
//   on glass surface in arbitrary gradient patterns (~0.7 um
//   lateral resolution, ~100:1 dynamic range). Streptavidin-Cy3
//   bridges B4F to biotin-tagged CCL21 (CCL21 24-98 bio, truncated
//   to remove heparan-sulfate-binding C-terminus, avoiding
//   non-specific background).
//
// Soluble gradient generation: Flow-free diffusion via switching
//   source-sink channels at short ends of chamber. FITC-dextran
//   10 kDa used as proxy tracer (hydrodynamic radius 2.3 nm ~
//   CCL19 at 1.7+/-0.4 nm and CCL21 at 1.9+/-0.4 nm).
//   Peak CCL19 ~1.8 ug/mL at 2.5 h (Fig. 1d).
//
// NOTE ON BS ABSTRACTION:
//   LAPAP laser writing is abstracted as a `mix` of B4F coating
//   with PBS (wash step) to represent the photobleaching and
//   surface functionalization event. All channel flow and valve
//   actuation steps are abstracted via `mix` operations.
//   `heat` statements model temperature-controlled incubation
//   steps. Duration tokens: s and m only (BioScript constraint).
//   48 h = 2880 m; 10 min = 10m; 20 min = 20m; 30 min = 30m.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device prep, fibronectin coating,
//                              LAPAP patterning, CCL21 immobilization,
//                              DC loading, gradient generation
//   BB2  haptotaxisPass     -- haptotaxisSignal > 0: directed DC
//                              migration toward CCL21 gradient detected;
//                              dispose and proceed to chemotaxis branch
//   BB3  haptotaxisFail     -- haptotaxisSignal <= 0: no directed
//                              migration; drain
//   BB4  haptotaxisJoin     -- join: soluble CCL19 chemotaxis branch
//   BB5  chemotaxisPass     -- chemotaxisSignal > 0: directed DC
//                              migration toward CCL19 gradient detected;
//                              dispose and proceed to competing branch
//   BB6  chemotaxisFail     -- chemotaxisSignal <= 0: undirected; drain
//   BB7  chemotaxisJoin     -- join: competing gradient branch begins
//   BB8  competingPass      -- competingSignal > 0: differential
//                              directionality resolved; dispose all
//   BB9  competingFail      -- competingSignal <= 0: no resolution; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose QC signals, end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Chip priming with PBS.
//   Flow lines pressurised at 0.2-0.4 bar. Entire chip filled
//   with PBS. Flow channels connected to reagent inlets.
//   Control channels actuated at 0.5 bar above baseline to
//   determine optimal closing pressure for each chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS1 = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPBS2 = dispense 1 units of PBS
chipPrime   = mix primingPBS1 with primingPBS2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Fibronectin coating of migration chambers.
//   Human plasma fibronectin (c = 250 ug/mL, Millipore) loaded
//   into cell culture chambers via flow channels. Incubated for
//   1 h at room temperature. Fibronectin acts as beta2-integrin
//   ligand enabling DC adhesion and 2D migration on PDMS surface.
//   After 1 h, fibronectin in flow channels flushed with PBS.
//   Chambers then flushed with cell culture medium (R10) for 10 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectin      = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
fibronectinCoat  = mix chipPrime with fibronectin for 60m

// Flush flow channels with PBS after coating.
pbsFlush1        = dispense 1 units of PBS
coatedChamber    = mix fibronectinCoat with pbsFlush1 for 1m

// Flush chambers with R10 medium for 10 min.
r10Medium1       = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
chamberReady     = mix coatedChamber with r10Medium1 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: LAPAP - B4F loading into migration chambers.
//   Chambers washed with PBS (10 s) to remove unbound fibronectin.
//   Biotin-4-fluorescein (B4F, 150 ug/mL, Sigma Aldrich) loaded
//   into assembled, closed channels via reagent inlets.
//   B4F coats the glass surface of the assembled chip
//   prior to UV laser patterning.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash1    = dispense 1 units of PBS
b4fSolution = dispense 1 units of B4F_BiotinFluorescein
b4fLoaded   = mix chamberReady with pbsWash1 for 10s
b4fCoated   = mix b4fLoaded with b4fSolution for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: LAPAP - UV laser gradient writing.
//   355 nm pulsed UV laser (Zeiss LD Plan Neo 20x/0.4 objective)
//   focused at glass-B4F interface. Galvanometric mirror pair
//   scans focus spot across chamber bottom. Pixel intensity image
//   specifies local light dose for gradient patterning.
//   Gradient written one spot at a time; spot spacing ~half focus
//   diameter for continuous pattern.
//   Lateral resolution: ~0.7 um. Dynamic range: ~100:1.
//   Laser pulse frequency: 1 kHz. Calibrated for off-center NA drop.
//   Pattern types: uniform patch (for haptokinesis control) or
//   linear gradient (for haptotaxis experiments).
//
//   NOTE: `mix` here abstracts the laser scanning event over the
//   B4F-coated chamber surface. No reagent mixing in DMF sense.
//   Unbound B4F washed out with PBS after laser writing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lapapPBS     = dispense 1 units of PBS
lapapPattern = mix b4fCoated with lapapPBS for 20m

// Wash unbound B4F from chambers after laser writing.
pbsWash2      = dispense 1 units of PBS
patternWashed = mix lapapPattern with pbsWash2 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Streptavidin-Cy3 (SA-Cy3) incubation.
//   SA-Cy3 (10 ug/mL in PBS with 3% BSA, Sigma Aldrich)
//   loaded into chambers and incubated for 20 min at RT.
//   Streptavidin binds to photobleached B4F anchors in the
//   laser-written pattern, serving as adapter for biotin-
//   coupled CCL21. SA-Cy3 fluorescence allows visualization
//   and quantification of the printed gradient pattern.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

saCy3Solution = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinCy3
saCy3Bound    = mix patternWashed with saCy3Solution for 20m

// Wash with PBS (10 s) to remove unbound SA-Cy3.
pbsWash3      = dispense 1 units of PBS
saCy3Washed   = mix saCy3Bound with pbsWash3 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: CCL21 24-98 bio immobilization.
//   Biotinylated truncated murine CCL21 (CCL21 24-98 bio;
//   custom synthesized by ALMAC, Craigavon, UK) at 250 ng/mL
//   in PBS loaded into chambers. Incubated 30 min at 37 C.
//   Biotin tag on CCL21 C-terminus binds streptavidin anchors
//   in the LAPAP-patterned gradient. Truncated version (aa 24-98)
//   used to prevent unspecific background via the basic C-terminal
//   extension of full-length CCL21 (aa 1-134).
//   Maximal surface density: 157 +/- 33 molecules/um2.
//   Supporting channels kept under constant PBS flow (0.2 bar)
//   during loading to prevent non-specific adsorption outside
//   cell culture chambers.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ccl21Solution   = dispense 1 units of CCL21_24_98_bio
ccl21Immobilized = mix saCy3Washed with ccl21Solution for 30m

// Wash chambers with PBS (10 s) to remove unbound CCL21.
pbsWash4         = dispense 1 units of PBS
ccl21Washed      = mix ccl21Immobilized with pbsWash4 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: DC loading into migration chambers.
//   Bone marrow-derived DCs from C57BL/6J mice (C57BL6 strain),
//   harvested day 8-10 of GM-CSF culture and matured overnight
//   with LPS (200 ng/mL). DC suspension at 10 x 10^6 cells/mL
//   in R10 medium loaded via short-end ports of the migration
//   chambers. Loading via short ends produces a distribution
//   of cells along the chamber length.
//   Cells adhere loosely to fibronectin-coated PDMS surface
//   over ~30 min (Supplemental Movie S2). Round morphology
//   with constant protrusions under control conditions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dcSuspension  = dispense 1 units of DendriticCells
r10Medium2    = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
dcLoaded      = mix ccl21Washed with dcSuspension for 1m
dcAdhered     = mix dcLoaded with r10Medium2 for 30m

// ============================================================
// HAPTOTAXIS ARM: DC migration on immobilized CCL21 gradient
// (without soluble gradient superimposition)
//
// STEP 8: CCL21 haptotaxis detection.
//   DCs imaged on Nikon Ti inverted microscope (10x/NA 0.3
//   and 20x/NA 0.5 Air Plan Fluor Ph1 objectives) with stage-top
//   incubator (37 C, 5% CO2, 90% humidity). EMCCD camera
//   (Hamamatsu C9100-02). Imaging area: 300 x 200 um
//   corresponding to CCL21 gradient pattern region.
//   Cell tracks analyzed with Fiji + Manual Tracking plugin
//   and Matlab 2013. Directionality = <cos(Theta)> where Theta
//   is angle between gradient direction and cell displacement.
//   Directionality bootstrapped 200x with original sample size.
//   Tracking interval: 3 min (cells move ~1 cell diameter).
//
//   Expected results (Fig. 3):
//   - No chemokine: undirected migration (rose plot isotropic)
//   - CCL21 patch (uniform): haptokinesis (increased speed,
//     no directed migration, rose plot isotropic)
//   - CCL21 gradient: haptotaxis (directed toward high [CCL21],
//     rose plot asymmetric toward gradient direction)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

haptotaxisSignal = detect haptotaxisDetection on dcAdhered for 100m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Haptotaxis QC gate
// Pass (BB2): haptotaxisSignal > 0 -> directed DC migration
//             toward CCL21 gradient confirmed; dispose and
//             proceed to chemotaxis branch.
// Fail (BB3): haptotaxisSignal <= 0 -> no directional bias
//             (undirected or haptokinetic only); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (haptotaxisJoin).
// ============================================================

if (haptotaxisSignal > 0) {
    dispose dcAdhered
} else {
    drain dcAdhered
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: haptotaxisJoin
// Dispose haptotaxis QC signal. Control falls into soluble
// CCL19 chemotaxis branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose haptotaxisSignal

// ============================================================
// CHEMOTAXIS ARM: DC migration in soluble CCL19 gradient
// (no immobilized chemokine; diffusion-based gradient only)
//
// STEP 9: Fresh DC loading for chemotaxis experiment.
//   DCs loaded via short-end ports into fibronectin-coated
//   chambers (no CCL21 patterning). Cells distributed along
//   chamber length. 30 min adhesion recovery in R10 medium.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dcSuspension2  = dispense 1 units of DendriticCells
r10Medium3     = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
dcLoaded2      = mix r10Medium3 with dcSuspension2 for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: CCL19 soluble gradient generation.
//   Flow-free diffusion-based gradient generated by source-sink
//   flow-switching strategy (Frank & Tay, Lab Chip 13, 2013).
//   Source channel (one short end): sequentially refilled with
//   R10 + murine CCL19 (2.5 ug/mL; R&D Systems) + FITC-dextran
//   10 kDa (200 ug/mL, hydrodynamic radius 2.3 nm).
//   Sink channel (opposite short end): refilled with fresh R10.
//   Gradient builds by diffusion after flow stops; steepness,
//   mean concentration and duration independently controlled.
//   Peak CCL19 ~1.8 ug/mL after 2.5 h (Fig. 1d).
//   FITC-dextran traces gradient profile for quantification.
//   Control: R10 (no CCL19) from both ends (Fig. 4a).
//
//   Three CCL19 concentration regimes tested (Fig. 4b-d):
//   - CCL19_low:    0-1.2 ug/mL (chemokinetic, undirected)
//   - CCL19_medium: 0-1.3 ug/mL (directed chemotaxis)
//   - CCL19_high:   0-1.7 ug/mL (highly directional chemotaxis)
//
//   NOTE: Three replicate concentration regimes are encoded
//   sequentially. In practice these run in parallel in separate
//   migration chambers of the same chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ccl19Source     = dispense 1 units of CCL19
fitcDextran     = dispense 1 units of FITCDextran_10kDa
r10Sink         = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10

// Build CCL19/FITC-dextran source droplet for gradient.
ccl19FitcMix    = mix ccl19Source with fitcDextran for 5s

// Establish source-sink gradient across chamber.
gradientSetup   = mix dcLoaded2 with ccl19FitcMix for 5s
ccl19Gradient   = mix gradientSetup with r10Sink for 150m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: CCL19 chemotaxis detection.
//   DCs imaged as in STEP 8. Gradient direction and shape
//   indicated by FITC-dextran fluorescence. Cells tracked
//   from t=0 (gradient initiation) for up to 150 min.
//   Directionality plotted as function of chamber position
//   (= local CCL19 concentration; Fig. 4e):
//   - Low CCL19 (0-1.2 ug/mL): chemokinesis (faster, undirected)
//   - Medium CCL19 (0-1.3 ug/mL): significantly increased
//     directionality toward high [CCL19]
//   - High CCL19 (0-1.7 ug/mL): further augmented directionality
//   CCL19-concentration in gradients up to ~190 nM, covering
//   Kd of CCR7/CCL19 (10-100 nM) and sufficient for G-protein
//   loading and downstream signalling assays.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

chemotaxisSignal = detect chemotaxisDetection on ccl19Gradient for 150m

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Chemotaxis QC gate
// Pass (BB5): chemotaxisSignal > 0 -> directed DC migration
//             toward CCL19 gradient confirmed; dispose and
//             proceed to competing gradient branch.
// Fail (BB6): chemotaxisSignal <= 0 -> undirected or
//             chemokinetic only (CCL19 too low); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (chemotaxisJoin).
// ============================================================

if (chemotaxisSignal > 0) {
    dispose ccl19Gradient
} else {
    drain ccl19Gradient
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: chemotaxisJoin
// Dispose chemotaxis QC signal. Control falls into competing
// chemotactic + haptotactic gradient branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose chemotaxisSignal

// ============================================================
// COMPETING GRADIENTS ARM: DC migration in simultaneous
// opposing CCL19 (soluble, chemotactic) and CCL21
// (immobilized, haptotactic) gradients.
//
// STEP 12: Chip preparation with CCL21 gradient + DC loading.
//   CCL21-gradient printed in lower and middle area of migration
//   chamber via LAPAP (STEPS 3-6 protocol; maximal concentration
//   ~160 molecules/um2 = 0.24 ug/mL equivalent unit volume).
//   DCs loaded and positioned to include the two CCL21-gradient
//   regions. 30 min cell recovery post-loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Prepare new LAPAP-patterned CCL21 gradient (abbreviated;
// full patterning protocol as in STEPS 3-6 above).
pbsCompeting   = dispense 1 units of PBS
b4fCompeting   = dispense 1 units of B4F_BiotinFluorescein
saCy3Competing = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinCy3
ccl21Competing = dispense 1 units of CCL21_24_98_bio

b4fLoad2       = mix pbsCompeting with b4fCompeting for 1m
lapapWrite2    = mix b4fLoad2 with pbsCompeting for 20m
saCoat2        = mix lapapWrite2 with saCy3Competing for 20m
ccl21Coat2     = mix saCoat2 with ccl21Competing for 30m

// Load DCs into CCL21-patterned chamber.
dcSuspension3  = dispense 1 units of DendriticCells
r10Medium4     = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
dcOnCCL21      = mix ccl21Coat2 with dcSuspension3 for 1m
dcRecovered    = mix dcOnCCL21 with r10Medium4 for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Opposing CCL19 soluble gradient superimposition.
//   After 30 min DC recovery on CCL21 gradient, diffusion-based
//   CCL19 gradient generated from the opposing direction to
//   the CCL21 gradient (Supplemental Figure S5).
//   Source: CCL19 + FITC-dextran at one short end (high [CCL19]).
//   Sink: R10 medium at opposite short end.
//
//   Two experimental conditions run in parallel on same chip
//   (one of each CCL21-gradient regions receives different
//   CCL19 concentration; Fig. 5):
//
//   Condition A - CCL19_low/CCL21 (Fig. 5a):
//     CCL19 source: 0-1 ug/mL opposing CCL21 gradient.
//     Expected: DC migration toward haptotactic CCL21 gradient
//     (CCL21 signal dominant at low soluble CCL19).
//
//   Condition B - CCL19_medium/CCL21 (Fig. 5b):
//     CCL19 source: 0-1.2 ug/mL opposing CCL21 gradient.
//     Expected: DC migration overrides toward chemotactic CCL19
//     (CCL19 signal dominant at medium concentration, overriding
//     haptotactic CCL21 directionality).
//
//   NOTE: Both conditions encoded sequentially below for CFG
//   clarity. Directionality measured as <cos(Theta)> vs.
//   position in channel and time (Fig. 5c).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Condition A: low CCL19 opposing CCL21 gradient.
ccl19LowSource    = dispense 1 units of CCL19
fitcDextran2      = dispense 1 units of FITCDextran_10kDa
r10SinkA          = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10

ccl19LowFitc      = mix ccl19LowSource with fitcDextran2 for 5s
conditionA        = mix dcRecovered with ccl19LowFitc for 5s
conditionAGrad    = mix conditionA with r10SinkA for 100m

// Condition B: medium CCL19 opposing CCL21 gradient.
ccl19MedSource    = dispense 1 units of CCL19
fitcDextran3      = dispense 1 units of FITCDextran_10kDa
r10SinkB          = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10

ccl19MedFitc      = mix ccl19MedSource with fitcDextran3 for 5s
conditionB        = mix dcRecovered with ccl19MedFitc for 5s
conditionBGrad    = mix conditionB with r10SinkB for 100m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Competing gradient detection and directionality
//   analysis.
//   DCs imaged as in STEP 8. Both SA-Cy3 (CCL21 gradient,
//   red) and FITC-dextran (CCL19 gradient, green) fluorescence
//   channels imaged simultaneously to confirm gradient
//   orientation and overlap.
//   Cell tracks analyzed for directionality over three time
//   windows (0-33, 33-66, 66-100 min) during CCL19 gradient
//   build-up phase (Fig. 5c).
//
//   Expected outcomes (Fig. 5):
//   - CCL19_low/CCL21: directionality toward CCL21 (haptotaxis
//     dominant at all time points; Fig. 5a, 5c right panel)
//   - CCL19_medium/CCL21: directionality switches toward CCL19
//     after gradient build-up (chemotaxis dominant; Fig. 5b,
//     5c left panel)
//   Interpretation: soluble CCL19 can override immobilized
//   CCL21 signal above a threshold concentration (~1 ug/mL).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

competingSignal = detect competingGradientDetection on conditionAGrad for 100m

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Competing gradient QC gate
// Pass (BB8): competingSignal > 0 -> differential directionality
//             between low and medium CCL19 conditions resolved;
//             dispose all droplets (experiment complete).
// Fail (BB9): competingSignal <= 0 -> no differential resolution
//             between conditions; drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (competingSignal > 0) {
    dispose conditionAGrad
    dispose conditionBGrad
} else {
    drain conditionAGrad
    drain conditionBGrad
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose competing gradient QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose competingSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module eclDetection

manifest MagneticParticles
manifest TargetSequence
manifest HybridizationBuffer
manifest RuPhen3Cl2
manifest PBS
manifest TPA
manifest PluronicF68

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Electrochemiluminescence on Digital Microfluidics for
// microRNA Analysis
// Shamsi, Choi, Ng, Chamberlain, Wheeler
// Biosensors and Bioelectronics, 2015
// DOI: 10.1016/j.bios.2015.10.036
//
// Protocol: Magnetic particle-based oligonucleotide
// hybridization assay on DMF coupled to ECL detection.
// miRNA-143 (ds-143) is captured by ss-143-modified
// Dynabeads M-280 Streptavidin and detected via
// [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2 intercalation and TPA co-reactant
// at ITO working electrodes on the DMF top-plate.
//
// REAGENT NOTES:
//   MagneticParticles: 4.5 uL aliquots of Dynabeads M-280
//     Streptavidin (10 mg/mL, ~6-7e8 particles/mL in PBS,
//     0.1% BSA, 0.02% NaN3) pre-coated with ss-143 probe
//     DNA via avidin-biotin chemistry. All solutions
//     supplemented with 0.05% Pluronics F68 v/v.
//   TargetSequence: ds-143 in hybridization buffer (0, 10,
//     100, or 1000 nM). For cell lysate assays, MCF-7 or
//     MDA-MB-231 lysate diluted 1:10 in sample dilution
//     buffer (pH 8.0, Tris-base 7.7 mM, Tris-HCl 12.2 mM,
//     NaCl 200 mM, MgCl2 5 mM, BSA 4% w/v, Pluronic L64
//     0.05% w/v).
//   HybridizationBuffer: 20 mM Tris-HCl, 0.2 M NaCl,
//     5 mM MgCl2, pH 8.0.
//   RuPhen3Cl2: 200 uM [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2 in PBS (1x), pH 7.5.
//   PBS: phosphate buffered saline (1x), pH 7.5.
//   TPA: 20 mM tripropylamine in PBS (1x), pH 7.5.
//   PluronicF68: 0.05% v/v in all above solutions.
//
// ECL DETECTION NOTE:
//   eclDetection module abstracts the ITO working electrode
//   (WE, 800 um dia.) and Ag/Au/ITO counter/pseudoreference
//   (CE/RE, 560 um x 560 um) on the DMF top-plate. 1.5 V
//   DC applied for 45 s; maximum ECL photon count recorded
//   within the first 10 s via PMT (CV ~10%).
//   Ru(Phen)3(2+) intercalates dsDNA (4 bp per ion); signal
//   is proportional to hybridized ds-143 captured on beads.
//   LOD: 1.1 nM (CLOD), 1.5 femtomoles (absolute). Total
//   assay time: ~40 min for two parallel assays.
//
// MAGNETIC SEPARATION NOTE:
//   All `heat` steps marked "magnet" abstract the permanent
//   magnet positioned below the DMF bottom plate to
//   immobilize Dynabeads while the supernatant droplet is
//   transported away by electrode actuation. The temperature
//   parameter (25c) reflects ambient/room temperature;
//   no thermal effect is intended at these steps.
//
// PRE-ASSAY STEP (off-chip, not encoded in BioScript):
//   Cathodic electrochemical cleaning of ITO WEs:
//   cyclic voltammetry in 20 uL PBS (1x) on DMF top-plate,
//   10 cycles from -1 V to 0 V at 100 mV/s using ITO WE
//   and Ag/Au/ITO CE/RE.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: particle dispense and
//                             magnetic separation; target
//                             hybridization; wash x4;
//                             Ru(Phen)3 labeling; wash x2;
//                             TPA addition; ECL detection
//   BB2  eclPass           -- eclSignal > 0: valid ECL above
//                             blank; dispose final droplet
//   BB3  eclFail           -- eclSignal <= 0: no signal
//                             (below LOD or reagent failure);
//                             drain final droplet
//   BB4  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose ECL signal
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Dispense magnetic particle droplets and merge.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "three unit droplets containing
//   magnetic particles were dispensed from their reservoir
//   and merged." (For cell lysate assays, five unit droplets
//   were used instead of three; three used here for the
//   standard synthetic target protocol.)
//   Each unit droplet ~1.8 uL; three merged = ~5.4 uL total.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beads1 = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
beads2 = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
beads3 = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles

beadsMerge1 = mix beads1 with beads2 for 5s
beadsMerged = mix beadsMerge1 with beads3 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Magnetic separation - pellet beads, remove
//   supernatant (storage buffer). Magnet applied below device;
//   supernatant droplet actuated away from bead pellet.
//   `heat` at 25c for 30s abstracts magnet hold time.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat beadsMerged at 25c for 30s
dispose beadsMerged

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Dispense target sequence droplets and merge.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "two unit droplets of target sequence
//   solution were dispensed, merged, and delivered to the
//   immobilized particles for resuspension and incubation
//   for 15 min."
//   TargetSequence reservoir: ds-143 in hybridization buffer
//   at test concentration (10/100/1000 nM) or cell lysate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

target1 = dispense 1 units of TargetSequence
target2 = dispense 1 units of TargetSequence

targetMerged = mix target1 with target2 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Hybridization incubation.
//   Deliver merged target droplet to bead pellet; resuspend
//   by electrode actuation (mixing) and incubate for 15 min.
//   ds-143 hybridizes to ss-143 immobilized on beads.
//   `mix` abstracts both resuspension and incubation; the
//   15m duration encodes the hybridization dwell time.
//
//   NOTE: beadsMerged was disposed after magnetic separation
//   (step 2). The bead pellet physically remains on-device
//   at the electrode; targetMerged is merged with a freshly
//   dispensed bead pellet representation. In BioScript,
//   re-dispense from MagneticParticles models the pellet
//   being resuspended by the incoming target droplet, which
//   is the physical reality of the protocol (the magnet is
//   removed and electrode actuation drives resuspension).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pelletForHybrid = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
hybridDroplet   = mix pelletForHybrid with targetMerged for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Magnetic separation - remove unbound target.
//   Magnet applied; beads pellet; supernatant (unbound ds-143)
//   actuated away. `heat` at 25c for 30s = magnet hold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat hybridDroplet at 25c for 30s
dispose hybridDroplet

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Wash cycle x4 (hybridization buffer).
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "particles were washed four times in
//   series by re-suspending and mixing with one unit droplet
//   of hybridization buffer followed by magnetic separation
//   from the supernatant."
//   Each wash: dispense 1 unit HybridizationBuffer, mix 1m
//   to resuspend beads, apply magnet 30s, dispose supernatant.
//   Four serial wash cycles encoded explicitly below.
//
//   As in STEP 4, pellet re-dispense from MagneticParticles
//   models the retained bead pellet at each wash cycle.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Wash 1
pelletW1   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf1   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix1   = mix pelletW1 with washBuf1 for 1m
heat washMix1 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix1

// Wash 2
pelletW2   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf2   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix2   = mix pelletW2 with washBuf2 for 1m
heat washMix2 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix2

// Wash 3
pelletW3   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf3   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix3   = mix pelletW3 with washBuf3 for 1m
heat washMix3 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix3

// Wash 4
pelletW4   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf4   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix4   = mix pelletW4 with washBuf4 for 1m
heat washMix4 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix4

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2 intercalation labeling.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "two unit droplets of [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2
//   solution were dispensed, merged, and delivered to the
//   particles, where they were re-suspended and mixed for
//   2 min. The particles were then separated from the
//   supernatant droplet."
//   Ru(Phen)3(2+) intercalates into dsDNA (4 bp per ion);
//   does not bind ssDNA or RNA. Signal is proportional to
//   amount of hybridized ds-143 on bead surface.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pelletForRu  = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
ruDrop1      = dispense 1 units of RuPhen3Cl2
ruDrop2      = dispense 1 units of RuPhen3Cl2

ruMerged     = mix ruDrop1 with ruDrop2 for 5s
ruLabelMix   = mix pelletForRu with ruMerged for 2m

// Magnetic separation: remove unbound Ru(Phen)3(2+).
heat ruLabelMix at 25c for 30s
dispose ruLabelMix

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: PBS wash x2 (remove excess Ru(Phen)3(2+)).
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "particles were washed two times with
//   2 droplets of PBS as in step 3."
//   Each wash: 1 unit PBS, mix 1m, magnet 30s, dispose.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// PBS Wash 1
pelletPW1  = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
pbsWash1   = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsMix1    = mix pelletPW1 with pbsWash1 for 1m
heat pbsMix1 at 25c for 30s
dispose pbsMix1

// PBS Wash 2
pelletPW2  = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
pbsWash2   = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsMix2    = mix pelletPW2 with pbsWash2 for 1m
heat pbsMix2 at 25c for 30s
dispose pbsMix2

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: TPA co-reactant addition.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "two droplets of TPA solution were
//   dispensed, merged, and delivered to the particles, where
//   they were re-suspended and mixed for 1 min."
//   TPA (tripropylamine) is the ECL co-reactant; oxidized
//   simultaneously with Ru(Phen)3(2+) at the ITO WE.
//   The TPA(+) radical reduces the luminophore to the
//   excited state that emits at ~610 nm.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pelletForTPA = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
tpaDrop1     = dispense 1 units of TPA
tpaDrop2     = dispense 1 units of TPA

tpaMerged    = mix tpaDrop1 with tpaDrop2 for 5s
finalDroplet = mix pelletForTPA with tpaMerged for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: ECL measurement.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "the final droplet containing TPA and
//   Ru(Phen)3(2+)-labeled DNA modified particles was actuated
//   to the ECL electrodes on the top-plate for ECL
//   measurements."
//   1.5 V DC applied between ITO WE and Ag/Au/ITO CE/RE
//   for 45 s. Maximum ECL counts recorded within first 10 s.
//   eclDetection module abstracts the PMT readout.
//   LOD: CLOD = 1.1 nM; absolute LOD = 1.5 femtomoles.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

eclSignal = detect eclDetection on finalDroplet for 45s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: ECL QC gate
// Pass (BB2): eclSignal > 0 -> ECL counts above blank
//             (hybridization detected); dispose final droplet.
// Fail (BB3): eclSignal <= 0 -> signal at or below blank
//             (no hybridization or below LOD); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (eclSignal > 0) {
    dispose finalDroplet
} else {
    drain finalDroplet
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose ECL signal droplet. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose eclSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module scADPLSignalDetection
module ddPCRQuantification
module qPCRQuantification
module fluorescenceImaging

manifest PBS
manifest PluronicF127
manifest MCPLysisBuffer
manifest MCF7_Cells
manifest SKOV3_Cells
manifest OVCAR3_Cells
manifest HEK293T_Cells
manifest MDA_MB_231_Cells
manifest PatientDerivedOrganoids
manifest CatBio_Probe
manifest FPBio_Probe
manifest StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
manifest AntiBody_OligoConjugate
manifest SplintOligonucleotide
manifest LigationBuffer
manifest PreamplificationMix
manifest qPCR_MasterMix
manifest JW480_Inhibitor
manifest FITC_AntiCD45_Antibody
manifest RPhycoerythrin_Spike

// ============================================================
// Single-Cell Chemoproteomics Identifies Metastatic Activity
// Signatures in Breast Cancer
// Smitha Pillai, Laxton, Li, Lin, Karginova, Nanda, Olopade,
// Tay, Moellering - Sci. Adv. 10, eadp2622 (2024)
// DOI: 10.1126/sciadv.adp2622
//
// Platform: Single-Cell Activity-Dependent Proximity Ligation
// (scADPL) coupled to a valve-based push-up PDMS microfluidic
// chip with five chamber zones per assay unit:
//   I   Input fluid artery
//   II  Single-cell trapping chamber (8 um constriction)
//   III Cell lysis chamber (MCP lysis buffer)
//   IV  Proximity barcoding element incubation (whole proteome)
//   V   Proximity barcode ligation
// Output: barcoded amplicons retrieved off-chip by qPCR/ddPCR.
//
// This file encodes the full experimental pipeline:
//   PHASE 1  Single-plex validation (CTSL via ddPCR, NCEH1 via
//            qPCR) in SKOV3 cells.
//   PHASE 2  Multiplexed Ag-6 panel (NCEH1, MGLL, CTSL, FAAH,
//            CTSB, uPA) profiling with inhibitor specificity QC.
//   PHASE 3  Heterogeneity profiling across cell lines (HEK293T
//            vs SKOV3; SKOV3 vs OVCAR3).
//   PHASE 4  Patient-derived organoid (PDO) profiling from TNBC
//            primary and metastatic tumors, including ER+ within-
//            patient pleural effusion vs lymph node samples.
//
// CHEMICAL PROBES:
//   Cat-Bio (5 uM, 2 h, 37 C): cathepsin family-wide probe
//            targeting CTSL, CTSB (cysteine protease family).
//   FP-Bio (2 uM, 30 min, 37 C): serine hydrolase family-wide
//            probe targeting NCEH1, MGLL, FAAH, uPA.
//   Both probes applied simultaneously in multiplexed runs.
//
// DETECTION CHEMISTRY:
//   On-chip: streptavidin-oligo (SA-oligo) recognises biotin
//   tag on FP-Bio / Cat-Bio probe-protein complexes; antibody-
//   oligo conjugate (ab-oligo) recognises the target protein.
//   Proximity ligation: splint oligo bridges SA-oligo and
//   ab-oligo when probe-protein complex is formed; Ampligase
//   seals the nick (40 C, 45 min). Preamplification (18 cycles)
//   feeds into qPCR (Taqman, target-specific barcode channels)
//   or ddPCR (CTSL single-plex validation).
//   Spike-in control: R-phycoerythrin (RPE) added at lysis step
//   for inter-cell normalisation.
//
// KEY QUANTITATIVE PARAMETERS:
//   - sADPL sensitivity threshold: 10 pg whole proteome (36).
//   - Single HeLa cell protein content: ~2 ng (37).
//   - Average scADPL CTSL signal: 54-fold over vehicle control.
//   - Average scADPL NCEH1 signal: ~64-fold over vehicle control.
//   - Multiplexed reproducibility: Pearson r = 0.9981 (day1/day2).
//   - scADPL vs bulk sADPL correlation: Pearson r = 0.9288.
//   - JW480 (NCEH1 inhibitor, 2 uM): >90% NCEH1 signal inhibition;
//     no significant effect on other five targets.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device priming, probe labelling,
//                              single-plex CTSL validation (ddPCR),
//                              NCEH1 inhibitor specificity QC
//   BB2  ctslPass           -- ctslSignal > 0: probe-dependent CTSL
//                              barcodes detected; dispose
//   BB3  ctslFail           -- ctslSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  ctslJoin           -- join: NCEH1 branch begins
//   BB5  nceh1Pass          -- nceh1Signal > 0: valid NCEH1 signal
//                              and JW480 inhibition confirmed; dispose
//   BB6  nceh1Fail          -- nceh1Signal <= 0: no NCEH1 signal; drain
//   BB7  nceh1Join          -- join: Ag-6 multiplexed panel begins
//   BB8  multiplexPass      -- ag6Signal > 0: all six targets detected
//                              above background; dispose
//   BB9  multiplexFail      -- ag6Signal <= 0: multiplex failure; drain
//   BB10 multiplexJoin      -- join: cell-line heterogeneity profiling
//   BB11 heterogeneityPass  -- heteroSignal > 0: PCA clustering
//                              resolves SKOV3 vs OVCAR3; dispose
//   BB12 heterogeneityFail  -- heteroSignal <= 0: no separation; drain
//   BB13 heterogeneityJoin  -- join: PDO patient sample branch
//   BB14 pdoPass            -- pdoSignal > 0: metastatic Ag-6
//                              signature detected in PDOs; dispose
//   BB15 pdoFail            -- pdoSignal <= 0: no PDO signal; drain
//   BB16 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 1: Prime microfluidic device.
//   2% Pluronics F-127 in PBS flowed through all channels
//   for 5 min to passivate PDMS surfaces and reduce non-
//   specific cell adhesion before cell loading.
//   Chip is a three-layer push-up PDMS valve device bonded
//   to glass (127.76 x 85.48 x 1 mm). Five chamber zones
//   per assay unit. SU-8-3025 photoresist features at 22 mm
//   and 70 mm heights; AZ40XT dome valve layer at 18 mm.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS       = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic  = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix       = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 2: Pulse-label SKOV3 cells with activity probes
//   off-chip prior to on-chip loading.
//   Cat-Bio: 5 uM, 2 h, 37 C in DMEM-F12 + 10% FBS.
//   FP-Bio:  2 uM, 30 min, 37 C in DMEM-F12 + 10% FBS.
//   Cells washed with PBS after labelling; resuspended in PBS
//   at 50,000-100,000 cells/mL for microfluidic loading.
//   NOTE: In PHASE 1, CTSL single-plex uses Cat-Bio only;
//         NCEH1 single-plex uses FP-Bio only. Both probes are
//         combined in PHASE 2 multiplexed runs.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

skov3Cells      = dispense 1 units of SKOV3_Cells
catBioProbe     = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioProbe      = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

// Cat-Bio labelling: 2 h at 37 C (= 120 min)
labelledCatBio  = mix skov3Cells with catBioProbe for 5s
heat labelledCatBio at 37c for 120m

// FP-Bio labelling: 30 min at 37 C
labelledFPBio   = mix skov3Cells with fpBioProbe for 5s
heat labelledFPBio at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 3: Load probe-labelled SKOV3 cells on-chip.
//   Cells flow through input artery (I) into single-cell
//   trapping chamber (II) via hydrodynamic trapping.
//   NOTE: `mix` here abstracts a pressure-driven channel flow
//   event (single-cell capture), not DMF electrode mixing.
//   Each assay chamber captures exactly one cell per run.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rpeSpike             = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
trappedCatBioCell    = mix labelledCatBio with primingMix for 2s
trappedFPBioCell     = mix labelledFPBio with primingMix for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 4: On-chip cell lysis (Chamber III).
//   Cells lysed in MCP lysis buffer:
//   25 mM Tris pH 7.5, 150 mM NaCl, 1 mM EDTA, 1 mM EGTA,
//   0.5% Triton X-100, 0.5% sodium deoxycholate.
//   RPE spike-in control added at lysis step for each cell.
//   Whole-proteome lysate fills nanoliter dead volume of
//   chamber III; volume reduced vs bulk sADPL to maximise
//   sensitivity (working proteome concentration optimised
//   to match bulk sADPL window; fig. S2 in paper).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisBuffer          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateCatBio         = mix trappedCatBioCell with lysisBuffer for 1m
lysateCatBio2        = mix lysateCatBio with rpeSpike for 5s

rpeSpike2            = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
lysateFPBio          = mix trappedFPBioCell with lysisBuffer for 1m
lysateFPBio2         = mix lysateFPBio with rpeSpike2 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 5: On-chip proximity barcoding (Chamber IV).
//   SA-oligo (4000 pM) recognises biotin tag on probe-protein
//   complex; ab-oligo (200 pM, target-specific) recognises
//   the protein epitope. Both recognition elements bind the
//   same probe-protein complex in nanoliter volume, bringing
//   the two oligos into proximity.
//   Incubation: 2 h at room temperature (25 C) on-chip.
//   Final concentrations mirror validated bulk sADPL window
//   (36) scaled to chip dead volume.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

saOligo              = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOligo              = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate

barcodingReagents    = mix saOligo with abOligo for 5s
barcodedCatBio       = mix lysateCatBio2 with barcodingReagents for 2m
heat barcodedCatBio at 25c for 120m

saOligo2             = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOligo2             = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate

barcodingReagents2   = mix saOligo2 with abOligo2 for 5s
barcodedFPBio        = mix lysateFPBio2 with barcodingReagents2 for 2m
heat barcodedFPBio at 25c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 6: On-chip proximity ligation (Chamber V).
//   Splint oligonucleotide bridges SA-oligo and ab-oligo when
//   both are bound to the same probe-protein complex.
//   Ampligase (0.05 U) seals the nick under:
//     100 nM splint oligo, 0.3 mM NAD+, 10 mM DTT,
//     20 mM Tris-HCl pH 8.3, 50 mM KCl, 1.5 mM MgCl2.
//   Ligation: 40 C for 45 min (= 45 min).
//   Ligated barcoded amplicons are the quantifiable readout.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

splintOligo          = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligBuf               = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer

ligationMixCat       = mix barcodedCatBio with splintOligo for 2s
ligationMixCat2      = mix ligationMixCat with ligBuf for 2s
heat ligationMixCat2 at 40c for 45m

splintOligo2         = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligBuf2              = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer

ligationMixFP        = mix barcodedFPBio with splintOligo2 for 2s
ligationMixFP2       = mix ligationMixFP with ligBuf2 for 2s
heat ligationMixFP2 at 40c for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 7: Amplicon retrieval and preamplification.
//   Ligated product flushed out using 9 uL water off-chip.
//   Preamplification PCR (18 cycles):
//     2.5x buffer, 100 nM primers, 200 uM dNTPs,
//     9 U Phusion high-fidelity DNA polymerase.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the off-chip flush and preamplification
//   step; the BioScript variable holds the preamplified product
//   ready for downstream quantification.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

preampMix            = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedCatBio   = mix ligationMixCat2 with preampMix for 18m

preampMix2           = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedFPBio    = mix ligationMixFP2 with preampMix2 for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 8: CTSL quantification by ddPCR.
//   ddPCR: 5 uL preamplified product into ddPCR reaction;
//   absolute quantification of barcoded amplicons (amplicons/uL).
//   Average signal: 54-fold above vehicle-only control.
//   (Fig. 1B in paper; n=2 independent biological replicates)
//   DETECTION: scADPLSignalDetection abstracts the ddPCR
//   instrument readout; ddPCRQuantification validates amplicon
//   count above noise threshold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ctslSignal = detect ddPCRQuantification on preamplifiedCatBio for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: CTSL single-plex QC gate
// Pass (BB2): ctslSignal > 0 -> probe-dependent CTSL barcodes
//             detected above background (>54-fold expected).
// Fail (BB3): ctslSignal <= 0 -> no detectable amplicons;
//             likely probe labelling or ligation failure.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (ctslJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ctslSignal > 0) {
    dispose preamplifiedCatBio
} else {
    drain preamplifiedCatBio
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: ctslJoin
// Dispose CTSL QC signal. Control falls into NCEH1 branch.
// ============================================================

dispose ctslSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 9: NCEH1 specificity validation with JW480.
//   Parallel experiment: SKOV3 cells labelled with FP-Bio
//   then pre-treated with JW480 (2 uM, selective NCEH1
//   inhibitor) before on-chip processing.
//   Expected: JW480 inhibits NCEH1-specific scADPL signal
//   by >90% with no significant effect on other Ag-6 targets.
//   qPCR readout selected over ddPCR from this step forward:
//   higher SNR, amenable to multiplexing across target channels.
//   (Fig. 1C, Fig. 2B in paper)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

skov3CellsQC    = dispense 1 units of SKOV3_Cells
fpBioProbeQC    = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe
jw480           = dispense 1 units of JW480_Inhibitor

// Pre-treat with JW480 before FP-Bio labelling to confirm
// target-selective inhibition (2 uM JW480, 30 min, 37 C)
jw480Treated    = mix skov3CellsQC with jw480 for 5s
heat jw480Treated at 37c for 30m

// FP-Bio labelling post-inhibitor treatment
labelledQC      = mix jw480Treated with fpBioProbeQC for 5s
heat labelledQC at 37c for 30m

// On-chip: trap, lyse, barcode, ligate (same as STEP 3-6)
rpeSpike3       = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primingMix2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedQCCell   = mix labelledQC with primingMix2 for 2s

lysisBuffer2    = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateQC        = mix trappedQCCell with lysisBuffer2 for 1m
lysateQC2       = mix lysateQC with rpeSpike3 for 5s

saOligoQC       = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOligoQC       = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodingQC     = mix saOligoQC with abOligoQC for 5s
barcodedQC      = mix lysateQC2 with barcodingQC for 2m
heat barcodedQC at 25c for 120m

splintQC        = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligBufQC        = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligationQC      = mix barcodedQC with splintQC for 2s
ligationQC2     = mix ligationQC with ligBufQC for 2s
heat ligationQC2 at 40c for 45m

preampQC        = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedQC  = mix ligationQC2 with preampQC for 18m

// qPCR detection on NCEH1-specific barcode channel
// Expected: signal suppressed >90% vs no-inhibitor control
nceh1Signal = detect qPCRQuantification on preamplifiedQC for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: NCEH1 inhibitor specificity QC gate
// Pass (BB5): nceh1Signal > 0 -> residual signal present
//             (confirms partial probe labelling competed by
//             JW480); target specificity validated when compared
//             to uninhibited control. Dispose.
// Fail (BB6): nceh1Signal <= 0 -> no signal at all; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (nceh1Join).
// NOTE: A valid experiment expects nceh1Signal to be >90% lower
// than the uninhibited preamplifiedFPBio signal. The binary QC
// gate here checks for the presence of a processed product;
// the >90% inhibition fold-change comparison is performed
// off-chip by the qPCR instrument software.
// ============================================================

if (nceh1Signal > 0) {
    dispose preamplifiedQC
} else {
    drain preamplifiedQC
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: nceh1Join
// Dispose NCEH1 QC signal. Control falls into Ag-6 multiplexed
// panel branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose nceh1Signal

// ============================================================
// PHASE 2: Multiplexed Ag-6 Panel in SKOV3 Single Cells
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 - STEP 1: Pulse-label SKOV3 cells with both probes
//   simultaneously.
//   Cat-Bio 5 uM (2 h, 37 C) + FP-Bio 2 uM (30 min, 37 C)
//   applied to same cells for dual-probe multiplexing.
//   FP-Bio labels NCEH1, MGLL, FAAH, uPA (serine hydrolases).
//   Cat-Bio labels CTSL, CTSB (cathepsin family).
//   Six orthogonal barcode channels enable simultaneous
//   qPCR quantification from the same single-cell lysate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

skov3Ag6        = dispense 1 units of SKOV3_Cells
catBioAg6       = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioAg6        = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

// Sequential labelling: FP-Bio first (30 min), then Cat-Bio
// added to ongoing FP-Bio incubation for remaining 90 min
// such that both probes are present for the final 30 min.
// Simplified here as sequential mix operations.
labelledFP_Ag6  = mix skov3Ag6 with fpBioAg6 for 5s
heat labelledFP_Ag6 at 37c for 30m

labelledDual    = mix labelledFP_Ag6 with catBioAg6 for 5s
heat labelledDual at 37c for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 - STEP 2: Single-cell capture, lysis, and barcoding.
//   Cells resuspended to 50,000-100,000 cells/mL in PBS.
//   Loaded onto chip; single cells trapped per assay chamber.
//   MCP lysis buffer + RPE spike-in at Chamber III.
//   SA-oligo (4000 pM) and ab-oligo cocktail (200 pM each,
//   six antibody-oligo conjugates for six Ag-6 targets)
//   added to whole-proteome lysate in Chamber IV.
//   Incubation 2 h at 25 C; ligation 45 min at 40 C.
//   NOTE: n = 8 single cells profiled per condition (Fig. 2A).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rpeAg6          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primingAg6      = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedAg6Cell  = mix labelledDual with primingAg6 for 2s

lysisAg6        = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateAg6       = mix trappedAg6Cell with lysisAg6 for 1m
lysateAg6b      = mix lysateAg6 with rpeAg6 for 5s

saAg6           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abAg6           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodingAg6    = mix saAg6 with abAg6 for 5s
barcodedAg6     = mix lysateAg6b with barcodingAg6 for 2m
heat barcodedAg6 at 25c for 120m

splintAg6       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligAg6          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixAg6       = mix barcodedAg6 with splintAg6 for 2s
ligMixAg6b      = mix ligMixAg6 with ligAg6 for 2s
heat ligMixAg6b at 40c for 45m

preampAg6       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedAg6 = mix ligMixAg6b with preampAg6 for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 - STEP 3: Multiplexed qPCR quantification (Ag-6).
//   Six orthogonal Taqman barcode channels simultaneously
//   quantified on CFX384 Real-Time System (384-well plates).
//   0.9 uM primers + 0.45 uM Taqman probe per channel in
//   Luna Universal Probe qPCR Master Mix.
//   Values normalised to RPE spike-in control per cell.
//   Expected fold-changes vs no-probe DMSO control (Fig. 2A):
//     NCEH1: >20-fold, MGLL: >20-fold, CTSL: >20-fold
//     FAAH: detectable, CTSB: detectable, uPA: detectable
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qpcrMix         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
ag6WithQPCR     = mix preamplifiedAg6 with qpcrMix for 2s
ag6Signal       = detect qPCRQuantification on ag6WithQPCR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Ag-6 multiplexed panel QC gate
// Pass (BB8): ag6Signal > 0 -> all six target barcode channels
//             detected above no-probe background; dispose.
// Fail (BB9): ag6Signal <= 0 -> multiplex failure (ligation
//             or preamplification failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (multiplexJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ag6Signal > 0) {
    dispose ag6WithQPCR
} else {
    drain ag6WithQPCR
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: multiplexJoin
// Dispose Ag-6 QC signal. Control falls into heterogeneity
// profiling branch (BB11/BB12).
// ============================================================

dispose ag6Signal

// ============================================================
// PHASE 3: Heterogeneity Profiling Across Cell Lines
// (HEK293T vs SKOV3; SKOV3 vs OVCAR3)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3 - STEP 1: Prepare and label HEK293T and OVCAR3 cells.
//   HEK293T: non-cancer kidney control (tissue-type mismatch
//            comparison vs SKOV3 ovarian cancer; Fig. 3A).
//   OVCAR3:  low-aggressiveness ovarian cancer (tissue-matched
//            comparison vs SKOV3 high-aggressiveness; Fig. 3B).
//   Both cell lines dual-probe labelled identically to PHASE 2.
//   n > 10 isolated single cells per target per cell line.
//   Activity normalised to HEK293T (Fig. 3A) or OVCAR3 (Fig. 3B)
//   as respective internal reference populations.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hek293t         = dispense 1 units of HEK293T_Cells
ovcar3          = dispense 1 units of OVCAR3_Cells

catBioHetero    = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioHetero     = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

// Label HEK293T cells
labelledHEK_FP  = mix hek293t with fpBioHetero for 5s
heat labelledHEK_FP at 37c for 30m

catBioH2        = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
labelledHEK     = mix labelledHEK_FP with catBioH2 for 5s
heat labelledHEK at 37c for 90m

// Label OVCAR3 cells
fpBioO          = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe
labelledOVC_FP  = mix ovcar3 with fpBioO for 5s
heat labelledOVC_FP at 37c for 30m

catBioO         = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
labelledOVC     = mix labelledOVC_FP with catBioO for 5s
heat labelledOVC at 37c for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3 - STEP 2: On-chip scADPL for both control cell lines.
//   Same chamber-by-chamber workflow as PHASE 2.
//   HEK293T and OVCAR3 processed on separate chip runs.
//   Each cell trapped, lysed, barcoded, and ligated individually.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// HEK293T on-chip processing
rpeHEK          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primHEK         = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedHEK      = mix labelledHEK with primHEK for 2s

lysHEK          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateHEK       = mix trappedHEK with lysHEK for 1m
lysateHEKb      = mix lysateHEK with rpeHEK for 5s

saHEK           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abHEK           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodeHEK      = mix saHEK with abHEK for 5s
barcodedHEK     = mix lysateHEKb with barcodeHEK for 2m
heat barcodedHEK at 25c for 120m

splintHEK       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligHEK          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixHEK       = mix barcodedHEK with splintHEK for 2s
ligMixHEKb      = mix ligMixHEK with ligHEK for 2s
heat ligMixHEKb at 40c for 45m

preampHEK       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplHEK      = mix ligMixHEKb with preampHEK for 18m

// OVCAR3 on-chip processing
rpeOVC          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primOVC         = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedOVC      = mix labelledOVC with primOVC for 2s

lysOVC          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateOVC       = mix trappedOVC with lysOVC for 1m
lysateOVCb      = mix lysateOVC with rpeOVC for 5s

saOVC           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOVC           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodeOVC      = mix saOVC with abOVC for 5s
barcodedOVC     = mix lysateOVCb with barcodeOVC for 2m
heat barcodedOVC at 25c for 120m

splintOVC       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligOVC          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixOVC       = mix barcodedOVC with splintOVC for 2s
ligMixOVCb      = mix ligMixOVC with ligOVC for 2s
heat ligMixOVCb at 40c for 45m

preampOVC       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplOVC      = mix ligMixOVCb with preampOVC for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3 - STEP 3: qPCR and fluorescence imaging readout.
//   qPCRQuantification: six-channel Ag-6 qPCR on each cell line.
//   fluorescenceImaging: abstracts PCA dimensional reduction
//   and heatmap visualisation of Z-score activity profiles
//   across single cells (Fig. 3D/E/F in paper).
//   Key finding: SKOV3 significantly higher Ag-6 activity vs
//   both HEK293T (all six targets, p <= 0.0001-0.03) and
//   OVCAR3 (five of six targets significant, Fig. 3B).
//   PCA separates SKOV3 vs OVCAR3 at PC1 = 84.67%.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qpcrHEK         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
hekWithQPCR     = mix preamplHEK with qpcrHEK for 2s

qpcrOVC         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
ovcWithQPCR     = mix preamplOVC with qpcrOVC for 2s

heteroSignal    = detect fluorescenceImaging on hekWithQPCR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: Cell-line heterogeneity QC gate
// Pass (BB11): heteroSignal > 0 -> significant Ag-6 activity
//              difference between SKOV3 and control lines
//              resolved; PCA clustering validates; dispose.
// Fail (BB12): heteroSignal <= 0 -> no measurable difference;
//              drain.
// Both branches converge at BB13 (heterogeneityJoin).
// ============================================================

if (heteroSignal > 0) {
    dispose hekWithQPCR
    dispose ovcWithQPCR
} else {
    drain hekWithQPCR
    drain ovcWithQPCR
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: heterogeneityJoin
// Dispose heterogeneity QC signal. Control falls into PDO
// patient sample branch (BB14/BB15).
// ============================================================

dispose heteroSignal

// ============================================================
// PHASE 4: Patient-Derived Organoid (PDO) Profiling
// Samples: TNBC between-patient (PDO1-PDO6) and ER+ within-
// patient (pleural effusion L/R, lymph node metastasis).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4 - STEP 1: PDO preparation.
//   Fresh core needle biopsies enzymatically digested 1 h to
//   generate cell suspension. Pleural effusion cells collected
//   by centrifugation at 450g for 10 min.
//   Cells mixed with Matrigel (MG), plated in 24-well plates,
//   solidified at 37 C. BC PDO media supplemented.
//   PDOs cultured to 50-100 mm diameter before dissociation.
//   Dissociation: Dispase 37 C 20 min; TrypLE 37 C 5-10 min.
//   Final suspension: 500 uL BC PDO media, kept on ice.
//   ANTI-CD45 staining: cells labelled with FITC-anti-CD45
//   (30 min on ice) to identify and exclude immune cells
//   during on-chip imaging, preventing contamination of
//   tumour-cell activity signatures. (fig. S6 in paper)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pdoSuspension   = dispense 1 units of PatientDerivedOrganoids
fitcAntiCD45    = dispense 1 units of FITC_AntiCD45_Antibody
stainedPDO      = mix pdoSuspension with fitcAntiCD45 for 30m

// CD45 staining on ice (4 C = cold approximation at 4c)
heat stainedPDO at 4c for 30m

// Probe labelling of PDO single-cell suspension
catBioPDO       = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioPDO        = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

labelledPDO_FP  = mix stainedPDO with fpBioPDO for 5s
heat labelledPDO_FP at 37c for 30m

labelledPDO     = mix labelledPDO_FP with catBioPDO for 5s
heat labelledPDO at 37c for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4 - STEP 2: On-chip scADPL for PDO single cells.
//   CD45+ immune cells identified by on-chip fluorescence
//   imaging (FITC channel) and excluded from scADPL analysis.
//   Only CD45- tumour cells proceed through lysis and barcoding.
//   NOTE: `detect fluorescenceImaging` at trapping step
//   abstracts the brightfield + FITC fluorescence screen used
//   to confirm single tumour cell capture per chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rpePDO          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primPDO         = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedPDO      = mix labelledPDO with primPDO for 2s

// On-chip CD45 imaging QC: confirm FITC-negative (tumour) cell
pdoTumourSignal = detect fluorescenceImaging on trappedPDO for 10s

lysPDO          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysatePDO       = mix trappedPDO with lysPDO for 1m
lysatePDOb      = mix lysatePDO with rpePDO for 5s

saPDO           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abPDO           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodePDO      = mix saPDO with abPDO for 5s
barcodedPDO     = mix lysatePDOb with barcodePDO for 2m
heat barcodedPDO at 25c for 120m

splintPDO       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligPDO          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixPDO       = mix barcodedPDO with splintPDO for 2s
ligMixPDOb      = mix ligMixPDO with ligPDO for 2s
heat ligMixPDOb at 40c for 45m

preampPDO       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplPDO      = mix ligMixPDOb with preampPDO for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4 - STEP 3: qPCR Ag-6 quantification on PDO cells.
//   Values normalised to RPE spike-in and within each target
//   to PDO1 (primary tumour reference) for TNBC samples, or
//   to Lymph met for ER+ within-patient samples.
//   Key finding: Ag-6 activity highest in metastatic vs
//   primary tumour PDOs; peak in liver metastases (PDO3/PDO4).
//   scADPL vs bulk sADPL concordance confirmed in ER+ patient
//   pleural effusion and lymph node samples (Fig. 4D/E).
//   scADPL resolves intra-tumour single-cell heterogeneity
//   not visible in bulk organoid measurements.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qpcrPDO         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
pdoWithQPCR     = mix preamplPDO with qpcrPDO for 2s
pdoSignal       = detect qPCRQuantification on pdoWithQPCR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: PDO patient sample QC gate
// Pass (BB14): pdoSignal > 0 -> Ag-6 barcoded amplicons
//              detected in PDO single cells; metastatic activity
//              signature confirmed; dispose.
// Fail (BB15): pdoSignal <= 0 -> no amplicons (PDO preparation
//              or probe labelling failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB16 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (pdoSignal > 0) {
    dispose pdoWithQPCR
    dispose pdoTumourSignal
} else {
    drain pdoWithQPCR
    drain pdoTumourSignal
}

// ============================================================
// BB16: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends. Results: Ag-6 enzyme panel activity
// increases with metastatic potential across BC cell lines
// and patient-derived organoids; scADPL resolves single-cell
// heterogeneity invisible to bulk proteomic methods.
// ============================================================

dispose pdoSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module gradientDetection
module nfkbTranslocationDetection
module geneExpressionDetection
module viabilityDetection

manifest Fibronectin
manifest PBS
manifest DMEM_HighGlucose
manifest RelA_DsRed_3T3_Fibroblasts
manifest RelA_GFP_RAW264_Macrophages
manifest LPS_50ngmL
manifest TNFa_30ngmL
manifest Hoechst33342
manifest TrypLE
manifest LysisBuffer
manifest CyanonineFive
manifest FreshMedium

instructions:

// ============================================================
// High-throughput co-culture system for analysis of
// spatiotemporal cell-cell signaling
// Son, Wang, Kenna, Tay -- Biosensors and Bioelectronics 2023
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bios.2023.115089
//
// v2 fixes (FIX1-FIX4):
//   FIX1: heat at 4c for 960m replaces heat at -80c
//          (compiler strips negative sign: -80c -> 80.0CELSIUS)
//   FIX2: false branches use explicit waste variable so
//          compiler emits drain() not dispose() in IR
//   FIX3: removed dead lysisBufferStock variable
//   FIX4: imagingChamber uses two distinct operands
//          (sinkFlow + gradientJoin) instead of self-mix
//
// CFG structure (main arm):
//   BB1(main) -> BB2/BB3 -> BB4(join) -> BB5/BB6
//   -> BB7(join) -> BB8/BB9 -> BB10(terminal)
//
// CFG structure (supplemental TNF-a arm, continuation):
//   BB10 -> BB11/BB12 -> BB13(terminal/NOP)
// ============================================================


// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// STEP 1: Fibronectin coating of receiving chambers.
// 30 min at 25 C; washed with DMEM before cell loading.
fibronectinCoat       = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
pbsWash1              = dispense 1 units of PBS
coatingMix            = mix fibronectinCoat with pbsWash1 for 5s
heat coatingMix at 25c for 30m

washBuffer1           = dispense 1 units of DMEM_HighGlucose
chambersCoated        = mix coatingMix with washBuffer1 for 2s

// STEP 2: RelA-DsRed 3T3 fibroblast loading.
// 5e5 cells/mL; ~70% confluency (200-400 cells/chamber).
// 5 h adhesion at 37 C (midpoint of 4-6 h window).
fibroblasts           = dispense 1 units of RelA_DsRed_3T3_Fibroblasts
dmemBase              = dispense 1 units of DMEM_HighGlucose
fibroblastSuspension  = mix fibroblasts with dmemBase for 5s
loadedFibroblasts     = mix chambersCoated with fibroblastSuspension for 5s
heat loadedFibroblasts at 37c for 300m

// STEP 3: Hoechst 33342 nuclear staining (optional; 10 min).
hoechstStain          = dispense 1 units of Hoechst33342
stainedFibroblasts    = mix loadedFibroblasts with hoechstStain for 10m

// STEP 4: RelA-GFP RAW264.7 macrophage loading into pre-chamber.
// 10-100 cells (controlled: 60 +/- 15); separator valve CLOSED.
// Settle 30 min at 37 C.
macrophages           = dispense 1 units of RelA_GFP_RAW264_Macrophages
macrophageMedium      = dispense 1 units of DMEM_HighGlucose
macrophageSuspension  = mix macrophages with macrophageMedium for 5s
loadedMacrophages     = mix macrophageSuspension with stainedFibroblasts for 2s
heat loadedMacrophages at 37c for 30m

// STEP 5: LPS stimulation (50 ng/mL, 10 min, separator CLOSED).
// Wash pre-chamber with fresh DMEM to remove LPS.
lpsStimulus           = dispense 1 units of LPS_50ngmL
macrophageStimulated  = mix loadedMacrophages with lpsStimulus for 10m
washBuffer2           = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
lpsWashed             = mix macrophageStimulated with washBuffer2 for 2s

// STEP 6: Separator valve open; cytokine gradient formation.
// Cy5 tracer for gradient QC; 400 min development window.
cy5Tracer             = dispense 1 units of CyanonineFive
gradientChamber       = mix lpsWashed with cy5Tracer for 5s
heat gradientChamber at 37c for 400m
gradientSignal        = detect gradientDetection on gradientChamber for 10s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Gradient QC gate
// FIX2: false branch uses explicit waste variable.
// ============================================================

if (gradientSignal > 0) {
    dispose gradientChamber
} else {
    gradientWaste = mix gradientChamber with washBuffer2 for 2s
    drain gradientWaste
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: gradientJoin
// FIX4: sinkFlow and gradientJoin are two distinct variables
//        so imagingChamber is not a self-mix.
// ============================================================

dispose gradientSignal

// STEP 7: Live-cell NF-kB imaging (200 min at 37 C).
sinkFlow              = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
gradientJoin          = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
imagingChamber        = mix sinkFlow with gradientJoin for 2s
heat imagingChamber at 37c for 200m
nfkbSignal            = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on imagingChamber for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: NF-kB QC gate
// FIX2: false branch uses explicit waste variable.
// ============================================================

if (nfkbSignal > 0) {
    dispose imagingChamber
} else {
    nfkbWaste = mix imagingChamber with sinkFlow for 2s
    drain nfkbWaste
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: nfkbJoin
// FIX3: lysisBufferStock removed; per-region lysis variables
//        are dispensed inline only where consumed.
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbSignal

// STEP 8: Spatially resolved cell retrieval (near / mid / far).
// TrypLE 10 s flow + 60 s incubation = 70 s total detachment.
// FIX1: heat at 4c for 960m (not -80c; compiler strips sign).
//        Biological intent: -80 C long-term cryostorage.
trypLESolution        = dispense 1 units of TrypLE
pbsRetrieval          = dispense 1 units of PBS
detachedCells         = mix trypLESolution with pbsRetrieval for 70s

pbsNear               = dispense 1 units of PBS
lysisNear             = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
nearCells             = mix detachedCells with pbsNear for 5s
nearLysate            = mix nearCells with lysisNear for 5s

pbsMid                = dispense 1 units of PBS
lysisMid              = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
midCells              = mix detachedCells with pbsMid for 5s
midLysate             = mix midCells with lysisMid for 5s

pbsFar                = dispense 1 units of PBS
lysisFar              = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
farCells              = mix detachedCells with pbsFar for 5s
farLysate             = mix farCells with lysisFar for 5s

heat nearLysate at 4c for 960m
heat midLysate  at 4c for 960m
heat farLysate  at 4c for 960m

geneExprSignal        = detect geneExpressionDetection on nearLysate for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Gene expression QC gate
// FIX2: false branch uses explicit waste variables.
// ============================================================

if (geneExprSignal > 0) {
    dispose nearLysate
    dispose midLysate
    dispose farLysate
} else {
    lysateWasteN = mix nearLysate with pbsNear for 2s
    lysateWasteM = mix midLysate  with pbsMid  for 2s
    lysateWasteF = mix farLysate  with pbsFar  for 2s
    drain lysateWasteN
    drain lysateWasteM
    drain lysateWasteF
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: terminal / join into supplemental TNF-a arm
// ============================================================

dispose geneExprSignal

// ============================================================
// SUPPLEMENTAL ARM: Fixed-dose TNF-a stimulation
// Section 3.4, Fig. 4 -- no macrophages; 30 ng/mL TNF-a
// loaded directly into pre-chamber.
// Continues from BB10; compiler will assign BB11-BB13.
// Same four fixes applied as main arm above.
// ============================================================

// STEP S1: Fibronectin coating.
fibronectinCoat2      = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
pbsWash2              = dispense 1 units of PBS
coatingMix2           = mix fibronectinCoat2 with pbsWash2 for 5s
heat coatingMix2 at 25c for 30m

washBuffer3           = dispense 1 units of DMEM_HighGlucose
chambersCoated2       = mix coatingMix2 with washBuffer3 for 2s

// STEP S2: Fibroblast loading.
fibroblasts2          = dispense 1 units of RelA_DsRed_3T3_Fibroblasts
dmemBase2             = dispense 1 units of DMEM_HighGlucose
fibroblastSusp2       = mix fibroblasts2 with dmemBase2 for 5s
loadedFibroblasts2    = mix chambersCoated2 with fibroblastSusp2 for 5s
heat loadedFibroblasts2 at 37c for 300m

hoechstStain2         = dispense 1 units of Hoechst33342
stainedFibroblasts2   = mix loadedFibroblasts2 with hoechstStain2 for 10m

// STEP S3: 30 ng/mL TNF-a loaded into pre-chamber; 8 h imaging.
tnfaStimulus          = dispense 1 units of TNFa_30ngmL
tnfaChamber           = mix stainedFibroblasts2 with tnfaStimulus for 5s
heat tnfaChamber at 37c for 480m

// FIX4: two distinct operands for imagingChamber2.
sinkFlow2             = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
gradientJoin2         = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
imagingChamber2       = mix sinkFlow2 with gradientJoin2 for 2s
heat imagingChamber2 at 37c for 480m
geneExprSignal2       = detect geneExpressionDetection on imagingChamber2 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: Gene expression QC gate (supplemental arm)
// FIX2: false branch uses explicit waste variables.
// ============================================================

if (geneExprSignal2 > 0) {
    dispose imagingChamber2
} else {
    tnfaWaste = mix imagingChamber2 with sinkFlow2 for 2s
    drain tnfaWaste
}

// STEP S4: Cell retrieval (near / mid / far).
// FIX1: heat at 4c for 960m (not -80c).
trypLE2               = dispense 1 units of TrypLE
pbs2                  = dispense 1 units of PBS
detached2             = mix trypLE2 with pbs2 for 70s

pbsNear2              = dispense 1 units of PBS
lysisNear2            = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
nearCells2            = mix detached2 with pbsNear2 for 5s
nearLysate2           = mix nearCells2 with lysisNear2 for 5s

pbsMid2               = dispense 1 units of PBS
lysisMid2             = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
midCells2             = mix detached2 with pbsMid2 for 5s
midLysate2            = mix midCells2 with lysisMid2 for 5s

pbsFar2               = dispense 1 units of PBS
lysisFar2             = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
farCells2             = mix detached2 with pbsFar2 for 5s
farLysate2            = mix farCells2 with lysisFar2 for 5s

heat nearLysate2 at 4c for 960m
heat midLysate2  at 4c for 960m
heat farLysate2  at 4c for 960m

geneExprSignal3       = detect geneExpressionDetection on nearLysate2 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB13 (assigned by compiler) / terminal
// FIX2: false branch uses explicit waste variables.
// ============================================================

if (geneExprSignal3 > 0) {
    dispose nearLysate2
    dispose midLysate2
    dispose farLysate2
} else {
    lysateWasteN2 = mix nearLysate2 with pbsNear2 for 2s
    lysateWasteM2 = mix midLysate2  with pbsMid2  for 2s
    lysateWasteF2 = mix farLysate2  with pbsFar2  for 2s
    drain lysateWasteN2
    drain lysateWasteM2
    drain lysateWasteF2
}

dispose geneExprSignal2
dispose geneExprSignal3

// [terminal -- NOP]

module nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection
module geneExpressionDetection
module viabilityDetection

manifest MEF_p65_DsRed_H2BGFPCells
manifest TNF_Alpha
manifest IL1Beta
manifest Pam2CSK4
manifest DMEM_FluoroBrite
manifest Fibronectin_PBS
manifest TrypsinEDTA
manifest LysisBuffer
manifest FDA_PI_Stain

// ============================================================
// Input Dose Differentiation by NF-kB
// Son, Wang, Tu, Metzig, Patel, Husain, Lin, Murugan,
// Hoffmann, Tay -- bioRxiv 752394, September 2019.
//
// Protocol: Microfluidic live-cell analysis of NF-kB
// (p65-DsRed) nuclear localization dynamics in 3T3 MEFs
// under dynamically varying cytokine (TNF / IL-1beta / Pam)
// concentrations delivered via a multiplexed PDMS microfluidic
// chip. Includes: device priming, cell loading, cytokine
// stimulation under instant / linear / exponential / random
// input dynamics, live-cell fluorescence imaging, downstream
// RT-qPCR gene expression measurement, and cell viability QC.
//
// PLATFORM: Two-layer PDMS microfluidic chip (64 independent
// chambers, >500 cells/chamber). Flow layer: AZ40XT (25 um) +
// SU-8 3025 (30 um). Control layer: SU-8 3025 (25 um).
// Lithography: Heidelberg MLA150, 375 nm, 280 mJ/cm2.
// Actuated at 25-30 psi via solenoid valves (Matlab GUI).
// Input media pressurized at 3-4 psi through PEEK tubing.
//
// IMAGING: Nikon Ti2, 20x, CMOS (Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash4.0 V2),
// 5-min intervals. p65-DsRed: 555 nm ex, 0.5-1 s exposure.
// H2B-GFP: 485 nm ex, 50-100 ms exposure.
// ~100,000 cells inspected manually; ~30,000 selected for
// analysis. NF-kB traces extracted via custom Matlab software
// using nuclear H2B-GFP mask + p65-DsRed nuclear fluorescence.
//
// KEY FINDING: NF-kB responds to log(delta_cytokine), not to
// absolute cytokine level -- behaving as a dose differentiator.
// A20 and IkBa negative feedbacks provide short-term memory
// of prior cytokine level and continuously reset IKK cycling.
//
// NOTE ON `mix` ABSTRACTION: `mix` steps in the cell loading
// and stimulation blocks abstract microfluidic channel-based
// delivery events (flow-through feeding via valve actuation),
// not DMF electrode mixing. Reagent delivery is pressure-driven
// through PEEK tubing; chamber feeding is automated via GUI.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports s and m only.
// Long incubations (e.g. overnight coating) are expressed in
// minutes: 12 h = 720m.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                -- device priming, fibronectin
//                               coating, cell loading, baseline
//                               imaging, cytokine stimulation
//                               (instant / linear / exponential
//                               / random input dynamics)
//   BB2  nfkbPass            -- nfkbSignal > 0: valid oscillatory
//                               NF-kB response detected; carry
//                               forward to viability and gene
//                               expression branches
//   BB3  nfkbFail            -- nfkbSignal <= 0: no NF-kB
//                               response (e.g. dead cells or
//                               failed stimulation); drain
//   BB4  nfkbJoin            -- join: viability QC branch
//   BB5  viabilityPass       -- viabilitySignal > 0: cells
//                               viable post-experiment; carry
//                               forward to gene expression
//   BB6  viabilityFail       -- viabilitySignal <= 0: low
//                               viability; drain
//   BB7  viabilityJoin       -- join: gene expression branch
//   BB8  geneExprPass        -- geneExprSignal > 0: target gene
//                               mRNA successfully detected by
//                               RT-qPCR; dispose lysate
//   BB9  geneExprFail        -- geneExprSignal <= 0: qPCR
//                               failure; drain lysate
//   BB10 finalCleanup        -- terminal: dispose all QC
//                               signals; experiment ends
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Fibronectin surface coating of microfluidic chambers.
//         Chambers filled with 1:3 fibronectin (1 mg/mL) in
//         sterile PBS and incubated overnight at room
//         temperature (~25 C) for thorough coating before
//         cell loading.
//         12 h incubation = 720 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinSolution = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin_PBS

// Overnight coating at room temperature (25 C, 720 min).
heat fibronectinSolution at 25c for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Flush chambers with FluoroBrite DMEM to remove
//         unbound fibronectin and equilibrate the device to
//         cell culture conditions (37 C, 5% CO2) before
//         cell loading.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts a pressure-driven channel
//         flush event, not DMF mixing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

flushMedia      = dispense 1 units of DMEM_FluoroBrite
primedChamber   = mix fibronectinSolution with flushMedia for 5m

// Equilibrate device to cell culture environment.
heat primedChamber at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Load 3T3 MEFs (p65-DsRed / H2B-GFP) into
//         microfluidic chambers.
//         Cell concentration: 5 x 10^6 cells/mL targeting
//         ~50% confluency per chamber (>500 cells/chamber).
//         Cells settle for at least 60 min after loading
//         before any stimulation begins.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the gravity-assisted cell
//         sedimentation and channel loading event.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mefCells        = dispense 1 units of MEF_p65_DsRed_H2BGFPCells
loadedChamber   = mix mefCells with primedChamber for 2s

// 60 min settling period at 37 C / 5% CO2 before stimulation.
heat loadedChamber at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Baseline imaging (pre-stimulation, t = 0).
//         Nuclear p65-DsRed and H2B-GFP images acquired every
//         5 min to establish pre-stimulus NF-kB localization
//         baseline in each cell (n > 200 per condition).
//         Acquisition: 555 nm ex / 485 nm ex, 20x, 5-min
//         intervals. This detect call abstracts the live-cell
//         fluorescence imaging module used throughout the
//         experiment; the same module is reused for all
//         downstream imaging time points.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

baselineSignal  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on loadedChamber for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5a: Instant (step) cytokine increase -- TNF.
//          TNF-alpha (Life Technologies, PMC3014) instantly
//          increased to 10 ng/mL and maintained at that level.
//          Chambers also replenished with 10 ng/mL TNF every
//          60 min to compensate for degradation (Fig. 7).
//          Strong initial NF-kB translocation peak at ~25 min,
//          followed by exponential decay in oscillation amplitude
//          -- demonstrating desensitisation to constant input.
//          NOTE: `mix` abstracts pressure-driven media exchange
//          (valve actuation, 3-4 psi, via Matlab GUI).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfInstant      = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimInstantTNF  = mix loadedChamber with tnfInstant for 5s

// Record NF-kB nuclear localization during 300 min constant
// TNF stimulation (imaging every 5 min; total 60 frames).
nfkbInstantTNF  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimInstantTNF for 300m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5b: Instant (step) cytokine increase -- IL-1beta.
//          IL-1beta (R&D Systems, 401ML010CF) instantly
//          increased to 2.5 ng/mL and maintained.
//          Response dynamics parallel TNF (Fig. 1A): strong
//          initial peak, followed by oscillation decay.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

il1bInstant     = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimInstantIL1B = mix loadedChamber with il1bInstant for 5s

nfkbInstantIL1B = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimInstantIL1B for 300m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6a: Linear ramp -- TNF.
//          TNF concentration increased in linear stepwise
//          increments of 1 ng/mL every 60 min until the
//          maximum dose is reached. Sustained NF-kB
//          oscillations observed with constant peak AUC at
//          each ramping step, consistent with differentiator
//          behaviour (NF-kB ~ log(delta_cytokine)).
//          NOTE: Each ramp step modelled as a sequential mix
//          representing a new media exchange event at the
//          next concentration.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfLinear1      = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimLinTNF_s1   = mix loadedChamber with tnfLinear1 for 5s
nfkbLinTNF_s1   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinTNF_s1 for 60m

tnfLinear2      = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimLinTNF_s2   = mix stimLinTNF_s1 with tnfLinear2 for 5s
nfkbLinTNF_s2   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinTNF_s2 for 60m

tnfLinear3      = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimLinTNF_s3   = mix stimLinTNF_s2 with tnfLinear3 for 5s
nfkbLinTNF_s3   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinTNF_s3 for 60m

tnfLinear4      = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimLinTNF_s4   = mix stimLinTNF_s3 with tnfLinear4 for 5s
nfkbLinTNF_s4   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinTNF_s4 for 60m

tnfLinear5      = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimLinTNF_s5   = mix stimLinTNF_s4 with tnfLinear5 for 5s
nfkbLinTNF_s5   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinTNF_s5 for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6b: Linear ramp -- IL-1beta.
//          IL-1beta increased in linear steps of 0.5 ng/mL
//          every 60 min (Fig. 2A). Peak AUC remains constant
//          across all steps (dose differentiation confirmed).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

il1bLinear1     = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimLinIL1B_s1  = mix loadedChamber with il1bLinear1 for 5s
nfkbLinIL1B_s1  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinIL1B_s1 for 60m

il1bLinear2     = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimLinIL1B_s2  = mix stimLinIL1B_s1 with il1bLinear2 for 5s
nfkbLinIL1B_s2  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinIL1B_s2 for 60m

il1bLinear3     = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimLinIL1B_s3  = mix stimLinIL1B_s2 with il1bLinear3 for 5s
nfkbLinIL1B_s3  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinIL1B_s3 for 60m

il1bLinear4     = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimLinIL1B_s4  = mix stimLinIL1B_s3 with il1bLinear4 for 5s
nfkbLinIL1B_s4  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinIL1B_s4 for 60m

il1bLinear5     = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimLinIL1B_s5  = mix stimLinIL1B_s4 with il1bLinear5 for 5s
nfkbLinIL1B_s5  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimLinIL1B_s5 for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7a: Exponential ramp -- TNF.
//          TNF concentration doubled every 60 min (from a
//          starting dose up to maximum 10 ng/mL).
//          NF-kB AUC increases linearly with log(delta_TNF);
//          fitted slope R^2 ~ 0.963 (Fig. 2B).
//          Each step represents a 2-fold increase in TNF
//          delivered by media exchange.
//          5 doublings: covering ~6 min to 120 min doubling
//          times across experiments (Supplementary Fig. 1-3).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfExp1         = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimExpTNF_s1   = mix loadedChamber with tnfExp1 for 5s
nfkbExpTNF_s1   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpTNF_s1 for 60m

tnfExp2         = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimExpTNF_s2   = mix stimExpTNF_s1 with tnfExp2 for 5s
nfkbExpTNF_s2   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpTNF_s2 for 60m

tnfExp3         = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimExpTNF_s3   = mix stimExpTNF_s2 with tnfExp3 for 5s
nfkbExpTNF_s3   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpTNF_s3 for 60m

tnfExp4         = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimExpTNF_s4   = mix stimExpTNF_s3 with tnfExp4 for 5s
nfkbExpTNF_s4   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpTNF_s4 for 60m

tnfExp5         = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimExpTNF_s5   = mix stimExpTNF_s4 with tnfExp5 for 5s
nfkbExpTNF_s5   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpTNF_s5 for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7b: Exponential ramp -- IL-1beta.
//          IL-1beta doubled every 60 min up to 2.5 ng/mL max
//          (Fig. 2B). AUC at each step fitted to log(delta)
//          with same differentiator relationship as TNF.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

il1bExp1        = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimExpIL1B_s1  = mix loadedChamber with il1bExp1 for 5s
nfkbExpIL1B_s1  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpIL1B_s1 for 60m

il1bExp2        = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimExpIL1B_s2  = mix stimExpIL1B_s1 with il1bExp2 for 5s
nfkbExpIL1B_s2  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpIL1B_s2 for 60m

il1bExp3        = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimExpIL1B_s3  = mix stimExpIL1B_s2 with il1bExp3 for 5s
nfkbExpIL1B_s3  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpIL1B_s3 for 60m

il1bExp4        = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimExpIL1B_s4  = mix stimExpIL1B_s3 with il1bExp4 for 5s
nfkbExpIL1B_s4  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpIL1B_s4 for 60m

il1bExp5        = dispense 1 units of IL1Beta
stimExpIL1B_s5  = mix stimExpIL1B_s4 with il1bExp5 for 5s
nfkbExpIL1B_s5  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpIL1B_s5 for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Random fluctuating input -- TNF.
//         TNF levels increased and decreased in random order
//         (0 to 10 ng/mL range) every 60 min (Fig. 2C).
//         AUC vs delta_TNF: linear for positive changes
//         (correlation coefficient ~0.91), sharp drop for
//         any decrease -- confirming rectified differentiator
//         behaviour under arbitrary input complexity.
//         4 random steps modelled as sequential media
//         exchanges; the alternating increase/decrease pattern
//         is represented by alternating dispense-and-mix cycles
//         (abstraction of Matlab GUI-driven valve scheduling).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfRand1        = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimRandTNF_s1  = mix loadedChamber with tnfRand1 for 5s
nfkbRandTNF_s1  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimRandTNF_s1 for 60m

tnfRand2        = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimRandTNF_s2  = mix stimRandTNF_s1 with tnfRand2 for 5s
nfkbRandTNF_s2  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimRandTNF_s2 for 60m

tnfRand3        = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimRandTNF_s3  = mix stimRandTNF_s2 with tnfRand3 for 5s
nfkbRandTNF_s3  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimRandTNF_s3 for 60m

tnfRand4        = dispense 1 units of TNF_Alpha
stimRandTNF_s4  = mix stimRandTNF_s3 with tnfRand4 for 5s
nfkbRandTNF_s4  = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimRandTNF_s4 for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: TLR2 ligand control -- Pam2CSK4 exponential ramp.
//         Pam (InvivoGen, tlrl-pm2s) doubled every 30 or 60 min
//         from 0.2 to 12.8 ng/mL (Fig. 3A).
//         Single-cell clustering (Matlab linkage, ward/
//         correlation) shows majority of cells exhibit 1-2
//         sharp peaks only; AUC slopes span negative to
//         positive values -- confirming absence of dose
//         differentiation for TLR2 ligand.
//         Differentiator behaviour is cytokine-receptor-
//         specific (TNFR/IL-1R pathway, not TLR2).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pamExp1         = dispense 1 units of Pam2CSK4
stimExpPam_s1   = mix loadedChamber with pamExp1 for 5s
nfkbExpPam_s1   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpPam_s1 for 60m

pamExp2         = dispense 1 units of Pam2CSK4
stimExpPam_s2   = mix stimExpPam_s1 with pamExp2 for 5s
nfkbExpPam_s2   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpPam_s2 for 60m

pamExp3         = dispense 1 units of Pam2CSK4
stimExpPam_s3   = mix stimExpPam_s2 with pamExp3 for 5s
nfkbExpPam_s3   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpPam_s3 for 60m

pamExp4         = dispense 1 units of Pam2CSK4
stimExpPam_s4   = mix stimExpPam_s3 with pamExp4 for 5s
nfkbExpPam_s4   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpPam_s4 for 60m

pamExp5         = dispense 1 units of Pam2CSK4
stimExpPam_s5   = mix stimExpPam_s4 with pamExp5 for 5s
nfkbExpPam_s5   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on stimExpPam_s5 for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: NF-kB response QC gate.
//          Composite NF-kB signal from the exponential TNF
//          ramp arm (nfkbExpTNF_s5) is used as QC anchor:
//          a valid differentiator response requires sustained
//          oscillatory peaks with positive AUC slope across
//          steps. Signal > 0 indicates valid NF-kB oscillation
//          detected by the imaging module.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nfkbSignal      = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on nfkbExpTNF_s5 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: NF-kB response QC gate
// Pass (BB2): nfkbSignal > 0 -> valid oscillatory NF-kB
//             response confirmed; carry forward.
// Fail (BB3): nfkbSignal <= 0 -> no response (cell death,
//             stimulation failure); drain chamber contents.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (nfkbJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nfkbSignal > 0) {
    dispose nfkbExpTNF_s5
} else {
    drain nfkbExpTNF_s5
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: nfkbJoin
// Dispose NF-kB QC signal. Control falls into the
// viability assay branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Cell viability assay.
//          After stimulation, cells are stained with FDA/PI
//          to assess viability. FDA (ex 490 nm / em 526 nm)
//          labels live cells; PI (ex 488 nm / em 617 nm)
//          labels dead cells. 10 min staining at room temp.
//          Expected viability > 80% for valid experiment.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fdaPiStain      = dispense 1 units of FDA_PI_Stain
stainedCells    = mix loadedChamber with fdaPiStain for 10m

viabilitySignal = detect viabilityDetection on stainedCells for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Viability QC gate
// Pass (BB5): viabilitySignal > 0 -> cells viable (>80%);
//             carry forward to gene expression measurement.
// Fail (BB6): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> low viability; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (viabilityJoin).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedCells
} else {
    drain stainedCells
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: viabilityJoin
// Dispose viability QC signal. Control falls into the
// gene expression measurement branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: Cell retrieval and lysis for RT-qPCR.
//          At designated time points during TNF ramping
//          (instant vs. exponential, Fig. 7), the corner of
//          the microfluidic chip is cut and cells are
//          trypsinized (~1 min), then washed into the open
//          outlet channel with PBS. A 2-3 uL cell droplet
//          accumulates and is retrieved by pipette into
//          5 uL lysis buffer (CellsDirect Kit) and snap-
//          frozen at -80 C. RT and pre-amplification performed
//          with CellsDirect One-Step RT-qPCR kit.
//          NOTE: `mix` abstracts the trypsinization and PBS
//          wash/retrieval step. `heat` at -80 C models snap
//          freezing; BioScript supports negative temperature
//          values as per compiler spec.
//          Targets: A20, RANTES, Ccl2, Zfp36, Casp4,
//          Serpina3g (normalised to GAPDH by 2^(Cq_target -
//          Cq_GAPDH)). TaqMan probes on Biorad CFX384.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypsinSolution = dispense 1 units of TrypsinEDTA
lysisBuffer     = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer

trypsinizedCells = mix loadedChamber with trypsinSolution for 1m
retrievedCells   = mix trypsinizedCells with lysisBuffer for 30s

// NOTE: snap-freeze at -80 C is a storage step only and is not
// representable in BioScript (compiler drops negative sign on
// temperature; lilott8/BioScript limitation). Freezing is
// implied between retrievedCells dispense and geneExprSignal
// detect; no heat call is emitted here.

// RT-qPCR: detect NF-kB target gene mRNA levels.
// geneExpressionDetection module abstracts CellsDirect RT,
// pre-amplification, and TaqMan qPCR readout on CFX384.
geneExprSignal  = detect geneExpressionDetection on retrievedCells for 120m

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Gene expression QC gate
// Pass (BB8): geneExprSignal > 0 -> target gene mRNA
//             detected above GAPDH baseline (valid qPCR);
//             dispose lysate.
// Fail (BB9): geneExprSignal <= 0 -> no mRNA detected
//             (lysis failure or qPCR error); drain lysate.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (geneExprSignal > 0) {
    dispose retrievedCells
} else {
    drain retrievedCells
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose baseline and gene expression QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose baselineSignal
dispose geneExprSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module nfkbTranslocationDetection
module geneExpressionDetection
module cellViabilityDetection

manifest TNFalpha
manifest IL1beta
manifest LPS
manifest PAM2CSK4
manifest PBS
manifest CompleteMedia
manifest PluronicF127
manifest FluorescentNFkBCells
manifest FDA_PI_Stain

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Processing Stimulus Dynamics by the NF-kB Network in
// Single Cells.
// Son, Wang, Keisham, Tay - Experimental & Molecular Medicine
// (2023) 55:2531-2540.
// DOI: 10.1038/s12276-023-01133-7
//
// This BioScript encodes the core microfluidic single-cell
// NF-kB signaling protocol described in the review, covering:
//   (1) Device priming and single-cell loading
//   (2) Pulsatile TNF-a stimulation (low vs. high frequency)
//   (3) Sequential multi-ligand stimulation
//         (TNF-a -> IL-1b -> LPS -> PAM2CSK4)
//   (4) NF-kB translocation detection at single-cell resolution
//   (5) Downstream gene expression readout
//   (6) Cell viability QC gate
//
// BIOLOGICAL CONTEXT:
//   Cells used are mouse fibroblasts (or equivalent cell line)
//   stably expressing fluorescently tagged NF-kB (e.g. p65-RFP
//   or p65-GFP) enabling real-time nuclear translocation
//   tracking by live fluorescence microscopy. The microfluidic
//   device provides high-throughput, precise temporal control
//   over cytokine delivery to cells in isolated chambers
//   (up to 64 experimental conditions in parallel, Son et al.
//   Sci. Signal. 2021).
//
// STIMULATION STRATEGY:
//   The paper tests three classes of dynamic input:
//     (A) Pulsatile: repeated short TNF-a exposures at varying
//         inter-pulse intervals (60, 100, 200 min periods).
//     (B) Increasing dose: stepwise or ramp increases in TNF-a
//         or IL-1b, revealing differentiator-like NF-kB behaviour
//         (response tracks change in level, not absolute dose).
//     (C) Sequential multi-ligand: TNF-a followed by IL-1b,
//         LPS, and PAM2CSK4 in defined 8 h sequences, encoding
//         stimulus identity and order into NF-kB dynamics via
//         ligand-specific feedback memory (IRAK1, IkBd, A20).
//
// NOTE ON STIMULATION ABSTRACTION:
//   `mix` operations model microfluidic perfusion of stimulus
//   into a cell-containing channel chamber. They do not
//   represent DMF electrode mixing. Each `dispense` abstracts
//   a programmable microfluidic valve-controlled bolus.
//   Duration arguments to `mix` encode the perfusion window
//   (i.e. the pulse duration or the incubation period).
//
// NOTE ON TIME UNITS:
//   BioScript supports `s` (seconds) and `m` (minutes) only.
//   All durations are expressed in `m` or `s` accordingly.
//   Inter-pulse recovery periods (e.g. 200 min) are encoded
//   as `heat` steps at physiological temperature (37 C) to
//   model the incubation/wash period between pulses.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                -- entry: priming, cell loading,
//                               pulsatile stimulation arm,
//                               NF-kB translocation detection
//   BB2  nfkbPass            -- nfkbSignal > 0: oscillatory
//                               NF-kB response confirmed;
//                               proceed to sequential stimulation
//   BB3  nfkbFail            -- nfkbSignal <= 0: no translocation
//                               detected; drain cells
//   BB4  nfkbJoin            -- join: sequential ligand arm begins
//   BB5  seqPass             -- seqSignal > 0: sequence-encoded
//                               NF-kB dynamics confirmed;
//                               proceed to gene expression readout
//   BB6  seqFail             -- seqSignal <= 0: no sequence
//                               encoding detected; drain
//   BB7  seqJoin             -- join: gene expression & viability
//   BB8  expressionPass      -- expressionSignal > 0: target gene
//                               upregulation confirmed; dispose
//   BB9  expressionFail      -- expressionSignal <= 0: no
//                               expression; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup        -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime microfluidic device.
//   2% Pluronics F-127 in PBS perfused for 5 min to prevent
//   non-specific cell adhesion to PDMS channel walls.
//   Consistent with standard microfluidic cell culture setup
//   (Son et al. Biosens. Bioelectron. 2023; Samlali et al.
//   Small 2020).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix      = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Load fluorescently tagged NF-kB reporter cells.
//   Cells expressing p65-RFP (or equivalent) are flowed into
//   individual microfluidic chambers at low density to achieve
//   single-cell isolation per chamber. This enables real-time
//   tracking of NF-kB nuclear translocation by fluorescence
//   microscopy (Nelson et al. J. Cell Sci. 2002; Tay et al.
//   Nature 2010).
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts channel-based cell loading; no
//   reagent mixing in the DMF sense occurs at this step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

reporterCells   = dispense 1 units of FluorescentNFkBCells
loadedCells     = mix reporterCells with primingMix for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Equilibration.
//   Allow cells to settle and adhere in chambers at 37 C,
//   5% CO2 for 30 min prior to stimulation. Ensures baseline
//   NF-kB is cytoplasmic before stimulus delivery.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat loadedCells at 37c for 30m

// ============================================================
// PULSATILE STIMULATION ARM (Pulse 1 of 3)
// Low-frequency pulsatile TNF-a (200 min inter-pulse period).
// From Ashall et al. Science 2009 and Kellogg & Tay Cell 2015.
// Low-frequency pulses (>200 min period) allow full NF-kB
// system reset between pulses, maintaining full-amplitude
// response across repeated stimulations.
//
// Protocol: 15 min TNF-a pulse -> 185 min wash/recovery ->
//           repeat x3. 15-min pulses at ~10 ng/mL TNF-a.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Pulsatile TNF-a - Pulse 1.
//   Deliver TNF-a (10 ng/mL) for 15 min via programmable
//   valve. Continuous TNF-a is required for oscillatory
//   NF-kB dynamics; brief pulses elicit single translocation
//   events (Nelson et al. Science 2004; Turner et al.
//   J. Cell Sci. 2010).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfPulse1       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha
stimulation1    = mix loadedCells with tnfPulse1 for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Inter-pulse wash and recovery (Pulse 1 -> Pulse 2).
//   Replace TNF-a with PBS to terminate stimulation.
//   185 min recovery at 37 C allows NF-kB to return to
//   cytoplasm, IKK to reset via A20/IkBa negative feedback,
//   and cells to exit the refractory state before next pulse.
//   Total inter-pulse period = 185 + 15 = 200 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

washPBS1        = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedCells1    = mix stimulation1 with washPBS1 for 5m
heat washedCells1 at 37c for 185m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Pulsatile TNF-a - Pulse 2.
//   Second 15 min TNF-a pulse. At 200 min period, NF-kB
//   oscillation is fully reset; second pulse produces
//   full-amplitude response (Ashall et al. Science 2009).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfPulse2       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha
stimulation2    = mix washedCells1 with tnfPulse2 for 15m

washPBS2        = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedCells2    = mix stimulation2 with washPBS2 for 5m
heat washedCells2 at 37c for 185m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Pulsatile TNF-a - Pulse 3.
//   Third 15 min TNF-a pulse. Confirms entrainment or
//   persistent NF-kB response amplitude at low-frequency
//   pulsatile regime. Kellogg & Tay (Cell 2015) showed noise
//   in NF-kB oscillation facilitates entrainment and
//   downstream gene expression over a range of frequencies.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfPulse3       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha
stimulation3    = mix washedCells2 with tnfPulse3 for 15m

washPBS3        = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedCells3    = mix stimulation3 with washPBS3 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: NF-kB translocation detection (pulsatile arm).
//   nfkbTranslocationDetection module abstracts live-cell
//   fluorescence imaging of p65-RFP nuclear-to-cytoplasmic
//   ratio (N:C ratio) measured in single cells at each time
//   point. Translocation confirmed by N:C ratio > 1 at peak.
//   Image acquisition: every 3-5 min over the full 8 h
//   stimulation window (consistent with Ashall et al. and
//   Kellogg & Tay protocols).
//   Detection window: 90 s per chamber scan.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nfkbSignal      = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on washedCells3 for 90s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: NF-kB translocation QC gate (pulsatile arm)
// Pass (BB2): nfkbSignal > 0 -> oscillatory NF-kB translocation
//             confirmed across all three pulses; proceed to
//             sequential ligand stimulation arm (BB4).
// Fail (BB3): nfkbSignal <= 0 -> no detectable translocation;
//             cells may be unhealthy or reporter not expressed;
//             drain and discard this chamber population.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (nfkbJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nfkbSignal > 0) {
    dispose washedCells3
} else {
    drain washedCells3
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: nfkbJoin
// Dispose pulsatile arm NF-kB signal. Control falls into
// the sequential multi-ligand stimulation arm (BB5/BB6).
// A fresh population of loaded cells is used for this arm
// (independent experimental condition on same device).
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbSignal

// ============================================================
// SEQUENTIAL MULTI-LIGAND STIMULATION ARM
// From Wang, Son et al. Cell Rep. 2022 (ref 15 in paper).
// Four-ligand sequence over 8 h: TNF-a -> IL-1b -> LPS -> PAM.
// Each ligand delivered for ~2 h (120 min) then washed off.
// NF-kB dynamics encode stimulus identity and sequence via
// ligand-specific negative feedback memory:
//   - IRAK1 autophosphorylation: encodes IL-1b / LPS memory
//     (cross-tolerance between IL-1b and LPS; not TNF-a)
//   - IkBd (p100 homodimer): broad cross-tolerance on 24 h scale
//   - A20: upstream of IKK; inhibits signaling from most ligands
// The sequence produces distinct NF-kB oscillation patterns
// for each ligand-order combination (Wang et al. Cell Rep. 2022).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Load fresh reporter cells for sequential arm.
//   New cell chamber or washed chamber re-loaded with
//   p65-RFP reporter cells. Same priming and equilibration
//   as Steps 1-3.
//   NOTE: primingMix2 / loadedCells2 are independent variables;
//   they do not reuse the pulsatile arm cell population.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic2 = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix2     = mix primingPBS2 with primingPluronic2 for 5m

reporterCells2  = dispense 1 units of FluorescentNFkBCells
loadedCells2    = mix reporterCells2 with primingMix2 for 2m
heat loadedCells2 at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Sequential stimulus 1 - TNF-a (0-120 min).
//   TNF-a (10 ng/mL) delivered for 120 min.
//   TNF-a signals via TNFR -> TRADD/RIP1/TRAF2/5 -> TAK1 -> IKK.
//   Does NOT activate IRAK1/MyD88 myddosome pathway.
//   Primary NF-kB response: damped oscillation, 1-3 peaks.
//   A20 induced as negative feedback, partially suppressing
//   subsequent TRAF2/5-dependent signals.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfSeq          = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha
seqStim1        = mix loadedCells2 with tnfSeq for 120m

washSeq1        = dispense 1 units of PBS
seqWashed1      = mix seqStim1 with washSeq1 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Sequential stimulus 2 - IL-1b (120-240 min).
//   IL-1b (10 ng/mL) delivered for 120 min beginning at t=120m.
//   IL-1b signals via IL-1R -> MyD88/IRAK1/TRAF6 (myddosome).
//   After prior TNF-a, A20 levels are elevated. However,
//   IL-1b can overcome A20 inhibition (different receptor
//   complex) and produce NF-kB reactivation without attenuation
//   (Adamson et al. Nat. Commun. 2016; DeFelice et al.
//   Sci. Signal. 2019 - ref 64 in paper).
//   IRAK1 begins to autophosphorylate, encoding IL-1b memory.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

il1bSeq         = dispense 1 units of IL1beta
seqStim2        = mix seqWashed1 with il1bSeq for 120m

washSeq2        = dispense 1 units of PBS
seqWashed2      = mix seqStim2 with washSeq2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: Sequential stimulus 3 - LPS (240-360 min).
//   LPS (100 ng/mL) delivered for 120 min beginning at t=240m.
//   LPS signals via TLR4 -> MyD88/IRAK1/TRAF6 (myddosome) AND
//   TRIF-TRAM pathway (after TLR4 endocytosis).
//   LPS and IL-1b share the IRAK1/MyD88 myddosome. If IRAK1 is
//   autophosphorylated and aggregated from prior IL-1b stimulation,
//   cells enter cross-tolerance state: LPS-driven NF-kB response
//   is attenuated (DeFelice et al. Sci. Signal. 2019 - ref 64).
//   Dose-dependent: 100 ng/mL LPS drives stronger IRAK1
//   clustering than lower doses, deepening cross-tolerance.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsSeq          = dispense 1 units of LPS
seqStim3        = mix seqWashed2 with lpsSeq for 120m

washSeq3        = dispense 1 units of PBS
seqWashed3      = mix seqStim3 with washSeq3 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Sequential stimulus 4 - PAM2CSK4 (360-480 min).
//   PAM2CSK4 (100 ng/mL) delivered for 120 min (t=360-480m).
//   PAM2CSK4 signals via TLR1/2 -> MyD88/IRAK1/TRAF6 (same
//   myddosome as IL-1b and LPS). After IRAK1 clustering from
//   prior IL-1b + LPS, PAM response is significantly attenuated.
//   Son et al. (Sci. Signal. 2021 - ref 13 in paper) showed
//   PAM exhibits a differentiator-like NF-kB response to
//   concentration CHANGES but NOT to absolute levels, unlike
//   TNF-a and IL-1b. Sequence memory in IRAK1 further modulates
//   PAM response amplitude in a dose-dependent manner.
//   Full 8 h sequence total: TNF(2h) -> IL-1b(2h) -> LPS(2h) ->
//   PAM(2h), encoding 4-ligand sequential identity as distinct
//   NF-kB oscillation patterns (Wang et al. Cell Rep. 2022).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pamSeq          = dispense 1 units of PAM2CSK4
seqStim4        = mix seqWashed3 with pamSeq for 120m

washSeq4        = dispense 1 units of PBS
seqWashed4      = mix seqStim4 with washSeq4 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: NF-kB translocation detection (sequential arm).
//   Same nfkbTranslocationDetection module applied to the
//   sequential stimulation cell population. Readout captures
//   the composite NF-kB dynamics across all 4 ligands:
//   oscillation period, amplitude, damping coefficient, and
//   inter-peak intervals encode the stimulus sequence and
//   feedback memory state of each cell.
//   Detection window: 90 s per chamber (consistent with Step 8).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

seqSignal       = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on seqWashed4 for 90s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Sequential stimulation NF-kB QC gate
// Pass (BB5): seqSignal > 0 -> sequence-encoded NF-kB dynamics
//             detected; distinct oscillation patterns for each
//             ligand confirmed; proceed to gene expression arm.
// Fail (BB6): seqSignal <= 0 -> NF-kB not responding to any
//             ligand in sequence; drain this chamber population.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (seqJoin).
// ============================================================

if (seqSignal > 0) {
    dispose seqWashed4
} else {
    drain seqWashed4
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: seqJoin
// Dispose sequential arm NF-kB signal. Control falls into
// the downstream gene expression and viability QC arm
// (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose seqSignal

// ============================================================
// DOWNSTREAM GENE EXPRESSION AND CELL VIABILITY ARM
// The paper demonstrates that distinct NF-kB oscillation
// dynamics (amplitude, duration, period) produce distinct
// transcriptional outputs. Lane et al. (Cells 2017 - ref 120)
// linked NF-kB dynamics to proinflammatory gene expression
// profiles in single cells. Cheng et al. (Science 2021 - ref
// 14) showed macrophage NF-kB oscillations produce lasting
// epigenetic changes. This arm validates gene expression
// downstream of the sequential stimulation.
//
// Cell viability is assessed with FDA/PI staining consistent
// with Samlali et al. (Small 2020) to confirm stimulation
// protocol does not induce significant apoptosis.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 15: Downstream gene expression readout.
//   After 8 h multi-ligand sequential stimulation, cells are
//   lysed (or fixed for smFISH) to assess mRNA levels of
//   NF-kB target genes (e.g. IL-6, CXCL8/IL-8, IkBa, A20,
//   TNF-a). geneExpressionDetection abstracts quantitative
//   RT-PCR or single-molecule FISH readout, normalised to
//   housekeeping genes. NF-kB oscillation period and amplitude
//   in the preceding imaging window are correlated with
//   target gene expression levels at the single-cell level
//   (Lane et al. Cells 2017; Wang et al. Cell Rep. 2022).
//   Detection window: 30 min for lysis + qPCR abstraction.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

expressCells    = dispense 1 units of FluorescentNFkBCells
expressMedia    = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
expressMix      = mix expressCells with expressMedia for 5m

expressionSignal = detect geneExpressionDetection on expressMix for 30m

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Gene expression QC gate
// Pass (BB8): expressionSignal > 0 -> NF-kB target gene
//             upregulation confirmed (IL-6, CXCL8, IkBa
//             elevated above baseline); dispose cells.
// Fail (BB9): expressionSignal <= 0 -> no detectable gene
//             expression response; cells may be refractory
//             or dead; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (expressionSignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // Cell viability QC (pass path only):
    //   FDA (live, green) and PI (dead, red) staining to
    //   confirm >80% viability across the 8 h stimulation.
    //   Viability is critical for interpreting NF-kB dynamics
    //   as true signaling responses, not death signals.
    //   (Son et al. Sci. Signal. 2021 - ref 13)
    //   Incubate stain for 10 min at room temperature.
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    fdaPiStain      = dispense 1 units of FDA_PI_Stain
    stainedCells    = mix expressMix with fdaPiStain for 10m

    viabilitySignal = detect cellViabilityDetection on stainedCells for 30s

    dispose stainedCells
    dispose viabilitySignal
    dispose expressMix
} else {
    drain expressMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends. NF-kB stimulus dynamics protocol complete.
// ============================================================

dispose expressionSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module nfkbActivationDetection
module geneExpressionDetection

manifest TNF_Solution
manifest LPS_Stimulant
manifest RAW264_7_Macrophage
manifest NIH_3T3_Fibroblast
manifest Fibronectin_PBS
manifest FreshMedium
manifest TrypLE_Express
manifest PBS
manifest LysisSolution
manifest RT_qPCR_A20_Probe
manifest RT_qPCR_Casp4_Probe
manifest RT_qPCR_RANTES_Probe

// ============================================================
// Spatiotemporal NF-kB Dynamics Encodes the Position,
// Amplitude, and Duration of Local Immune Inputs
// Son, Frank, Holst-Hansen, Wang, Junkin, Kashaf,
// Trusina, Tay - Sci. Adv. 8, eabn6240 (2022)
// DOI: 10.1126/sciadv.abn6240
//
// PROTOCOL OVERVIEW:
// This file encodes the TNF diffusion microfluidic coculture
// experiment (primary experimental arm, Figs. 1-3 and 6).
// A custom PDMS two-chamber microfluidic chip separates a
// cytokine source chamber from a fibroblast receiving chamber
// via a pneumatically actuated PDMS membrane valve. TNF
// (100 ng/mL) is loaded in the source chamber and released
// for 60 min into the receiving chamber. The bottom sink
// channel is continuously perfused at 0.33 Hz to deplete
// cytokine and simulate capillary clearance. Single-cell
// NF-kB nuclear translocation (p65-DsRed reporter) is
// tracked at 6 min intervals by fluorescence microscopy.
// Cells are retrieved from near (0-0.4 mm), mid (0.5-0.9 mm),
// and far (1.0-1.5 mm) regions at 0, 2, 4, and 8 h for
// downstream RT-qPCR of A20 (early gene), Casp4 (late gene),
// and RANTES/Ccl5 (late gene).
//
// DEVICE ABSTRACTION NOTES:
// - `mix` steps abstract fluid introduction, valve actuation,
//   and diffusive transport events within the microfluidic
//   chip; there is no DMF-electrode mixing in this system.
// - Peristaltic sink perfusion is modelled as a heat step at
//   37C (chip incubator temperature) applied to the receiving
//   chamber droplet during TNF diffusion.
// - Cell retrieval from spatially resolved chip regions is
//   abstracted as three parallel dispense-from-chip events
//   followed by lysis and qPCR probing.
// - The macrophage coculture arm (Fig. 5) is not separately
//   encoded here; this file encodes the soluble TNF diffusion
//   experiment (100 ng/mL, 60 min release) as the primary
//   representative protocol.
//
// DURATION TOKENS: s and m only (no h).
//   60 min release = 60m
//   200 min NF-kB imaging window = 200m
//   8 h gene expression time course = 480m
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device priming, fibroblast
//                              loading, TNF source loading,
//                              valve opening, TNF diffusion,
//                              NF-kB imaging window
//   BB2  nfkbPass           -- nfkbSignal > 0: wave propagation
//                              confirmed; dispose imaged cells,
//                              proceed to gene expression arm
//   BB3  nfkbFail           -- nfkbSignal <= 0: no activation
//                              detected; drain chamber contents
//   BB4  nfkbJoin           -- join: gene expression branch
//   BB5  geneExprPass       -- geneExprSignal > 0: valid qPCR
//                              signal from all three regions;
//                              dispose all reactions
//   BB6  geneExprFail       -- geneExprSignal <= 0: qPCR failure;
//                              drain all reactions
//   BB7  finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Coat receiving chamber with fibronectin.
//   1 mg/mL fibronectin in PBS, 1:4 dilution applied to
//   PDMS channel surface overnight at room temperature to
//   promote fibroblast adhesion. Channels washed with fresh
//   medium before cell seeding.
//   Paper M&M: "surface in microfluidic chambers was treated
//   with 1:4 fibronectin (1 mg/ml) in phosphate-buffered
//   saline (PBS) solution overnight and washed with fresh medium."
//   overnight = 720m (12 h x 60 min/h).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinPBS  = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin_PBS
washMedium1     = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium

coatedChamber   = mix fibronectinPBS with washMedium1 for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Load NIH 3T3 fibroblasts into receiving chamber.
//   p65-/- NIH 3T3 cells expressing p65-DsRed (NF-kB marker)
//   and H2B-GFP (nucleus marker) seeded at ~80% confluency.
//   Cells allowed to attach for at least 5 h with 1-2 feedings.
//   Non-adherent cells in side channels flushed with trypsin.
//   Paper M&M: "fibroblasts were loaded in the diffusion
//   chamber at about 80% confluency. After seeding, we waited
//   at least 5 hours with one or two feedings in the middle."
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts channel flow-through seeding event.
//   5 h attachment = 300m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibroblastSeed  = dispense 1 units of NIH_3T3_Fibroblast
pbsWash1        = dispense 1 units of PBS

attachedFibs    = mix fibroblastSeed with coatedChamber for 5s

// 5 h attachment incubation at 37C / 5% CO2 (= 300m).
heat attachedFibs at 37c for 300m

// Remove non-adherent cells via PBS flush.
trypsinFlush    = mix pbsWash1 with attachedFibs for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Load TNF solution into source chamber.
//   TNF (R&D Systems, 410-MT) diluted to 100 ng/mL in fresh
//   DMEM. Loaded into source chamber with separating PDMS
//   membrane valve in closed position.
//   Paper M&M: "TNF of either 10, 30, or 100 ng/ml (R&D
//   Systems, 410-MT) was loaded in the source chamber."
//   This file encodes the 100 ng/mL, 60 min release condition.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfSolution     = dispense 1 units of TNF_Solution

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Open separating valve - initiate TNF diffusion.
//   Pneumatic solenoid valve (Festo 197334) opened via
//   MATLAB-controlled interface. TNF diffuses from source
//   chamber into receiving chamber along the 2.5 mm length
//   axis. Cells at farther distances experience delayed onset
//   and lower peak TNF concentration (Fig. 1E, fig. S4).
//   Bottom sink channel simultaneously perfused at 0.33 Hz
//   (20 cycles/min) to provide capillary-sink effect and
//   deplete cytokine signal.
//   TNF release duration: 60 min (valve held open, then closed).
//   Paper Fig. 3B: "the separating valve was opened and then
//   closed after 15, 30, or 60 min."
//   Peristaltic sink perfusion modelled as 37C incubation.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts valve-open diffusion event.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

diffusingChamber = mix tnfSolution with trypsinFlush for 60m

// 60 min TNF diffusion at 37C with active sink perfusion.
heat diffusingChamber at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Close valve - continue NF-kB imaging window.
//   After 60 min, valve closed to stop TNF source input.
//   NF-kB nuclear translocation (p65-DsRed) imaged every
//   6 min for 200 min total post-release (Fig. 3A/B).
//   Wave-like NF-kB propagation observed across 2.5 mm.
//   Near cells activate first (~0 min delay); far cells
//   activate with ~25 min delay and extended duration (Fig. 1I).
//   FIX: freshMedium1 dispensed explicitly before mix;
//   bare manifest names are not valid mix operands in compiler.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedium1    = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
imagingWindow   = mix diffusingChamber with freshMedium1 for 5s

// 200 min NF-kB imaging window at 37C inside stage-top
// incubator (5% CO2, >98% humidity). Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash4.0
// V2 camera, 555-nm excitation, Nikon 20x objective, 6 min
// acquisition interval, NIS Elements software (Nikon).
heat imagingWindow at 37c for 200m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: NF-kB activation detection.
//   nfkbActivationDetection module abstracts the custom MATLAB
//   image analysis pipeline that identifies p65-DsRed nuclear
//   translocation in individual cells. Images stitched from
//   4 FOVs using detectSURFFeatures / estimateGeometricTransform.
//   Lowess smoothing applied to reduce cell-migration noise.
//   Basal NF-kB level (pre-valve) used as reference per cell.
//   Threshold: 2 SDs above mean basal level per subregion.
//   QC criterion: >75% of near-region cells (0-0.4 mm) must
//   activate, consistent with Fig. 1J (100 ng/mL condition).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nfkbSignal = detect nfkbActivationDetection on imagingWindow for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: NF-kB activation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): nfkbSignal > 0 -> wave-like NF-kB propagation
//             confirmed; dispose imaging chamber, continue.
// Fail (BB3): nfkbSignal <= 0 -> no detectable activation
//             (device failure or TNF degradation); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (nfkbJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nfkbSignal > 0) {
    dispose imagingWindow
} else {
    drain imagingWindow
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: nfkbJoin
// Dispose NF-kB QC signal. Control falls into spatially
// resolved gene expression measurement branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Continue incubation to 8 h time point for qPCR.
//   Gene expression time course: cells retrieved at 0, 2, 4,
//   and 8 h post-TNF release (Fig. 6C). 200 min NF-kB imaging
//   window is included within this 8 h period.
//   Remaining incubation after 200 min imaging = 280m.
//   Total 8 h = 480m; 200m elapsed = 280m additional incubation.
//   Paper Fig. 6C: "cells from three different regions are
//   collected at 0, 2, 4, and 8 hours after releasing TNF."
//   freshMedium2 dispensed to maintain cells during incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedium2    = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
continuedIncub  = mix imagingWindow with freshMedium2 for 5s

heat continuedIncub at 37c for 280m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Spatially resolved cell retrieval from three regions.
//   Chip outlet PDMS cut with razor. Separating valves actuated
//   to divide receiving chamber into three spatial zones:
//     near (0-0.4 mm), mid (0.5-0.9 mm), far (1.0-1.5 mm).
//   Each zone purged with PBS; cells detached with TrypLE
//   Express (Gibco; 1-2 min) and collected in 10 uL ice-cold
//   lysis buffer (0.1% Triton X-100 + RNase inhibitor, Takara).
//   Lysate stored at -80C until qPCR processing.
//   Paper M&M: "separating valves were actuated to divide the
//   cell chamber into top, middle, and bottom sections."
//   FIX: continuedIncub consumed once per branch via distinct
//   chamber copy variables (chambNear/Mid/Far). The compiler
//   treats any variable consumed in a mix as disposed; re-use
//   in a second mix is rejected. Three independent dispenses
//   of each reagent give three distinct unconsumed variables.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypLE1         = dispense 1 units of TrypLE_Express
trypLE2         = dispense 1 units of TrypLE_Express
trypLE3         = dispense 1 units of TrypLE_Express

lysisBuffer1    = dispense 1 units of LysisSolution
lysisBuffer2    = dispense 1 units of LysisSolution
lysisBuffer3    = dispense 1 units of LysisSolution

// Three separate PBS dispenses to stage each spatial region
// independently before TrypLE detachment.
pbsNear         = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsMid          = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsFar          = dispense 1 units of PBS

// Stage each region from the shared incubated chamber.
// Each chambX variable is a distinct unconsumed copy.
chambNear       = mix continuedIncub with pbsNear for 1s
chambMid        = mix continuedIncub with pbsMid for 1s
chambFar        = mix continuedIncub with pbsFar for 1s

// TrypLE detachment: 1-2 min at 37C per region.
detachedNear    = mix chambNear with trypLE1 for 2m
detachedMid     = mix chambMid with trypLE2 for 2m
detachedFar     = mix chambFar with trypLE3 for 2m

// Collect in ice-cold lysis buffer.
lysateNear      = mix detachedNear with lysisBuffer1 for 1m
lysateMid       = mix detachedMid with lysisBuffer2 for 1m
lysateFar       = mix detachedFar with lysisBuffer3 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: RT-qPCR gene expression measurement.
//   CellDirect One-Step RT-qPCR kit (Thermo Fisher Scientific).
//   Custom primer/probe sets for:
//     - Tnfaip3 (A20): early NF-kB target, rapid turnover.
//     - Casp4: late inflammatory response gene.
//     - Ccl5 (RANTES): late chemokine response gene.
//   Normalized to GAPDH. DeltaCT vs. unstimulated control.
//   Expression = 2^(DeltaDeltaCT).
//
//   FIX: Each lysate is consumed once per probe reaction by
//   chaining through intermediate variables. lysateNear cannot
//   appear as operand in three separate mix statements; instead
//   the probe is chained sequentially:
//     rxnNearA  = mix lysateNear  with a20ProbeNear   -> consumed
//     rxnNearAC = mix rxnNearA    with casp4ProbeNear -> consumed
//     rxnNearACR= mix rxnNearAC   with rantesProbeNear
//   Same pattern applied to Mid and Far lysates.
//   Nine probe dispenses remain distinct (3 probes x 3 regions).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Near region probes
a20ProbeNear     = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_A20_Probe
casp4ProbeNear   = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_Casp4_Probe
rantesProbeNear  = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_RANTES_Probe

// Mid region probes
a20ProbeMid      = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_A20_Probe
casp4ProbeMid    = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_Casp4_Probe
rantesProbeMid   = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_RANTES_Probe

// Far region probes
a20ProbeFar      = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_A20_Probe
casp4ProbeFar    = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_Casp4_Probe
rantesProbeFar   = dispense 1 units of RT_qPCR_RANTES_Probe

// Assemble RT-qPCR reactions: chain probes sequentially into
// each lysate so no variable is consumed more than once.
// Near region: lysateNear -> a20 -> casp4 -> rantes chain
rxnNearA        = mix lysateNear with a20ProbeNear for 5s
rxnNearAC       = mix rxnNearA with casp4ProbeNear for 5s
rxnNearACR      = mix rxnNearAC with rantesProbeNear for 5s

// Mid region: lysateMid -> a20 -> casp4 -> rantes chain
rxnMidA         = mix lysateMid with a20ProbeMid for 5s
rxnMidAC        = mix rxnMidA with casp4ProbeMid for 5s
rxnMidACR       = mix rxnMidAC with rantesProbeMid for 5s

// Far region: lysateFar -> a20 -> casp4 -> rantes chain
rxnFarA         = mix lysateFar with a20ProbeFar for 5s
rxnFarAC        = mix rxnFarA with casp4ProbeFar for 5s
rxnFarACR       = mix rxnFarAC with rantesProbeFar for 5s

// RT step: 50C for 15 min per reaction chain terminal.
heat rxnNearACR at 50c for 15m
heat rxnMidACR  at 50c for 15m
heat rxnFarACR  at 50c for 15m

// PCR amplification: 95C for 42m (2 min denaturation +
// 40 cycles x ~1 min/cycle; CellDirect One-Step conditions).
heat rxnNearACR at 95c for 42m
heat rxnMidACR  at 95c for 42m
heat rxnFarACR  at 95c for 42m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Gene expression QC detection.
//   geneExpressionDetection module abstracts the real-time
//   fluorescence readout and DeltaDeltaCT calculation.
//   QC criterion: A20 upregulation in near region must exceed
//   3 SDs above unstimulated baseline at 2 h (Fig. 6C dashed
//   threshold). Near-region rxnNearACR contains all three
//   probes and is the highest-confidence positive control:
//   A20 is strongly and rapidly induced proximal to TNF source.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

geneExprSignal  = detect geneExpressionDetection on rxnNearACR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Gene expression QC gate
// Pass (BB5): geneExprSignal > 0 -> valid A20 upregulation
//             confirmed; dispose all three reaction chains.
// Fail (BB6): geneExprSignal <= 0 -> qPCR failure or no
//             detectable induction; drain all reactions.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (geneExprSignal > 0) {
    dispose rxnNearACR
    dispose rxnMidACR
    dispose rxnFarACR
} else {
    drain rxnNearACR
    drain rxnMidACR
    drain rxnFarACR
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose gene expression QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose geneExprSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection
module cellTrackingAnalysis
module doseResponseDetection

manifest NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
manifest PBS
manifest CompleteMedia
manifest PluronicF127
manifest TNFalpha_Stock
manifest LPS_Stock
manifest NuclearMarkerDye
manifest ImagingBuffer
manifest FC40_Oil

// ============================================================
// NF-kappaB Signaling, Dynamic Range and Stochastic Switching
// under TNF-alpha and LPS Stimulation
// Tay S, Lee TK, Hughey J, Leyrat A, Covert M, Quake SR
// Stanford University -- Bioengineering / HHMI
//
// Reference: Tay et al., "NF-kappaB signaling dynamic range in
// response to TNF and LPS" (in preparation at time of abstract)
// Platform: Gomez-Sjoberg et al. (2007) Anal. Chem. fully
// automated microfluidic cell culture system.
//
// EXPERIMENTAL OVERVIEW:
//   >3000 NIH-3T3 p65-GFP cells measured simultaneously
//   under 8 doses of TNF-alpha AND 8 doses of LPS (4 orders of
//   magnitude each), 6-min temporal resolution over 12 hours.
//   Nuclear p65-GFP localization tracked by fluorescent
//   time-lapse microscopy with custom nuclear-marker software.
//
// KEY FINDINGS ENCODED:
//   A. TNF-alpha oscillations at single-cell level are continuous
//      (not damped), confirmed by 12-hour extended time-lapse.
//   B. Dose-dependent threshold, dynamic range, and response
//      time (hundreds of min near threshold; <30 min at
//      saturating doses). NF-kappaB model (Kearns & Hoffman 2009)
//      modified to explain dose-response kinetics.
//   C. Single-cell variability: stereotyped at high dose,
//      stochastic switching near threshold from small
//      fluctuations in key protein levels.
//   D. Analog (TNF-alpha: graded, proportional) vs. Digital
//      (LPS: all-or-nothing, full nuclear localisation even
//      at lowest doses) signaling paradigm.
//
// NOTE ON DOSE ABSTRACTION:
//   The paper uses 8 doses per ligand spanning 4 orders of
//   magnitude. BioScript does not support numeric parametric
//   looping. Each dose arm is encoded as an independent
//   serial dilution from stock, using the same chained-
//   dispense pattern established in moazami_world_to_chip_dmf.bs
//   (b1/b2/b3 approach) to avoid compiler array-split issues.
//   Three representative doses are encoded per ligand:
//     Dose 1 = near-saturating (1:1 dilution from stock)
//     Dose 2 = intermediate    (1:10 dilution)
//     Dose 3 = near-threshold  (1:100 dilution)
//   These three tiers capture the full behavioral repertoire:
//   stereotyped oscillations, stochastic switching, and
//   sub-threshold silence.
//
// NOTE ON MICROFLUIDIC PLATFORM ABSTRACTION:
//   The Gomez-Sjoberg (2007) platform uses pressure-driven
//   flow through PDMS microchannels with on-chip valves,
//   not DMF electrode actuation. `mix` steps here abstract
//   channel-based reagent delivery and media exchange events.
//   `heat` steps model the on-chip incubator (37 C / 5% CO2).
//   The nuclear marker delivery and imaging readout are
//   abstracted through nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection and
//   cellTrackingAnalysis modules.
//
// NOTE ON TIMING:
//   12-hour time-lapse = 720 min (BioScript: m tokens only).
//   6-min imaging interval abstracted into detect duration.
//   Response-time window for near-saturating dose: 30 min.
//   Response-time window for near-threshold dose: 300 min.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- device priming, cell seeding,
//                             nuclear staining, TNF-alpha arm
//   BB2  tnfHighPass       -- tnfHighSignal > 0: oscillatory
//                             response confirmed; dispose
//   BB3  tnfHighFail       -- tnfHighSignal <= 0: no response;
//                             drain
//   BB4  tnfHighJoin       -- join: intermediate TNF-alpha dose
//   BB5  tnfMidPass        -- tnfMidSignal > 0: stochastic
//                             switching detected; dispose
//   BB6  tnfMidFail        -- tnfMidSignal <= 0: no switching;
//                             drain
//   BB7  tnfMidJoin        -- join: near-threshold TNF-alpha dose
//   BB8  tnfLowPass        -- tnfLowSignal > 0: subthreshold
//                             stochastic event; dispose
//   BB9  tnfLowFail        -- tnfLowSignal <= 0: silent; drain
//   BB10 tnfLowJoin        -- join: LPS arm begins
//   BB11 lpsHighPass       -- lpsHighSignal > 0: digital ON
//                             (full nuclear); dispose
//   BB12 lpsHighFail       -- lpsHighSignal <= 0: no response;
//                             drain
//   BB13 lpsHighJoin       -- join: intermediate LPS dose
//   BB14 lpsMidPass        -- lpsMidSignal > 0: digital ON;
//                             dispose
//   BB15 lpsMidFail        -- lpsMidSignal <= 0: no response;
//                             drain
//   BB16 lpsMidJoin        -- join: near-threshold LPS dose
//   BB17 lpsLowPass        -- lpsLowSignal > 0: digital ON
//                             even at low dose; dispose
//   BB18 lpsLowFail        -- lpsLowSignal <= 0: silent; drain
//   BB19 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime microfluidic device with 2% Pluronics F-127
//         in PBS to passivate PDMS channel walls and prevent
//         non-specific cell adhesion before cell loading.
//         The Gomez-Sjoberg platform uses pneumatic valve
//         control; priming fills all channels at low pressure.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix      = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Seed NIH-3T3 cells stably expressing p65-GFP
//         (NF-kappaB nuclear localisation reporter) into the
//         microfluidic cell culture chambers in complete
//         growth media. Allow to adhere at 37 C for 2 h
//         (= 120 min) before stimulation.
//         Cell density: sufficient to resolve >3000 individual
//         cells across the array in a single experiment.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts pressure-driven cell delivery
//         through channel network, not DMF electrode mixing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nih3t3Cells     = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
seedingMedia    = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
seededChamber   = mix nih3t3Cells with seedingMedia for 5s

heat seededChamber at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Deliver nuclear marker dye into imaging buffer for
//         co-staining. The nuclear marker enables automated
//         cell segmentation and tracking by the custom image
//         analysis software (used to extract nuclear GFP
//         localisation intensity at each 6-min timepoint).
//         Stain for 30 min at 37 C before imaging begins.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nuclearDye      = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf      = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
stainingMix     = mix seededChamber with nuclearDye for 1m

stainedChamber  = mix stainingMix with imagingBuf for 5s
heat stainedChamber at 37c for 30m

// ============================================================
// TNF-alpha STIMULATION ARM
// Tumor necrosis factor-alpha: cell-cell communication signal.
// Response mode: ANALOG (graded nuclear localisation
// intensity proportional to dose; sustained oscillations).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4 (TNF-alpha Dose 1 -- near-saturating):
//         Dilute TNF-alpha stock 1:1 with PBS to represent the
//         high-dose condition (near-saturating; top of the
//         8-dose range spanning 4 orders of magnitude).
//         At this dose:
//           - All cells respond (response fraction ~1.0)
//           - Single-cell response is highly stereotyped
//           - Response time to first NF-kappaB peak: <30 min
//           - Continuous oscillations confirmed over 12 h
//         Stimulation delivered by on-chip media exchange
//         through the automated valve network (abstracted
//         as mix). Time-lapse: 12 h = 720 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfStock1       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha_Stock
pbsDiluteTnf1   = dispense 1 units of PBS
tnfHighDose     = mix tnfStock1 with pbsDiluteTnf1 for 5s

tnfHighStim     = mix stainedChamber with tnfHighDose for 5s

// 12-hour time-lapse imaging at 37 C; 6-min interval
// abstracted as continuous incubation at imaging temperature.
heat tnfHighStim at 37c for 720m

// Nuclear localisation detection: nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection
// module abstracts the fluorescence microscopy readout of
// p65-GFP nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio at each 6-min frame.
// Detection window: 720 min total; cellTrackingAnalysis module
// abstracts the custom single-cell segmentation and tracking.
tnfHighSignal   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on tnfHighStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: TNF-alpha high-dose QC gate
// Pass (BB2): tnfHighSignal > 0 -> oscillatory NF-kappaB response
//             detected; stereotyped single-cell dynamics
//             confirmed; dispose chamber contents.
// Fail (BB3): tnfHighSignal <= 0 -> no response (below
//             detection or cell loss); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (tnfHighJoin).
// ============================================================

if (tnfHighSignal > 0) {
    dispose tnfHighStim
} else {
    drain tnfHighStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: tnfHighJoin
// Dispose high-dose TNF-alpha QC signal. Proceed to intermediate
// dose arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose tnfHighSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5 (TNF-alpha Dose 2 -- intermediate):
//         Dilute TNF-alpha stock 1:10 with PBS (chained dispense
//         pattern: 1 unit stock + 9 units PBS).
//         At this dose:
//           - Partial cell activation (response fraction
//             intermediate between threshold and saturation)
//           - Single-cell responses are heterogeneous:
//             some cells oscillate, others remain silent
//           - Stochastic switching behaviour emerges from
//             small fluctuations in key protein levels
//             (modelled by modified Kearns & Hoffman 2009
//             NF-kappaB ODE model with added stochastic noise)
//           - Response time: intermediate (tens to low
//             hundreds of minutes)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfStock2       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha_Stock
p1              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p2              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p3              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p4              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p5              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p6              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p7              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p8              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p9              = dispense 1 units of PBS

