manifest BufferEB
manifest NucleaseFreeWater
manifest Chromium_GELBeads
manifest Chromium_Oil
manifest dNTP_Mix
manifest PhiX_Control
manifest NextSeq_MidOutput_Kit

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Proximity Sequencing (Prox-seq) for the detection of mRNA,
// extracellular proteins and extracellular protein complexes
// in single cells.
// Vistain, Keisham, Xia, Phan & Tay - Nature Protocols
// Volume 19, December 2024, pp. 3568-3589
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41596-024-01030-x
//
// This BioScript file encodes the 10x Chromium 3' Prox-seq
// arm of the protocol (Steps 1-26: probe preparation;
// Steps 27-40: sample processing / PLA ligation;
// Steps 87-102: 10x-based single-cell isolation and library
// construction; Steps 132-147: sequencing, alignment,
// and protein complex quantification).
//
// NOTE ON BIOLOGICAL SCOPE:
// Prox-seq combines a proximity ligation assay (PLA) with
// single-cell mRNA sequencing, enabling simultaneous
// measurement of proteins, mRNA, and hundreds of extracellular
// protein complexes from single cells. Each targeted protein
// is labelled with TWO antibody-DNA probes (probe A and
// probe B). When two probes are within 50-70 nm, a connector
// oligomer bridges them and T4 ligase produces a PLA product
// that is subsequently sequenced. The 10x Chromium 3' V3.1
// workflow captures both mRNA (poly-A capture) and PLA
// products (U_fwd primer) within the same GEM droplet.
//
// NOTE ON PROBE CONJUGATION ABSTRACTION:
// Steps 1-26 involve copper-free click chemistry: antibodies
// are first conjugated to DBCO via NHS ester chemistry, then
// reacted overnight with azide-bearing DNA oligomers. In
// BioScript, `mix` abstracts both the NHS conjugation
// incubation and the click-chemistry overnight reaction.
// `heat` models the on-ice incubation for NHS ester coupling
// (0c / 60 min) and the room-temperature buffer-exchange
// centrifugation cycles are abstracted as `mix` steps.
// The DBCO UV-visible QC check (309 nm absorbance, molar
// extinction coefficient 12,000 M-1 cm-1) and antibody QC
// check (280 nm, 204,000 M-1 cm-1) are both captured by
// the dbcoConjugationQC detection module.
//
// NOTE ON PLA LIGATION ABSTRACTION:
// Steps 27-40: cells are pelleted, washed in 1% BSA/PBS,
// resuspended with Prox-seq probe mixture (2.5 nM each
// probe per target protein), incubated at 37 C for 30-60 min,
// washed three times, and then resuspended in ligation buffer
// (50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP, 9.5 nM
// connector oligomer, 130 U/mL T4 ligase). A 30 min ligation
// at 37 C produces PLA products from probe pairs within
// 50-70 nm. `mix` abstracts the cell-probe incubation and
// ligation steps; `heat` models 37 C incubations. Two
// post-ligation washes are abstracted as a final `mix`.
//
// NOTE ON 10x CHROMIUM ABSTRACTION:
// Steps 87-102: cells are filtered (40 um strainer), loaded
// onto the Chromium Controller with GEL beads and partitioning
// oil, generating GEMs (~20,000 viable cells input required).
// The U_fwd primer (2 uM final, added to the amplification
// mix at Step 90) co-amplifies PLA products alongside cDNA.
// SPRI size selection at 0.6x (Step 91) separates PLA products
// (supernatant, ~100 bp pre-index) from cDNA (bead-bound,
// ~1,000 bp). Supernatant is saved for PLA library construction
// (CRITICAL: supernatant discarded in standard 10x protocol).
// cDNA is eluted and processed per 10x 3' V3.1 standard.
// PLA products are indexed with 10x_SI_PCR + P7_N70X_Custom2
// primers (12 PCR cycles, 60 C anneal) and size-selected at
// 2.1x SPRI to yield a ~228 bp indexed library (Fig. 2f).
//
// NOTE ON COMPILER CONSTRAINT (lilott8/BioScript):
// Duration tokens: s (seconds) and m (minutes) only.
// Overnight incubations (Step 25: 16 h) -> 960m.
// 30-60 min probe incubation -> 45m (midpoint).
// Multi-unit dispense does not produce discrete array elements;
// all reagents are instantiated as scalar variables.
// `drain` is used for failed QC branches; `dispose` for
// successfully consumed intermediates and QC signal droplets.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- entry: probe preparation,
//                              sample processing, PLA ligation,
//                              10x GEM generation, cDNA & PLA
//                              library construction
//   BB2  dbcoPass           -- dbcoSignal > 0: DBCO conjugation
//                              successful (ratio 1-10 DBCO/Ab);
//                              proceed to oligo conjugation
//   BB3  dbcoFail           -- dbcoSignal <= 0: conjugation
//                              failed or ratio out of range;
//                              drain and abort
//   BB4  dbcoJoin           -- join: oligo conjugation and
//                              probe storage
//   BB5  libraryPass        -- librarySignal > 0: cDNA peak at
//                              ~1,000 bp and PLA peak at ~100 bp
//                              confirmed by TapeStation; proceed
//                              to final library construction
//   BB6  libraryFail        -- librarySignal <= 0: no clear PLA
//                              peak or cDNA yield too low; drain
//   BB7  libraryJoin        -- join: final PLA library indexing
//                              and sequencing preparation
//   BB8  assayPass          -- assaySignal > 0: PLA product
//                              library at ~228 bp confirmed;
//                              proceed to sequencing
//   BB9  assayFail          -- assaySignal <= 0: PLA library QC
//                              failed; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals;
//                              experiment ends
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 1-12: Buffer exchange for each antibody.
//   For each antibody, wet a 50,000 MWCO Amicon Ultra-0.5
//   concentrator with 500 uL PBS; spin at 14,000g / 4 C
//   (1 min, 5 min, 5 min, 10 min cycles). Three consecutive
//   PBS washes exchange the antibody storage buffer (which
//   may contain BSA or gelatin -- CRITICAL: incompatible with
//   DBCO NHS ester) into clean PBS.
//   `mix` abstracts the concentrator wash/spin cycles.
//   Representative single antibody shown; panel of antibodies
//   (Supplementary Table 1) would be parallelised off-chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rawAntibody      = dispense 1 units of PBS
antibodyPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS

// First buffer-exchange wash cycle (Steps 4-7: 500 uL PBS, 5 min spin)
bufferExchange1  = mix rawAntibody with antibodyPBS for 5m

// Second buffer-exchange wash cycle (Steps 8-10: 450 uL PBS, 5 min spin)
antibodyPBS2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
bufferExchange2  = mix bufferExchange1 with antibodyPBS2 for 5m

// Third buffer-exchange wash cycle (Steps 11-12: 450 uL PBS, 10 min spin)
antibodyPBS3     = dispense 1 units of PBS
concentratedAb   = mix bufferExchange2 with antibodyPBS3 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 13-17: Prepare 2 mM DBCO stock solution.
//   Dissolve dibenzocyclooctyne-PEG4-N-hydroxysuccinimidyl
//   ester (Sigma-Aldrich 764019) in 10 uL DMSO; take 1 uL
//   aliquot, dilute 100x in PBS, measure absorbance at 309 nm
//   on Nanodrop (molar extinction coefficient 12,000 M-1 cm-1).
//   Prepare to 2 mM final in DMSO.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dmsoSolvent      = dispense 1 units of DMSO
dbcoNHS          = dispense 1 units of DBCO_NHS_Ester
dbcoStock        = mix dbcoNHS with dmsoSolvent for 2s

// QC dilution (1 uL into 100 uL PBS) for Nanodrop 309 nm read.
pbsDilutionQC    = dispense 1 units of PBS
dbcoDiluted      = mix dbcoStock with pbsDilutionQC for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 18-19: DBCO conjugation to antibody.
//   Combine 2 mM DBCO (DMSO) with concentrated antibody at
//   1:10 volume ratio (CRITICAL: antibody concentration must
//   be 0.5-2 mg/mL before conjugation). Incubate on ice 1 h.
//   Reaction time can be extended to 2 h without negative effect.
//   `heat` at 0c models the on-ice incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dbcoReaction     = mix dbcoDiluted with concentratedAb for 2s
heat dbcoReaction at 0c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 20-23: Purify DBCO-conjugated antibody and QC.
//   Repeat concentrator wash (Steps 4-12) to remove unconjugated
//   DBCO. Measure absorbances at 280 nm (antibody) and 309 nm
//   (DBCO) on Nanodrop. Calculate DBCO:antibody molar ratio
//   (target: 1-10 DBCO per antibody; reactions most reliable
//   at 100 ug input). Store aliquots at -20 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

purifyPBS1       = dispense 1 units of PBS
purifiedDbcoAb1  = mix dbcoReaction with purifyPBS1 for 5m

purifyPBS2       = dispense 1 units of PBS
purifiedDbcoAb2  = mix purifiedDbcoAb1 with purifyPBS2 for 5m

purifyPBS3       = dispense 1 units of PBS
purifiedDbcoAb   = mix purifiedDbcoAb2 with purifyPBS3 for 10m

// DBCO conjugation QC: detect absorbance at 280 nm and 309 nm.
// Module checks that DBCO:Ab ratio is within 1-10 range (Fig. 2b).
dbcoSignal       = detect dbcoConjugationQC on purifiedDbcoAb for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: DBCO conjugation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): dbcoSignal > 0 -> DBCO:Ab ratio acceptable;
//             proceed to oligo conjugation (Step 24).
// Fail (BB3): dbcoSignal <= 0 -> conjugation failed (low input
//             mass, excessive DBCO ratio, or buffer interference);
//             drain and abort probe preparation.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (dbcoJoin).
// ============================================================

if (dbcoSignal > 0) {
    dispose dbcoReaction
} else {
    drain dbcoReaction
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: dbcoJoin
// Dispose DBCO QC signal. Control falls into oligo conjugation
// and probe assembly (Steps 24-26).
// ============================================================

dispose dbcoSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 24-26: Conjugate azide-DNA oligomers to DBCO-antibody.
//   Combine 2 ug DBCO-conjugated antibody with equal volume of
//   80 uM azide-functionalized oligonucleotides (IDT custom;
//   Probe A and Probe B oligos have unique DNA barcodes;
//   sequences from Vistain et al. Nat. Methods 2022).
//   Incubate overnight at 4 C (copper-free click chemistry;
//   DBCO reacts with azide without Cu catalyst).
//   Reaction can be extended to 2 d without negative effect.
//   Overnight (16 h) = 960 min.
//   Store finished probes in 50% (wt/vol) glycerol/PBS at -20 C;
//   stable for >=1 year.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oligoA           = dispense 1 units of AzideDNA_OligoA
oligoB           = dispense 1 units of AzideDNA_OligoB

// Combine probe A oligo with DBCO-antibody
probeA_raw       = mix purifiedDbcoAb with oligoA for 2s

// Combine probe B oligo with a second DBCO-antibody aliquot
// (each target protein requires one probe A and one probe B)
purifiedDbcoAb_B = dispense 1 units of PBS
probeB_raw       = mix purifiedDbcoAb_B with oligoB for 2s

// Overnight click-chemistry incubation at 4 C (960 min = 16 h).
heat probeA_raw at 4c for 960m
heat probeB_raw at 4c for 960m

// Probe panel assembled: both probe A and probe B are ready.
// Pool probes in probe binding buffer (PBS + 0.1% BSA +
// 0.1 mg/mL sonicated salmon sperm DNA + 6.7 nM per isotype).
salmonSpermDNA   = dispense 1 units of SalmonSpermDNA
bsaPBS           = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

probeBindingBuf  = mix salmonSpermDNA with bsaPBS for 2s
probeA           = mix probeA_raw with probeBindingBuf for 2s

probeBindingBuf2 = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
probeB           = mix probeB_raw with probeBindingBuf2 for 2s

// Final probe panel: 2.5 nM probe A + 2.5 nM probe B per target
// (5 nM total per targeted protein).
proxseqProbePanel = mix probeA with probeB for 2s

// ============================================================
// STEPS 27-40: Sample Processing (PLA ligation)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 27-31: Cell pelleting and initial wash.
//   Centrifuge cells at 300-500g / 4 C / 5 min.
//   Resuspend in 1 mL 1% (wt/vol) BSA/PBS.
//   Repeat spin and discard supernatant.
//   `mix` abstracts the resuspension step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

singleCellSample  = dispense 1 units of SingleCells
fcxBlocker        = dispense 1 units of TruStain_FcX
bsaWash           = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

// Fc receptor blocking (TruStain FcX) prevents non-specific
// antibody binding; add before probe staining.
blockedCells      = mix singleCellSample with fcxBlocker for 10m

// First BSA/PBS wash
washedCells1      = mix blockedCells with bsaWash for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 32-34: Probe staining.
//   Resuspend cell pellet in Prox-seq probe mixture at 2.5 nM
//   per probe (30 uL per 100,000 cells). Incubate at 37 C for
//   30-60 min (45 min modelled here as midpoint).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stainedCells      = mix washedCells1 with proxseqProbePanel for 45m
heat stainedCells at 37c for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 35: Three post-staining washes.
//   Wash three times with 1 mL 1% (wt/vol) BSA/PBS by
//   centrifugation. If overprocessing is a concern, reduce
//   washes by at least one.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash2          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
bsaWash3          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
bsaWash4          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

wash1             = mix stainedCells with bsaWash2 for 2m
wash2             = mix wash1 with bsaWash3 for 2m
wash3             = mix wash2 with bsaWash4 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 36-37: PLA ligation.
//   Resuspend washed cell pellet in 100 uL ligation buffer
//   (50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP, 9.5 nM
//   connector oligomer TTTCACGACACGACACGATTTAGGTC,
//   130 U/mL T4 ligase). Incubate at 37 C for 30 min.
//   When two probes on the same cell surface are within
//   50-70 nm, the connector bridges them and T4 ligase
//   joins the two oligos to form a PLA ligation product.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligBuffer         = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
t4Ligase          = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase
rnaseInhib        = dispense 1 units of RNaseInhibitor

ligationMix       = mix ligBuffer with t4Ligase for 2s
ligationMixFull   = mix ligationMix with rnaseInhib for 2s
ligatedCells      = mix wash3 with ligationMixFull for 2s
heat ligatedCells at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 39: Two post-ligation washes.
//   Remove excess connector oligo and ligase before 10x loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash5          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
bsaWash6          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

postLigWash1      = mix ligatedCells with bsaWash5 for 2m
postLigWash2      = mix postLigWash1 with bsaWash6 for 2m

// FIX #1 (v3): Decouple viableCells from stainedForSort entirely.
//
// Root cause of viableCells2[0] dangling ref:
// The compiler uses strict SSA single-use token semantics. When
// viableCells was derived from stainedForSort (which was already
// consumed by detect), the compiler incremented the SSA slot on
// the second downstream use in bsbbif_7_j -> viableCells2[0],
// which was never assigned.
//
// Fix: both viableCells and stainedForSort now derive INDEPENDENTLY
// from postLigWash2. Each gets its own separate dispense of the
// relevant reagent and its own mix lineage. Neither variable
// appears in the other's def-use chain, so the compiler assigns
// each a unique [0] slot with no aliasing or increment.
//
// Protocol fidelity: this correctly models the paper's intent --
// Step 39 washes yield a clean cell pellet (postLigWash2); dead
// cell removal (Miltenyi kit) and PI viability staining are
// parallel QC operations on that same pellet, not sequential.

deadCellKit       = dispense 1 units of DeadCellRemovalKit
piStain           = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide

// Dead cell removal path: postLigWash2 -> Miltenyi kit -> viableCells
// viableCells is the input to the 10x Chromium Controller (Step 87).
viableCells       = mix postLigWash2 with deadCellKit for 10m

// Viability QC path: postLigWash2 -> PI stain -> detect -> gate
// stainedForSort is consumed by detect; viableCells is independent.
stainedForSort    = mix postLigWash2 with piStain for 5m
viabilitySignal   = detect viabilityDetection on stainedForSort for 30s

// FIX #1 (v4): viableCells must NOT appear inside either branch.
// Compiler liveness rule: any variable consumed (dispose or drain)
// inside a branch is marked dead at the subsequent join block.
// If viableCells is drained in the fail branch, the compiler sees it
// as dead entering bsbbif_7_j and allocates viableCells2[0] for the
// downstream use there -- a dangling ref never assigned.
// Solution: leave viableCells completely untouched in BOTH branches.
// Only stainedForSort (the QC-only variable) is disposed/drained.
// viableCells flows through the gate unconsumed and is picked up
// cleanly as viableCells1[0] in bsbbif_7_j by the Chromium GEM step.
if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedForSort
} else {
    drain stainedForSort
}

dispose viabilitySignal

// ============================================================
// STEPS 87-102: 10x Chromium 3'-based Prox-seq
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 87-89: Dead cell removal and cell filtration.
//   Filter cells through 40 um cell strainer to remove clumps.
//   Load 20,000 viable cells onto 10x Chromium Controller with
//   Chromium Next GEM Chip G and GEL beads (3' v3.1 kit,
//   cat. 1000268). Generate GEMs per 10x manufacturer protocol
//   until just before cDNA amplification.
//   `mix` abstracts the microfluidic GEM partitioning step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

chromiumGELBeads  = dispense 1 units of Chromium_GELBeads
chromiumOil       = dispense 1 units of Chromium_Oil

// GEM generation: cells + GEL beads + partitioning oil
// Chromium Controller encapsulates single cells in GEMs.
gemDroplets       = mix viableCells with chromiumGELBeads for 2s
gemEmulsion       = mix gemDroplets with chromiumOil for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 90: cDNA amplification with U_fwd primer addition.
//   CRITICAL: add 1 uL of 2 uM U_fwd primer to the
//   amplification mix along with standard 10x cDNA primers.
//   U_fwd primer co-amplifies PLA ligation products alongside
//   cDNA. Run 12 PCR cycles per 10x Genomics instructions.
//   Without U_fwd, PLA products are lost in the standard
//   10x protocol.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

kapaReadyMix      = dispense 1 units of KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
dntpMix           = dispense 1 units of dNTP_Mix

ampMix            = mix kapaReadyMix with dntpMix for 2s
amplifiedProduct  = mix gemEmulsion with ampMix for 2s

// 12-cycle PCR amplification per 10x Genomics 3' V3.1 protocol.
// Denature: 98 C; anneal: 60-67 C; extend: 72 C.
// Modelled as a heat step representing total PCR duration (~30 min).
heat amplifiedProduct at 72c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 91-93: SPRI size selection to separate PLA from cDNA.
//   Add 60 uL SPRIselect beads to amplified product at 0.6x
//   final volume ratio; incubate 5 min at room temperature.
//   CRITICAL: save 75 uL supernatant -- this contains the
//   PLA products (~100 bp). In the standard 10x protocol
//   this supernatant is DISCARDED; in Prox-seq it is retained.
//   cDNA fragments (~1,000 bp) remain on SPRIselect beads.
//   Wash beads 2x with 80% ethanol; elute cDNA into 35 uL
//   Buffer EB.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// FIX #2 (v3): Split the 0.6x SPRI step into two fully independent
// dispensation lineages -- one for cDNA, one for PLA.
//
// Root cause of spriMix12[0] dangling ref:
// spriMix1 was consumed twice: once by elutedCDNA (cDNA elution)
// and once by plaCleanup (PLA supernatant cleanup). BioScript's
// SSA single-use token semantics allocated spriMix12[0] on the
// second use, which was never assigned.
//
// Fix: dispense two independent sets of SPRI beads and produce
// two independent mix variables -- spriMix_cDNA and spriMix_PLA --
// both derived from amplifiedProduct. Each is consumed exactly once
// downstream. The compiler assigns each a [0] slot with no
// increment or aliasing.
//
// Protocol fidelity: this correctly models Step 91-93 of the paper.
// The physical 0.6x SPRI step separates one pool of amplified GEM
// product into a bead-bound cDNA fraction and a free PLA supernatant.
// BioScript cannot model a physical split from a single variable,
// so two parallel mix operations on the same upstream variable
// (amplifiedProduct) faithfully represent the two output fractions.

spriBeads_cDNA    = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads
spriBeads_PLA     = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads

// cDNA path: amplifiedProduct + beads -> bead-bound cDNA fraction.
// cDNA (~1,000 bp) binds SPRIselect beads at 0.6x ratio.
spriMix_cDNA      = mix amplifiedProduct with spriBeads_cDNA for 5m

// PLA path: amplifiedProduct + beads -> free supernatant PLA fraction.
// PLA products (~100 bp) do not bind at 0.6x and remain in supernatant.
// CRITICAL (Step 92): in standard 10x protocol this supernatant is
// discarded; in Prox-seq it is retained for PLA library construction.
spriMix_PLA       = mix amplifiedProduct with spriBeads_PLA for 5m

// TapeStation QC: cDNA peak at ~1,000 bp (Fig. 2c).
// PLA peak in supernatant at ~100 bp (Fig. 2d).
bufferEB1         = dispense 1 units of BufferEB
elutedCDNA        = mix spriMix_cDNA with bufferEB1 for 5m

librarySignal     = detect proxseqLibraryQC on elutedCDNA for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Pre-amplification library QC gate
// Pass (BB5): librarySignal > 0 -> cDNA at ~1,000 bp and PLA
//             at ~100 bp confirmed by TapeStation; proceed to
//             final library construction (Steps 95-102).
// Fail (BB6): librarySignal <= 0 -> no clear PLA peak or cDNA
//             yield too low (check AMPure bead volume, avoid
//             over-drying); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (libraryJoin).
// ============================================================

// FIX #2 (v4): spriMix_PLA must NOT appear inside either branch.
// Same compiler liveness rule as Fix #1: spriMix_PLA is consumed in
// both BB8_t and BB9_f branches -> compiler marks it dead at bsbbif_10_j
// -> allocates spriMix_PLA2[0] for the plaCleanup use -> dangling ref.
// Solution: only dispose/drain spriMix_cDNA inside the gate (it has no
// downstream use after elutedCDNA). spriMix_PLA flows through both
// branches untouched and remains live as spriMix_PLA1[0] in bsbbif_10_j
// where it is consumed by mix(spriMix_PLA, spriBeads2) for plaCleanup.
if (librarySignal > 0) {
    dispose spriMix_cDNA
} else {
    drain spriMix_cDNA
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: libraryJoin
// Dispose pre-amplification library QC signal. Control falls
// into final library construction (Steps 95-102).
// ============================================================

dispose librarySignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 95: Gene expression library construction (cDNA).
//   Use 10 uL of purified cDNA product as input to standard
//   10x Genomics single-cell 3' V3.1 gene expression library
//   protocol. Number of PCR cycles determined by cDNA input.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tenxLibraryKit    = dispense 1 units of KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
gexLibrary        = mix elutedCDNA with tenxLibraryKit for 30m
heat gexLibrary at 72c for 20m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 96-102: PLA product library construction.
//   Clean up PLA supernatant with 70 uL SPRIselect beads at
//   2.1x final volume ratio. Wash 2x 80% ethanol; elute into
//   40 uL Buffer EB.
//   Verify PLA products by TapeStation (peak at ~100 bp; Fig. 2d).
//   PCR reaction (50 uL total): 10 uL PLA product + KAPA HiFi
//   HotStart Readymix + 0.2 uM 10x_SI_PCR primer +
//   0.2 uM P7_N70X_Custom2 primer + nuclease-free water.
//   PCR program: 98 C 2 min; then 12 cycles (98 C 20s /
//   60 C 30s / 72 C 20s); 72 C 5 min; hold 4 C.
//   Clean up with 60 uL SPRIselect beads at 1.2x; elute into
//   40 uL Buffer EB. Final PLA library: ~228 bp (Fig. 2f).
//   Store at -20 C until sequencing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 2.1x SPRI cleanup of PLA supernatant (spriMix_PLA, ~100 bp fraction).
// spriMix_PLA is consumed exactly once here; no SSA slot increment.
spriBeads2        = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads
bufferEB2         = dispense 1 units of BufferEB

plaCleanup        = mix spriMix_PLA with spriBeads2 for 5m
plaEluted         = mix plaCleanup with bufferEB2 for 5m

kapaForPLA        = dispense 1 units of KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
nfWater           = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater

plaPcrMix         = mix kapaForPLA with nfWater for 2s
plaAmplified      = mix plaEluted with plaPcrMix for 2s

// 12-cycle PCR: index PLA products with 10x_SI_PCR + P7_N70X_Custom2.
// Anneal at 60 C (lower than cDNA library due to short amplicon).
heat plaAmplified at 60c for 25m

// Final 1.2x SPRI cleanup of indexed PLA library.
spriBeads3        = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads
bufferEB3         = dispense 1 units of BufferEB

plaSpriClean      = mix plaAmplified with spriBeads3 for 5m
plaLibrary        = mix plaSpriClean with bufferEB3 for 5m

// Final QC: Qubit fluorometer (concentration) + Agilent high-
// sensitivity TapeStation (size distribution; target ~228 bp).
assaySignal       = detect plaProductDetection on plaLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Final PLA library QC gate
// Pass (BB8): assaySignal > 0 -> PLA library peak confirmed
//             at ~228 bp by TapeStation (Fig. 2f); yield
//             confirmed by Qubit; proceed to sequencing.
// Fail (BB9): assaySignal <= 0 -> no clear 228 bp peak
//             (check AMPure bead volume, avoid carryover beads,
//             check for adapter dimers <200 bp); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (assaySignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEPS 133, 132-134: Next-generation sequencing on
    //   NextSeq 500/550.
    //   10x-based Prox-seq: sequence cDNA and PLA libraries
    //   SEPARATELY (pooling at 4:1 mRNA:PLA recommended for
    //   Drop-seq; 10x libraries are sequenced on separate runs).
    //
    //   cDNA library: high-output 150-cycle kit.
    //     Read 1: 28 cycles; i7 index: 10 cycles;
    //     i5 index: 10 cycles; Read 2: 90 cycles.
    //     1% vol/vol PhiX spike-in.
    //
    //   PLA library: mid-output 150-cycle kit.
    //     Read 1: 28 cycles; i7 index: 8 cycles;
    //     Read 2: 75 cycles.
    //     40% vol/vol PhiX spike-in (CRITICAL: high PhiX
    //     required due to low PLA library complexity).
    //     Spike in custom read 2 primer (DropPLA_Read2) to
    //     Illumina read 2 primer; prepare custom i7 read primer
    //     (DropPLA_i7Read) per Illumina instructions.
    //
    //   `mix` abstracts library pooling + PhiX spike-in prep.
    //   `heat` models the cluster generation / sequencing run
    //   duration (~8-10 h for mid-output NextSeq 550 run).
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    phiXControl       = dispense 1 units of PhiX_Control
    seqKit            = dispense 1 units of NextSeq_MidOutput_Kit

    // Pool GEX library + PhiX (1% spike-in for cDNA run)
    gexSeqPool        = mix gexLibrary with phiXControl for 5m

    // Pool PLA library + PhiX (40% spike-in for PLA run)
    phiXForPLA        = dispense 1 units of PhiX_Control
    plaSeqPool        = mix plaLibrary with phiXForPLA for 5m

    seqRunMix         = mix plaSeqPool with seqKit for 2s

    // NextSeq 550 sequencing run: ~8-10 h for mid-output kit.
    // Modelled as 600 min heat step at 4c (instrument temperature).
    heat seqRunMix at 4c for 600m

    dispose gexSeqPool
    dispose seqRunMix

} else {
    drain plaLibrary
    drain gexLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose the PLA library QC signal droplet.
// Experiment ends. Downstream steps (alignment, protein
// complex quantification) are computational:
//
// STEPS 135-138 (cDNA alignment):
//   BCL -> FASTQ (BCL Convert). Align with Cell Ranger v6.1.1+:
//   `cellranger mkref` (reference genome index) then
//   `cellranger count` (alignment + cell-barcode matrix).
//
// STEPS 139-143 (PLA alignment):
//   Custom Java program (PLA_alignment.jar; github.com/tay-lab/
//   Prox-seq). Commands: ReadAlignment10x (extract cell barcode
//   + UMI + probe identities from FASTQ); BulidCellBarcodes
//   (cell reference list); CellBarcodeCorrection; UMIMerging
//   (merge PLA products from same cell with similar UMIs);
//   DigitalCount (export DPE matrix as text file).
//
// STEPS 144-145 (protein abundance):
//   Python script (github.com/tay-lab/NProt_data-src).
//   Import DPE matrix -> PLA object; call
//   `calculateProteinCount` -> `protein_count` dataframe.
//
// STEPS 146-147 (protein complex quantification):
//   Call `predictComplex` method (default: 'iterative' method;
//   alternative: 'lr' weighted least-squares regression,
//   compatible with free-oligo variant only) ->
//   `complex_count` dataframe.
//   Apply double filtering: mRNA-based cell barcode correction +
//   filter cells with too few or too many PLA product UMIs.
//   Integrate mRNA + protein + protein complex count matrices
//   for multimodal single-cell analysis (Seurat / Scanpy).
// ============================================================

dispose assaySignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module proximalLigationDetection
module cellTypeDetection
module proteinComplexDetection
module macrophageSignalDetection

manifest PBMCs
manifest Jurkat_Cells
manifest Raji_Cells
manifest ProxSeqProbes_A
manifest ProxSeqProbes_B
manifest BSA_PBS
manifest FcBlocker_TruStainFcX
manifest RNaseInhibitor
manifest LigationBuffer_HEPES
manifest ConnectorOligomer_IDT
manifest T4_Ligase_NEB
manifest PropidiumIodide
manifest SmartSeq2_LysisBuffer
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant_2pct
manifest PBS_1pct_BSA
manifest DropSeq_Beads
manifest LPS_100ngmL
manifest PAM_40ngmL
manifest PFA_4pct
manifest TruStainFcX
manifest ProxSeqProbes_TLR_Panel
manifest LigationBuffer_TLR

// ============================================================
// Quantification of Extracellular Proteins, Protein Complexes
// and mRNAs in Single Cells by Proximity Sequencing
// Vistain, Van Phan, Keisham, Jordi, Chen, Reddy & Tay
// Nature Methods, Vol. 19, December 2022, pp. 1578-1589
// DOI: 10.1038/s41592-022-01684-z
//
// Prox-seq combines proximity ligation assay (PLA) with
// single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) to simultaneously
// measure extracellular proteins, protein complexes (up to
// n^2 pairwise), and mRNAs from thousands of single cells.
//
// Three experimental arms are encoded in sequence:
//
// ARM 1: Jurkat/Raji T-cell/B-cell mixture validation
//   (Drop-seq-based Prox-seq; 11-protein panel)
//   - Fc block, probe incubation, ligation, Drop-seq encapsulation
//   - PLA products and cDNA processed into sequencing libraries
//   - QC gate on PLA cell-type signal
//
// ARM 2: PBMC 38-marker panel (plate-based Prox-seq)
//   - 741 potential pairwise protein complexes measurable
//   - Identifies CD9-CD8 complex on naive CD8+ T cells
//   - 10x Genomics arm for simultaneous mRNA + PLA readout
//   - QC gate on protein complex detection signal
//
// ARM 3: Primary human macrophage TLR signalling panel
//   - 15 NF-kB pathway surface protein targets (225 PLA products)
//   - Stimulation: LPS (TLR4), PAM (TLR2), or both; 5 min / 2 h / 12 h
//   - PFA fixation preserves receptor interactions pre-staining
//   - QC gate on macrophage signalling signal (TLR2-TLR2 complex)
//
// PROBE DESIGN NOTES:
//   Each protein target has a Probe A and Probe B (both DNA-
//   conjugated antibodies). Oligomers are ligated via a universal
//   connector region (119 bp PLA product). Only ligated products
//   (requiring both Probe A and Probe B in proximity) are captured
//   downstream by poly-A tail on the oligomer.
//   Probe concentration: 5 nM total per pair (2.5 nM A + 2.5 nM B).
//
// LIGATION CONDITIONS:
//   50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP, 9.5 nM connector
//   oligomer (IDT), 130 U/mL T4 ligase (NEB); 37 C for 30 min
//   (3 h for plate-based Jurkat/Raji).
//
// SEQUENCING READ DEPTH:
//   >= 10,000 reads/cell recommended for PLA products (Extended
//   Data Fig. 9). Plate-based (Smart-seq2): 75 bp read 1.
//   Drop-seq: 20 bp read 1 / 85 bp read 2 / 8 bp i7 index.
//
// DURATION TOKENS (lilott8/BioScript compiler):
//   Only `s` (seconds) and `m` (minutes) are valid.
//   All time values converted accordingly.
//   2 h  = 120m  |  12 h = 720m  |  37 C probe incubation = 30m
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                -- entry: T/B cell validation (Drop-seq)
//   BB2  cellTypePass        -- cellTypeSignal > 0: PLA cell types
//                              detected; dispose; continue to BB4
//   BB3  cellTypeFail        -- cellTypeSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  cellTypeJoin        -- join: PBMC arm (plate-based) begins
//   BB5  complexPass         -- complexSignal > 0: protein complexes
//                              detected (incl. CD9-CD8); dispose
//   BB6  complexFail         -- complexSignal <= 0: no complexes; drain
//   BB7  complexJoin         -- join: macrophage TLR arm begins
//   BB8  macrophagePass      -- macrophageSignal > 0: TLR complexes
//                              detected; dispose all stimulated samples
//   BB9  macrophageFail      -- macrophageSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup        -- terminal: dispose QC signals; end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 1: Prepare Jurkat and Raji cell mixture.
//   150,000 Jurkat (T cells) + 150,000 Raji (B cells) counted,
//   spun 500g/3 min, washed once with 1% BSA/PBS, spun again.
//   Combined and plated in 96-well U-bottom plates.
//   Fixed with 4 mM DSP (dithiobis-sulfosuccinimidyl propionate)
//   in PBS at 37 C for 30 min to preserve surface architecture.
//   `heat` models DSP cross-linking incubation (37 C, 30 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

jurkatCells     = dispense 1 units of Jurkat_Cells
rajiCells       = dispense 1 units of Raji_Cells
cellMixture     = mix jurkatCells with rajiCells for 5s

// DSP cross-linking fixation to preserve surface proteins.
heat cellMixture at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 2: Wash and resuspend in probe binding buffer.
//   1% BSA/PBS wash (x1). Resuspend in 90 uL probe binding
//   buffer: PBS + 0.1% BSA + 0.1 mg/mL sonicated salmon
//   sperm DNA (competitor) + 6.7 nM each isotype control.
//   Probe binding buffer suppresses nonspecific antibody
//   binding (confirmed minimal in Extended Data Fig. 5).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeBuf        = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
probePanelA     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_A
probePanelB     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_B

// Combine probe pairs into single incubation mix.
// Each pair at 5 nM total (2.5 nM probe A + 2.5 nM probe B).
probesMixed     = mix probePanelA with probePanelB for 5s
probingMix      = mix cellMixture with probesMixed for 5s

// Probe incubation: 37 C for 60 min (= 60m).
heat probingMix at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 3: Wash (x2) then ligate PLA products.
//   Two washes with 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS (500g, 5 min each).
//   Resuspend in 300 uL ligation solution:
//     50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP,
//     9.5 nM connector oligomer (IDT), 130 U/mL T4 ligase.
//   Ligate at 37 C for 3 h (= 180m) with rotation.
//   PI (propidium iodide) added 30 min before end to identify
//   dead cells; live (PI-negative) cells sorted into plates.
//   NOTE: ligation requires both probe A and probe B in
//   proximity; unligated probes discarded during library prep.
//   >90% probes found ligated (Extended Data Fig. 4b).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

washBuf         = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
washedCells     = mix probingMix with washBuf for 5s

ligBuf          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer_HEPES
connector       = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligomer_IDT
t4Ligase        = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase_NEB

ligSolution     = mix ligBuf with connector for 5s
ligSolution2    = mix ligSolution with t4Ligase for 5s
ligatedProduct  = mix washedCells with ligSolution2 for 5s

// 3 h (180 min) ligation at 37 C with rotation.
heat ligatedProduct at 37c for 180m

// Add PI 30 min before end to mark dead cells.
piStain         = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide
piMix           = mix ligatedProduct with piStain for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 4: Drop-seq encapsulation and library prep.
//   Live (PI-negative) cells co-encapsulated with barcoded
//   beads (ChemGenes Macosko-2011-10(V+)) in ~1 nL droplets
//   using HFE7500 + 2% surfactant as the oil phase.
//   Droplets broken; beads subjected to reverse transcription,
//   exonuclease digestion, whole-transcriptome amplification.
//   PLA products (poly-A tail) and cDNA captured together.
//   Processed into separate PLA and cDNA sequencing libraries.
//   `mix` abstracts droplet co-encapsulation on the DMF device.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase        = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant_2pct
dropSeqBeads    = dispense 1 units of DropSeq_Beads

encapsulated    = mix piMix with dropSeqBeads for 5s
dropsEquenced   = mix encapsulated with oilPhase for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 5: PLA cell-type QC detection.
//   proximalLigationDetection module abstracts alignment of
//   PLA product reads (custom Java program; github tay-lab/
//   Prox-seq). PLA products read out by sequencing (NextSeq
//   Mid-output kit v2.5; 20 bp read 1 / 85 bp read 2).
//   Expected: PD1-CD3 and CD3-CD3 enriched in Jurkat cluster;
//   ICAM1-HLADR and HLADR-HLADR enriched in Raji cluster.
//   cellTypeDetection abstracts the t-SNE / PCA clustering
//   step confirming cell-type segregation (Fig. 1e-j).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellTypeSignal  = detect cellTypeDetection on dropsEquenced for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Cell-type PLA QC gate
// Pass (BB2): cellTypeSignal > 0 -> Jurkat and Raji clusters
//             correctly identified by PLA products; dispose.
// Fail (BB3): cellTypeSignal <= 0 -> no cell-type separation
//             in PLA space; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (cellTypeJoin).
// ============================================================

if (cellTypeSignal > 0) {
    dispose dropsEquenced
} else {
    drain dropsEquenced
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: cellTypeJoin
// Dispose cell-type QC signal. Control falls into PBMC
// 38-marker plate-based Prox-seq arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose cellTypeSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 1: Prepare PBMCs.
//   1 million rested PBMCs collected, all centrifugation at
//   300g/3 min. Resuspend in 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS; pellet.
//   Resuspend in Fc blocker: 95 uL 1% BSA/PBS + 5 uL
//   TruStain FcX (BioLegend); incubate 5 min RT.
//   All buffers supplemented with 1:1000 RNase inhibitor (NEB).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcCells       = dispense 1 units of PBMCs
fcBlock         = dispense 1 units of FcBlocker_TruStainFcX
rnaseInh        = dispense 1 units of RNaseInhibitor

blockedPBMCs    = mix pbmcCells with fcBlock for 5m
blockedRNase    = mix blockedPBMCs with rnaseInh for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 2: 38-marker probe incubation (PBMC panel).
//   Panel targeting 38 immune cell markers (primary focus: T
//   cell markers; Supplementary Table 3). Measures up to 741
//   unique protein complexes. Antibody cocktail divided into
//   3 serial portions due to volume; each portion incubated
//   37 C for 15 min before adding the next. Total ~45 min.
//   `mix` steps model the three sequential incubation portions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcProbesA     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_A
pbmcProbesB     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_B

pbmcProbesMix   = mix pbmcProbesA with pbmcProbesB for 5s

// Portion 1 (15 min, 37 C).
pbmcPortion1    = mix blockedRNase with pbmcProbesMix for 5s
heat pbmcPortion1 at 37c for 15m

// Portion 2 (15 min, 37 C).
pbmcPortion2    = mix pbmcPortion1 with pbmcProbesMix for 5s
heat pbmcPortion2 at 37c for 15m

// Portion 3 (15 min, 37 C).
pbmcPortion3    = mix pbmcPortion2 with pbmcProbesMix for 5s
heat pbmcPortion3 at 37c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 3: Wash (x3) and ligate.
//   Three washes with 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS (300g, 3 min each).
//   Resuspend in ligation solution (same formulation as ARM 1).
//   Ligate 37 C for 30 min (= 30m).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcWash1       = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
pbmcWash2       = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
pbmcWash3       = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA

pbmcWashed1     = mix pbmcPortion3 with pbmcWash1 for 5s
pbmcWashed2     = mix pbmcWashed1 with pbmcWash2 for 5s
pbmcWashed3     = mix pbmcWashed2 with pbmcWash3 for 5s

pbmcLigBuf      = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer_HEPES
pbmcConnector   = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligomer_IDT
pbmcLigase      = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase_NEB

pbmcLigSol      = mix pbmcLigBuf with pbmcConnector for 5s
pbmcLigSol2     = mix pbmcLigSol with pbmcLigase for 5s
pbmcLigated     = mix pbmcWashed3 with pbmcLigSol2 for 5s

// 30 min ligation at 37 C.
heat pbmcLigated at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 4: Plate-based library prep (Smart-seq2).
//   PI stain added (1 ug/mL final); live PI-negative cells
//   sorted into 96-well plates (1 cell/well) containing 4 uL
//   Smart-seq2 lysis buffer (0.1% Triton X-100, 1 U/uL RNase
//   inhibitor, 2.5 mM dNTPs, 2.5 uM oligodTVN, 2.5 uM
//   oligodTGT). Non-PFA cells stored -80 C until processing.
//   Plates thawed on ice; incubated 72 C/3 min before library
//   prep. 2-4 uL/well used for PLA product pre-amplification,
//   followed by PCR to attach cell indexes and sequencing
//   adaptor. NextSeq Mid-output kit v2.5 (75 bp read 1).
//   `mix` abstracts Smart-seq2 lysis and library capture.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcPI          = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide
pbmcLysisBuffer = dispense 1 units of SmartSeq2_LysisBuffer

pbmcPIStained   = mix pbmcLigated with pbmcPI for 5s
pbmcLibrary     = mix pbmcPIStained with pbmcLysisBuffer for 5s

// Lysis/RT pre-step at 72 C for 3 min.
heat pbmcLibrary at 72c for 3m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 5: Protein complex QC detection.
//   proteinComplexDetection module abstracts the Protein Complex
//   Estimation Algorithm (iterative quadratic solver; Fig. 2a).
//   Algorithm computes expected random PLA count per complex,
//   subtracts background, identifies statistically significant
//   complexes (one-sided t-test, Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted
//   p < 0.05). 37 protein complexes expected from 10x arm
//   (Supplementary Table 4); CD9-CD8 on naive CD8+ T cells
//   is the key novel finding (Fig. 3f, Fig. 4f).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

complexSignal   = detect proteinComplexDetection on pbmcLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Protein complex QC gate
// Pass (BB5): complexSignal > 0 -> protein complexes (incl.
//             CD9-CD8 on naive CD8+ T cells) detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): complexSignal <= 0 -> no significant complexes
//             above random ligation background; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (complexJoin).
// ============================================================

if (complexSignal > 0) {
    dispose pbmcLibrary
} else {
    drain pbmcLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: complexJoin
// Dispose complex QC signal. Control falls into macrophage
// TLR signalling arm (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose complexSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 1: Primary macrophage culture and stimulation.
//   Thawed primary human macrophages (STEMCELL Technologies)
//   plated in 10 wells of a non-tissue-culture 24-well plate.
//   Rested overnight in RPMI + 10% FBS at 37 C.
//   Stimulation: 300g/3 min spin then incubate 5 min / 2 h /
//   12 h with 100 ng/mL LPS (TLR4 agonist), 40 ng/mL Pam2CSK4
//   (TLR2 agonist), or both, in RPMI + 10% FBS.
//   Untreated cells serve as control (10 conditions total:
//   3 ligands x 3 time points + 1 control).
//
//   This BioScript file encodes the 5-minute stimulation arm
//   for LPS, PAM, and both simultaneously -- the time point
//   at which PLA products peak (Fig. 5e). Separate branches
//   share the same fixation and staining procedure.
//
//   NOTE ON FIXATION: Cells are fixed with 4% PFA (15 min RT)
//   AFTER stimulation to preserve receptor interactions at the
//   moment of signalling. The antibody cocktail is applied
//   POST-FIXATION. `heat` at 37 C for 5 min models the
//   stimulation; 25 C for 15 min models PFA fixation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macrophageCells = dispense 1 units of PBMCs
lpsStimulus     = dispense 1 units of LPS_100ngmL
pamStimulus     = dispense 1 units of PAM_40ngmL

// Combined LPS + PAM stimulation (both arm).
stimulusMix     = mix lpsStimulus with pamStimulus for 5s
stimulatedMacro = mix macrophageCells with stimulusMix for 5s

// 5-minute stimulation at 37 C.
heat stimulatedMacro at 37c for 5m

// PFA fixation (4% PFA, room temperature 25 C, 15 min)
// to lock receptor interactions at the stimulation endpoint.
pfaSolution     = dispense 1 units of PFA_4pct
fixedMacro      = mix stimulatedMacro with pfaSolution for 5s
heat fixedMacro at 25c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 2: Fc block and 15-marker TLR probe incubation.
//   Resuspend fixed cells in 95 uL 1% BSA/PBS + 5 uL TruStain
//   FcX (5 min RT). Resuspend in 54 uL 5 nM Prox-seq probes
//   (15-protein NF-kB panel: CD14, CD36, IL-1R, IL-6Ra, IL-8Rb,
//   IL-10R, LBP, MD2, MMP15, MMP16, TGFBR1, TLR1, TLR2, TLR4,
//   TLR6; Supplementary Table 5). Measures up to 225 protein
//   dimers. Incubate 30 min at 37 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macroFcBlock    = dispense 1 units of TruStainFcX
macroBlocked    = mix fixedMacro with macroFcBlock for 5m

tlrProbesA      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_TLR_Panel
tlrProbesB      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_TLR_Panel

tlrProbeMix     = mix tlrProbesA with tlrProbesB for 5s
macroProbed     = mix macroBlocked with tlrProbeMix for 5s

// 30 min probe incubation at 37 C.
heat macroProbed at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 3: Wash (x3) and ligate TLR PLA products.
//   Three washes with 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS (300g, 3 min each).
//   Resuspend in ligation solution and incubate 37 C for 30 min.
//   Fixed cells use modified Smart-seq2 lysis buffer (0.1%
//   Triton X-100, 1000 U/mL RNase inhibitor, 20 U/mL proteinase
//   K, 2.5 mM dNTPs, 2.5 uM oligodTVN, 2.5 uM oligodTGT in
//   TE buffer) sorted into 96-well plates.
//   Plates incubated 56 C / 1 h then 95 C / 10 min before
//   storage at -80 C. Library prep same as ARM 2.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macroWash1      = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
macroWash2      = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
macroWash3      = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA

macroWashed1    = mix macroProbed with macroWash1 for 5s
macroWashed2    = mix macroWashed1 with macroWash2 for 5s
macroWashed3    = mix macroWashed2 with macroWash3 for 5s

tlrLigBuf       = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer_TLR
tlrConnector    = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligomer_IDT
tlrLigase       = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase_NEB

tlrLigSol       = mix tlrLigBuf with tlrConnector for 5s
tlrLigSol2      = mix tlrLigSol with tlrLigase for 5s
macroLigated    = mix macroWashed3 with tlrLigSol2 for 5s

// 30 min ligation at 37 C.
heat macroLigated at 37c for 30m

// Fixed-cell plate sorting protocol:
// Sorted into plates; 56 C for 60 min then 95 C for 10 min.
macroLysisBuffer = dispense 1 units of SmartSeq2_LysisBuffer
macroPlated     = mix macroLigated with macroLysisBuffer for 5s

// 56 C / 60 min proteinase K digestion step.
heat macroPlated at 56c for 60m

// 95 C / 10 min to inactivate proteinase K.
heat macroPlated at 95c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 4: Macrophage TLR signalling QC detection.
//   macrophageSignalDetection module abstracts the logistic
//   regression classifier trained on PLA product levels at
//   the 2-h time point (AUC = 0.82 +/- 0.08; Fig. 6a/b).
//   Key classifier feature: TLR2-TLR2 PLA product (highest
//   logistic regression coefficient for LPS-like response;
//   Fig. 6b). The module also captures the CD36 co-receptor
//   rearrangement observable at 5 min post-LPS (Fig. 6c/d/e).
//   Additive integration of LPS and PAM signals confirmed
//   (non-synergistic; Fig. 5e/f).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macrophageSignal = detect macrophageSignalDetection on macroPlated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Macrophage TLR signalling QC gate
// Pass (BB8): macrophageSignal > 0 -> TLR2-TLR2 and CD36
//             complexes detected; LPS/PAM-like response
//             classified; dispose stimulated samples.
// Fail (BB9): macrophageSignal <= 0 -> no receptor complex
//             signal above baseline; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (macrophageSignal > 0) {
    dispose macroPlated
} else {
    drain macroPlated
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose macrophage signalling QC signal.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose macrophageSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module nfkbDynamicsDetection
module atacSeqDetection
module rnaSeqDetection

manifest BoneMarrowCells
manifest PBS
manifest CompleteMCM
manifest MCSF
manifest Fibronectin
manifest HoechstStain
manifest LPS
manifest TNFa
manifest PolyIC
manifest CpG
manifest PAM2CSK4
manifest IL1b
manifest Accutase
manifest TransposaseReactionMix
manifest ATACLibraryPrimers
manifest NexteraXTKit
manifest RLT_Buffer

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Macrophage memory emerges from coordinated transcription
// factor and chromatin dynamics
// Wang, Son, Gorin et al., Cell Systems 16, 101171 (2025)
// DOI: 10.1016/j.cels.2025.101171
//
// This BioScript file encodes the full experimental protocol:
//   PROTOCOL 1 - Bone-marrow-derived macrophage (BMDM)
//                differentiation and microfluidic device priming.
//   PROTOCOL 2 - Systematic sequential ligand screen (80 conditions)
//                using Ligand A -> Ligand B stimulation on-chip;
//                the polyI:C -> TNF-a arm is encoded as the
//                representative condition (priming arm).
//                The CpG -> TNF-a arm is encoded in parallel
//                (tolerance arm).
//   PROTOCOL 3 - NF-kB dynamics live-cell imaging detection
//                and QC gating (priming vs tolerance).
//   PROTOCOL 4 - ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility profiling
//                following single and sequential stimulation.
//   PROTOCOL 5 - RNA-seq transcriptomic profiling for synergy/
//                antagonism classification.
//
// NOTE ON TIMING CONVENTIONS:
//   BioScript duration tokens are s (seconds) and m (minutes).
//   Hours are converted to minutes (e.g., 4h = 240m, 8h = 480m,
//   48h = 2880m, 7 days = 10080m).
//
// NOTE ON MICROFLUIDIC ABSTRACTION:
//   `mix` operations abstract channel-flow and electrode-driven
//   mixing events inside the 64-chamber microfluidic device
//   (PDMS multilayer; 14-input programmable pneumatic valve
//   control). No DMF electrode merging is implied.
//   `heat` statements model TEC or incubator actuation at the
//   stated temperature for the stated duration.
//
// NOTE ON SCOPE:
//   The systematic 80-condition ligand screen (Figures 1-3)
//   is represented here by two representative sequential-stimulus
//   arms: polyI:C -> TNFa (priming) and CpG -> TNFa (tolerance).
//   All other ligand identity / dose / duration combinations
//   follow the same structural pattern and would each require
//   a separate .bs file or parameterised extension.
//
// FIXES APPLIED (v2 -- post IR/DOT review):
//   FIX #1: Removed `module viabilityDetection` -- declared but
//           never referenced in any detect call; dead code that
//           may cause module-resolution warnings in strict mode.
//   FIX #2: Removed `manifest TrizolReagent` -- declared but
//           never referenced in any dispense call; dead manifest.
//   FIX #3: Split `deviceWithCells` into `deviceWithCells_arm1`
//           and `deviceWithCells_arm2` so that the priming arm
//           (polyI:C -> TNFa) and the tolerance arm (CpG -> TNFa)
//           each consume a distinct variable. The original code
//           caused both stimulatedArmA and stimulatedCpgA to mix
//           from the same deviceWithCells1[0] in the IR, which is
//           a double-consumption and will fail under stricter
//           compiler modes. Each arm now has its own independent
//           cell-loading variable reflecting the separate physical
//           chamber sets on the 64-chamber device.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                -- BMDM differentiation, device priming,
//                               cell loading
//   BB2  primingPass         -- nfkbPrimingSignal > 0: priming detected
//                               (polyI:C -> TNFa); dispose and continue
//   BB3  primingFail         -- nfkbPrimingSignal <= 0: no priming;
//                               drain stimulated cells
//   BB4  stimJoin            -- join: ATAC-seq branch begins
//   BB5  atacPass            -- atacSignal > 0: valid accessible
//                               chromatin peaks; dispose and continue
//   BB6  atacFail            -- atacSignal <= 0: library prep failed;
//                               drain nuclei lysate
//   BB7  atacJoin            -- join: RNA-seq branch begins
//   BB8  rnaSeqPass          -- rnaSignal > 0: valid transcriptomic
//                               data; dispose and end
//   BB9  rnaSeqFail          -- rnaSignal <= 0: low-quality library;
//                               drain RNA lysate
//   BB10 finalCleanup        -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 1: Isolate bone marrow cells from femurs
//   and tibias of 6-12 week old male/female RelA(mVenus/mVenus)
//   (RelA^V/V) C57BL/6J transgenic mice.
//   Cells are cultured in Complete Macrophage Culture Media
//   (RPMI + 10% FBS + 1% P/S + 1% NEAA + 1% HEPES + 1%
//   sodium pyruvate + 1% L-glutamine + 0.1% b-mercaptoethanol)
//   supplemented with 20 ng/mL recombinant murine m-CSF
//   for 7-9 days to drive macrophage differentiation.
//   Fed on Days 2, 4, and 6 with fresh supplemented media.
//   7-9 day differentiation = 10080-12960 min. 7 days used here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

boneMarrow      = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
baseMCM         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf1           = dispense 1 units of MCSF

// Initial culture seeding
cultureMedia_D0 = mix baseMCM with mcsf1 for 5s
seededCulture   = mix boneMarrow with cultureMedia_D0 for 2m

// Day 2 feed
mcm_D2          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf_D2         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
feed_D2         = mix mcm_D2 with mcsf_D2 for 5s
culture_D2      = mix seededCulture with feed_D2 for 2880m

// Day 4 feed
mcm_D4          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf_D4         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
feed_D4         = mix mcm_D4 with mcsf_D4 for 5s
culture_D4      = mix culture_D2 with feed_D4 for 2880m

// Day 6 feed
mcm_D6          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf_D6         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
feed_D6         = mix mcm_D6 with mcsf_D6 for 5s
culture_D6      = mix culture_D4 with feed_D6 for 2880m

// Day 7-9: lift adherent BMDMs with 10 mM EDTA in PBS,
// wash and resuspend at 10^7 cells/mL in phenol-red-free RPMI
// for loading into microfluidic device. Modelled as 1440 min
// (Day 7 lift, 1 additional day of rest post-lift before use).
lift_PBS        = dispense 1 units of PBS
matureBMDMs     = mix culture_D6 with lift_PBS for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 2: Microfluidic device preparation.
//   PDMS multilayer device (64 cell-culture chambers, 14 inputs).
//   Coat chambers overnight with 0.2-0.4 mg/mL fibronectin in
//   PBS to promote cell adhesion. Flush with complete media.
//   Mounted on Nikon Ti2 epifluorescence microscope, live-
//   imaging apparatus set to 37 C / 5% CO2 / 98% humidity.
//   `mix` abstracts fibronectin coating and chamber flush.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinSoln  = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
primingPBS       = dispense 1 units of PBS
deviceCoating    = mix fibronectinSoln with primingPBS for 480m

flushMedia       = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
devicePrimed     = mix deviceCoating with flushMedia for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 3: Load BMDMs onto microfluidic device.
//   Cells loaded at 10^7/mL in phenol-red-free RPMI. Nuclei
//   stained with 1 uM Hoechst 33342 for 5 min, washed,
//   then allowed to adhere. Imaged at 6-min intervals,
//   20x magnification (mVenus: 508 nm, 1 s; Hoechst: 395 nm,
//   50 ms; Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash4.0 V2 camera).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hoechstStain     = dispense 1 units of HoechstStain
stainedBMDMs     = mix matureBMDMs with hoechstStain for 5m

washPBS          = dispense 1 units of PBS
loadedCells      = mix stainedBMDMs with washPBS for 2s

// FIX #3: Split into two independent device-with-cells variables
// so that Arm 1 (polyI:C -> TNFa) and Arm 2 (CpG -> TNFa) each
// consume a distinct variable. Both map to separate physical
// chamber sets on the 64-chamber microfluidic device.
// Using the same variable for both arms causes the compiler to
// see a double-consumption of deviceWithCells1[0] in the IR,
// which may trigger a use-after-consume error in stricter
// compilation modes.
deviceWithCells_arm1 = mix loadedCells with devicePrimed for 30m

// Arm 2 requires an independent device loading from the same
// cell and device preparation. Fresh dispense of cells and
// primed device modelled as a second parallel load.
loadedCells2         = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
devicePrimed2        = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
deviceWithCells_arm2 = mix loadedCells2 with devicePrimed2 for 30m

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2 - Sequential Ligand Stimulation Screen
// Representative Arm 1: polyI:C -> TNF-a (PRIMING arm)
//   polyI:C activates TLR3/TRIF pathway; primes NF-kB response
//   to subsequent TNF-a stimulation.
//   Ligand A: polyI:C (100-1000 ng/mL); encoded at 300 ng/mL
//             (highest priming dose, Fig 1F/2A/2C).
//             Duration: 4 hours (240 min) of Ligand A.
//   Ligand B: TNF-a (10 ng/mL); duration 4 hours (240 min).
//   Total imaging window: 480 min per cell condition.
//   >300 individual cells tracked per condition.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 4 (Arm 1): Dispense and deliver
//   Ligand A = polyI:C (300 ng/mL in complete media + m-CSF).
//   Delivered via PEEK tubing at 4 psi to minimise shearing.
//   Each microfluidic experiment includes positive controls
//   (media -> 10 ng/mL TNF-a; media -> 1 ng/mL LPS) and a
//   negative control (complete media only).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

polyIC_LigA      = dispense 1 units of PolyIC
mcm_LigA         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
polyIC_Stimulus  = mix polyIC_LigA with mcm_LigA for 5s

// Stimulate cells with polyI:C for 4 h (240 min) on-chip.
// `mix` abstracts pneumatic valve-driven channel perfusion.
stimulatedArmA   = mix deviceWithCells_arm1 with polyIC_Stimulus for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 5 (Arm 1): Switch to Ligand B = TNF-a
//   (10 ng/mL in complete media + m-CSF) after 4 h of Ligand A.
//   Ligand A is aspirated; Ligand B delivered via same channel.
//   NF-kB nuclear translocation (RelA-mVenus nuclear/cytoplasmic
//   ratio) tracked during the entire Ligand B window (240 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

TNFa_LigB        = dispense 1 units of TNFa
mcm_LigB         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
TNFa_Stimulus    = mix TNFa_LigB with mcm_LigB for 5s

// Stimulate with TNF-a for 4 h (240 min) post-polyI:C.
stimulatedArmB   = mix stimulatedArmA with TNFa_Stimulus for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 6 (Arm 2): CpG -> TNF-a (TOLERANCE arm)
//   CpG activates TLR9/MyD88 pathway; tolerises NF-kB response
//   to subsequent TNF-a stimulation.
//   Ligand A: CpG (100 nM = highest tolerising dose; Fig 1E).
//   Duration: 4 hours (240 min).
//   Ligand B: TNF-a (10 ng/mL); duration 4 hours (240 min).
//   Parallel run on separate device chambers (independent
//   sample; same BioScript run models parallel chambers).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

CpG_LigA         = dispense 1 units of CpG
mcm_CpG          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
CpG_Stimulus     = mix CpG_LigA with mcm_CpG for 5s

// Arm 2 now consumes deviceWithCells_arm2 (not arm1).
stimulatedCpgA   = mix deviceWithCells_arm2 with CpG_Stimulus for 240m

TNFa_LigB2       = dispense 1 units of TNFa
mcm_LigB2        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
TNFa_Stimulus2   = mix TNFa_LigB2 with mcm_LigB2 for 5s

stimulatedCpgB   = mix stimulatedCpgA with TNFa_Stimulus2 for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 7: Live-cell NF-kB dynamics detection.
//   nfkbDynamicsDetection module abstracts:
//     - Single-cell nuclear segmentation (Hoechst channel).
//     - RelA-mVenus nuclear/cytoplasmic (Nuc/Cyto) ratio
//       calculation every 6 min over 480 min total.
//     - AUC (trapezoidal) and maximum amplitude extraction.
//     - Normalisation to naive Ligand B AUC (AUC_0).
//     - Mutual information analysis (20-point dynamic vector)
//       using Jetka et al. (2019) PLOS Comp Biol method.
//   QC gate: normalised AUC > 1 = priming; < 1 = tolerance.
//   >300 cells per condition; two independent preparations.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Detect NF-kB dynamics for the priming arm (polyI:C -> TNFa).
nfkbPrimingSignal = detect nfkbDynamicsDetection on stimulatedArmB for 240m

// Detect NF-kB dynamics for the tolerance arm (CpG -> TNFa).
nfkbToleranceSignal = detect nfkbDynamicsDetection on stimulatedCpgB for 240m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: NF-kB dynamics QC gate (priming arm)
// Pass (BB2): nfkbPrimingSignal > 0 -> priming confirmed
//             (normalised AUC > naive); dispose stimulated cells.
// Fail (BB3): nfkbPrimingSignal <= 0 -> priming not detected;
//             drain stimulated cells (re-stimulate off-protocol).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (stimJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nfkbPrimingSignal > 0) {
    dispose stimulatedArmB
} else {
    drain stimulatedArmB
}

// Dispose tolerance arm stimulated cells after detection
// (tolerance QC is encoded implicitly; CpG data used in
// ATAC/RNA-seq branches below regardless of NF-kB outcome
// as paper uses four representative conditions for seq.)
dispose stimulatedCpgB

// ============================================================
// BB4: stimJoin
// Dispose NF-kB QC signal droplets. Control falls into
// ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility profiling branch.
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbPrimingSignal
dispose nfkbToleranceSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 4 - ATAC-seq Chromatin Accessibility Profiling
//   BMDMs replated at 7.5e5 cells/well in 6-well plates (Day 7).
//   Stimulated: LPS (1 ng/mL), CpG (100 nM), polyI:C (1 ug/mL),
//   TNF-a (10 ng/mL) -- single stimulus conditions.
//   Sequential: polyI:C/CpG -> TNF-a/LPS (4 h each).
//   Cells lifted with Accutase + gentle scraping; 5e4 cells used.
//   ATAC performed using Buenrostro et al. (2013) Nat Methods
//   protocol: cold lysis buffer -> transposase reaction (30 min,
//   37 C, 800 rpm shaking) -> MinElute purification ->
//   PCR amplification (Nextera primers) -> NovaSeq SP (50 bp PE).
//   Alignment: bowtie2 (mm10, MAPQ>30); deduplication: Picard;
//   peak calling: MACS3 (FDR 0.01, BAMPE, mm genome, nomodel);
//   motif enrichment: monaLisa / JASPAR2022.
//
// Here the ATAC protocol is encoded for the representative
// polyI:C single-stimulus condition. The same block structure
// applies to CpG, LPS, TNF-a, and sequential conditions.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 8: Plate BMDMs for ATAC-seq.
//   Fresh matureBMDMs dispense into well plates for replating.
//   Overnight rest in complete media + m-CSF before stimulation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

atacBMDMs        = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
atacMedia        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
atacMCSF         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
atacCultureMix   = mix atacMedia with atacMCSF for 5s
atacPlated       = mix atacBMDMs with atacCultureMix for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 9: Single-stimulus ATAC-seq condition.
//   polyI:C (1 ug/mL) for 4 h (240 min). One representative
//   condition; paper runs all six ligands in parallel.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

polyIC_ATAC      = dispense 1 units of PolyIC
atacMediaPIC     = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
polyIC_ATACStim  = mix polyIC_ATAC with atacMediaPIC for 5s

atacStimulated   = mix atacPlated with polyIC_ATACStim for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 10: Cell lysis and nuclei isolation.
//   Cells lifted with Accutase (ThermoFisher) + gentle scraping.
//   5e4 cells pelleted; lysed in cold lysis buffer
//   (10 mM Tris-HCl pH 7.5, 3 mM MgCl2, 10 mM NaCl,
//   0.1% IGEPAL CA-630). Centrifuge 10 min, 500 x g.
//   `mix` abstracts Accutase lift, lysis, and centrifugation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

accutase         = dispense 1 units of Accutase
liftedCells      = mix atacStimulated with accutase for 5m

lysisBuffer      = dispense 1 units of PBS
// PBS here abstracts the cold lysis buffer composition.
// lysis on ice for 3 min (cold step modelled as 4 C, 3 min).
nucleiLysate     = mix liftedCells with lysisBuffer for 3m
heat nucleiLysate at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 11: Transposase reaction.
//   Nuclei resuspended in transposase mix (25 uL 2X TD Buffer
//   + 2.5 uL TD Enzyme 1 [Illumina] + 22.5 uL nuclease-free
//   water). Incubated 30 min at 37 C, 800 rpm shaker.
//   Abstracted as heat at 37 C for 30 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

transposaseMix   = dispense 1 units of TransposaseReactionMix
tagmentedDNA     = mix nucleiLysate with transposaseMix for 5s
heat tagmentedDNA at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 12: PCR amplification and library prep.
//   Purified with MinElute kit (Qiagen). Amplified with Nextera
//   XT sequencing primers. Libraries pooled and sequenced on
//   Illumina NovaSeq SP (50 bp paired-end).
//   Modelled as mix (primer addition) + heat (PCR cycles).
//   PCR: 72 C 5 min initial extension, then 98 C 30s /
//   63 C 30s / 72 C 1 min for n cycles. 12 cycles typical.
//   Simplified here as 37c (post-PCR hold) for 30m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

atacPrimers      = dispense 1 units of ATACLibraryPrimers
atacLibrary      = mix tagmentedDNA with atacPrimers for 5s
heat atacLibrary at 72c for 30m

// ATAC-seq detection: atacSeqDetection module abstracts
// bowtie2 alignment, MACS3 peak calling, monaLisa motif
// enrichment, and edgeR/limma differential accessibility.
// QC: detects valid open chromatin peaks above noise.
atacSignal       = detect atacSeqDetection on atacLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: ATAC-seq QC gate
// Pass (BB5): atacSignal > 0 -> valid chromatin accessibility
//             peaks detected; dispose library and continue.
// Fail (BB6): atacSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed (low
//             signal-to-noise or alignment failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (atacJoin).
// ============================================================

if (atacSignal > 0) {
    dispose atacLibrary
} else {
    drain atacLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: atacJoin
// Dispose ATAC-seq QC signal. Control falls into RNA-seq
// transcriptomic profiling branch.
// ============================================================

dispose atacSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 5 - RNA-seq Transcriptomic Profiling
//   BMDMs replated at 1.5e5 cells/well in 24-well plates.
//   Four representative sequential-stimulus conditions:
//     polyI:C -> TNF-a  (priming)
//     CpG     -> TNF-a  (tolerance)
//     polyI:C -> LPS    (priming)
//     CpG     -> LPS    (tolerance)
//   Each: Ligand A 4 h (240 min) -> aspirate -> Ligand B 4 h
//   (240 min) -> aspirate -> RLT lysis.
//   RNA extraction: Dynabeads (Invitrogen); RT: Maxima HMinus
//   with poly-dT oligo + template-switching oligo; 2nd strand
//   synthesis with KAPA HiFi; Nextera XT library prep;
//   mean fragment size 400-600 bp; NextSeq550 (Illumina).
//   Alignment: STAR (GRCm38); quantification: featureCounts;
//   DEG: edgeR + limma (FDR < 0.01, FC > 1 vs naive).
//   Synergy/antagonism: DAB_memory formula vs null hypothesis.
//
// Encoded here: polyI:C -> TNF-a arm as representative.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 13: Plate BMDMs for RNA-seq.
//   Overnight rest in 24-well plate, complete media + m-CSF.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rnaBMDMs         = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
rnaMedia         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
rnaMCSF          = dispense 1 units of MCSF
rnaCultureMix    = mix rnaMedia with rnaMCSF for 5s
rnaPlated        = mix rnaBMDMs with rnaCultureMix for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 14: Stimulus A application (polyI:C,
//   4 h at 37 C, 5% CO2).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

polyIC_RNA       = dispense 1 units of PolyIC
rnaMediaA        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
polyIC_RNAStim   = mix polyIC_RNA with rnaMediaA for 5s
rnaStimA         = mix rnaPlated with polyIC_RNAStim for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 15: Aspirate Ligand A; apply Ligand B
//   (TNF-a, 10 ng/mL in complete media + m-CSF) for 4 h.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

TNFa_RNA         = dispense 1 units of TNFa
rnaMediaB        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
TNFa_RNAStim     = mix TNFa_RNA with rnaMediaB for 5s
rnaStimB         = mix rnaStimA with TNFa_RNAStim for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 16: Cell lysis and RNA extraction.
//   Aspirate Ligand B; lyse cells in RLT buffer + 1%
//   b-mercaptoethanol. RNA extracted using Dynabeads.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rltBuffer        = dispense 1 units of RLT_Buffer
rnaLysate        = mix rnaStimB with rltBuffer for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 17: Reverse transcription and library prep.
//   RT with Maxima HMinus + poly-dT oligo + TSO.
//   2nd strand with KAPA HiFi.
//   Nextera XT library preparation; NextSeq550 sequencing.
//   Modelled as heat (RT step: 55 C for 60 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nextXTKit        = dispense 1 units of NexteraXTKit
rnaLibrary       = mix rnaLysate with nextXTKit for 60m
heat rnaLibrary at 55c for 60m

// RNA-seq detection: rnaSeqDetection module abstracts
// STAR alignment, featureCounts quantification, edgeR/limma
// DE analysis, and synergy/antagonism classification using
// DAB_memory formula (threshold: +/-25% vs null hypothesis).
// QC: detects valid mapped library with adequate read depth.
rnaSignal        = detect rnaSeqDetection on rnaLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: RNA-seq QC gate
// Pass (BB8): rnaSignal > 0 -> valid transcriptomic library
//             detected (adequate read depth, alignment rate);
//             dispose library, proceed to final cleanup.
// Fail (BB9): rnaSignal <= 0 -> degraded RNA or library
//             failure (low RIN or low mapping rate); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rnaSignal > 0) {
    dispose rnaLibrary
} else {
    drain rnaLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal variables.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose rnaSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module iefFocusingDetection
module cgeDetection

manifest Ampholyte_3_10
manifest GlycerolMethylcellulose
manifest GFP_Sample
manifest OvalSample
manifest LDLPSample
manifest TrypsinInhibitorSample
manifest AcrylamideCoating
manifest AnolyteSolution
manifest CatholyteSolution
manifest CGE_GelBuffer
manifest CZE_Buffer

// ============================================================
// Two-Dimensional Protein Separation with Advanced Sample and
// Buffer Isolation Using Microfluidic Valves
// Wang, Choi, Han - Anal. Chem. 2004, 76, 4426-4431
// DOI: 10.1021/ac0497499
//
// Platform: Double-layer PDMS microfluidic chip with
// pneumatic monolith valves (Unger et al., Science 2000).
// Separation channels: 150 um wide, 12 um high. IEF channel:
// 10 mm. CE channel: 25 mm. Peak transfer region: 3 mm.
// Control channels: 300 um wide, 50 um high (5 mm thick PDMS).
// Substrate: poly(dimethylsiloxane) (PDMS) on flat glass.
//
// Objective: Integrate IEF (charge-based, 1st dimension) with
// CGE or CZE (size/charge-based, 2nd dimension) using active
// microvalve control to prevent buffer interdiffusion between
// incompatible separation media (ampholyte vs. CE buffer).
//
// Samples (labeled with fluorescein or Alexa Fluor 488):
//   GFP            (pI 5.6, MW 26 kDa)
//   Ovalbumin      (pI 5.1, MW 45 kDa)
//   LDL Protein    (pI 5.11, MW 179 kDa)
//   Trypsin Inhib. (pI 4.6, MW 20 kDa)
// IEF sample: 3-10 ampholyte + 1% methylcellulose + 10%
// glycerol + aqueous labeled proteins.
//
// This file encodes the IEF-CGE 2D separation arm (Figure 3/4
// in the paper) as the primary representative experiment.
// The IEF-CZE arm follows an identical four-step procedure
// with CGE_GelBuffer replaced by CZE_Buffer and a 250 V/cm
// field in the second dimension; it is noted in comments below
// but not separately encoded. See paper Section "IEF Coupled
// with Second-Dimension Capillary Zone Electrophoresis."
//
// NOTE ON PLATFORM COMPATIBILITY: This is a continuous-flow
// pressure-driven + electrokinetic chip, not a DMF/EWOD device.
// BioScript `mix` abstracts pressure-driven injection and
// electrokinetic buffer loading steps. `heat` abstracts
// electric field application (IEF focusing, CGE/CE separation)
// because BioScript has no native electrokinetic primitive.
// `detect` abstracts fluorescence microscopy readout
// (inverted epi-fluorescence, FITC filter, CCD camera,
// IPLab 3.6 at 1 frame/s).
//
// NOTE ON SURFACE PASSIVATION: The chip requires a static
// polyacrylamide coating (via 3-(trimethoxysilyl)propyl
// methacrylate adhesion promoter) followed by dynamic 0.5%
// methylcellulose coating before use. This is modelled as a
// dispense + heat step at 25 C for 30 min (polymerization
// under N2 purge in vacuum chamber). This is a one-time chip
// preparation step; it does not consume a droplet in the
// electrophoretic sense, but must appear before loading to
// satisfy fluid variable ownership rules.
//
// NOTE ON VALVE ACTUATION: Pneumatic valves are controlled by
// 80 psi pressure on the top control layer. Closing right
// valves (3,4) isolates the IEF channel from the CGE channel;
// closing left valves (1,2) traps the peak transfer region.
// BioScript has no native valve primitive; valve state changes
// are abstracted as mix steps transitioning between separation
// phases (loading, isolation, transfer). Dead volume at peak
// transfer region: 0.1 nL (smaller than commercial valves).
//
// NOTE ON h DURATION TOKEN: BioScript (lilott8 compiler)
// supports only `s` and `m` duration tokens. All durations
// are expressed in seconds (s) or minutes (m).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- chip prep, IEF buffer loading,
//                           sample loading, IEF focusing,
//                           peak isolation by valve closure
//   BB2  iefPass         -- iefSignal > 0: focused peaks
//                           detected in transfer region;
//                           dispose and proceed to CGE
//   BB3  iefFail         -- iefSignal <= 0: focusing failed
//                           (EOF too high or no peaks); drain
//   BB4  iefJoin         -- join: CGE separation branch begins
//   BB5  cgePass         -- cgeSignal > 0: proteins separated
//                           in 2nd dimension; dispose all
//   BB6  cgeFail         -- cgeSignal <= 0: no CGE signal; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup    -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Surface passivation - static polyacrylamide coating.
//   Coat PDMS channel with 3-(trimethoxysilyl)propyl
//   methacrylate adhesion promoter, then introduce acrylamide
//   + TEMED + APS solution under N2 purge (5 psi vacuum) for
//   30 min at 25 C to grow polyacrylamide polymer on surface.
//   Followed by 0.5% methylcellulose dynamic coating.
//   Modelled as heat at 25 C for 30 min (polymerization step).
//   `mix` abstracts the introduction of coating solution into
//   the microfluidic channel via pressure-driven flow.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

coatingBase   = dispense 1 units of AcrylamideCoating
viscosityAdd  = dispense 1 units of GlycerolMethylcellulose
coatingMix    = mix coatingBase with viscosityAdd for 5s

// Polymerization under N2 purge, 25 C, 30 min.
heat coatingMix at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Load CGE gel buffer into the second-dimension channel.
//   Right valves (3, 4) are closed first (80 psi) to isolate
//   the IEF channel. CGE gel buffer: SDS 14-200 (90% SDS
//   14-200 gel buffer + 1% methylcellulose) injected at
//   20-30 psi into the CE channel without contaminating the
//   IEF channel. Up to 60 psi can be applied without
//   breaking valve seal. Modelled as dispense + mix
//   abstracting pressure-driven injection into the CE channel.
//   (Paper Figure 1b: CE media loading step)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cgeGelBuffer  = dispense 1 units of CGE_GelBuffer
gelLoadedChannel = mix coatingMix with cgeGelBuffer for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Prepare IEF sample mixture.
//   IEF sample: 3-10 ampholyte (Beckman Coulter) + 10%
//   glycerol + 1% methylcellulose + labeled protein samples.
//   1% methylcellulose suppresses electroosmotic flow (EOF)
//   to keep focused peaks stable in the 10 mm IEF channel.
//   Four proteins loaded simultaneously.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ampholyteMix  = dispense 1 units of Ampholyte_3_10
glycerolMC    = dispense 1 units of GlycerolMethylcellulose

iefBase       = mix ampholyteMix with glycerolMC for 5s

gfpSample     = dispense 1 units of GFP_Sample
ovalSample    = dispense 1 units of OvalSample
ldlpSample    = dispense 1 units of LDLPSample
tiSample      = dispense 1 units of TrypsinInhibitorSample

// Combine all four labeled proteins into the ampholyte carrier.
sampleMix1    = mix gfpSample with ovalSample for 5s
sampleMix2    = mix ldlpSample with tiSample for 5s
proteinPool   = mix sampleMix1 with sampleMix2 for 5s

iefSample     = mix iefBase with proteinPool for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Load IEF sample + replace reservoir buffers.
//   Left valves (1, 2) closed (80 psi) to isolate CGE gel.
//   Right valves (3, 4) opened. Ampholyte-sample mixture
//   injected into the 10 mm IEF channel at low pressure.
//   Reservoir solutions then replaced: anolyte (0.1 M acetic
//   acid, pH 2.5) at anode end; catholyte (0.5% ammonium
//   hydroxide, pH 10.5) at cathode end.
//   (Paper Figure 1c: IEF ampholyte mixture loading step)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

anolyte       = dispense 1 units of AnolyteSolution
catholyte     = dispense 1 units of CatholyteSolution

// Buffer replacement at reservoirs modelled as mix.
anolyteLoad   = mix iefSample with anolyte for 5s
iefChannel    = mix anolyteLoad with catholyte for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: IEF focusing (1st dimension).
//   500 V/cm applied across 10 mm IEF channel (total: 500 V).
//   Proteins focus to stationary bands at their pI under the
//   pH 3-10 gradient. Focusing equilibration: < 30 s (2 orders
//   of magnitude faster than CIEF in 25-50 cm capillaries).
//   EOF mobilizes focused peaks slowly from anode to cathode.
//   IEF steady state confirmed by monitoring current.
//   Modelled as heat at 37 C for 130 s (electric field applied
//   130 s per paper Figure 3a caption; temperature abstraction
//   encodes field-driven step duration).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat iefChannel at 37c for 130s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Fluorescence detection - IEF peak verification.
//   Inverted epi-fluorescence microscope (Olympus, FITC filter,
//   100 W Hg lamp). CCD camera (Cooke Co., 1 frame/s).
//   Verify that protein peaks (GFP pI 5.6, Oval pI 5.1,
//   LDLP pI 5.11, TI pI 4.6) are resolved in IEF channel
//   and have entered the 3 mm peak transfer region.
//   iefFocusingDetection module abstracts fluorescence imaging
//   and peak position verification.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

iefSignal = detect iefFocusingDetection on iefChannel for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: IEF focusing QC gate
// Pass (BB2): iefSignal > 0 -> peaks detected in transfer
//             region; proceed to peak isolation and CGE.
// Fail (BB3): iefSignal <= 0 -> focusing failed (EOF too
//             high, no gradient, or no peaks in transfer
//             region); drain channel contents.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (iefJoin).
// ============================================================

if (iefSignal > 0) {
    dispose iefChannel
} else {
    drain iefChannel
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: iefJoin
// Dispose IEF QC signal. Control falls into CGE separation
// branch (BB5/BB6). Peak transfer region now holds isolated
// protein band(s) trapped by closed valve sets.
// ============================================================

dispose iefSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Peak isolation by valve closure.
//   After 130 s of IEF focusing, target protein peaks have
//   entered the 3 mm peak transfer region. Both valve sets
//   (1,2 and 3,4) are closed at 80 psi to physically isolate
//   the peak transfer region from both the IEF channel and
//   the CGE channel. Isolation resistance: > 1000 MOhm at
//   100 psi; no protein intercontamination observed after
//   30 min. Dead volume: 0.1 nL.
//   Modelled as dispense of isolated peak region (re-entry
//   of isolated fluid into BioScript variable scope).
//   (Paper Figure 1d: isolation of target proteins)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

isolatedPeaks = dispense 1 units of GFP_Sample

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Buffer equilibration before CGE field application.
//   Left valves (1, 2) opened. CGE buffer ions allowed to
//   diffuse into the peak transfer region for 30 s to prevent
//   abrupt conductivity jump at the buffer boundary. Protein
//   diffusion is slow (large molecules) relative to buffer
//   ion diffusion; this step does not degrade IEF resolution.
//   Small-MW ampholyte molecules co-isolated with proteins
//   will be rapidly eluted by electrophoresis (lower MW).
//   (Paper Figure 1e and 3b: 30 s equilibration period)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cgeEquil     = dispense 1 units of CGE_GelBuffer
equilibrated = mix isolatedPeaks with cgeEquil for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: CGE separation (2nd dimension).
//   250 V/cm applied across the 25 mm CE channel (total:
//   625 V). Proteins entering the high-conductivity CGE gel
//   buffer from the low-conductivity ampholyte stacking zone
//   experience sample stacking at the boundary: sudden
//   decrease in electrophoretic velocity creates a band-
//   narrowing effect. Stacking makes 1st and 2nd dimension
//   separations independent (Figure 5, paper).
//   Separation basis: charge-to-mass ratio (non-denaturing
//   CGE, no SDS). Ovalbumin (45 kDa) has higher mobility
//   than GFP (26 kDa) due to higher charge-to-mass ratio
//   (ovalbumin mu = -1.3e4 cm2/V.s; GFP mu = -1.0e4 cm2/V.s).
//   Full 2D separation achieved within 10 min total.
//   Modelled as heat at 37 C for 6m (250 V/cm for ~6 min
//   per Figure 4b electropherogram time axis).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat equilibrated at 37c for 6m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Fluorescence detection - CGE readout.
//   Electropherograms acquired at end of 25 mm CGE channel
//   by fluorescence intensity measurement. FITC filter set.
//   CCD camera, 1 frame/s, IPLab 3.6 acquisition.
//   cgeDetection module abstracts fluorescence electropherogram
//   acquisition and peak identification.
//   Expected elution order: Ovalbumin elutes before GFP
//   (higher charge-to-mass ratio, faster mobility).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cgeSignal = detect cgeDetection on equilibrated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: CGE separation QC gate
// Pass (BB5): cgeSignal > 0 -> protein peaks detected in
//             2nd-dimension electropherogram; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): cgeSignal <= 0 -> no CGE signal (stacking
//             failed, valve leak, or detector issue); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (cgeSignal > 0) {
    dispose equilibrated
} else {
    drain equilibrated
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose CGE QC signal droplet. Experiment ends.
// Total protocol time: ~10 min (per paper conclusion).
//
// NOTE ON IEF-CZE ARM: The paper also demonstrates IEF
// coupled with capillary zone electrophoresis (CZE/CE) using
// CZE_Buffer (0.375 M Tris-Cl, pH 8.6, 0.1% methylcellulose)
// instead of CGE_GelBuffer, and 250 V/cm in the 2nd dimension.
// The stacking mechanism still operates (liquid-liquid
// conductivity boundary). The CZE arm is structurally
// identical to the CGE arm above with reagent substitution.
// A separate .bs file should encode the IEF-CZE arm with
// CZE_Buffer substituted for CGE_GelBuffer at Steps 2 and 8.
// ============================================================

dispose cgeSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

