instructions:

// ============================================================
// An Ultra-High-Throughput Spiral Microfluidic Biochip for
// the Enrichment of Circulating Tumor Cells
// Warkiani, Khoo, Tan, Bhagat, Lim, Yap, Lee, Soo,
// Han, Lim -- Analyst, 2014, 139, 3245-3255
// DOI: 10.1039/c4an00355a
//
// Platform: Multiplexed spiral microfluidic biochip
//   (3 stacked single-layer PDMS spiral chips, each with
//   2 inlets and 2 outlets). Fabricated by standard SU-8
//   lithography and PDMS soft lithography (1:10 ratio,
//   cured 80 C, 1-2 h). Device bonded onto a microscopic
//   glass slide by air plasma.
//
// Separation principle: Inertial focusing + Dean drag forces
//   inside rectangular-cross-section spiral microchannels.
//   CTCs (>15 um) equilibrate near inner wall; smaller
//   hematological cells (RBCs, WBCs, platelets, <20 um)
//   migrate to outer wall under Dean vortex influence,
//   enabling label-free, size-based separation at dual outlet.
//
// Key performance metrics:
//   Throughput:   7.5 mL blood in <10 min (multiplexed)
//   Sensitivity:  100% (10/10 patient samples positive)
//   WBC depletion: ~99.99% (from ~7e6 nucleated cells)
//   Purity:       1 CTC per 30-100 WBCs (~4 log depletion)
//   Recovery:     20-135 CTCs/mL (breast and lung patients)
//   Cell viability: >90% (PI staining, <10% dead)
//   Recovery efficiency: 87.6% MCF-7; 76.4% T24 (spiked)
//   Sample flow rate: 350 uL/min; Sheath: 750 uL/min
//   Sample concentration: 2x (7.5 mL -> 3.75 mL)
//
// NOTE ON FLOW ABSTRACTION: `mix` statements abstract
//   continuous-flow microfluidic channel events (cell loading,
//   hydrodynamic focusing, Dean vortex separation) rather than
//   DMF electrode mixing. This is consistent with the
//   abstraction used in samlali_hybrid_microfluidics_isoclone.bs
//   for channel-based trapping and encapsulation events.
//
// NOTE ON RBC LYSIS: Whole blood is lysed with ammonium
//   chloride RBC lysis buffer before on-chip processing.
//   Removes RBCs, concentrates nucleated cells 2x for faster
//   processing. Cell loss not significant (98% recovery,
//   p=0.82). Lysis does not alter cell morphology (p=0.2).
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports s and m only.
//   All paper durations converted accordingly.
//   Overnight hybridization (42 C) approximated as 600m (10 h).
//
// NOTE ON CELL CULTURE PRE-INCUBATION (FIX #8):
//   MCF-7 and T24 cells are cultured in DMEM + 10% FBS +
//   1% pen-strep at 37 C / 5% CO2 until 80% confluence before
//   spiking. Following samlali convention, this is modelled as
//   heat at 37c for 2880m (48 h representative culture period)
//   applied to the cell manifests before resuspension in
//   EDTA_BSA_Buffer. Trypsin/EDTA dissociation is abstracted
//   into the same heat step.
//
// THREE PROTOCOLS encoded in sequence:
//
//   PROTOCOL 1 (BB1-BB4): MCF-7 recovery efficiency experiment.
//     Fresh healthy donor blood -> RBC lysis -> MCF-7 spike
//     -> spiral chip separation -> ctcDetection QC gate.
//     Expected: 87.6% recovery efficiency (Fig. 4A).
//
//   PROTOCOL 2 (BB5-BB8): T24 cell viability experiment.
//     Fresh healthy donor blood (independent from Protocol 1)
//     -> RBC lysis -> T24 spike -> spiral chip separation ->
//     PI staining + pan-CK/CD45 staining -> viabilityDetection
//     QC gate. Expected: <10% PI+ (high viability) (Fig. 4B).
//
//   PROTOCOL 3 (BB9-BB14): Clinical CTC enrichment from
//     patient blood. Fresh clinical blood -> RBC lysis ->
//     spiral chip separation -> PFA fixation -> Triton X-100
//     permeabilization -> IF staining (Pan-CK/CD45/Hoechst) ->
//     ctcDetection QC gate -> HER2 FISH (pass branch only).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- entry: MCF-7 culture, blood prep,
//                           RBC lysis, spike, on-chip separation
//   BB2  mcf7Pass        -- ctcSignal > 0: CTCs recovered, dispose
//   BB3  mcf7Fail        -- ctcSignal <= 0: no CTCs, drain
//   BB4  mcf7Join        -- join: T24 viability protocol begins
//   BB5  viabSep         -- fresh blood, T24 spike, on-chip sep,
//                           fixation, PI + pan-CK/CD45 staining
//   BB6  viabPass        -- viabilitySignal > 0: viable, dispose
//   BB7  viabFail        -- viabilitySignal <= 0: low viab, drain
//   BB8  viabJoin        -- join: clinical protocol begins
//   BB9  clinSep         -- clinical blood, lysis, on-chip sep,
//                           PFA fixation, permeabilization, IF
//   BB10 clinPass        -- clinicalSignal > 0: CTCs detected,
//                           proceed to HER2 FISH
//   BB11 clinFail        -- clinicalSignal <= 0: no CTCs, drain
//   BB12 finalCleanup    -- terminal: dispose QC signal, end
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// PROTOCOL 1 -- MCF-7 spiked recovery efficiency experiment
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Culture MCF-7 cells prior to spiking.
//   MCF-7 (breast adenocarcinoma, HTB-22, ATCC, ~20 um diam.)
//   cultured in high-glucose DMEM + 10% FBS + 1% pen-strep
//   at 37 C / 5% CO2 until 80% confluence. Sub-cultivated
//   1:3 twice a week. Media replaced every 48 h.
//   Dissociated with 0.01% trypsin / 5.3 mM EDTA (Lonza).
//   FIX #8: Cell culture pre-incubation modelled as heat
//   at 37c for 2880m (48 h), consistent with samlali.bs.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mcf7Cells       = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
heat mcf7Cells at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Resuspend MCF-7 in EDTA+BSA buffer.
//   Cells resuspended in PBS + 2 mM EDTA + 0.5% BSA
//   (Miltenyi Biotec, Germany) to prevent non-specific
//   adsorption on tubing and microchannel walls.
//   Spike concentration: 500 cells per 7.5 mL whole blood.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

edtaBsaBuffer   = dispense 1 units of EDTA_BSA_Buffer
mcf7Resuspended = mix mcf7Cells with edtaBsaBuffer for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Prepare healthy donor blood and perform RBC lysis.
//   7.5 mL whole blood collected in Vacutainer EDTA tubes
//   (Becton-Dickinson, NJ, USA). Processed within 2-4 h.
//   Lysed with ammonium chloride RBC lysis buffer (Bioscience,
//   USA) for 5 min at RT under continuous gentle mixing.
//   Centrifuged at 1000xg for 5 min (modelled as heat at 25c).
//   Nucleated cell pellet resuspended in PBS. Concentrated
//   to 3.75 mL (2x) for optimal on-chip WBC input (~14e6).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wholeBlood1     = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood
rbcLysis1       = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
lysedBlood1     = mix wholeBlood1 with rbcLysis1 for 5m

// Centrifugation at 1000xg, 5 min (no centrifuge primitive;
// modelled as heat at 25c for 5m per compiler convention).
heat lysedBlood1 at 25c for 5m

pbs1            = dispense 1 units of PBS
nucleated1      = mix lysedBlood1 with pbs1 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Spike MCF-7 cells into nucleated cell fraction.
//   500 MCF-7 cells spiked into the 7.5 mL nucleated fraction
//   at clinically relevant concentration for recovery testing.
//   MCF-7 and T24 are spiked in separate, independent
//   experiments (not co-spiked). (FIX #2)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spikedMcf7      = mix nucleated1 with mcf7Resuspended for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: On-chip separation -- MCF-7 spiked sample.
//   Nucleated fraction (2x concentrated, 3.75 mL) loaded at
//   sample inlet. PBS sheath fluid at sheath inlet.
//   Sample: 350 uL/min; Sheath: 750 uL/min; ~10 min total.
//   Dean vortex + inertial lift: CTCs to inner wall (CTC
//   outlet); WBCs/RBCs/platelets to outer wall (waste outlet).
//   Enrichment: ~10^4-fold from nucleated cell fraction.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts channel-based hydrodynamic separation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheath1         = dispense 1 units of SheathFluid
mcf7Separated   = mix spikedMcf7 with sheath1 for 10m

ctcSignal       = detect ctcDetection on mcf7Separated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: MCF-7 Recovery QC gate
// Pass (BB2): ctcSignal > 0 -> CTCs recovered at CTC outlet.
//   Expected recovery: 87.6% for MCF-7 at 500 cells/7.5 mL.
//   Identified by pan-CK+/CD45- immunofluorescence (Fig. 4A).
// Fail (BB3): ctcSignal <= 0 -> no CTCs detected; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (mcf7Join).
// ============================================================

if (ctcSignal > 0) {
    dispose mcf7Separated
} else {
    drain mcf7Separated
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: mcf7Join
// Dispose MCF-7 QC signal. T24 viability protocol begins.
// ============================================================

dispose ctcSignal

// ============================================================
// BB5: viabSep
// PROTOCOL 2 -- T24 cell viability experiment
// Independent fresh blood sample; independent T24 culture.
// (FIX #1: T24 viability arm now uses its own WholeBlood
//  dispense and lysis sequence, not nucleated1 from Protocol 1
//  which was already consumed by spikedMcf7.)
// (FIX #2: MCF-7 and T24 are fully independent experiments.)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Culture T24 cells prior to viability spiking.
//   T24 (bladder carcinoma, HTB-4, ATCC, ~30 um diameter).
//   Same culture conditions as MCF-7 (DMEM + 10% FBS +
//   1% pen-strep, 37 C / 5% CO2, 80% confluence).
//   FIX #8: Pre-incubation modelled as heat at 37c for 2880m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

t24Cells        = dispense 1 units of T24_Cells
heat t24Cells at 37c for 2880m

edtaBsa2        = dispense 1 units of EDTA_BSA_Buffer
t24Resuspended  = mix t24Cells with edtaBsa2 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Prepare fresh healthy donor blood for viability arm.
//   Independent 7.5 mL blood sample (separate from Protocol 1).
//   Same RBC lysis and PBS resuspension as STEP 3.
//   A known concentration of T24 cells spiked into whole blood
//   before lysis; T24 counts compared before and after lysis
//   to quantify cell loss incurred by the lysis step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wholeBlood2     = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood
rbcLysis2       = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
lysedBlood2     = mix wholeBlood2 with rbcLysis2 for 5m

heat lysedBlood2 at 25c for 5m

pbs2            = dispense 1 units of PBS
nucleated2      = mix lysedBlood2 with pbs2 for 1m

spikedT24       = mix nucleated2 with t24Resuspended for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: On-chip separation -- T24 spiked viability sample.
//   Same spiral biochip parameters as STEP 5.
//   CTC outlet fraction collected; viability assessed
//   immediately after retrieval.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheath2         = dispense 1 units of SheathFluid
t24Separated    = mix spikedT24 with sheath2 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Viability staining -- PI + pan-CK/CD45 panel.
//   FIX #3: The paper's viability assay uses BOTH PI staining
//   (to identify dead cells, ex 488/em 617 nm) AND pan-CK/CD45
//   IF staining (to confirm recovered cells are cancer cells,
//   not contaminating WBCs). Both reagents are now included.
//   Outlet samples fixed with 4% PFA for 10 min at RT.
//   Permeabilized with 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS.
//   FIX #4: PFA fixation and Triton X-100 permeabilization
//   are now explicitly represented with their own manifests
//   and mix/heat steps, matching the paper's IF protocol.
//   Antibody cocktail: pan-CK FITC (1:100) + APC-CD45 (1:100)
//   + Hoechst + PI in PBS buffer, 30 min on ice.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Fixation: 4% paraformaldehyde (PFA), 10 min at RT (25 C).
pfa1            = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
t24Fixed        = mix t24Separated with pfa1 for 10m
heat t24Fixed at 25c for 10m

// Permeabilization: 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS, brief wash.
triton1         = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
pbs3            = dispense 1 units of PBS
tritonPbs1      = mix triton1 with pbs3 for 1m
t24Permeabilized = mix t24Fixed with tritonPbs1 for 5m

// Staining cocktail: pan-CK FITC + APC-CD45 + Hoechst + PI.
panCK1          = dispense 1 units of PanCytokeratinFITC
cd45Ab1         = dispense 1 units of CD45_APC
hoechst1        = dispense 1 units of Hoechst
piStain         = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide

viabStainMix1   = mix panCK1 with cd45Ab1 for 1m
viabStainMix2   = mix viabStainMix1 with hoechst1 for 1m
viabStainFull   = mix viabStainMix2 with piStain for 1m

stainedViability = mix t24Permeabilized with viabStainFull for 30m

// Incubation on ice (4 C) for 30 min (paper: antibody
// cocktail + Hoechst in PBS buffer, 30 min on ice).
heat stainedViability at 4c for 30m

// Viability detection: <10% PI+ cells = high viability.
// Quantified by BD Accuri C6 flow cytometer; cells gated
// on forward/side scatter and fluorescence intensity.
viabilitySignal = detect viabilityDetection on stainedViability for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB6 / BB7: Viability QC gate
// Pass (BB6): viabilitySignal > 0 -> <10% PI+ (high viability,
//   >90% viable). Neither lysis nor spiral shear significantly
//   impacts cell viability (p=0.6687 vs control, N=3).
// Fail (BB7): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> >10% PI+ (low viability;
//   lysis or shear damage); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB8 (viabJoin).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedViability
} else {
    drain stainedViability
}

// ============================================================
// BB8: viabJoin
// Dispose viability QC signal. Clinical protocol begins.
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal

// ============================================================
// BB9: clinSep
// PROTOCOL 3 -- Clinical CTC enrichment from patient blood
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Collect clinical blood sample.
//   7.5 mL whole blood from Stage IV metastatic breast or
//   lung cancer patient. Collected in Vacutainer EDTA tubes.
//   Processed within 2-4 h to prevent blood coagulation.
//   10 patient samples total (5 breast cancer, 5 NSCLC).
//   5 healthy donor samples used as controls.
//   IRB-approved protocol (Institutional Review Board).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

clinicalBlood   = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: RBC lysis of clinical sample.
//   Same ammonium chloride lysis protocol as STEP 3.
//   7.5 mL lysed, centrifuged at 1000xg for 5 min, resuspended
//   in PBS and concentrated to 3.75 mL (2x) for on-chip input.
//   Optimal WBC input: ~14e6 WBCs (2x concentration selected
//   by characterisation experiments, Fig. 2B).
//   Input velocity: 350 uL/min sample, 750 uL/min sheath.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rbcLysis3       = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
clinLysed       = mix clinicalBlood with rbcLysis3 for 5m

heat clinLysed at 25c for 5m

pbs4            = dispense 1 units of PBS
clinNucleated   = mix clinLysed with pbs4 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: On-chip separation of clinical sample.
//   Multiplexed spiral biochip (3 stacked chips):
//   Sample: 350 uL/min; Sheath: 750 uL/min; ~10 min total.
//   CTCs (15-35 um, pan-CK+/CD45-) collected at inner outlet.
//   WBCs (12-15 um, CD45+) exit at waste outlet.
//   WBC depletion: ~99.99% from 7e6 input nucleated cells.
//   Robustness confirmed: ~900-1200 WBCs collected/5 min
//   uniformly across 0-30 min processing window (Fig. 2C).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheath3         = dispense 1 units of SheathFluid
clinSeparated   = mix clinNucleated with sheath3 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: PFA fixation and Triton X-100 permeabilization.
//   FIX #4: Fixation and permeabilization now explicitly
//   encoded as separate steps with their own manifests,
//   matching the paper's IF staining protocol (Section 2.3).
//   CTC outlet fraction fixed with 4% PFA for 10 min at RT.
//   Permeabilized with 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS.
//   These steps are required before antibody staining for
//   intracellular pan-cytokeratin detection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Fixation: 4% PFA, 10 min at RT (25 C).
pfa2            = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
clinFixed       = mix clinSeparated with pfa2 for 10m
heat clinFixed at 25c for 10m

// Permeabilization: 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS.
triton2         = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
pbs5            = dispense 1 units of PBS
tritonPbs2      = mix triton2 with pbs5 for 1m
clinPermeabilized = mix clinFixed with tritonPbs2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Immunofluorescence (IF) staining for CTC ID.
//   Staining panel (Miltenyi Biotec Asia Pacific, Singapore):
//     - Hoechst (DNA, nuclear counterstain)
//     - Pan-cytokeratin-FITC antibody (1:100, epithelial marker)
//     - APC-conjugated anti-CD45 antibody (1:100, WBC marker)
//   Incubated 30 min on ice in PBS buffer.
//   CTC scoring: Hoechst+ / Pan-CK+ / CD45-
//   Imaged by epi-fluorescence microscopy and/or BD Accuri C6.
//   Cells gated on forward/side scatter and fluorescence.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

panCK2          = dispense 1 units of PanCytokeratinFITC
cd45Ab2         = dispense 1 units of CD45_APC
hoechst2        = dispense 1 units of Hoechst

ifStainMix      = mix panCK2 with cd45Ab2 for 1m
ifStainFull     = mix ifStainMix with hoechst2 for 1m

stainedClinical = mix clinPermeabilized with ifStainFull for 30m
heat stainedClinical at 4c for 30m

clinicalSignal  = detect ctcDetection on stainedClinical for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: Clinical CTC detection QC gate
// Pass (BB10): clinicalSignal > 0 -> CTCs detected
//   (Hoechst+/Pan-CK+/CD45-). Proceed to HER2 FISH.
//   Expected counts: 20-67 CTCs/mL (breast cancer, n=5);
//   33-135 CTCs/mL (lung cancer, n=5). 100% detection (10/10).
//   Healthy donor background: 1-4 CK+ cells/mL (controls).
// Fail (BB11): clinicalSignal <= 0 -> no CTCs above threshold;
//   drain (consistent with healthy donor control result).
// Both branches converge at BB12 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (clinicalSignal > 0) {

    // ----------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 15: HER2 FISH analysis on isolated CTCs.
    //   Performed on HER2+ breast cancer patient samples (n=5).
    //   Paper protocol (Section 2.4 - DNA fluorescence FISH):
    //
    //   (a) Cytospin onto slides (600 rpm, 6 min).
    //   (b) Fix in 4% PFA, 10 min RT.
    //   (c) Dehydrate via ethanol series (80%, 90%, 100%).
    //   (d) RNase treatment: 4 mg/mL, 40 min at 37 C.
    //       FIX #6: RNase step now explicitly encoded.
    //   (e) Denature: 70% formamide/2xSSC, 80 C, 10 min.
    //       FIX #5: 80 C denaturation step now encoded.
    //   (f) Hybridize HER2 probe (HER-2/neu gene locus, red)
    //       + CEP17 (chr.17 centromere, green) at 42 C overnight.
    //       Approximated as 600m (10 h) per BioScript s/m limit.
    //   (g) Post-hybridization wash: 50% formamide/2xSSC then
    //       2xSSC at 45 C under shaking.
    //       FIX #7: Wash steps at 45 C now explicitly encoded.
    //   (h) DAPI counterstain; coverslip (50x50 mm, Fisher).
    //
    //   HER2 amplification criterion: HER2/CEP17 ratio > 2
    //   in single nuclei.
    //   Result: 3 of 5 HER2+ patients showed HER2-negative CTCs
    //   (HER2/CEP17 < 2), indicating CTC heterogeneity vs.
    //   primary tumor (Fig. 5C).
    //
    //   NOTE ON REAGENT MANIFESTS: Formamide_SSC encodes
    //   70% formamide/2xSSC (denaturation, step e) and
    //   50% formamide/2xSSC (post-hybridization wash, step g).
    //   SSC_Wash encodes the 2xSSC final wash (step g).
    //   Both are separately dispensed at their respective steps.
    // ----------------------------------------------------------

    her2Probe       = dispense 1 units of HER2_FISHProbe
    dapiStain       = dispense 1 units of DAPI

    // (b+c) Fixation (4% PFA, 10 min RT) and ethanol
    //   dehydration series (80%, 90%, 100%) -- abstracted as
    //   a single heat step at 25c for 10m (RT processing).
    pfa3            = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
    fishFixed       = mix stainedClinical with pfa3 for 10m
    heat fishFixed at 25c for 10m

    // (d) RNase treatment: 4 mg/mL RNase in PBS/0.2% Tween 20,
    //   40 min at 37 C. Removes RNA to prevent non-specific
    //   probe binding. FIX #6.
    rnase           = dispense 1 units of RNase
    rnaseTreated    = mix fishFixed with rnase for 40m
    heat rnaseTreated at 37c for 40m

    // (e) Denaturation: 70% formamide/2xSSC, 80 C, 10 min.
    //   Denatures double-stranded DNA to allow probe access.
    //   FIX #5.
    formamideSsc    = dispense 1 units of Formamide_SSC
    denatured       = mix rnaseTreated with formamideSsc for 10m
    heat denatured at 80c for 10m

    // (f) Probe hybridization: HER2 + CEP17 probes applied
    //   directly to slides at 42 C overnight (approximated
    //   as 600m = 10 h per BioScript s/m constraint).
    //   Dark and humid conditions throughout.
    her2ProbeMix    = mix denatured with her2Probe for 1m
    heat her2ProbeMix at 42c for 600m

    // (g) Post-hybridization washes.
    //   Wash 1: 50% formamide/2xSSC at 45 C under shaking.
    //   Wash 2: 2xSSC at 45 C under shaking.
    //   FIX #7: Wash steps now explicitly encoded.
    formamideWash   = dispense 1 units of Formamide_SSC
    sscWash         = dispense 1 units of SSC_Wash

    washed1         = mix her2ProbeMix with formamideWash for 5m
    heat washed1 at 45c for 5m

    washed2         = mix washed1 with sscWash for 5m
    heat washed2 at 45c for 5m

    // (h) DAPI counterstain; coverslip (50x50 mm).
    dapiMix         = mix washed2 with dapiStain for 5m

    her2Signal      = detect her2FISHDetection on dapiMix for 30s

    dispose dapiMix
    dispose her2Signal

} else {
    drain stainedClinical
}

// ============================================================
// BB12: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose clinical CTC QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose clinicalSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module beadFocusingQC
module ctcDetection

manifest PBS
manifest BSA_Solution
manifest Ethanol70
manifest SheathBuffer
manifest RBCLysisBuffer
manifest QCBeadSuspension
manifest LysedBloodSample
manifest Paraformaldehyde
manifest TritonX100
manifest PanCK_FITC_Antibody
manifest CD45_APC_Antibody
manifest HoechstDye

// ============================================================
// Ultra-fast, label-free isolation of circulating tumor cells
// from blood using spiral microfluidics.
// Warkiani, Khoo, Wu, Tay, Bhagat, Han, Lim
// Nature Protocols, Vol. 11, No. 1, pp. 134-148 (2016)
// DOI: 10.1038/nprot.2016.003
//
// Platform: spiral inertial microfluidic biochip (PDMS/glass).
// Channel dimensions: 500 um wide x 170 um deep, two-loop
// spiral, radius ~10 mm, two inlets (sample outer / sheath
// inner), two outlets (CTC inner / waste outer).
// Inlet split: 75 um sample / 425 um sheath.
// Outlet split: 150 um CTC collection / 350 um waste.
// Operating flow rates: sample 100 uL/min; sheath 750 uL/min
// (single chip). Multiplexed 3x chip: sheath 2100 uL/min.
//
// Separation physics: combined inertial lift force (FL) and
// Dean drag force (FD) in a curvilinear microchannel. CTCs
// (>15 um) focus near the inner wall; RBCs, WBCs, platelets
// (<15 um) migrate along Dean vortices toward outer wall.
// Dean number De = Re * sqrt(DH / 2*RC).
//
// Sample: 7.5 mL whole blood lysed with ammonium chloride RBC
// lysis buffer, resuspended 2x concentrated (~14e6 nucleated
// cells/mL in 3.75 mL PBS) before spiral processing.
// Throughput: 7.5 mL in 37.5 min (single), 12.5 min (3x).
// Performance: >=85% CTC recovery; 99.99% WBC depletion.
//
// NOTE ON FABRICATION ABSTRACTION: Steps 1-19 of the paper
// cover photolithography, DRIE, silanization, PDMS casting,
// soft lithography, and plasma bonding. These are off-chip
// physical fabrication steps that produce the spiral device.
// They are abstracted in BB1 as chip priming operations,
// consistent with BioScript conventions for prior protocols
// in this library. The first on-chip liquid handling step is
// chip priming (Step 20 onward in the paper procedure).
//
// NOTE ON SHEATH/SAMPLE DUAL-INLET: The spiral biochip has
// two independent inlets (sheath buffer inner, sample outer).
// BioScript `mix` abstracts the co-flow merging event at the
// spiral inlet where the two streams combine hydrodynamically.
// This is not a DMF droplet merge; it represents the inertial
// focusing run where sheath and sample enter the spiral channel
// together. The separation occurs passively along the channel
// length via inertial and Dean forces.
//
// NOTE ON QC BEAD CHECK: Step 27 in the paper runs 3-6 um
// polystyrene bead suspension (0.1% v/v) through the primed
// device to confirm particle focusing behavior before patient
// sample processing. The beadFocusingQC module abstracts the
// high-speed camera / phase-contrast microscope readout at
// the outlet region (inner wall focus = pass).
//
// NOTE ON IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE: Staining targets three markers:
//   pan-CK (FITC) -- epithelial marker; CTC positive
//   CD45 (APC)    -- leukocyte marker; CTC negative
//   Hoechst       -- nuclear stain; all nucleated cells
// Putative CTCs: pan-CK+, CD45-, Hoechst+, round nuclei,
// high nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio.
// Detection threshold (negative control): >7 CK+ cells/sample.
// ctcDetection module abstracts the fluorescence enumeration
// readout (Olympus IX71/81, ET460/50m / ET535/50m / ET605/70m
// filter set, automated MetaMorph stage scan, ImageJ threshold).
//
// NOTE ON DURATIONS: BioScript duration tokens are `s` and `m`
// only. All hour-based incubations are converted to minutes.
//   5 min priming      = 5m
//   10 min lysis       = 10m
//   37.5 min run       = 37m (single spiral, 7.5 mL lysed blood)
//   30-60 min staining = 30m (antibody incubation on ice)
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main           -- chip priming, bead QC, blood prep,
//                          spiral processing, cell collection
//   BB2  beadPass       -- beadSignal > 0: correct focusing,
//                          proceed to blood processing; dispose
//   BB3  beadFail       -- beadSignal <= 0: focusing incorrect
//                          (wrong channel depth or flow rate);
//                          drain bead suspension, abort run
//   BB4  beadJoin       -- join: blood prep and staining branch
//   BB5  ctcPass        -- ctcSignal > 0: CTC enumeration valid
//                          (>7 pan-CK+ cells); dispose all
//   BB6  ctcFail        -- ctcSignal <= 0: no CTCs detected
//                          (below threshold); drain stained cells
//   BB7  finalCleanup   -- terminal: dispose QC signal, end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CHIP PRIMING - STEP 1 (Paper Steps 20-22): Sterilize the
//   primed spiral biochip by flowing 70% (v/v) ethanol in
//   sterile deionized water for 5 min at 750 uL/min to
//   remove air bubbles and sterilize the channel interior.
//   Required for downstream cell culture applications.
//   NOTE: Chip fabrication (Steps 1-19: photolithography,
//   DRIE, silanization, PDMS soft lithography, plasma bonding)
//   is performed off-chip and is not encoded here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ethanolPrime = dispense 1 units of Ethanol70
channelWash  = mix ethanolPrime with ethanolPrime for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CHIP PRIMING - STEP 2 (Paper Steps 23-25): Flush residual
//   ethanol and coat microchannel surfaces with sheath buffer
//   (1x sterile PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA) at 750 uL/min for 5 min.
//   BSA coating minimises non-specific cell adhesion to the
//   PDMS channel walls during spiral processing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaSolution    = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
sheathPriming  = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
surfaceCoating = mix bsaSolution with sheathPriming for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CHIP PRIMING - STEP 3 (Paper Step 26): Inspect for bubbles
//   using inverted microscope (bright-field mode). Increasing
//   sheath flow rate dislodges residual air pockets.
//   Model as an additional sheath buffer flush.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheathFlush    = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
bubbleRemoval  = mix surfaceCoating with sheathFlush for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// QC BEAD CHECK (Paper Step 27): Load 3-6 um polystyrene bead
//   suspension (0.1% v/v) at 100 uL/min (sample inlet, outer
//   wall) co-flowing with sheath buffer at 750 uL/min (inner
//   inlet). Observe particle distribution across channel width
//   at outlet using phase-contrast microscope + high-speed
//   camera (VisionResearch Phantom v9).
//   Pass criterion: 6 um beads undergo complete Dean cycle
//   (inner -> outer wall migration visible); 15 um beads focus
//   tightly near inner wall at outlet.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the co-flow hydrodynamic event at
//   the spiral inlet (not a DMF electrode merge).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beadSuspension = dispense 1 units of QCBeadSuspension
sheathQC       = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
beadRun        = mix beadSuspension with sheathQC for 5m

beadSignal     = detect beadFocusingQC on beadRun for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Bead focusing QC gate
// Pass (BB2): beadSignal > 0 -> correct particle focusing
//             confirmed (channel depth 165-170 um verified);
//             dispose bead run and proceed to blood processing.
// Fail (BB3): beadSignal <= 0 -> incorrect focusing (channel
//             depth out of tolerance, <160 or >170 um due to
//             improper DRIE); drain, abort run, fabricate new
//             master mold (Table 1, Step 27 troubleshooting).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (beadJoin).
// ============================================================

if (beadSignal > 0) {
    dispose beadRun
} else {
    drain beadRun
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: beadJoin
// Dispose bead focusing QC signal. Control falls into the
// blood preparation and spiral processing branch.
// ============================================================

dispose beadSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BLOOD PREPARATION - STEP 1 (Paper Steps 28-29): Lyse RBCs
//   using 3x ammonium chloride RBC lysis buffer at 1:3 v/v
//   ratio. Invert conical tube to mix. Incubate 10 min at
//   room temperature (24-26 C) on shaking platform until
//   sample color changes to dark red (complete lysis).
//   NOTE: If spiking with cancer cell lines, cancer cells
//   must be added before lysis step (Reagent Setup in paper).
//   Lysis substantially reduces untargeted blood cells,
//   mitigating cell-cell interactions that impair inertial
//   focusing. Total cell loss from lysis + centrifugation <8%.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rbcLysisBuffer = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
lysedBlood1    = dispense 1 units of LysedBloodSample
lysisReaction  = mix lysedBlood1 with rbcLysisBuffer for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BLOOD PREPARATION - STEP 2 (Paper Step 29): Pellet nucleated
//   cells by centrifugation at 1000g for 5 min at room temp.
//   Resuspend pellet in 1x PBS to 2x concentrated sample
//   (~14e6 nucleated cells/mL; 7.5 mL blood -> 3.75 mL PBS).
//   Model centrifugation as a heat step at room temperature.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsResuspend   = dispense 1 units of PBS
heat lysisReaction at 25c for 5m
resuspendedSample = mix lysisReaction with pbsResuspend for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// SPIRAL PROCESSING (Paper Steps 32-37): Co-flow lysed blood
//   (100 uL/min, outer sample inlet) with sheath buffer
//   (750 uL/min, inner sheath inlet) through the two-loop
//   spiral biochip. CTCs (>15 um) focus near the inner wall
//   via inertial lift (FL) overcoming Dean drag (FD); smaller
//   blood cells (RBCs, WBCs, platelets, <15 um) exit from
//   the outer waste outlet following Dean vortex streamlines.
//   Total run: ~37 min for 7.5 mL lysed blood (single chip);
//   <13 min for 3x multiplexed chip (sheath 2100 uL/min).
//   CTC fraction collected from inner outlet into 15 mL tube.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the hydrodynamic co-flow separation
//   event in the spiral channel. The CTCs continuously exit
//   from the inner outlet during this step; this is not a
//   discrete droplet merge but a continuous flow separation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheathRun      = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
spiralRun      = mix resuspendedSample with sheathRun for 37m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CELL CONCENTRATION (Paper Step 38): Centrifuge collected CTC
//   fraction at 300g for 3 min at room temperature to pellet
//   cells and remove excess volume before staining.
//   Resuspend in ~250 uL PBS for downstream immunostaining.
//   Model centrifugation as a heat step at room temperature.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat spiralRun at 25c for 3m
pbsResuspend2       = dispense 1 units of PBS
concentratedCells   = mix spiralRun with pbsResuspend2 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 1 (Paper Step 40): Fix cells with
//   4% w/v paraformaldehyde (PFA) in PBS for 10 min at room
//   temperature. PFA crosslinks cellular proteins to preserve
//   morphology and antigen epitopes for antibody staining.
//   CAUTION: PFA is a suspected carcinogen; handle with PPE.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pfaFixative  = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
fixedCells   = mix concentratedCells with pfaFixative for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 2 (Paper Step 41): Wash fixed
//   cells with 1-2 mL PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA, centrifuge at
//   300g for 3 min at room temperature to remove residual PFA.
//   Resuspend in ~250 uL PBS before permeabilization.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash1     = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
pbsWash1     = dispense 1 units of PBS
washBuffer1  = mix bsaWash1 with pbsWash1 for 30s
heat washBuffer1 at 25c for 3m
washedFixed  = mix fixedCells with washBuffer1 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 3 (Paper Step 42): Permeabilize
//   cells with 0.1% v/v Triton X-100 in PBS for 1-5 min at
//   room temperature. Triton X-100 solubilizes the plasma
//   membrane to allow intracellular antibody access for
//   pan-cytokeratin (pan-CK) staining of the cytoskeleton.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tritonX100     = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
permeaCells    = mix washedFixed with tritonX100 for 3m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 4 (Paper Step 43): Wash
//   permeabilized cells with 1-2 mL PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA,
//   centrifuge at 300g for 3 min at room temperature to
//   remove Triton X-100 before antibody incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash2     = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
pbsWash2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
washBuffer2  = mix bsaWash2 with pbsWash2 for 30s
heat washBuffer2 at 25c for 3m
washedPermea = mix permeaCells with washBuffer2 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 5 (Paper Step 44): Incubate cells
//   on ice with conjugated antibody cocktail for 30 min:
//     - FITC pan-cytokeratin (pan-CK) 1:100 -- CTC marker
//       (CK8, CK9, CK18, CK19; epithelial cytokeratins).
//       Miltenyi Biotec Asia Pacific. Excitation 490 nm,
//       emission 526 nm.
//     - APC CD45 1:100 -- leukocyte marker (WBC counter-stain
//       to exclude contaminating WBCs from CTC count).
//       Miltenyi Biotec Asia Pacific.
//     - Hoechst 33342 1:1000 (1 M stock) -- nuclear stain
//       for all nucleated cells; confirms CTC nuclei.
//   Putative CTCs: pan-CK+, CD45-, Hoechst+, round nuclei,
//   high nuclear-to-cytoplasmic (N/C) ratio.
//   Incubation on ice prevents antigen internalization and
//   non-specific binding. Model as heat at 4c for 30m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

panCKAntibody  = dispense 1 units of PanCK_FITC_Antibody
cd45Antibody   = dispense 1 units of CD45_APC_Antibody
hoechstDye     = dispense 1 units of HoechstDye

antibodyMix    = mix panCKAntibody with cd45Antibody for 5s
fullStainMix   = mix antibodyMix with hoechstDye for 5s
stainedCells   = mix washedPermea with fullStainMix for 30m
heat stainedCells at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 6 (Paper Step 45): Wash stained
//   cells with 1-2 mL PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA, centrifuge at
//   300g for 3 min to remove unbound antibody. Resuspend in
//   ~250 uL PBS and transfer to a single 96-well plate well.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash3      = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
pbsWash3      = dispense 1 units of PBS
washBuffer3   = mix bsaWash3 with pbsWash3 for 30s
heat washBuffer3 at 25c for 3m
washedStained = mix stainedCells with washBuffer3 for 1m

pbsFinal      = dispense 1 units of PBS
finalCells    = mix washedStained with pbsFinal for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CTC DETECTION (Paper Step 47): Fluorescence enumeration of
//   pan-CK+/CD45-/Hoechst+ cells with round nuclei and high
//   N/C ratio. Platform: Olympus inverted microscope (IX71/81)
//   with phase-contrast, emission filters ET460/50m (Hoechst),
//   ET535/50m (pan-CK FITC), ET605/70m (CD45 APC); automated
//   stage (MetaMorph); 12-bit EM-CCD camera (Andor iXon+885).
//   Each 96-well plate well scanned in 1x1 mm grid.
//   Threshold: >7 CK+ cells per sample = positive patient.
//   Clinical range: 12-1275 CK+ breast CTCs; 10-1535 lung CTCs.
//   ctcDetection module abstracts the fluorescence readout and
//   cell classification step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ctcSignal = detect ctcDetection on finalCells for 45m

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: CTC detection gate
// Pass (BB5): ctcSignal > 0 -> pan-CK+/CD45-/Hoechst+ cells
//             enumerated above threshold (>7 CK+ cells);
//             positive patient sample confirmed. Dispose.
// Fail (BB6): ctcSignal <= 0 -> no CTCs detected above
//             threshold (healthy donor control or run failure);
//             drain stained cells.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ctcSignal > 0) {
    dispose finalCells
} else {
    drain finalCells
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose CTC detection QC signal. Experiment ends.
// Downstream options for recovered CTCs (from inner outlet
// collected prior to staining): culture (37 C / 5% CO2),
// DNA/RNA-FISH (ALK break-apart probe, HER2/neu), KRAS
// codon 12 mutation by ICE-COLD PCR + Sanger sequencing,
// single-cell analysis. These are encoded as separate protocols.
// ============================================================

dispose ctcSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module serialDilutionDetection
module proteinDigestionDetection

manifest AnalyteFluorescein
manifest InternalStandardRhodamine123
manifest Diluent
manifest AF_BSA
manifest PepsinSolution
manifest TrypsinSolution
manifest PluronicF68

// ============================================================
// Multilayer Hybrid Microfluidics: A Digital-to-Channel
// Interface for Sample Processing and Separations
// Watson, Jebrail, Wheeler - Anal. Chem. 2010, 82, 6680-6686
// DOI: 10.1021/ac101379g
//
// This file encodes two on-chip protocols demonstrated on a
// two-plate DMF multilayer hybrid device (glass substrate,
// 13 driving electrodes 2.2x2.2 mm, 3 reservoir electrodes
// 3x3 mm or 5x5 mm). The DMF layer (substrates 1+2) sits
// atop a microchannel network (substrate 3, 100 um wide x
// 20 um deep). Droplets processed on the top DMF layer are
// delivered through a vertical digital-channel interface
// (drilled hole, 2 mm dia.) into microchannels below for
// capillary electrophoresis (CE) analysis with LIF detection
// (488 nm excitation, 536/40 nm emission).
//
// AC actuation: 20 kHz, 100-200 Vrms.
// Spacer gap: 280 um (4x double-sided tape).
// Unit droplet: ~3 uL (fills the 2 mm dia. x 1 mm deep hole).
// Separation buffer: 20 mM borate pH 9.0 (dilution) or
//                   100 mM borate pH 9.0 (enzyme digests).
// Pluronic F-68 added to all protein-containing droplets at
// 0.1% wt to minimise surface adsorption.
//
// PROTOCOL 1: On-Chip Serial Dilution Calibration Curve
//   Stock droplet: 1 uM fluorescein + 1 uM rhodamine 123 in
//   20 mM borate pH 9.0. Diluent: 1 uM rhodamine 123 in
//   20 mM borate pH 9.0 (internal standard maintained constant).
//   Dilution 1: stock + diluent -> mix (circular, ~10 s) ->
//     split into two equal subdroplets (2x dilution, ~0.5 uM Flu).
//     Daughter A: drive to interface for CE-LIF analysis.
//     Daughter B: store on array for second dilution step.
//   Dilution 2: stored Daughter B + fresh diluent -> mix ->
//     split. Daughter C: drive to interface for CE-LIF analysis.
//   Precision: RSD = 2.9% (stock), 3.7% (1st), 7.4% (2nd).
//   Efficiency: 1.1e6 plates/m for rhodamine 123.
//   R^2 = 0.9937 across five replicates.
//
// PROTOCOL 2: Multistep Enzymatic Protein Digestion
//   Model protein: AF-BSA (Alexa Fluor 488 labeled bovine serum
//   albumin, 20 ug/mL in DI water + 0.1% F-68).
//   Pepsin: 1 mg/mL in 1 mM acetate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 4.5.
//     Cleaves at aromatic residues (Phe, Tyr, Trp). 30 min.
//   Trypsin: 1 mg/mL in 50 mM borate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 9.0.
//     Cleaves at basic residues (Lys, Arg). 30 min.
//   Sequential digest: AF-BSA -> pepsin (30 min) -> split ->
//     subdroplet to interface for CE; stored half merged with
//     trypsin (30 min) -> deliver to interface.
//   Incubation: device stored in humidified Petri dish (water-
//     saturated wipe) during 30 min steps to limit evaporation.
//   Total process time: ~2 h including both incubation steps.
//
// NOTE ON split ABSTRACTION: BioScript does not have a native
//   `split` statement. Physical droplet splitting on the array
//   (two daughter droplets of equal volume) is abstracted here
//   as a `mix` step with a secondary dispense that represents
//   the stored subdroplet being retained on the array. The
//   subdroplet driven to the digital-channel interface is the
//   primary product variable at each split point. This is a
//   compiler-compatible representation; the actual split is
//   performed by reversing the electrode actuation sequence
//   while the droplet straddles two electrodes.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript accepts s and m only.
//   30 min incubations are encoded as 30m.
//   Circular mixing for several seconds is encoded as 10s.
//
// NOTE ON dispense RESTRICTION: Only manifest-declared reagents
//   may appear as the source in a dispense statement.
//   The digital-channel interface transfer (droplet driven to
//   the microchannel inlet) is modelled via detect statements
//   using the serialDilutionDetection or proteinDigestionDetection
//   modules, which abstract CE-LIF analysis in the channel layer.
//
// NOTE ON VARIABLE REASSIGNMENT: BioScript does not permit
//   reassignment of a variable once bound. All intermediate
//   droplets (post-mix, post-detect) use unique identifiers.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- entry: serial dilution protocol
//                           (dispense, dilution 1, dilution 2)
//                           followed by protein digestion protocol
//   BB2  dilutionPass     -- dilutionSignal > 0: valid CE peaks
//                           detected; dispose analysed droplets
//   BB3  dilutionFail     -- dilutionSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  dilutionJoin     -- join: protein digestion branch begins
//   BB5  digestionPass    -- digestionSignal > 0: valid digest
//                           peaks; dispose all digestion droplets
//   BB6  digestionFail    -- digestionSignal <= 0: no peaks; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose QC signals; end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: On-Chip Serial Dilution Calibration Curve
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Dispense stock droplet.
//   Reservoir contains 1 uM fluorescein + 1 uM rhodamine 123
//   in 20 mM borate buffer pH 9.0. Unit droplet: ~3 uL.
//   Actuation: 20 kHz, 100-200 Vrms, two-plate format.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stockDroplet = dispense 1 units of AnalyteFluorescein

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Dispense first diluent droplet.
//   Reservoir contains 1 uM rhodamine 123 (internal standard)
//   in 20 mM borate buffer pH 9.0. No fluorescein present.
//   Merging with stock will halve fluorescein concentration
//   while maintaining constant internal standard.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

diluent1 = dispense 1 units of Diluent

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Merge stock and first diluent droplet.
//   Merged droplet (~0.5 uM fluorescein, ~1 uM rhodamine 123).
//   Circular mixing pattern (several electrode actuations)
//   ensures thorough homogenisation before splitting.
//   Mix duration: ~10 s on-chip (paper: "several seconds").
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mergedDrop1 = mix stockDroplet with diluent1 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Dilution 1 - split merged droplet.
//   Physical split: reverse electrode sequence while droplet
//   straddles two driving electrodes; two ~1.5 uL subdroplets
//   result. Daughter A is driven to the digital-channel
//   interface. Daughter B is stored on the array.
//   Abstracted here: the split product variable represents
//   the daughter subdroplet A (~0.5 uM Flu, ~1 uM Rho).
//   A second dispense of Diluent abstracts the stored
//   Daughter B remaining on the electrode array.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Daughter A: subdroplet analysed by CE-LIF at channel interface.
dilution1Analysed = mix mergedDrop1 with diluent1 for 2s

// Daughter B: stored on array for second dilution.
// NOTE: A fresh diluent dispense models the stored half-droplet
// equivalent volume; it is the logical placeholder for the
// retained subdroplet that will be further diluted in STEP 6.
storedDrop1 = dispense 1 units of Diluent

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: CE-LIF detection at digital-channel interface.
//   Daughter A is actuated to the interface electrode (2.2x2.2
//   mm, overlapping the 2 mm dia. drilled hole by ~1 mm).
//   The droplet spontaneously wets and settles into the hole.
//   DC voltages (LabSmith sequencer) drive sample through the
//   cross injector into the 3 cm separation channel.
//   Loading: S=900V, SW=0V, B=650V, BW=850V.
//   Injection: S=500V, SW=500V, B=1000V, BW=0V.
//   LIF detection at 3 cm downstream (488 nm, 20 mW argon ion,
//   60x objective, 536/40 nm BP filter, PMT readout).
//   Peak area (AA) relative to IS (AIS) recorded.
//   The sample waste channel removes the previous analysed
//   sample by suction before the next injection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dilutionSignal1 = detect serialDilutionDetection on dilution1Analysed for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Dilution 2 - merge stored Daughter B with fresh diluent.
//   Stored subdroplet (Daughter B, ~0.5 uM Flu) merged with a
//   second unit diluent droplet. Result: ~0.25 uM fluorescein,
//   ~1 uM rhodamine 123 (4x dilution relative to original stock).
//   Mixed circularly for ~10 s to homogenise.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

diluent2 = dispense 1 units of Diluent
mergedDrop2 = mix storedDrop1 with diluent2 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Dilution 2 - split and deliver second daughter droplet.
//   Daughter C (~0.25 uM Flu, ~1 uM Rho) driven to interface.
//   Previous sample removed from channel by suction before
//   this injection, without removing the DMF top-plate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dilution2Analysed = mix mergedDrop2 with diluent2 for 2s

// CE-LIF detection for the second dilution point.
dilutionSignal2 = detect serialDilutionDetection on dilution2Analysed for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Serial dilution QC gate
// Keyed on dilutionSignal1 (undiluted first daughter;
// highest fluorescein signal, most reliable peak detection).
// Pass (BB2): dilutionSignal1 > 0 -> valid electropherogram
//             peaks resolved; baseline separation confirmed;
//             dispose analysed droplets.
// Fail (BB3): dilutionSignal1 <= 0 -> no peaks (interface
//             transfer failed or separation column clogged);
//             drain and abort calibration run.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (dilutionJoin).
// ============================================================

if (dilutionSignal1 > 0) {
    dispose dilution1Analysed
    dispose dilution2Analysed
} else {
    drain dilution1Analysed
    drain dilution2Analysed
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: dilutionJoin
// Dispose serial dilution QC signal droplets.
// Control falls into protein digestion branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose dilutionSignal1
dispose dilutionSignal2

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: Multistep Enzymatic Protein Digestion (AF-BSA)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Dispense AF-BSA droplet.
//   20 ug/mL AF-BSA in DI water + 0.1% Pluronic F-68.
//   Unit droplet: ~3 uL. F-68 additive minimises protein
//   adsorption to device surfaces (Parylene-C / Teflon-AF).
//   Device uses 100 mM borate buffer pH 9.0 as channel fill
//   for enzymatic digest runs (higher ionic strength for
//   protein fragment separation).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

afbsaDroplet = dispense 1 units of AF_BSA

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Dispense pepsin droplet.
//   1 mg/mL pepsin in 1 mM acetate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 4.5.
//   Pepsin cleaves at aromatic residues (Phe, Tyr, Trp),
//   generating multiply charged peptide fragments.
//   Unit droplet: ~3 uL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pepsinDroplet = dispense 1 units of PepsinSolution

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Merge AF-BSA with pepsin and incubate.
//   Merged droplet (~6 uL, 2 units) contains AF-BSA + pepsin
//   in equal volumes. Mixed briefly on the DMF array to ensure
//   homogeneous enzyme-substrate contact before incubation.
//   Device transferred to humidified chamber (Petri dish with
//   water-saturated wipe) to limit droplet evaporation during
//   the 30 min incubation at room temperature.
//   After incubation, AF-BSA peak at t=58 s is absent from
//   CE electropherogram, confirming complete digestion.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pepsinReaction = mix afbsaDroplet with pepsinDroplet for 5s
heat pepsinReaction at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Split pepsin digest; deliver first subdroplet to
//   digital-channel interface for CE-LIF analysis.
//   Daughter D: driven to interface (pepsin-only digest).
//   Daughter E: stored on array for sequential trypsin step.
//   CE electropherogram shows multiple peaks eluting at a range
//   of times relative to the AF-BSA reactant peak (multiply
//   charged aromatic peptides generated by pepsin cleavage).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Daughter D: analysed by CE-LIF (pepsin digest only).
pepsinAnalysed = mix pepsinReaction with pepsinDroplet for 2s

// Daughter E: stored subdroplet (logical placeholder).
storedPepsinDrop = dispense 1 units of AF_BSA

// CE-LIF detection for pepsin-only digest.
digestionSignalPepsin = detect proteinDigestionDetection on pepsinAnalysed for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: Dispense trypsin droplet.
//   1 mg/mL trypsin in 50 mM borate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 9.0.
//   Trypsin cleaves at basic residues (Lys, Arg), reducing the
//   multiply charged peptides from pepsin into smaller fragments
//   that elute closer together in the CE separation.
//   Unit droplet: ~3 uL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypsinDroplet = dispense 1 units of TrypsinSolution

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Merge stored pepsin digest half with trypsin and
//   incubate for a second 30 min digestion at room temperature.
//   Sequential two-enzyme digest: pepsin then trypsin generates
//   singly charged peptides observable in the top CE trace
//   (Fig 6, paper). Device returned to humidified chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypsinReaction = mix storedPepsinDrop with trypsinDroplet for 5s
heat trypsinReaction at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Deliver sequential digest subdroplet to interface.
//   Full pepsin+trypsin digest driven to digital-channel
//   interface for CE-LIF analysis. Previous sample removed
//   from channel by suction (fine needle + vacuum flask)
//   without removing the DMF top-plate between injections.
//   CE electropherogram shows new series of peaks (peptides
//   eluting closer together vs pepsin-only digest).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sequentialDigestAnalysed = mix trypsinReaction with trypsinDroplet for 2s

// CE-LIF detection for sequential pepsin + trypsin digest.
digestionSignalSeq = detect proteinDigestionDetection on sequentialDigestAnalysed for 60s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Protein digestion QC gate
// Keyed on pepsin-only digestion signal (Step 11 detection;
// most diagnostic -- loss of intact AF-BSA peak at t=58 s
// confirms complete first-stage digestion).
// Pass (BB5): digestionSignalPepsin > 0 -> valid CE peaks
//             detected (peptide fragments resolved); dispose
//             all digestion droplets.
// Fail (BB6): digestionSignalPepsin <= 0 -> no signal (enzyme
//             inactive, transfer failed, or column blocked);
//             drain all digestion droplets.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (digestionSignalPepsin > 0) {
    dispose pepsinAnalysed
    dispose sequentialDigestAnalysed
} else {
    drain pepsinAnalysed
    drain sequentialDigestAnalysed
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all QC signal droplets. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose digestionSignalPepsin
dispose digestionSignalSeq

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

