// ============================================================
// Droplet-Based High-Throughput Cultivation for Accurate
// Screening of Antibiotic Resistant Gut Microbes.
// Watterson et al., eLife 2020;9:e56998.
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.56998
//
// Platform: Anaerobic vinyl chamber (Coy Laboratory Products),
// 86% N2 / 10% CO2 / 4% H2 atmosphere, <1 ppm O2. All droplet
// generation, cultivation, and sorting steps are performed
// inside the anaerobic chamber. External computer controls
// syringe pumps, high-frame-rate camera (Basler acA640-750um,
// 925 Hz, 59 us exposure), and sorting electrodes (10 kHz,
// 800 V p-p, 30% duty cycle, 10 ms actuation).
//
// DROPLET GENERATION: Flow-focusing junction. Oil phase:
// Bio-Rad Droplet Generation Oil for EvaGreen. Droplet volumes:
// ~65-115 pL. Fecal cell suspension diluted 200x so that
// ~2-12% of droplets contain exactly one viable cell
// (Poisson statistics). ~4-15 million droplets per run.
//
// SORTING: Wavelet OD image analysis (discrete wavelet frame
// decomposition, biorthogonal 3.1 wavelets, LL High subband,
// 15x15 px window, 5 px step, 15 grey levels, 3x3 px
// displacement). Wavelet OD in [0.3, 0.7] = sparse/slow-growing
// colony (KEEP). OD < 0.3 = empty. OD > 0.7 = dense colony.
// Sorting rate: ~30 Hz. Dielectrophoretic deflection into
// keep/waste path.
//
// SEQUENCING: Paired-end 16S rRNA V4 amplicon sequencing
// (Illumina MiSeq, 2x151). Library prep by Argonne National
// Laboratory Earth Microbiome Project protocol. ASVs inferred
// by Minimum Entropy Decomposition (MED); taxonomy by SILVA.
//
// BIOLOGICAL SCOPE: This file encodes the full experiment
// in sequence:
//   PROTOCOL 1 - Rich media droplet cultivation (BHIS, GMM,
//     YCFA), with slow-grower sorting enrichment.
//   PROTOCOL 2 - Antibiotic resistance screening in droplets
//     (Ampicillin, Ciprofloxacin, Vancomycin in BHIS).
// Each protocol block is self-contained with its own QC gate.
//
// NOTE ON INCUBATION TIME: BioScript duration tokens are
// s / m only. All hour-based incubations are converted to
// minutes. Plates: up to 7 days = 10080 min. Droplets:
// up to 2 days = 2880 min.
//
// NOTE ON DISPENSE ABSTRACTION: `dispense 1 units of X`
// models the generation of one droplet batch (~0.5-1 mL
// emulsion) from a given medium/reagent reservoir. Each
// dispense into oil at the flow-focusing junction produces
// the full set of encapsulated droplets for that condition.
// The oil phase (HFE7500_SurfactantOil) is modelled as a
// co-dispense step via `mix`, abstracting the two-pump
// (aqueous + oil) flow-focusing generation event.
//
// NOTE ON POISSON ENCAPSULATION: Stochastic single-cell
// isolation by Poisson statistics is implicit in the
// dispense step. There is no reagent-mixing in the DMF
// sense; `mix` abstracts a droplet generation/coalescence
// event at the flow-focusing junction.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device setup; BHIS rich media
//                              droplet cultivation
//   BB2  bhisDropletPass    -- bhisCultSignal > 0: growth
//                              detected; proceed to sorting
//   BB3  bhisDropletFail    -- bhisCultSignal <= 0: no growth;
//                              drain emulsion
//   BB4  bhisCultJoin       -- join: slow-grower sorting
//   BB5  bhisSortPass       -- bioxSortSignal > 0: slow-grower
//                              colonies kept; proceed to seq
//   BB6  bhisSortFail       -- bioxSortSignal <= 0: sort failed;
//                              drain sorted fraction
//   BB7  bhisSortJoin       -- join: GMM cultivation arm
//   BB8  gmmDropletPass     -- gmmCultSignal > 0: growth; proceed
//   BB9  gmmDropletFail     -- gmmCultSignal <= 0: no growth; drain
//   BB10 gmmCultJoin        -- join: YCFA cultivation arm
//   BB11 ycfaDropletPass    -- ycfaCultSignal > 0: growth; proceed
//   BB12 ycfaDropletFail    -- ycfaCultSignal <= 0: no growth; drain
//   BB13 ycfaCultJoin       -- join: antibiotic screening arm
//   BB14 ampDropletPass     -- ampResistSignal > 0: resistant
//                              organisms detected; proceed
//   BB15 ampDropletFail     -- ampResistSignal <= 0: none; drain
//   BB16 ampScreenJoin      -- join: ciprofloxacin arm
//   BB17 ciproDropletPass   -- ciproResistSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB18 ciproDropletFail   -- ciproResistSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB19 ciproScreenJoin    -- join: vancomycin arm
//   BB20 vancoDropletPass   -- vancoResistSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB21 vancoDropletFail   -- vancoResistSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB22 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: RICH MEDIA DROPLET CULTIVATION
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 1: Prepare BHIS emulsion.
//   Fecal cell suspension (FMT donor, previously characterised
//   by Lee et al. 2017) diluted 200x into Brain Heart Infusion
//   Supplemented medium (BHIS: 18.5 g BHI broth, 2.5 g yeast
//   extract, 0.25 g L-cysteine per 500 mL; autoclaved; + 0.5 mL
//   0.1% Vitamin K + 0.5 mL hemin 5 mg/mL).
//   Live cell density: ~1.5 +/- 1.0 x10^8 cells/mL.
//   Poisson loading: ~2-12% of droplets contain one live cell.
//   Droplet generation flow-focusing junction; HFE7500 oil
//   phase abstracts the two-pump co-dispense event.
//   Total emulsion: ~0.5-1 mL of 65-115 pL droplets
//   (~4-15 million droplets).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisCells      = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
bhisMedium     = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
bhisOil        = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

// Mix abstracts the flow-focusing droplet generation event:
// aqueous (cells + medium) sheared into oil at junction.
bhisPreEmulsion  = mix bhisCells with bhisMedium for 5s
bhisEmulsion     = mix bhisPreEmulsion with bhisOil for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 2: Incubate BHIS droplets.
//   Emulsion stored in 15 mL snap-cap culture tube at 37 C
//   inside the anaerobic chamber incubator. Cultured up to
//   2 days (2880 min). Each isolated droplet acts as an
//   independent microreactor; slow-growers avoid competitive
//   overgrowth from fast-growing populations.
//   NOTE: Droplet volume reduction begins after ~4 days due
//   to evaporation in the arid anaerobic atmosphere; cultures
//   are limited to 2 days to avoid this artefact.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat bhisEmulsion at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 3: Image-based colony density detection.
//   High-frame-rate camera + LabView code detects each droplet
//   approaching the sorting junction. Wavelet OD computed per
//   droplet. This detect step abstracts the imaging pass to
//   assess whether colonies have grown in the emulsion before
//   sorting. A positive signal (> 0) indicates colonies
//   present in the emulsion at detectable density.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisCultSignal = detect imagingODDetection on bhisEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: BHIS cultivation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): bhisCultSignal > 0 -> colony-containing droplets
//             detected; carry emulsion forward to sorting.
// Fail (BB3): bhisCultSignal <= 0 -> no growth detected;
//             drain emulsion (all droplets empty).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (bhisCultJoin).
// ============================================================

if (bhisCultSignal > 0) {
    dispose bhisCultSignal
} else {
    drain bhisEmulsion
    dispose bhisCultSignal
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: bhisCultJoin
// Control falls into the slow-grower sorting arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 4: Slow-grower sorting in BHIS droplets.
//   Two independent sorting experiments (biological replicates).
//   Droplets re-injected at 20 uL/hr; oil spacing phase at
//   180 uL/hr. Camera detects each droplet; Wavelet OD computed.
//   Droplets with Wavelet OD in [0.3, 0.7] (sparse colony)
//   are deflected to the keep path via 10 kHz, 800 V p-p
//   electrode actuation for 10 ms. Dense colonies (OD > 0.7)
//   and empty droplets (OD < 0.3) pass to waste.
//   Sorting rate: ~30 Hz. False positive rate: <= 8%.
//   Sorted volume much less than 100 uL (limited by ~30 Hz rate);
//   sorted layer is ~1-10 uL on top of oil.
//   Result: shift in rank-abundance curve; average amplified
//   ASVs from <1% to >1%: 6.5 (unsorted) vs 12.5 (sorted)
//   out of 158 total ASVs detected.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bioxSortSignal = detect waveletODSorting on bhisEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: BHIS slow-grower sort QC gate
// Pass (BB5): bioxSortSignal > 0 -> slow-grower colonies
//             successfully isolated in keep path; proceed
//             to sequencing.
// Fail (BB6): bioxSortSignal <= 0 -> sort failed (no sparse
//             colonies present); drain sorted fraction.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (bhisSortJoin).
// ============================================================

if (bioxSortSignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // Recovery and sequencing (pass path only):
    // Sorted droplets (~1-10 uL) mixed with equal volume of
    // 1H,1H,2H,2H-Perfluoro-1-octanol (PFO) for demulsification.
    // Vortex + centrifuge; oil and PFO removed. For sorted
    // volumes, add 150 uL DNA-free water + 150 uL PFO first.
    // DNA extracted using Qiagen DNeasy Blood and Tissue Kit.
    // Paired-end 16S rRNA V4 amplicon sequencing (Illumina
    // MiSeq 2x151); ASVs by MED; taxonomy by SILVA.
    // Separately: streaked sorted droplets onto BHIS agar,
    // cultured 2 days at 37 C; 24 random colonies picked for
    // Sanger sequencing (16S, 27F/1492R primers).
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    pfo1             = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer1       = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedBHIS  = mix bhisEmulsion with pfo1 for 1m
    extractedDNA_BHIS = mix demulsifiedBHIS with dnaBuffer1 for 1m

    bhisSeqSignal    = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_BHIS for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_BHIS
    dispose bhisSeqSignal
} else {
    drain bhisEmulsion
}

dispose bioxSortSignal

// ============================================================
// BB7: bhisSortJoin
// BHIS arm complete. Control falls into GMM cultivation arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 5: Prepare and incubate GMM emulsion.
//   Gut Microbiota Medium (GMM), prepared per Goodman et al.
//   2011. Same fecal cell suspension, same Poisson loading
//   (200x dilution), same droplet volume range (65-115 pL).
//   Parallel plate cultures also prepared for comparison
//   (up to 7 days, 10080 min on plates vs 2880 min in droplets).
//   Droplets show 16S-based richness increase relative to
//   plate cultures across all media (p<0.005, Mann-Whitney U).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gmmCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
gmmMedium    = dispense 1 units of GMM_Medium
gmmOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

gmmPreEmulsion  = mix gmmCells with gmmMedium for 5s
gmmEmulsion     = mix gmmPreEmulsion with gmmOil for 5s

heat gmmEmulsion at 37c for 2880m

gmmCultSignal   = detect imagingODDetection on gmmEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: GMM cultivation QC gate
// Pass (BB8): gmmCultSignal > 0 -> growth detected; extract
//             DNA and sequence.
// Fail (BB9): gmmCultSignal <= 0 -> no growth; drain.
// Both converge at BB10 (gmmCultJoin).
// ============================================================

if (gmmCultSignal > 0) {
    pfo2              = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer2        = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedGMM    = mix gmmEmulsion with pfo2 for 1m
    extractedDNA_GMM  = mix demulsifiedGMM with dnaBuffer2 for 1m

    gmmSeqSignal      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_GMM for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_GMM
    dispose gmmSeqSignal
} else {
    drain gmmEmulsion
}

dispose gmmCultSignal

// ============================================================
// BB10: gmmCultJoin
// GMM arm complete. Control falls into YCFA cultivation arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 6: Prepare and incubate YCFA emulsion.
//   Yeast Casitones Fatty Acid medium (YCFA), modified DSMZ
//   media 1611: 10 g casitone, 2.5 g yeast extract, 5 g
//   dextrose, MgSO4, CaCl2, KH2PO4, K2HPO4, NaCl, resazurin,
//   volatile fatty acids (acetic, propionic, iso-butyric,
//   n-valeric, iso-valeric); pH 6.7-6.8 + vitamin solution
//   post-autoclaving.
//   YCFA showed the largest richness increase (up to 410%)
//   over plate cultures (p<0.005, Mann-Whitney U test).
//   Notable lack of Bacteroidetes on YCFA plates (competitive
//   exclusion) was abolished in droplets (phyla-broad growth).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ycfaCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
ycfaMedium    = dispense 1 units of YCFA_Medium
ycfaOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

ycfaPreEmulsion  = mix ycfaCells with ycfaMedium for 5s
ycfaEmulsion     = mix ycfaPreEmulsion with ycfaOil for 5s

heat ycfaEmulsion at 37c for 2880m

ycfaCultSignal   = detect imagingODDetection on ycfaEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: YCFA cultivation QC gate
// Pass (BB11): ycfaCultSignal > 0 -> growth detected; extract
//              DNA and sequence.
// Fail (BB12): ycfaCultSignal <= 0 -> no growth; drain.
// Both converge at BB13 (ycfaCultJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ycfaCultSignal > 0) {
    pfo3               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer3         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedYCFA    = mix ycfaEmulsion with pfo3 for 1m
    extractedDNA_YCFA  = mix demulsifiedYCFA with dnaBuffer3 for 1m

    ycfaSeqSignal      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_YCFA for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_YCFA
    dispose ycfaSeqSignal
} else {
    drain ycfaEmulsion
}

dispose ycfaCultSignal

// ============================================================
// BB13: ycfaCultJoin
// All rich media cultivation arms complete.
// Control falls into antibiotic resistance screening arm.
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: ANTIBIOTIC RESISTANCE SCREENING IN DROPLETS
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 1: Ampicillin resistance screening.
//   BHIS medium supplemented with ampicillin at 100 ug/mL.
//   Concentration chosen to be commensurate with commercially
//   available antibiotic selection plates (Boente et al. 2010).
//   Same fecal cell suspension; same Poisson loading (200x
//   dilution); same droplet volume range (65-115 pL).
//   Cultured for 1 day (1440 min) inside the anaerobic chamber.
//   After incubation: optical density-based sorting removes
//   empty droplets (dead/nonviable cells) so that only droplets
//   with a grown colony contribute to sequencing reads.
//   Plate control: stool diluted 10000x; plated on BHIS +
//   ampicillin; cultured 3 days; DNA from plate scraping.
//   Result: 21 total unique resistant organisms detected only
//   in droplets across all three antibiotics.
//   Ampicillin droplets recovered known Bacteroides spp. and
//   Parabacteroides spp. resistance (Boente et al. 2010) and
//   revealed novel Pseudomonas spp. and Shewanella spp.
//   resistance undetected on plates.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ampCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
ampMedium    = dispense 1 units of Ampicillin_BHIS
ampOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

ampPreEmulsion  = mix ampCells with ampMedium for 5s
ampEmulsion     = mix ampPreEmulsion with ampOil for 5s

// 1 day incubation = 1440 min.
heat ampEmulsion at 37c for 1440m

// Sort to remove dead/nonviable droplets (OD < 0.3).
// Only colony-containing droplets enter the sequencing step.
ampResistSignal = detect waveletODSorting on ampEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: Ampicillin screen QC gate
// Pass (BB14): ampResistSignal > 0 -> resistant colonies
//              detected and sorted; extract DNA, sequence.
// Fail (BB15): ampResistSignal <= 0 -> no viable colonies
//              in ampicillin droplets; drain.
// Both converge at BB16 (ampScreenJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ampResistSignal > 0) {
    pfo4               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer4         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedAMP     = mix ampEmulsion with pfo4 for 1m
    extractedDNA_AMP   = mix demulsifiedAMP with dnaBuffer4 for 1m

    ampSeqSignal       = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_AMP for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_AMP
    dispose ampSeqSignal
} else {
    drain ampEmulsion
}

dispose ampResistSignal

// ============================================================
// BB16: ampScreenJoin
// Ampicillin screen complete. Control falls into ciprofloxacin arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 2: Ciprofloxacin resistance screening.
//   BHIS medium supplemented with ciprofloxacin at 5 ug/mL.
//   Fluoroquinolone class antibiotic; concentration commensurate
//   with commercially available selection plates.
//   Expected resistors: Enterococcus spp. and Enterobacteriaceae
//   (Hooper 2002; Paterson 2006). Gram-positive bacteria show
//   reduced susceptibility (Poole 2000).
//   Droplet screening also reveals Bacteroides spp. and
//   Parabacteroides spp. fluoroquinolone resistance
//   (Snydman et al. 2017) undetected on plates.
//   Plate control: 4 Clostridium spp. showed higher growth on
//   plates than droplets (only 5 organisms total showed plate
//   preference across all 3 antibiotics).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ciproCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
ciproMedium    = dispense 1 units of Ciprofloxacin_BHIS
ciproOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

ciproPreEmulsion  = mix ciproCells with ciproMedium for 5s
ciproEmulsion     = mix ciproPreEmulsion with ciproOil for 5s

heat ciproEmulsion at 37c for 1440m

ciproResistSignal = detect waveletODSorting on ciproEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB17 / BB18: Ciprofloxacin screen QC gate
// Pass (BB17): ciproResistSignal > 0 -> resistant colonies
//              detected and sorted; extract DNA, sequence.
// Fail (BB18): ciproResistSignal <= 0 -> no viable colonies;
//              drain.
// Both converge at BB19 (ciproScreenJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ciproResistSignal > 0) {
    pfo5               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer5         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedCIPRO   = mix ciproEmulsion with pfo5 for 1m
    extractedDNA_CIPRO = mix demulsifiedCIPRO with dnaBuffer5 for 1m

    ciproSeqSignal     = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_CIPRO for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_CIPRO
    dispose ciproSeqSignal
} else {
    drain ciproEmulsion
}

dispose ciproResistSignal

// ============================================================
// BB19: ciproScreenJoin
// Ciprofloxacin screen complete. Control falls into vancomycin arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 3: Vancomycin resistance screening.
//   BHIS medium supplemented with vancomycin at 10 ug/mL.
//   Concentration commensurate with commercially available
//   selection plates.
//   Expected resistors: Enterobacteriaceae gen. spp. (intrinsic
//   resistance; Citron et al. 2012).
//   Droplet screening additionally revealed Pseudomonas spp.
//   and Shewanella spp. (Shewanella is a known progenitor of
//   antibiotic resistance genes in humans; Yousfi et al. 2017)
//   resistant to vancomycin -- organisms undetected on plates.
//   These 21 unique droplet-only resistant organisms represent
//   a significant extension of the plate-based assessment.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

vancoCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
vancoMedium    = dispense 1 units of Vancomycin_BHIS
vancoOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

vancoPreEmulsion  = mix vancoCells with vancoMedium for 5s
vancoEmulsion     = mix vancoPreEmulsion with vancoOil for 5s

heat vancoEmulsion at 37c for 1440m

vancoResistSignal = detect waveletODSorting on vancoEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB20 / BB21: Vancomycin screen QC gate
// Pass (BB20): vancoResistSignal > 0 -> resistant colonies
//              detected and sorted; extract DNA, sequence.
// Fail (BB21): vancoResistSignal <= 0 -> no viable colonies;
//              drain.
// Both converge at BB22 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (vancoResistSignal > 0) {
    pfo6               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer6         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedVANCO   = mix vancoEmulsion with pfo6 for 1m
    extractedDNA_VANCO = mix demulsifiedVANCO with dnaBuffer6 for 1m

    vancoSeqSignal     = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_VANCO for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_VANCO
    dispose vancoSeqSignal
} else {
    drain vancoEmulsion
}

dispose vancoResistSignal

// ============================================================
// BB22: finalCleanup (terminal)
// All protocol arms complete. No further instructions.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module colonyDensityDetection
module sixteenSrRNASequencing
module dropletViabilityDetection

manifest FetalCellSuspension
manifest BHIS_Medium
manifest GMM_Medium
manifest YCFA_Medium
manifest FC40_Oil
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant
manifest PFO_BreakingAgent
manifest FDA_PI_Stain
manifest ASF_FecalPellet
manifest BHIS_ASF_Medium
manifest DNAExtractionKit

instructions:

// ============================================================
// High-throughput Isolation and Sorting of Gut Microbes
// Reduce Biases of Traditional Cultivation Strategies
// Watterson et al., bioRxiv 2019 (doi: 10.1101/759969)
// Tay Lab / Eren Lab, University of Chicago
//
// Platform: Droplet microfluidic devices operated inside a
// vinyl anaerobic chamber (Coy Lab Products) supplied with
// 86% N2 / 10% O2 / 4% H2. O2 < 1 ppm maintained throughout.
// Droplets: ~65-115 pL picoliter droplets generated at a
// flow-focusing junction from liquid culture medium into oil
// (Bio-Rad Droplet Generation Oil for EvaGreen).
// Encapsulation: Fecal cell suspensions diluted such that
// ~20-30% of droplets contain exactly 1 live bacterial cell
// (Poisson statistics). Sorting: image-based wavelet OD
// measurement at ~30 Hz; no fluorescent reporters required.
//
// PROTOCOL STRUCTURE:
//   Phase 1 -- ASF model community validation (mouse gut,
//              8-species Altered Schaedler's Flora).
//   Phase 2 -- Human stool cultivation across 3 rich media
//              (BHIS, GMM, YCFA) vs. conventional agar plates.
//   Phase 3 -- Slow-growing colony sorting by colony density
//              (wavelet OD between 0.3 and 0.7) to further
//              amplify rare/low-abundance taxa (<1% in raw
//              stool amplified to >1% in sorted fraction).
//   Phase 4 -- Viability confirmation: streaking sorted
//              droplets onto agar plates for colony growth.
//
// NOTE ON ANAEROBIC ABSTRACTION: All `heat` statements at
// 37c model incubation inside the anaerobic chamber incubator.
// `mix` steps abstract microfluidic droplet generation and
// encapsulation events, not DMF electrode mixing.
//
// NOTE ON SORTING ABSTRACTION: The wavelet OD-based sorting
// (LabView, Basler camera at 925 Hz, 672x360 px, 59 us
// exposure; biorthogonal 3.1 wavelets, LLH subband) is
// abstracted as a `detect colonyDensityDetection` call
// followed by an if/else QC gate. Slow-growing colonies
// satisfy: 0.3 < waveletOD < 0.7.
//
// NOTE ON 16S AMPLICON ABSTRACTION: Post-cultivation DNA
// extraction (PFO emulsion break, DNeasy kit) and 16S V4
// amplicon sequencing (Illumina MiSeq 2x300 paired-end,
// primers from Caporaso et al. 2012) followed by MED/
// oligotyping analysis are abstracted as `detect
// sixteenSrRNASequencing` calls.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- anaerobic chamber init; ASF
//                             pure-strain droplet culture;
//                             ASF mixed-community culture;
//                             human stool BHIS droplets;
//                             human stool GMM droplets;
//                             human stool YCFA droplets;
//                             community richness QC gate
//   BB2  richnessPass      -- richnessSignal > 0: richness
//                             increase confirmed (droplets
//                             > plates); proceed to sorting
//   BB3  richnessFail      -- richnessSignal <= 0: no richness
//                             gain; drain cultivation output
//   BB4  richnessJoin      -- join: slow-grower sorting branch
//   BB5  sortingPass       -- sortingSignal > 0: low-density
//                             colonies successfully sorted;
//                             proceed to viability check
//   BB6  sortingFail       -- sortingSignal <= 0: no slow-
//                             growing colonies in fraction;
//                             drain sorted emulsion
//   BB7  sortingJoin       -- join: viability confirmation
//   BB8  viabilityPass     -- viabilitySignal > 0: bacteria
//                             viable after droplet cultivation;
//                             streak onto agar; dispose
//   BB9  viabilityFail     -- viabilitySignal <= 0: viability
//                             lost; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 1: Prime anaerobic chamber and microfluidic
//   device with FC-40 oil to establish anaerobic environment.
//   O2 < 1 ppm, H2 between 1.5-2.5% maintained throughout.
//   Devices fabricated by soft lithography (SU-8 3050 molds,
//   50 um channel height, PDMS bonded to glass). Channels
//   hydrophobized with Aquapel then Fluorinert FC-40.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPrime      = dispense 1 units of FC40_Oil
surfactantPrime = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
devicePrime   = mix oilPrime with surfactantPrime for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 2: Prepare ASF model community from fecal
//   pellet (Taconic Biosciences). Dissociate 3 fecal pellets
//   in 5 mL BHIS-ASF medium, sediment fecal solids, collect
//   supernatant, store at -80 C in 25% glycerol/25% BHIS/
//   50% cell suspension. Dilute 50x for droplet generation.
//   Note: ASF 360 (L. intestinalis) not detected in pellets;
//   7 of 8 strains confirmed by species-specific PCR.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

asfFecalStock  = dispense 1 units of ASF_FecalPellet
asfMedium      = dispense 1 units of BHIS_ASF_Medium
asfDiluted     = mix asfFecalStock with asfMedium for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 3: Generate ASF community droplets in anaerobic
//   chamber. Flow-focusing junction encapsulates ~20-30%
//   droplets with a single ASF cell (Poisson statistics).
//   Droplet volume: ~65-115 pL. Oil phase: HFE7500 with
//   2% surfactant. Droplet generation rate: ~0.5-1 mL
//   emulsion in 20 min to 1 hr.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

asfOilPhase    = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
asfDroplets    = mix asfDiluted with asfOilPhase for 3s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 4: Incubate ASF droplets at 37 C for 24 h
//   inside anaerobic chamber incubator. Single cells grow
//   clonally within confined droplet volumes, preventing
//   competitive overgrowth of fast-growing ASF 361
//   (L. murinus) over ASF 519 (P. goldsteinii) as occurs
//   in bulk broth. Extremely oxygen-sensitive species (ASF
//   356, 492, 500, 502) maintained below 1 ppm O2.
//   24 h = 1440 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat asfDroplets at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 5: Quantify ASF community composition by
//   droplet digital PCR (BioRad QX200). Species-specific
//   primers from Sarma-Rupavtarm et al. (2004). ddPCR mix:
//   10 uL QX200 ddPCR EvaGreen Supermix, 200 nM each primer,
//   thermocycle: 94 C 10 min; 35 cycles (94 C 1 min,
//   60 C 1 min, 72 C 2 min). Break emulsion with PFO before
//   DNA extraction (DNeasy Blood & Tissue Kit, 100 uL elution).
//   Expected: ASF 361 dominates bulk broth; droplets confine
//   ASF 361 and allow ASF 457 (34%) and ASF 519 (0.96%) to
//   reach higher relative abundance.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

asfBreakingAgent = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
asfKit           = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
asfBroken        = mix asfDroplets with asfBreakingAgent for 2s
asfDNA           = mix asfBroken with asfKit for 30m
asfComposition   = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on asfDNA for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 1: Prepare human fecal cell suspension for
//   droplet cultivation. Single stool sample from FMT donor
//   (IRB 132-0212, University of Chicago). Aliquots spun
//   down in PBS, supernatant stored at -80 C. Live cell
//   density: 1e9/mL; dead cell density: 3e9/mL (BacLight
//   Live/Dead assay). Dilute 200x for Poisson-based single-
//   cell encapsulation (~20-30% droplets with 1 live cell).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Three separate stool aliquots dispensed -- one per media arm.
// Each aliquot is an independent 200x-diluted glycerol stock
// unit; dispensing separately avoids reuse of a consumed variable
// across the three parallel cultivation branches.
humanStoolBhis   = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
humanStoolGmm    = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
humanStoolYcfa   = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 2: Generate BHIS droplets from human stool.
//   Brain Heart Infusion Supplemented (BHIS) medium: 500 mL
//   water, 18.5 g BHI broth, 2.5 g yeast extract, 0.25 g
//   L-cysteine, vitamin K (0.1% in 95% ethanol), hemin
//   (5 mg/mL in 0.1 M NaOH). Spread 100 uL stool on agar
//   plates (parallel control, 7-day culture). Droplets:
//   0.5-1 mL emulsion of ~65-115 pL droplets (4-15 million
//   droplets). Incubate 2 days for droplets, 7 days for plates.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisMedium       = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
bhisOil          = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
bhisSuspension   = mix humanStoolBhis with bhisMedium for 2s
bhisDroplets     = mix bhisSuspension with bhisOil for 3s

heat bhisDroplets at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 3: Generate GMM droplets from human stool.
//   Gut Microbiota Medium (GMM) prepared per Goodman et al.
//   2011 (PNAS 108:6252). Second arm of parallel cultivation.
//   Incubate 2 days inside anaerobic chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gmmMedium        = dispense 1 units of GMM_Medium
gmmOil           = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
gmmSuspension    = mix humanStoolGmm with gmmMedium for 2s
gmmDroplets      = mix gmmSuspension with gmmOil for 3s

heat gmmDroplets at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 4: Generate YCFA droplets from human stool.
//   Yeast Casitones Fatty Acid (YCFA, modified DSMZ 1611):
//   10 g casitone, 2.5 g yeast extract, 5 g dextrose,
//   short-chain fatty acids (acetic, propionic, isobutyric,
//   n-valeric, iso-valeric acids), NaHCO3, L-cysteine-HCl,
//   hemin, mucin, vitamin solution (biotin, folate,
//   pyridoxine-HCl, thiamine-HCl, riboflavin, nicotinic
//   acid, pantothenate, B12, PABA, thioctic acid).
//   pH 6.7-6.8. Incubate 2 days inside anaerobic chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ycfaMedium       = dispense 1 units of YCFA_Medium
ycfaOil          = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
ycfaSuspension   = mix humanStoolYcfa with ycfaMedium for 2s
ycfaDroplets     = mix ycfaSuspension with ycfaOil for 3s

heat ycfaDroplets at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 5: Break emulsions and extract DNA from all
//   three droplet cultures. Add equal part PFO to emulsion,
//   vortex and centrifuge, remove oil+PFO phase. Extract
//   DNA from aqueous layer using DNeasy Blood & Tissue Kit
//   (Qiagen); total elution volume: 100 uL per sample.
//   16S V4 amplicon sequencing (Illumina MiSeq 2x300,
//   primers from Caporaso et al. 2012) performed at Argonne
//   National Laboratory ESPSF. 35 PCR cycles; paired-end
//   joining in illumina-utils (min overlap 45 nt, <2
//   mismatches); ASVs inferred by MED/oligotyping v2.1;
//   taxonomy by GAST.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisBreaker      = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
gmmBreaker       = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
ycfaBreaker      = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent

bhisBroken       = mix bhisDroplets with bhisBreaker for 2s
gmmBroken        = mix gmmDroplets with gmmBreaker for 2s
ycfaBroken       = mix ycfaDroplets with ycfaBreaker for 2s

bhisKit          = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
gmmKit           = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
ycfaKit          = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit

bhisDNA          = mix bhisBroken with bhisKit for 30m
gmmDNA           = mix gmmBroken with gmmKit for 30m
ycfaDNA          = mix ycfaBroken with ycfaKit for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 6: 16S rRNA amplicon sequencing of all
//   three media conditions. MED decomposition identifies
//   ASVs with single-nucleotide resolution. Richness (R),
//   Shannon index (H'), and low-abundance ASV count (Rlow,
//   for ASVs < 1% in raw stool) computed per sample.
//   Expected: 37% (BHIS) to 410% (YCFA) richness increase
//   in droplets vs. agar plates (p < 0.005, Mann-Whitney U).
//   Bacteroides oligotype clustering closer to raw stool
//   in droplet cultures (p < 0.005, multiscale bootstrap).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisProfile      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on bhisDNA for 30s
gmmProfile       = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on gmmDNA for 30s
ycfaProfile      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on ycfaDNA for 30s

// Combine media profiles for richness QC gate.
// richnessSignal > 0 confirms droplets exceed plates in
// community richness across all three media conditions.
combinedProfiles   = mix bhisProfile with gmmProfile for 5s
richnessMeasure    = mix combinedProfiles with ycfaProfile for 5s
richnessSignal     = detect colonyDensityDetection on richnessMeasure for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Richness QC gate
// Pass (BB2): richnessSignal > 0 -> droplet richness confirmed
//             greater than plate richness across media;
//             proceed to slow-grower sorting (Phase 3).
// Fail (BB3): richnessSignal <= 0 -> no richness advantage
//             detected; drain cultivation output.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (richnessJoin).
// ============================================================

if (richnessSignal > 0) {
    dispose bhisDNA
    dispose gmmDNA
    dispose ycfaDNA
} else {
    drain bhisDNA
    drain gmmDNA
    drain ycfaDNA
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: richnessJoin
// Dispose richness QC measurements. Control passes to
// Phase 3 slow-grower sorting branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose richnessSignal
dispose bhisProfile
dispose gmmProfile
dispose ycfaProfile

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3, STEP 1: Prepare fresh BHIS droplet emulsion for
//   wavelet OD-based slow-grower sorting. Two independent
//   sorting experiments performed on human stool in BHIS
//   droplets. Droplets reinjected at 20 uL/hr with oil
//   spacing phase at 180 uL/hr. High-frame-rate camera
//   (Basler acA640-750um, 925 Hz, 672x360 px, 59 us exposure)
//   captures droplet image at sorting junction. Custom
//   LabView code applies biorthogonal 3.1 discrete wavelet
//   frame decomposition (Low Low High subband, 15x15 px
//   window, step 5 px, 15 gray levels, 3x3 px displacement).
//   Wavelet OD normalized 0 (empty) to 1 (dense colony).
//   Slow-growing colonies: 0.3 < waveletOD < 0.7.
//   Dense colonies: waveletOD > 0.7 -> waste path.
//   Empty droplets: waveletOD < 0.3 -> waste path.
//   Sorting rate: ~30 Hz. Electrode actuation: 10 kHz,
//   800 V p-p, 30% duty cycle, 10 ms per sort event.
//   False-positive sorting rate: at most 8% upper bound.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortingStool     = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
bhisSortMedium   = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
bhisSortOil      = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
sortSuspension   = mix sortingStool with bhisSortMedium for 2s
sortDroplets     = mix sortSuspension with bhisSortOil for 3s

heat sortDroplets at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3, STEP 2: Image-based sorting via wavelet OD.
//   colonyDensityDetection module abstracts LabView wavelet
//   image analysis and electrode deflection of slow-growers
//   into the "keep" path. Sorted fraction: ~1-10 uL total
//   volume (thin layer on oil; estimated by pipetting).
//   Sorting signal > 0 indicates slow-growing colonies
//   detected and successfully deflected to keep channel.
//   Expected amplification: 6.5 ASVs amplified from <1% to
//   >1% (unsorted) vs. 12.5 ASVs (sorted) out of 158 total
//   ASVs; taxa span wider phylogenetic range after sorting.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortingSignal = detect colonyDensityDetection on sortDroplets for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Sorting QC gate
// Pass (BB5): sortingSignal > 0 -> slow-growing colonies
//             detected in keep path; proceed to DNA extraction
//             and viability confirmation (Phase 4).
// Fail (BB6): sortingSignal <= 0 -> no qualifying low-density
//             droplets found; drain sorted emulsion.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (sortingJoin).
// ============================================================

if (sortingSignal > 0) {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    // PHASE 3, STEP 3 (pass path): Break sorted droplet emulsion
    //   and extract DNA. Due to low sorting rate (~30 Hz) the
    //   total sorted volume is only ~1-10 uL. Add 150 uL DNA-
    //   free water + 150 uL PFO to sorted emulsion, vortex,
    //   centrifuge. Extract with DNeasy kit. Sequence with same
    //   16S V4 protocol as unsorted samples. Kolmogorov-Smirnov
    //   test confirms shift in rank-abundance distribution
    //   between sorted and unsorted (p < 0.005).
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    sortedBreaker    = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
    sortedKit        = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
    sortedBroken     = mix sortDroplets with sortedBreaker for 2s
    sortedDNA        = mix sortedBroken with sortedKit for 30m
    sortedProfile    = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on sortedDNA for 30s
    dispose sortedDNA
    dispose sortedProfile
} else {
    drain sortDroplets
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: sortingJoin
// Dispose sorting QC signal. Control passes to Phase 4
// viability confirmation branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose sortingSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4, STEP 1: Confirm bacterial viability post-sorting.
//   Streak ~10 uL sorted droplet emulsion + oil onto BHIS
//   agar plate. Culture at 37 C for 2 days (2880 min).
//   Random picking of 24 colonies for Sanger sequencing
//   (27F/1492R primers, GoTaq Green Master Mix, 95 C 3 min;
//   30 cycles: 95 C 30 s, 54 C 30 s, 72 C 1 min; 72 C 10 min).
//   16S amplicons excised from 2% agarose gel, purified with
//   QIAquick Gel Extraction Kit (Qiagen), Sanger sequenced
//   (U. Chicago Comprehensive Cancer Center facility).
//   BLAST taxonomy assignment: Hafnia (12/24), Enterococcus
//   (8/24), Bacteroides (4/24).
//   FDA/PI live-dead staining (BacLight, ThermoFisher) used
//   as viability readout proxy in dropletViabilityDetection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortedForViability  = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
bhisAgarMedium      = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
platedSorted        = mix sortedForViability with bhisAgarMedium for 2s

heat platedSorted at 37c for 2880m

fdaPI_Stain         = dispense 1 units of FDA_PI_Stain
stainedPlated       = mix platedSorted with fdaPI_Stain for 10m

viabilitySignal     = detect dropletViabilityDetection on stainedPlated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Viability confirmation gate
// Pass (BB8): viabilitySignal > 0 -> colonies viable post-
//             sorting (Hafnia, Enterococcus, Bacteroides
//             confirmed by Sanger sequencing); dispose.
// Fail (BB9): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> no viable growth
//             observed on agar; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedPlated
    dispose platedSorted
} else {
    drain stainedPlated
    drain platedSorted
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends. Pure strain isolates confirmed viable
// and compatible with downstream microbiology workflows.
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal
dispose asfComposition
dispose asfDNA
dispose richnessMeasure
dispose combinedProfiles

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module proxSeqDetection
module viabilityDetection
module plaDetection
module seqLibraryQC

manifest JurkatCells
manifest RajiCells
manifest PBS
manifest ProxSeqProbeA
manifest ProxSeqProbeB
manifest FreeOligoA
manifest FreeOligoB
manifest LigationBuffer
manifest Ligase
manifest BlockingBuffer
manifest WashBuffer
manifest DNALibraryBuffer
manifest SequencingReagent
manifest IsotypeControlAntibody
manifest StopSolution

// ============================================================
// Computational Prediction of Protein Interactions in Single
// Cells by Proximity Sequencing.
// Xia J, Phan HV, Vistain L, Chen M, Khan AA, Tay S (2024)
// PLoS Comput Biol 20(3): e1011915.
// DOI: 10.1371/journal.pcbi.1011915
//
// This BioScript file encodes the experimental Prox-seq
// (Proximity Sequencing) protocol as described in the paper.
// Prox-seq simultaneously measures gene expression, protein
// expression, and protein complexes on single cells using a
// proximity ligation assay (PLA) with DNA-conjugated antibody
// probes (Probe A and Probe B). Ligation occurs only when
// two protein molecules are within 50-70 nm of each other.
// PLA products are sequenced alongside scRNA-seq cDNA
// libraries to yield multi-omic single-cell data.
//
// TWO CELL LINE ARMS encoded in sequence:
//   ARM 1: Jurkat T cells (CD3, CD28, PD1, CD147, ICAM1,
//           PDL1, HLADR, B7 protein panel)
//   ARM 2: Raji B cells (same probe panel, different
//           protein complex landscape)
//
// FREE OLIGO MODIFICATION: An experimentally modified
// Prox-seq procedure measures non-proximal (unligated)
// probes via FreeOligoA and FreeOligoB. These non-proximal
// counts are used by the linear regression (LR) method and
// ensemble method for proximity noise estimation.
//
// ISOTYPE CONTROL: IsotypeControlAntibody with
// oligonucleotide conjugation is included in both probe
// panels to estimate nonspecific antibody binding
// probability directly from observed data (Section 2.2).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: cell prep, Prox-seq
//                             probe staining, ligation, and
//                             library prep for Jurkat arm
//   BB2  jurkatLibPass     -- jurkatLibSignal > 0: library
//                             QC passed; dispose and proceed
//   BB3  jurkatLibFail     -- jurkatLibSignal <= 0: library
//                             failed; drain Jurkat products
//   BB4  jurkatLibJoin     -- join: Raji B cell arm begins
//   BB5  rajiLibPass       -- rajiLibSignal > 0: library
//                             QC passed; dispose Raji products
//   BB6  rajiLibFail       -- rajiLibSignal <= 0: library
//                             failed; drain Raji products
//   BB7  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signals;
//                             experiment ends; data sent for
//                             computational analysis
//
// NOTE ON LIGATION DISTANCE: The BioScript ligation step
// is abstracted via `mix`. Physical ligation occurs in the
// 50-70 nm proximity window defined by the DNA oligo linker
// length. Only Probe A + Probe B pairs within this distance
// produce a PLA product (dual-barcode requirement enforced
// at sequencing alignment stage, not modelled here).
//
// NOTE ON UMI COUNTING: PLA product quantification by
// counting unique molecular identifiers (UMIs) is performed
// computationally (off-chip, Python3/Anaconda3 v4.10.3).
// Code: https://github.com/tay-lab/Prox-seq_computation
// Raw data: GEO accession GSE196130.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports `s` (seconds)
// and `m` (minutes) only. All incubation times are
// expressed accordingly.
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 1: Prepare Jurkat T cell suspension.
//   Jurkat cells cultured under standard conditions.
//   Resuspend in PBS at appropriate concentration for
//   single-cell staining with Prox-seq probe panel.
//   Isotype control antibody included in probe panel
//   to estimate nonspecific binding background (Section 2.2).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

jurkatCells       = dispense 1 units of JurkatCells
cellPBS           = dispense 1 units of PBS
jurkatSuspension  = mix jurkatCells with cellPBS for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 2: Block nonspecific binding sites.
//   Incubate cells with blocking buffer for 10 min at 4 C
//   prior to Prox-seq probe addition. This reduces background
//   from nonspecific antibody binding (Section 2.2).
//   Paper notes nonspecific binding constitutes <1% of
//   both-specific PLA counts for extracellular proteins
//   (e.g. CD147:CD147 in Jurkat cells, S4 Fig).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

blockingBuf       = dispense 1 units of BlockingBuffer
blockedCells      = mix jurkatSuspension with blockingBuf for 10m
heat blockedCells at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 3: Stain with Prox-seq Probe A panel.
//   Each target protein is stained with a DNA-conjugated
//   Probe A antibody. Panel targets: CD3, CD28, PD1, CD147,
//   ICAM1, PDL1, HLADR, B7 (same panel as Ref [4]).
//   Isotype control antibody (oligonucleotide-conjugated)
//   included in Probe A panel for nonspecific binding QC.
//   Incubate 30 min at 4 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeAStain       = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeA
isotypeControl    = dispense 1 units of IsotypeControlAntibody
probeAWithControl = mix probeAStain with isotypeControl for 5s
probeAStained     = mix blockedCells with probeAWithControl for 30m
heat probeAStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 4: Wash to remove unbound Probe A.
//   Wash cells 3x with PBS to remove excess unbound
//   Probe A antibodies. Unbound probes do not contribute
//   to PLA signal because library preparation and sequence
//   alignment require barcodes from both Probe A and B.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1A = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2A = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3A = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

washedA1 = mix probeAStained with wash1A for 2m
washedA2 = mix washedA1 with wash2A for 2m
jurkatProbeAReady = mix washedA2 with wash3A for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 5: Stain with Prox-seq Probe B panel.
//   Each target protein is stained with a DNA-conjugated
//   Probe B antibody (same protein targets as Probe A panel).
//   Isotype control antibody (oligonucleotide-conjugated)
//   included in Probe B panel as well.
//   Incubate 30 min at 4 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeBStain       = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeB
probeBStained     = mix jurkatProbeAReady with probeBStain for 30m
heat probeBStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 6: Wash to remove unbound Probe B.
//   Wash 3x with PBS. After washing, cells carry both
//   Probe A and Probe B antibodies on surface proteins.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1B = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2B = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3B = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

washedB1 = mix probeBStained with wash1B for 2m
washedB2 = mix washedB1 with wash2B for 2m
jurkatDualStained = mix washedB2 with wash3B for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 7: Add Free Oligo probes (non-proximal
//   probe measurement modification).
//   FreeOligoA and FreeOligoB are added to measure the
//   non-proximal (unligated) probe counts. Free oligos
//   are not conjugated to antibodies; they generate
//   PLA products of the form:
//     Protein_X : free_oligo_B  (counts non-proximal Probe A)
//     free_oligo_A : Protein_Y  (counts non-proximal Probe B)
//   These non-proximal counts are essential for the LR
//   method and ensemble method (Section: LR method, Eq. 5).
//   Reference: Vistain et al. Nat Methods 2022 [4].
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freeOligoADrop = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoA
freeOligoBDrop = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoB

freeOligoMix = mix freeOligoADrop with freeOligoBDrop for 5s
jurkatWithFreeOligos = mix jurkatDualStained with freeOligoMix for 10m
heat jurkatWithFreeOligos at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 8: Proximity ligation reaction.
//   Add ligation buffer and T4 DNA ligase. Ligation occurs
//   between Probe A oligo and Probe B oligo only when the
//   two probes are within 50-70 nm of each other (i.e.,
//   their target proteins are co-localised or in complex).
//   Ligation distance threshold = 50 nm in simulation model.
//   Incubate at room temperature (25 C) for 30 min.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the proximity ligation event.
//   PLA products (ligated A+B barcodes) are the signal.
//   Random co-localisation generates proximity noise:
//   E(X_ij) = (d_ligation^2 / 4R^2) * A_i * B_j
//   (Methods: Theoretical calculation of proximity noise).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligBuf            = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligase            = dispense 1 units of Ligase
ligationReagents  = mix ligBuf with ligase for 5s
jurkatLigated     = mix jurkatWithFreeOligos with ligationReagents for 30m
heat jurkatLigated at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 9: Stop ligation and wash.
//   Add stop solution to quench ligase activity.
//   Wash 3x with PBS to remove ligation reagents prior
//   to single-cell encapsulation / library preparation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stopSol       = dispense 1 units of StopSolution
jurkatStopped = mix jurkatLigated with stopSol for 5m

wash1L = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2L = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3L = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

washedL1 = mix jurkatStopped with wash1L for 2m
washedL2 = mix washedL1 with wash2L for 2m
jurkatLigatedReady = mix washedL2 with wash3L for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 10: Single-cell encapsulation and
//   library preparation (scRNA-seq + Prox-seq).
//   Cells are encapsulated in individual droplets (10x
//   Genomics or equivalent microfluidic platform) and
//   lysed. mRNA is captured by poly-dT oligonucleotides.
//   PLA products are captured by their barcoded sequences.
//   cDNA (gene expression) and PLA product libraries are
//   generated simultaneously and sequenced together.
//   DNA library buffer is added to prepare the combined
//   library for sequencing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dnaLibBuf        = dispense 1 units of DNALibraryBuffer
jurkatLibPrep    = mix jurkatLigatedReady with dnaLibBuf for 30m
heat jurkatLibPrep at 37c for 30m

seqReagentJ      = dispense 1 units of SequencingReagent
jurkatSeqReady   = mix jurkatLibPrep with seqReagentJ for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 11: Library QC detection.
//   QC check on the Jurkat Prox-seq library before
//   sequencing. Checks for adequate library complexity,
//   correct fragment sizes for PLA products and cDNA,
//   and sufficient UMI diversity.
//   proxSeqDetection module abstracts fluorometric/
//   electrophoretic QC (e.g. Bioanalyzer, Qubit).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

jurkatLibSignal = detect seqLibraryQC on jurkatSeqReady for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Jurkat library QC gate
// Pass (BB2): jurkatLibSignal > 0 -> library QC passed;
//             dispose Jurkat library products and proceed
//             to Raji B cell arm.
// Fail (BB3): jurkatLibSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed
//             (low complexity, wrong fragment sizes, or
//             insufficient UMIs); drain Jurkat products.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (jurkatLibJoin).
// ============================================================

if (jurkatLibSignal > 0) {
    dispose jurkatSeqReady
} else {
    drain jurkatSeqReady
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: jurkatLibJoin
// Dispose Jurkat library QC signal. Control falls into
// Raji B cell arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose jurkatLibSignal

// ============================================================
// ARM 2: Raji B Cell Prox-seq Protocol
// Identical probe panel and procedural steps as Jurkat arm.
// Raji cells express ICAM1 (known homodimer on cell surface,
// Ref [14]), HLADR, PDL1 among other panel proteins.
// The ensemble method recovers ICAM1:ICAM1 complex
// in Raji cells (Fig 5d-f, paper Section: Comparison of
// all three analytical methods to real data).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 1: Prepare Raji B cell suspension.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rajiCells        = dispense 1 units of RajiCells
cellPBS2         = dispense 1 units of PBS
rajiSuspension   = mix rajiCells with cellPBS2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 2: Block nonspecific binding sites.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

blockingBuf2     = dispense 1 units of BlockingBuffer
rajiBlocked      = mix rajiSuspension with blockingBuf2 for 10m
heat rajiBlocked at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 3: Stain with Prox-seq Probe A panel.
//   Same panel as Jurkat arm (CD3, CD28, PD1, CD147,
//   ICAM1, PDL1, HLADR, B7 + isotype control).
//   Note: Raji cells do not express CD3 or PD1;
//   their PLA products for these targets are near zero,
//   validating specificity of the probe panel [4].
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeAStain2      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeA
isotypeControl2   = dispense 1 units of IsotypeControlAntibody
probeAWithCtrl2   = mix probeAStain2 with isotypeControl2 for 5s
rajiProbeAStained = mix rajiBlocked with probeAWithCtrl2 for 30m
heat rajiProbeAStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 4: Wash to remove unbound Probe A.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1A2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2A2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3A2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

rajiWashedA1 = mix rajiProbeAStained with wash1A2 for 2m
rajiWashedA2 = mix rajiWashedA1 with wash2A2 for 2m
rajiProbeAReady = mix rajiWashedA2 with wash3A2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 5: Stain with Prox-seq Probe B panel.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeBStain2      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeB
rajiProbeBStained = mix rajiProbeAReady with probeBStain2 for 30m
heat rajiProbeBStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 6: Wash to remove unbound Probe B.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1B2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2B2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3B2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

rajiWashedB1 = mix rajiProbeBStained with wash1B2 for 2m
rajiWashedB2 = mix rajiWashedB1 with wash2B2 for 2m
rajiDualStained = mix rajiWashedB2 with wash3B2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 7: Add Free Oligo probes.
//   Same free oligo modification as Jurkat arm.
//   Non-proximal probe counts for Raji cells are used
//   to calibrate proximity noise in the LR and ensemble
//   methods for Raji-specific protein complex detection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freeOligoA2    = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoA
freeOligoB2    = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoB
freeOligoMix2  = mix freeOligoA2 with freeOligoB2 for 5s
rajiWithFreeOligos = mix rajiDualStained with freeOligoMix2 for 10m
heat rajiWithFreeOligos at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 8: Proximity ligation reaction.
//   Same ligation conditions as Jurkat arm.
//   Ligation distance = 50 nm threshold.
//   Proximity noise for Raji arm:
//   E(X_ij) = (d_ligation^2 / 4R^2) * A_i * B_j
//   ICAM1:ICAM1 homodimer signal exceeds expected random
//   ligation background (Fig 5d-f, paper).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligBuf2           = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligase2           = dispense 1 units of Ligase
ligReagents2      = mix ligBuf2 with ligase2 for 5s
rajiLigated       = mix rajiWithFreeOligos with ligReagents2 for 30m
heat rajiLigated at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 9: Stop ligation and wash.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stopSol2       = dispense 1 units of StopSolution
rajiStopped    = mix rajiLigated with stopSol2 for 5m

wash1L2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2L2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3L2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

rajiWashedL1 = mix rajiStopped with wash1L2 for 2m
rajiWashedL2 = mix rajiWashedL1 with wash2L2 for 2m
rajiLigatedReady = mix rajiWashedL2 with wash3L2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 10: Single-cell encapsulation and
//   library preparation.
//   Same procedure as Jurkat arm.
//   Combined cDNA + PLA product library generated.
//   After sequencing, UMI counts per PLA product per
//   single Raji cell are the primary data for downstream
//   computational analysis (iterative, LR, ensemble methods).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dnaLibBuf2       = dispense 1 units of DNALibraryBuffer
rajiLibPrep      = mix rajiLigatedReady with dnaLibBuf2 for 30m
heat rajiLibPrep at 37c for 30m

seqReagentR      = dispense 1 units of SequencingReagent
rajiSeqReady     = mix rajiLibPrep with seqReagentR for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 11: Library QC detection.
//   Same QC procedure as Jurkat arm.
//   seqLibraryQC module abstracts Bioanalyzer/Qubit QC.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rajiLibSignal = detect seqLibraryQC on rajiSeqReady for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Raji library QC gate
// Pass (BB5): rajiLibSignal > 0 -> library QC passed;
//             dispose all Raji library products.
// Fail (BB6): rajiLibSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed;
//             drain all Raji products.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rajiLibSignal > 0) {
    dispose rajiSeqReady
} else {
    drain rajiSeqReady
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose library QC signals from both arms.
// Experiment ends. Sequencing data submitted to
// computational pipeline for proximity noise removal and
// protein complex prediction (iterative / LR / ensemble).
// Code: https://github.com/tay-lab/Prox-seq_computation
// Data: GEO GSE196130
// ============================================================

dispose rajiLibSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module libraryQCDetection

manifest PBS
manifest ATAC_RSB_Buffer
manifest Digitonin_2pct
manifest IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
manifest Tween20_10pct
manifest SUPERaseIN
manifest RNaseOUT
manifest PI_50X
manifest HEPES_1M
manifest NaCl_5M
manifest Spermidine_1M
manifest BSA_10pct
manifest EDTA_500mM
manifest MgCl2_250mM
manifest StopSolution_2X
manifest NucleiBuffer_20X
manifest DTT_100mM
manifest ATACBufferB
manifest BarcodingReagentMix
manifest TemplateSwitchOligo
manifest ReducingAgentB
manifest BarcodingEnzymeMix
manifest QuenchingAgent
manifest SPRIBeads
manifest DynaBeads
manifest PCRMasterMix
manifest AntiHistoneAntibody
manifest ProteinATn5_Assembled
manifest TargetCells

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Droplet-based Single-cell Joint Profiling of Histone
// Modification and Transcriptome (Droplet Paired-Tag)
// Xie Y., Zhu C., Wang Z., Tastemel M., Chang L., Li Y.E.,
// Ren B. -- Research Square preprint (2023)
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.pex-2310/v1
//
// Platform: 10x Chromium Next GEM Single Cell Multiome
// (ATAC + Gene Expression). pA-Tn5 tagmentation of histone
// modification epitopes (e.g. H3K27ac) combined with
// simultaneous RNA capture in droplets.
//
// PROTOCOL SCOPE: Three-day wet-lab workflow encoded as one
// representative cycle. Days are separated by comment headers.
// BioScript has no loop construct; one cycle is encoded by
// convention. Overnight incubation (Day 1 -> Day 2) is
// modelled as heat at 4c for 720m (12 h conservative minimum).
//
// DURATION CONVENTION: BioScript supports only `s` and `m`
// duration tokens (no `h`). All hour/overnight values are
// converted to minutes. Overnight ~ 720m (12 h).
//
// BUFFER CONSTRUCTION NOTE: OMNI lysis buffer and MED1/MED2
// high-salt buffers are freshly prepared from their component
// manifests at the start of each day. Each buffer is built
// via sequential mix steps from manifest-only dispenses.
// Where the same buffer is needed multiple times later in the
// protocol (e.g. MED1 for conjugation, MED1 for nuclei
// resuspension; MED2 for three wash/resuspend steps), each
// use-site builds a fresh instance from manifests directly --
// BioScript `dispense` is restricted to declared manifests
// and cannot draw from a computed mix variable.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- Day 1: buffer prep, pA-Tn5
//                            conjugation, nuclei lysis,
//                            overnight epitope targeting
//   BB2  main (cont.)     -- Day 2: tagmentation, droplet
//                            generation, RT + barcoding,
//                            product cleanup
//   BB3  main (cont.)     -- Day 3: pre-amplification,
//                            DNA/RNA library preparation
//   BB4  libraryPass      -- libraryQCSignal > 0: fragment
//                            size within spec; dispose
//   BB5  libraryFail      -- libraryQCSignal <= 0: library
//                            OOSpec; drain
//   BB6  finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose QC signal
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// DAY 1 -- PART A: Prepare OMNI Nuclei Lysis Buffer (instance 1)
// Used immediately for cell lysis in STEP A-3.
// Components (per 750 uL working volume):
//   693.75 uL ATAC-RSB buffer
//   7.5 uL Digitonin (2%)
//   7.5 uL IGEPAL-CA630 (10%)
//   7.5 uL Tween-20 (10%)
//   15 uL SUPERaseIN
//   7.5 uL RNaseOUT
//   15 uL 50X PI
// Mixed fresh before use; kept on ice.
// ============================================================

omni_base        = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer
omni_digitonin   = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
omni_igepal      = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
omni_tween       = dispense 1 units of Tween20_10pct
omni_supIn       = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
omni_rnaseOut    = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
omni_pi          = dispense 1 units of PI_50X

omni_mix1        = mix omni_base with omni_digitonin for 5s
omni_mix2        = mix omni_mix1 with omni_igepal for 5s
omni_mix3        = mix omni_mix2 with omni_tween for 5s
omni_mix4        = mix omni_mix3 with omni_supIn for 5s
omni_mix5        = mix omni_mix4 with omni_rnaseOut for 5s
omniBuffer       = mix omni_mix5 with omni_pi for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 1 -- PART A: Prepare MED Buffer #1 (MED1) -- instance 1
// Used for antibody-pA-Tn5 conjugation reaction (STEP A-2).
// High-salt buffer; components (per 1 mL):
//   20 uL HEPES (1 M, pH 7.5), 54.2 uL NaCl (5 M),
//   0.5 uL Spermidine (1 M), 20 uL 50X PI,
//   50 uL SUPERaseIN, 25 uL RNaseOUT,
//   1 uL IGEPAL-CA630 (10%), 5 uL Digitonin (2%),
//   4 uL EDTA (500 mM), 200 uL 10% BSA,
//   620.3 uL H2O (modelled as ATAC_RSB_Buffer diluent)
// NOTE: RNase inhibitor concentration doubled vs standard
// (per paper note; suitable for mouse embryos). For cultured
// cells or brain tissue, 50% of this concentration is tested
// to have no impact on RNA quality.
// ============================================================

m1a_hepes        = dispense 1 units of HEPES_1M
m1a_nacl         = dispense 1 units of NaCl_5M
m1a_spermidine   = dispense 1 units of Spermidine_1M
m1a_pi           = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
m1a_supIn        = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
m1a_rnaseOut     = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
m1a_igepal       = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
m1a_digitonin    = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
m1a_edta         = dispense 1 units of EDTA_500mM
m1a_bsa          = dispense 1 units of BSA_10pct
m1a_diluent      = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

m1a_mix1         = mix m1a_hepes with m1a_nacl for 5s
m1a_mix2         = mix m1a_mix1 with m1a_spermidine for 5s
m1a_mix3         = mix m1a_mix2 with m1a_pi for 5s
m1a_mix4         = mix m1a_mix3 with m1a_supIn for 5s
m1a_mix5         = mix m1a_mix4 with m1a_rnaseOut for 5s
m1a_mix6         = mix m1a_mix5 with m1a_igepal for 5s
m1a_mix7         = mix m1a_mix6 with m1a_digitonin for 5s
m1a_mix8         = mix m1a_mix7 with m1a_edta for 5s
m1a_mix9         = mix m1a_mix8 with m1a_bsa for 5s
med1BufferConj   = mix m1a_mix9 with m1a_diluent for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 1 -- STEP A-2: Antibody + pA-Tn5 Conjugation
// 1 ug rabbit polyclonal anti-histone antibody mixed with
// 1 uL assembled pA-Tn5 (0.4 mg/mL) in 50 uL MED1 buffer.
// Rotate 60 min at room temperature (25 C) to form the
// antibody-pA-Tn5 conjugate.
// ============================================================

antibody         = dispense 1 units of AntiHistoneAntibody
paTn5            = dispense 1 units of ProteinATn5_Assembled

abTn5PreMix      = mix antibody with paTn5 for 5s
abTn5Conjugate   = mix abTn5PreMix with med1BufferConj for 60m

// ============================================================
// DAY 1 -- STEP A-3: Nuclei Preparation (Cultured Cells)
// 0.25-1 million cells pelleted at 300 RCF / 5 min.
// Washed once with PBS; resuspended in OMNI buffer on ice
// for 5 min (lysis). Pelleted at 1,000 RCF / 10 min at 4 C;
// resuspended in 100 uL MED1 (fresh instance: med1BufferNuclei).
// `heat at 4c` models the 4 C centrifugation environment.
// ============================================================

cells            = dispense 1 units of TargetCells
pbs_wash1        = dispense 1 units of PBS

cellPellet       = mix cells with pbs_wash1 for 5s

// 300 RCF wash spin (5 min at 4 C)
heat cellPellet at 4c for 5m

// Lyse in OMNI buffer on ice for 5 min
nucleiLysate     = mix cellPellet with omniBuffer for 5m

// 1,000 RCF pellet (10 min at 4 C)
heat nucleiLysate at 4c for 10m

// Resuspend nuclei in MED1 (instance 2: fresh build from manifests)
m1b_hepes        = dispense 1 units of HEPES_1M
m1b_nacl         = dispense 1 units of NaCl_5M
m1b_spermidine   = dispense 1 units of Spermidine_1M
m1b_pi           = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
m1b_supIn        = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
m1b_rnaseOut     = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
m1b_igepal       = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
m1b_digitonin    = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
m1b_edta         = dispense 1 units of EDTA_500mM
m1b_bsa          = dispense 1 units of BSA_10pct
m1b_diluent      = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

m1b_mix1         = mix m1b_hepes with m1b_nacl for 5s
m1b_mix2         = mix m1b_mix1 with m1b_spermidine for 5s
m1b_mix3         = mix m1b_mix2 with m1b_pi for 5s
m1b_mix4         = mix m1b_mix3 with m1b_supIn for 5s
m1b_mix5         = mix m1b_mix4 with m1b_rnaseOut for 5s
m1b_mix6         = mix m1b_mix5 with m1b_igepal for 5s
m1b_mix7         = mix m1b_mix6 with m1b_digitonin for 5s
m1b_mix8         = mix m1b_mix7 with m1b_edta for 5s
m1b_mix9         = mix m1b_mix8 with m1b_bsa for 5s
med1BufferNuclei = mix m1b_mix9 with m1b_diluent for 5s

nucleiInMed1     = mix nucleiLysate with med1BufferNuclei for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 1 -- STEP A-4: Epitope Targeting (Overnight)
// 0.25-0.5 million nuclei pelleted at 1,000 RCF / 10 min
// at 4 C. Resuspended in 25 uL MED1 (instance 3).
// Conjugated antibody-pA-Tn5 added; incubated overnight at
// 4 C with rotation. Modelled as heat at 4c for 720m (12 h).
// ============================================================

// 1,000 RCF pellet (10 min at 4 C) before antibody incubation
heat nucleiInMed1 at 4c for 10m

// MED1 instance 3: resuspension before overnight incubation
m1c_hepes        = dispense 1 units of HEPES_1M
m1c_nacl         = dispense 1 units of NaCl_5M
m1c_spermidine   = dispense 1 units of Spermidine_1M
m1c_pi           = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
m1c_supIn        = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
m1c_rnaseOut     = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
m1c_igepal       = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
m1c_digitonin    = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
m1c_edta         = dispense 1 units of EDTA_500mM
m1c_bsa          = dispense 1 units of BSA_10pct
m1c_diluent      = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

m1c_mix1         = mix m1c_hepes with m1c_nacl for 5s
m1c_mix2         = mix m1c_mix1 with m1c_spermidine for 5s
m1c_mix3         = mix m1c_mix2 with m1c_pi for 5s
m1c_mix4         = mix m1c_mix3 with m1c_supIn for 5s
m1c_mix5         = mix m1c_mix4 with m1c_rnaseOut for 5s
m1c_mix6         = mix m1c_mix5 with m1c_igepal for 5s
m1c_mix7         = mix m1c_mix6 with m1c_digitonin for 5s
m1c_mix8         = mix m1c_mix7 with m1c_edta for 5s
m1c_mix9         = mix m1c_mix8 with m1c_bsa for 5s
med1BufferEpi    = mix m1c_mix9 with m1c_diluent for 5s

nucleiEpitopePrep = mix nucleiInMed1 with med1BufferEpi for 5s

// Add conjugated antibody-pA-Tn5; incubate overnight at 4 C
nucleiWithAbTn5  = mix nucleiEpitopePrep with abTn5Conjugate for 5s
heat nucleiWithAbTn5 at 4c for 720m

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- PART B-1: Prepare MED Buffer #2 (MED2) -- instance 1
// Used for first wash in STEP B-2.
// Identical to MED1 but without EDTA (Mg2+ must be free for
// tagmentation). Components (per 1 mL):
//   20 uL HEPES (1 M, pH 7.5), 54.2 uL NaCl (5 M),
//   0.5 uL Spermidine (1 M), 20 uL 50X PI,
//   50 uL SUPERaseIN, 25 uL RNaseOUT,
//   1 uL IGEPAL-CA630 (10%), 5 uL Digitonin (2%),
//   200 uL 10% BSA, 699.3 uL H2O (ATAC_RSB_Buffer diluent)
// ============================================================

m2a_hepes        = dispense 1 units of HEPES_1M
m2a_nacl         = dispense 1 units of NaCl_5M
m2a_spermidine   = dispense 1 units of Spermidine_1M
m2a_pi           = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
m2a_supIn        = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
m2a_rnaseOut     = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
m2a_igepal       = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
m2a_digitonin    = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
m2a_bsa          = dispense 1 units of BSA_10pct
m2a_diluent      = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

m2a_mix1         = mix m2a_hepes with m2a_nacl for 5s
m2a_mix2         = mix m2a_mix1 with m2a_spermidine for 5s
m2a_mix3         = mix m2a_mix2 with m2a_pi for 5s
m2a_mix4         = mix m2a_mix3 with m2a_supIn for 5s
m2a_mix5         = mix m2a_mix4 with m2a_rnaseOut for 5s
m2a_mix6         = mix m2a_mix5 with m2a_igepal for 5s
m2a_mix7         = mix m2a_mix6 with m2a_digitonin for 5s
m2a_mix8         = mix m2a_mix7 with m2a_bsa for 5s
med2BufferWash1  = mix m2a_mix8 with m2a_diluent for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- PART B-1: MED2 instance 2 (second wash)
// ============================================================

m2b_hepes        = dispense 1 units of HEPES_1M
m2b_nacl         = dispense 1 units of NaCl_5M
m2b_spermidine   = dispense 1 units of Spermidine_1M
m2b_pi           = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
m2b_supIn        = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
m2b_rnaseOut     = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
m2b_igepal       = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
m2b_digitonin    = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
m2b_bsa          = dispense 1 units of BSA_10pct
m2b_diluent      = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

m2b_mix1         = mix m2b_hepes with m2b_nacl for 5s
m2b_mix2         = mix m2b_mix1 with m2b_spermidine for 5s
m2b_mix3         = mix m2b_mix2 with m2b_pi for 5s
m2b_mix4         = mix m2b_mix3 with m2b_supIn for 5s
m2b_mix5         = mix m2b_mix4 with m2b_rnaseOut for 5s
m2b_mix6         = mix m2b_mix5 with m2b_igepal for 5s
m2b_mix7         = mix m2b_mix6 with m2b_digitonin for 5s
m2b_mix8         = mix m2b_mix7 with m2b_bsa for 5s
med2BufferWash2  = mix m2b_mix8 with m2b_diluent for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- PART B-1: MED2 instance 3 (tagmentation resuspend)
// ============================================================

m2c_hepes        = dispense 1 units of HEPES_1M
m2c_nacl         = dispense 1 units of NaCl_5M
m2c_spermidine   = dispense 1 units of Spermidine_1M
m2c_pi           = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
m2c_supIn        = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
m2c_rnaseOut     = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
m2c_igepal       = dispense 1 units of IGEPAL_CA630_10pct
m2c_digitonin    = dispense 1 units of Digitonin_2pct
m2c_bsa          = dispense 1 units of BSA_10pct
m2c_diluent      = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

m2c_mix1         = mix m2c_hepes with m2c_nacl for 5s
m2c_mix2         = mix m2c_mix1 with m2c_spermidine for 5s
m2c_mix3         = mix m2c_mix2 with m2c_pi for 5s
m2c_mix4         = mix m2c_mix3 with m2c_supIn for 5s
m2c_mix5         = mix m2c_mix4 with m2c_rnaseOut for 5s
m2c_mix6         = mix m2c_mix5 with m2c_igepal for 5s
m2c_mix7         = mix m2c_mix6 with m2c_digitonin for 5s
m2c_mix8         = mix m2c_mix7 with m2c_bsa for 5s
med2BufferTag    = mix m2c_mix8 with m2c_diluent for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- PART B-1: Prepare PBS + RNase Inhibitor Wash Buffer
// Used for post-tagmentation nuclei wash in STEP B-2.
// Components (per 1 mL):
//   20 uL 50X PI, 25 uL SUPERaseIN,
//   12.5 uL RNaseOUT, 942.5 uL 1X PBS
// ============================================================

pbsRI_pi         = dispense 1 units of PI_50X
pbsRI_supIn      = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
pbsRI_rnaseOut   = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
pbsRI_pbs        = dispense 1 units of PBS

pbsRI_mix1       = mix pbsRI_pi with pbsRI_supIn for 5s
pbsRI_mix2       = mix pbsRI_mix1 with pbsRI_rnaseOut for 5s
pbsRIBuffer      = mix pbsRI_mix2 with pbsRI_pbs for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- PART B-1: Prepare 1X Nuclei Buffer
// Final nuclei resuspension buffer before Chromium loading.
// Components (per 100 uL):
//   5 uL 20X Nuclei Buffer (10X Genomics PN-2000207),
//   1 uL DTT (100 mM), 5 uL SUPERaseIN,
//   2.5 uL RNaseOUT, 86.5 uL H2O (ATAC_RSB_Buffer diluent)
// ============================================================

nb_20x           = dispense 1 units of NucleiBuffer_20X
nb_dtt           = dispense 1 units of DTT_100mM
nb_supIn         = dispense 1 units of SUPERaseIN
nb_rnaseOut      = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
nb_diluent       = dispense 1 units of ATAC_RSB_Buffer

nb_mix1          = mix nb_20x with nb_dtt for 5s
nb_mix2          = mix nb_mix1 with nb_supIn for 5s
nb_mix3          = mix nb_mix2 with nb_rnaseOut for 5s
nucleiBuffer1X   = mix nb_mix3 with nb_diluent for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-2: Nuclei Washing (x2) and Tagmentation
// Nuclei pelleted at 300 RCF / 10 min at 4 C; washed twice
// with 50 uL MED2. Resuspended in 50 uL MED2.
// 2 uL MgCl2 (250 mM) added to activate Tn5 transposase.
// Tagmentation at 37 C / 60 min with 550 rpm agitation.
// ============================================================

// First MED2 wash (300 RCF / 10 min at 4 C)
nucleiWash1      = mix nucleiWithAbTn5 with med2BufferWash1 for 5s
heat nucleiWash1 at 4c for 10m

// Second MED2 wash (300 RCF / 10 min at 4 C)
nucleiWash2      = mix nucleiWash1 with med2BufferWash2 for 5s
heat nucleiWash2 at 4c for 10m

// Resuspend in 50 uL MED2; add MgCl2 to activate Tn5
mgcl2            = dispense 1 units of MgCl2_250mM
nucleiInMed2     = mix nucleiWash2 with med2BufferTag for 5s
tagmentationMix  = mix nucleiInMed2 with mgcl2 for 5s

// Tagmentation at 37 C for 60 min (550 rpm ThermoMixer)
heat tagmentationMix at 37c for 60m

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-2: Stop Tagmentation and Post-Tag Wash
// 2X Stop Solution added 1:1; terminate Tn5 activity.
// Pelleted at 500 RCF / 6 min at 4 C; washed once with
// PBS + RNase inhibitor buffer.
// ============================================================

stopSolution     = dispense 1 units of StopSolution_2X
stoppedNuclei    = mix tagmentationMix with stopSolution for 5s
heat stoppedNuclei at 4c for 6m

nucleiPostTag    = mix stoppedNuclei with pbsRIBuffer for 5s
heat nucleiPostTag at 4c for 6m

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-2: Resuspend Nuclei in 1X Nuclei Buffer
// Final resuspension in 20 uL 1X Nuclei Buffer for counting.
// 10,000-16,000 nuclei aliquoted in 8 uL.
// 7 uL ATAC Buffer B (10X Genomics PN-2000193) added
// immediately before loading onto Chromium chip.
// ============================================================

atac_bufB        = dispense 1 units of ATACBufferB
nucleiForLoading = mix nucleiPostTag with nucleiBuffer1X for 5s
nucleiChipReady  = mix nucleiForLoading with atac_bufB for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-3: Droplet Generation and RT Master Mix
// Reverse transcription + cell barcoding master mix:
//   49.5 uL Barcoding Reagent Mix (PN-2000267)
//   1.1 uL Template Switch Oligo (PN-3000228)
//   1.9 uL Reducing Agent B (PN-2000087)
//   7.5 uL Barcoding Enzyme Mix (PN-2000266)
// 60 uL master mix + 15 uL nuclei mixture loaded onto
// Chromium Next GEM Chip J; droplets generated in ChromiumX.
// NOTE: `mix` abstracts the microfluidic GEM droplet
// generation event, not a DMF electrode mixing step.
// ============================================================

bcReagentMix     = dispense 1 units of BarcodingReagentMix
tso              = dispense 1 units of TemplateSwitchOligo
reducingAgent    = dispense 1 units of ReducingAgentB
bcEnzymeMix      = dispense 1 units of BarcodingEnzymeMix

rtMix1           = mix bcReagentMix with tso for 5s
rtMix2           = mix rtMix1 with reducingAgent for 5s
rtMasterMix      = mix rtMix2 with bcEnzymeMix for 5s

// Load nuclei + RT master mix onto Chip J; generate GEM droplets
gemEmulsion      = mix nucleiChipReady with rtMasterMix for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-3: Reverse Transcription + Cell Barcoding
// in Droplet (10x GEM incubation program):
//   37 C for 45 min  -- cDNA synthesis (reverse transcription)
//   25 C for 30 min  -- template switching / barcoding
// Lid temperature set to 50 C to prevent condensation.
// Two sequential heat steps model the two-stage PCR program.
// ============================================================

heat gemEmulsion at 37c for 45m
heat gemEmulsion at 25c for 30m

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-3: Quench Reaction
// 5 uL Quenching Agent (PN-2000269) added to stop RT.
// ============================================================

quenchingAgent   = dispense 1 units of QuenchingAgent
quenchedEmulsion = mix gemEmulsion with quenchingAgent for 5s

// ============================================================
// DAY 2 -- STEP B-4: Products Cleanup
// Dynabeads + SPRI bead cleanup per 10X Multiome user guide
// (CG000338). Bead-based purification of barcoded cDNA and
// tagmented DNA fragments from the GEM emulsion.
// ============================================================

dynabeads        = dispense 1 units of DynaBeads
spriBeads        = dispense 1 units of SPRIBeads

dynaClean        = mix quenchedEmulsion with dynabeads for 5m
spriClean        = mix dynaClean with spriBeads for 5m

// ============================================================
// DAY 3 -- STEP C: Pre-amplification
// Follows 10X Multiome user guide (CG000338) with one
// modification: SPRI elution in 80 uL instead of 160 uL
// to concentrate tagmented fragments and maximise DNA library
// complexity (scCUT&Tag library complexity is lower than ATAC).
// DNA library input: 40 uL; RNA library input: 17.5 uL + H2O.
// PCR cycle guidance: 13 cycles for H3K27ac, 12 for H3K27me3.
// Pre-amplified product stable at -20 C for up to 6 months.
// ============================================================

pcrMix           = dispense 1 units of PCRMasterMix
preamplified     = mix spriClean with pcrMix for 5s
heat preamplified at 72c for 5m

// ============================================================
// DAY 3 -- STEP C: DNA and RNA Library Preparation
// DNA and RNA library preps run independently per CG000338.
// Encoded as a single representative SPRI cleanup producing
// the final indexed sequencing library. In practice:
//   40 uL -> DNA library (histone modification CUT&Tag)
//   17.5 uL + 17.5 uL H2O -> RNA library (gene expression)
// ============================================================

spriLib          = dispense 1 units of SPRIBeads
finalLibrary     = mix preamplified with spriLib for 5m

// ============================================================
// DAY 3 -- STEP D: Library QC and Sequencing
// Fragment size QC by TapeStation or Fragment Analyzer.
//   DNA library expected: 200-1,000 bp (nucleosome ladder).
//   RNA (cDNA) library expected: 400-500 bp peak (narrow).
// Illumina NextSeq 2000 sequencing:
//   DNA: 200-cycle kit; 100+8+24+100 cycles.
//   RNA: 100-cycle kit; 28+10+10+72 cycles.
// libraryQCDetection abstracts TapeStation fragment size gate.
// ============================================================

libraryQCSignal  = detect libraryQCDetection on finalLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB4 / BB5: Library QC Gate
// Pass (BB4): libraryQCSignal > 0 -> fragment size within
//             spec (DNA: 200-1000 bp; cDNA: 400-500 bp peak);
//             dispose final library.
// Fail (BB5): libraryQCSignal <= 0 -> library out of spec;
//             drain and re-evaluate PCR cycles or nuclei input.
// Both branches converge at BB6 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (libraryQCSignal > 0) {
    dispose finalLibrary
} else {
    drain finalLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB6: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose library QC signal; experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose libraryQCSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module speExtractionDetection
module fluorescenceDetection
module massSpecDetection

manifest ActivationSolvent
manifest EquilibrationSolvent
manifest WashSolvent
manifest ElutionSolvent
manifest MonomersC12
manifest FluoresceinSample
manifest PeptideSample
manifest AngiotensinII_NaCl
manifest AngiotensinII_Pluronic
manifest PluronicF68

// ============================================================
// A Digital Microfluidic Method for in Situ Formation of
// Porous Polymer Monoliths with Application to Solid-Phase
// Extraction.
// Yang, Mudrik, Jebrail, Wheeler - Anal. Chem. 2011, 83, 3824-3830.
// DOI: 10.1021/ac2002388
//
// Three sequential protocols encoded:
//
// PROTOCOL 1+2: PPM disc formation + standard DMF-SPE.
//   PPM formed by dispensing 1 uL C12 casting solution, driving
//   to centre electrode, UV-polymerizing (100 W, 365 nm, 5 min;
//   abstracted as heat at 25c for 5m). Disc: radius ~1 mm,
//   height 270 um, SSA 3.7 +/- 0.2 m2/g. Four-step SPE:
//   activation / equilibration / sample load / wash / elution.
//   Validated efficiency: 93 +/- 14% (n=3). Model analyte:
//   fluorescamine-labeled angiotensin IV (10 uM, 0.1% FA).
//
// PROTOCOL 3a: Preparative DMF-SPE -- desalting.
//   Sample: Ang II (1 uM) in 100 mM NaCl -> nanoESI-MS.
//   [M+H]+ at m/z 1047 recovered after SPE (Fig. 4a).
//
// PROTOCOL 3b: Preparative DMF-SPE -- surfactant removal.
//   Sample: Ang II (1 uM) in 0.05% w/v Pluronic F68 -> nanoESI-MS.
//   [M+H]+ at m/z 1047 recovered after SPE (Fig. 4b).
//
// FIX #1 -- heat is void in lilott8/BioScript:
//   `heat var at Tc for Td` mutates var in place and returns
//   nothing. Aliasing after heat (e.g. ppmDisc = centredDroplet)
//   creates an undefined token. Fix: use the heated variable
//   directly (centredDroplet / disc2 / disc3) without aliasing.
//
// FIX #2 -- each protocol consumes its PPM disc:
//   Protocol 2 drives solvents/sample through centredDroplet
//   via sequential mix ops, leaving it consumed. Protocols 3a
//   and 3b each form their own independent PPM disc (disc2,
//   disc3) via a fresh dispense + mix + heat sequence.
//
// NOTE ON mix FOR TRANSLATION: BioScript requires two operands
//   for mix. The physical droplet translation step (driving the
//   monomer droplet to the centre electrode) has no second
//   reagent. A second dispense of the same monomer is used as
//   the required second operand; no chemical change occurs.
//
// NOTE ON heat FOR UV EXPOSURE: No UV primitive exists in
//   BioScript. 100 W / 365 nm / 5 min UV polymerization is
//   abstracted as heat at 25c for 5m (isothermal hold).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main           -- disc1 formation + Protocol 2 DMF-SPE
//   BB2  spePass        -- speSignal > 0: dispose eluate
//   BB3  speFail        -- speSignal <= 0: drain eluate
//   BB4  speJoin        -- disc2 formation + Protocol 3a
//   BB5  desaltPass     -- desaltSignal > 0: dispose eluate
//   BB6  desaltFail     -- desaltSignal <= 0: drain eluate
//   BB7  desaltJoin     -- disc3 formation + Protocol 3b
//   BB8  surfactantPass -- surfactantSignal > 0: dispose eluate
//   BB9  surfactantFail -- surfactantSignal <= 0: drain eluate
//   BB10 finalCleanup   -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 -- PPM disc 1 formation.
//   Dispense 1 uL C12 casting solution; translate to centre
//   electrode via actuation (mix models translation; second
//   dispense of same monomer satisfies two-operand requirement);
//   UV-polymerize (heat at 25c for 5m abstracts UV step).
//   FIX #1: centredDroplet used directly after heat; no alias.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

monomer1a      = dispense 1 units of MonomersC12
monomer1b      = dispense 1 units of MonomersC12
centredDroplet = mix monomer1a with monomer1b for 10s
heat centredDroplet at 25c for 5m

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: Standard four-step DMF-SPE
// ============================================================

// Step 1a: Activation (0.1% v/v FA in ACN; 5 uL; 5x pass; 1 min)
activationSolvent1    = dispense 1 units of ActivationSolvent
activatedDisc1        = mix centredDroplet with activationSolvent1 for 1m
dispose activationSolvent1

// Step 1b: Equilibration (0.5% v/v FA in H2O; 5 uL; 5x pass; 1 min)
equilibrationSolvent1 = dispense 1 units of EquilibrationSolvent
equilibratedDisc1     = mix activatedDisc1 with equilibrationSolvent1 for 1m
dispose equilibrationSolvent1

// Step 2: Sample loading (1 uL; 5x pass; 2 min incubation).
//   2 min optimized (Fig. 3a: >80% bound; p=0.30 vs 4 min).
peptideSample1 = dispense 1 units of PeptideSample
loadedDisc1    = mix equilibratedDisc1 with peptideSample1 for 2m
dispose peptideSample1

// Step 3: Washing (2 x 5 uL; 0.5% v/v FA in H2O)
washSolvent1a  = dispense 1 units of WashSolvent
washedDisc1a   = mix loadedDisc1 with washSolvent1a for 30s
dispose washSolvent1a

washSolvent1b  = dispense 1 units of WashSolvent
washedDisc1b   = mix washedDisc1a with washSolvent1b for 30s
dispose washSolvent1b

// Step 4: Elution (2 x 5 uL; 0.1% v/v FA in ACN).
//   2 droplets optimized (Fig. 3b: >90% extracted; p=0.25 vs 3).
elutionSolvent1a = dispense 1 units of ElutionSolvent
eluate1a         = mix washedDisc1b with elutionSolvent1a for 30s

elutionSolvent1b = dispense 1 units of ElutionSolvent
eluate1b         = mix eluate1a with elutionSolvent1b for 30s

speSignal = detect speExtractionDetection on eluate1b for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Standard DMF-SPE QC gate
// Pass (BB2): speSignal > 0 -> valid extraction; dispose.
// Fail (BB3): speSignal <= 0 -> extraction failed; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (speJoin).
// ============================================================

if (speSignal > 0) {
    dispose eluate1b
} else {
    drain eluate1b
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: speJoin
// Dispose SPE QC signal. Form disc 2 for Protocol 3a.
// FIX #2: disc 2 is fresh; centredDroplet was consumed above.
// ============================================================

dispose speSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 3a: Preparative DMF-SPE -- Desalting
// Sample: Ang II (1 uM) in 100 mM NaCl. [M+H]+ m/z 1047
// absent without SPE (ion suppression); recovered after SPE.
// nanoESI-MS: LTQ Finnigan, 1.7-2.0 kV, 0.5 uL/min, 200 C.
// ============================================================

// Form PPM disc 2 (FIX #2: independent of disc 1)
monomer2a = dispense 1 units of MonomersC12
monomer2b = dispense 1 units of MonomersC12
disc2     = mix monomer2a with monomer2b for 10s
heat disc2 at 25c for 5m

// Step 1a: Activation
activationSolvent2    = dispense 1 units of ActivationSolvent
activatedDisc2        = mix disc2 with activationSolvent2 for 1m
dispose activationSolvent2

// Step 1b: Equilibration
equilibrationSolvent2 = dispense 1 units of EquilibrationSolvent
equilibratedDisc2     = mix activatedDisc2 with equilibrationSolvent2 for 1m
dispose equilibrationSolvent2

// Step 2: Sample loading (Ang II + 100 mM NaCl; 2 min)
angII_NaCl_Sample = dispense 1 units of AngiotensinII_NaCl
loadedDisc2       = mix equilibratedDisc2 with angII_NaCl_Sample for 2m
dispose angII_NaCl_Sample

// Step 3: Washing
washSolvent2a = dispense 1 units of WashSolvent
washedDisc2a  = mix loadedDisc2 with washSolvent2a for 30s
dispose washSolvent2a

washSolvent2b = dispense 1 units of WashSolvent
washedDisc2b  = mix washedDisc2a with washSolvent2b for 30s
dispose washSolvent2b

// Step 4: Elution (2 x; pooled -> nanoESI-MS)
desaltElution1 = dispense 1 units of ElutionSolvent
desaltEluate1  = mix washedDisc2b with desaltElution1 for 30s

desaltElution2 = dispense 1 units of ElutionSolvent
desaltEluate2  = mix desaltEluate1 with desaltElution2 for 30s

desaltSignal = detect massSpecDetection on desaltEluate2 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Desalting QC gate
// Pass (BB5): desaltSignal > 0 -> m/z 1047 detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): desaltSignal <= 0 -> suppression persists; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (desaltJoin).
// ============================================================

if (desaltSignal > 0) {
    dispose desaltEluate2
} else {
    drain desaltEluate2
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: desaltJoin
// Dispose desalting QC signal. Form disc 3 for Protocol 3b.
// FIX #2: disc 3 is fresh; disc 2 was consumed above.
// ============================================================

dispose desaltSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 3b: Preparative DMF-SPE -- Surfactant Removal
// Sample: Ang II (1 uM) in 0.05% w/v Pluronic F68.
// Pluronics: strong nanoESI suppressors (paper refs 47-48).
// [M+H]+ at m/z 1047 recovered after DMF-SPE (Fig. 4b).
// ============================================================

// Form PPM disc 3 (FIX #2: independent of disc 2)
monomer3a = dispense 1 units of MonomersC12
monomer3b = dispense 1 units of MonomersC12
disc3     = mix monomer3a with monomer3b for 10s
heat disc3 at 25c for 5m

// Step 1a: Activation
activationSolvent3    = dispense 1 units of ActivationSolvent
activatedDisc3        = mix disc3 with activationSolvent3 for 1m
dispose activationSolvent3

// Step 1b: Equilibration
equilibrationSolvent3 = dispense 1 units of EquilibrationSolvent
equilibratedDisc3     = mix activatedDisc3 with equilibrationSolvent3 for 1m
dispose equilibrationSolvent3

// Step 2: Sample loading (Ang II + 0.05% Pluronic F68; 2 min)
angII_Pluronic_Sample = dispense 1 units of AngiotensinII_Pluronic
loadedDisc3           = mix equilibratedDisc3 with angII_Pluronic_Sample for 2m
dispose angII_Pluronic_Sample

// Step 3: Washing
washSolvent3a = dispense 1 units of WashSolvent
washedDisc3a  = mix loadedDisc3 with washSolvent3a for 30s
dispose washSolvent3a

washSolvent3b = dispense 1 units of WashSolvent
washedDisc3b  = mix washedDisc3a with washSolvent3b for 30s
dispose washSolvent3b

// Step 4: Elution (2 x; pooled -> nanoESI-MS)
surfActElution1 = dispense 1 units of ElutionSolvent
surfActEluate1  = mix washedDisc3b with surfActElution1 for 30s

surfActElution2 = dispense 1 units of ElutionSolvent
surfActEluate2  = mix surfActEluate1 with surfActElution2 for 30s

surfactantSignal = detect massSpecDetection on surfActEluate2 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Surfactant removal QC gate
// Pass (BB8): surfactantSignal > 0 -> m/z 1047 detected;
//             Pluronic F68 removed; dispose eluate.
// Fail (BB9): surfactantSignal <= 0 -> suppression persists;
//             drain eluate.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (surfactantSignal > 0) {
    dispose surfActEluate2
} else {
    drain surfActEluate2
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose surfactantSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module denv1Detection
module denv2Detection
module denv3Detection
module denv4Detection

manifest HumanPlasma_DENV_RNA
manifest TRIzol_Reagent
manifest Chloroform
manifest ChitosanFilterDisc
manifest SDS_Wash
manifest DI_Water
manifest RT_PCR_MasterMix
manifest DENV1_Primers
manifest DENV2_Primers
manifest DENV3_Primers
manifest DENV4_Primers
manifest iScript_RT
manifest NucleaseFree_H2O
manifest PBS_4x
manifest PBS_0_1x
manifest DENV1_Oligoprobe_AEM
manifest DENV2_Oligoprobe_AEM
manifest DENV3_Oligoprobe_AEM
manifest DENV4_Oligoprobe_AEM

instructions:

// ============================================================
// A Non-Optical Multiplexed PCR Diagnostic Platform for
// Serotype-Specific Detection of Dengue Virus
// Yin et al., Sensors & Actuators B: Chemical 310 (2020) 127854
// DOI: 10.1016/j.snb.2020.127854
//
// Platform overview:
//   Three integrated steps (~90 min total):
//   STEP 1 - Filter paper-based RNA extraction from plasma (~10 min)
//   STEP 2 - On-chip multiplex RT-PCR amplification (~60 min)
//   STEP 3 - Ion-exchange membrane (IEM) sensor detection (~20 min)
//
// Four DENV serotypes detected in a single on-chip PCR reactor
// using four primer sets. Amplicons: DENV-1 = 110 bp,
// DENV-2 = 98 bp, DENV-3 = 78 bp, DENV-4 = 83 bp.
// Detection limit: 100 copies/mL RNA in spiked human plasma.
//
// NOTE ON TRIZOL / EXTRACTION ABSTRACTION:
//   TRIzol-chloroform phase separation is an off-chip chemical
//   lysis step. It is modelled here as mix + heat (room temp)
//   followed by a transfer (mix) of the aqueous phase to the
//   chitosan disc. This is a standard BioScript abstraction
//   for a phase-separation event; no physical DMF mixing is
//   implied. The ChitosanFilterDisc manifest represents the
//   1 mm diameter chitosan-modified Fusion 5 filter paper disc.
//
// NOTE ON RT-PCR THERMAL PROTOCOL:
//   Reverse transcription:  50 C for 30 min (1800 s)
//   RT inactivation:        95 C for  2 min  (120 s)
//   35 cycles of:
//     Denaturation:         95 C for 15 s
//     Annealing/extension:  55 C for 60 s
//   Total cycling modelled as a single `heat` at 95 C for the
//   denaturation phase (35 * 15 s = 525 s) followed by a
//   single `heat` at 55 C for the anneal phase (35 * 60 s =
//   2100 s). BioScript does not support loop constructs, so
//   the cyclic thermal profile is collapsed into sequential
//   heat statements per standard BioScript practice (see
//   moazami_world_to_chip_dmf.bs precedent).
//
// NOTE ON IEM SENSOR ARCHITECTURE:
//   Each AEM (anion-exchange nanomembrane) sensor is
//   functionalized with a serotype-specific oligoprobe. The
//   four sensors form isolated reservoirs on a single sensing
//   chip. Each is modelled as an independent detect call on
//   the corresponding oligoprobe manifest. The CVC shift
//   (overlimiting current regime) is abstracted as a module
//   detect event. Detection threshold: >0.2 V CVC shift
//   (cutoff established in Fig. 4 of paper).
//   Target CVC shifts: DENV-1 ~0.55 V, DENV-2 ~0.61 V,
//   DENV-3 ~0.67 V, DENV-4 ~0.53 V at 40 uA.
//
// NOTE ON DENATURE STEP:
//   After PCR, the amplicons are heated at 95 C for 5 min
//   (300 s) within the same chamber to generate ssDNA for
//   downstream IEM hybridisation. This is modelled as a
//   `heat` at 95 C for 300 s on the pcr_amplicons droplet.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- entry: RNA extraction, RT-PCR,
//                           ssDNA generation, IEM detection
//   BB2  denv1Pass       -- denv1Signal > 0: DENV-1 detected; dispose
//   BB3  denv1Fail       -- denv1Signal <= 0: not detected; drain
//   BB4  denv1Join       -- join: DENV-2 detection branch
//   BB5  denv2Pass       -- denv2Signal > 0: DENV-2 detected; dispose
//   BB6  denv2Fail       -- denv2Signal <= 0: not detected; drain
//   BB7  denv2Join       -- join: DENV-3 detection branch
//   BB8  denv3Pass       -- denv3Signal > 0: DENV-3 detected; dispose
//   BB9  denv3Fail       -- denv3Signal <= 0: not detected; drain
//   BB10 denv3Join       -- join: DENV-4 detection branch
//   BB11 denv4Pass       -- denv4Signal > 0: DENV-4 detected; dispose
//   BB12 denv4Fail       -- denv4Signal <= 0: not detected; drain
//   BB13 finalCleanup    -- terminal: dispose all detection signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1A: TRIzol lysis of DENV RNA-spiked human plasma.
//   10 uL extracted DENV RNA spiked into 1 mL human plasma.
//   TRIzol reagent added and vortexed 30 s; 0.2 mL chloroform
//   added and mixed 60 s to separate aqueous / organic phases.
//   Aqueous phase (contains DENV RNA) collected as supernatant.
//   Modelled as mix + heat (room temp, 90 s total lysis time).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

plasma_sample   = dispense 1 units of HumanPlasma_DENV_RNA
trizol          = dispense 1 units of TRIzol_Reagent
chloroform      = dispense 1 units of Chloroform

trizol_mix      = mix plasma_sample with trizol for 30s
lysed_sample    = mix trizol_mix with chloroform for 60s

// Phase separation at room temperature (25 C) for 2 min.
// Aqueous phase containing RNA rises to top.
heat lysed_sample at 25c for 120s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1B: Dip-and-rinse chitosan filter paper RNA capture.
//   1 mm diameter chitosan-modified Fusion 5 filter disc
//   immersed in aqueous phase for 5 min. Negatively charged
//   RNA molecules are electrostatically captured on the
//   positively charged chitosan matrix. PCR inhibitors
//   (Guanidinium thiocyanate etc.) are washed off.
//   Recovery: down to 50 copies RNA/mL; 98%+ extraction
//   efficiency for high-quality nucleic acid (Liu et al. 2017).
//   `mix` abstracts the immersion / dip event.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

chitosan_disc   = dispense 1 units of ChitosanFilterDisc
rna_captured    = mix lysed_sample with chitosan_disc for 5m

// SDS wash (1% SDS + DI water) to remove PCR inhibitors
// from filter surface before introducing into PCR chamber.
sds_wash        = dispense 1 units of SDS_Wash
di_water_wash   = dispense 1 units of DI_Water

wash1           = mix rna_captured with sds_wash for 30s
washed_disc     = mix wash1 with di_water_wash for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2A: Assemble multiplex RT-PCR master mix.
//   20 uL total reaction volume:
//     12.5 uL iTaq Universal SYBR Green One-Step master mix
//      0.5 uL forward + reverse primers for DENV-1 and DENV-3
//      0.25 uL forward + reverse primers for DENV-2 and DENV-4
//      0.5 uL iScript reverse transcriptase
//      5.0 uL nuclease-free H2O
//   Filter disc with RNA introduced after master mix assembly.
//   Four primer sets amplify all four serotypes in single reactor.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pcr_mix         = dispense 1 units of RT_PCR_MasterMix
primers_d1_d3   = dispense 1 units of DENV1_Primers
primers_d2_d4   = dispense 1 units of DENV2_Primers
primers_d3      = dispense 1 units of DENV3_Primers
primers_d4      = dispense 1 units of DENV4_Primers
iscript_rt      = dispense 1 units of iScript_RT
nf_water        = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFree_H2O

// Combine all primer sets into master mix.
primer_mix_1    = mix primers_d1_d3 with primers_d2_d4 for 5s
primer_mix_2    = mix primer_mix_1 with primers_d3 for 5s
primer_mix_all  = mix primer_mix_2 with primers_d4 for 5s

rt_master_mix   = mix pcr_mix with iscript_rt for 5s
full_mix        = mix rt_master_mix with primer_mix_all for 5s
rxn_mix         = mix full_mix with nf_water for 5s

// Introduce RNA-loaded filter disc into the PCR reaction mix.
pcr_reaction    = mix rxn_mix with washed_disc for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2B: Load assembled PCR reaction into on-chip chamber.
//   Inlets and outlets sealed after loading. Lab-developed
//   thermocouple plate provides calibrated thermal cycling.
//   Chip dimensions: 10 x 4 x 0.1 cm3 polycarbonate, 25 uL
//   on-chip PCR reactor. `mix` abstracts the chip-loading step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// No additional reagent mixing here; the loaded chip IS the
// pcr_reaction droplet in BioScript abstraction.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2C: Reverse transcription (50 C, 30 min = 1800 s).
//   DENV RNA -> cDNA. iScript reverse transcriptase active.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcr_reaction at 50c for 1800s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2D: RT inactivation (95 C, 2 min = 120 s).
//   Inactivates reverse transcriptase; initial denaturation
//   of cDNA:RNA hybrid and polymerase activation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcr_reaction at 95c for 120s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2E: PCR cycling - denaturation phase.
//   35 cycles x 15 s at 95 C = 525 s total denaturation time.
//   BioScript does not support loop constructs; collapsed to
//   single heat statement (see header NOTE ON RT-PCR THERMAL
//   PROTOCOL).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcr_reaction at 95c for 525s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2F: PCR cycling - annealing/extension phase.
//   35 cycles x 60 s at 55 C = 2100 s total anneal time.
//   All four serotype amplicons generated in this phase.
//   Expected amplicon sizes: 110 bp (D1), 98 bp (D2),
//   78 bp (D3), 83 bp (D4).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcr_reaction at 55c for 2100s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2G: Post-PCR ssDNA generation (95 C, 5 min = 300 s).
//   Amplicons heated to 95 C within the same PCR chamber to
//   denature dsDNA amplicons into ssDNA required for
//   hybridisation with AEM oligoprobes in STEP 3.
//   Paper Section 2.4: "heated at 95 C for 5 min in the
//   same chamber to get ssDNA for downstream detection."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcr_reaction at 95c for 300s

// pcr_reaction now contains ssDNA amplicons of all four
// DENV serotypes ready for IEM sensor detection.

// Rename for clarity in downstream detection steps.
ssdna_amplicons = mix pcr_reaction with nf_water for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3A: IEM Sensor 1 - DENV-1 detection.
//   AEM functionalized with DENV-1 specific oligoprobe.
//   ssDNA amplicons incubated on sensor for 15 min (900 s).
//   Wash with 4x PBS (removes non-specifically bound targets;
//   hydrodynamic shear via flow enhances selectivity).
//   CVC measured in 0.1x PBS at 0 -> 40 uA (step 1 uA/s).
//   Signal >0.2 V shift from probe baseline = DENV-1 positive.
//   Expected shift: ~0.55 V for DENV-1 target (paper Fig. 3B).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aem_denv1       = dispense 1 units of DENV1_Oligoprobe_AEM
sensor1_sample  = mix ssdna_amplicons with aem_denv1 for 15m

// 4x PBS wash (removes non-targets and non-specific PCR products).
pbs_wash_1      = dispense 1 units of PBS_4x
sensor1_washed  = mix sensor1_sample with pbs_wash_1 for 5m

// 0.1x PBS measurement buffer; CVC acquisition.
pbs_meas_1      = dispense 1 units of PBS_0_1x
sensor1_meas    = mix sensor1_washed with pbs_meas_1 for 1m

denv1Signal     = detect denv1Detection on sensor1_meas for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: DENV-1 detection QC gate
// Pass (BB2): denv1Signal > 0 -> DENV-1 serotype detected;
//             CVC shift exceeds 0.2 V cutoff; dispose.
// Fail (BB3): denv1Signal <= 0 -> not detected; drain.
// Both converge at BB4 (denv1Join).
// ============================================================

if (denv1Signal > 0) {
    dispose sensor1_meas
} else {
    drain sensor1_meas
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: denv1Join
// Dispose DENV-1 detection signal. Control falls into
// DENV-2 detection branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose denv1Signal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3B: IEM Sensor 2 - DENV-2 detection.
//   AEM functionalized with DENV-2 specific oligoprobe.
//   Same wash and CVC measurement protocol as Sensor 1.
//   Expected CVC shift: ~0.61 V for DENV-2 target (Fig. 3C).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aem_denv2       = dispense 1 units of DENV2_Oligoprobe_AEM
sensor2_sample  = mix ssdna_amplicons with aem_denv2 for 15m

pbs_wash_2      = dispense 1 units of PBS_4x
sensor2_washed  = mix sensor2_sample with pbs_wash_2 for 5m

pbs_meas_2      = dispense 1 units of PBS_0_1x
sensor2_meas    = mix sensor2_washed with pbs_meas_2 for 1m

denv2Signal     = detect denv2Detection on sensor2_meas for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: DENV-2 detection QC gate
// Pass (BB5): denv2Signal > 0 -> DENV-2 detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): denv2Signal <= 0 -> not detected; drain.
// Both converge at BB7 (denv2Join).
// ============================================================

if (denv2Signal > 0) {
    dispose sensor2_meas
} else {
    drain sensor2_meas
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: denv2Join
// Dispose DENV-2 detection signal. Control falls into
// DENV-3 detection branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose denv2Signal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3C: IEM Sensor 3 - DENV-3 detection.
//   AEM functionalized with DENV-3 specific oligoprobe.
//   Same wash and CVC measurement protocol as Sensor 1.
//   Expected CVC shift: ~0.67 V for DENV-3 target (Fig. 3D).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aem_denv3       = dispense 1 units of DENV3_Oligoprobe_AEM
sensor3_sample  = mix ssdna_amplicons with aem_denv3 for 15m

pbs_wash_3      = dispense 1 units of PBS_4x
sensor3_washed  = mix sensor3_sample with pbs_wash_3 for 5m

pbs_meas_3      = dispense 1 units of PBS_0_1x
sensor3_meas    = mix sensor3_washed with pbs_meas_3 for 1m

denv3Signal     = detect denv3Detection on sensor3_meas for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: DENV-3 detection QC gate
// Pass (BB8): denv3Signal > 0 -> DENV-3 detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB9): denv3Signal <= 0 -> not detected; drain.
// Both converge at BB10 (denv3Join).
// ============================================================

if (denv3Signal > 0) {
    dispose sensor3_meas
} else {
    drain sensor3_meas
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: denv3Join
// Dispose DENV-3 detection signal. Control falls into
// DENV-4 detection branch (BB11/BB12).
// ============================================================

dispose denv3Signal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3D: IEM Sensor 4 - DENV-4 detection.
//   AEM functionalized with DENV-4 specific oligoprobe.
//   Same wash and CVC measurement protocol as Sensor 1.
//   Expected CVC shift: ~0.53 V for DENV-4 target (Fig. 3E).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aem_denv4       = dispense 1 units of DENV4_Oligoprobe_AEM
sensor4_sample  = mix ssdna_amplicons with aem_denv4 for 15m

pbs_wash_4      = dispense 1 units of PBS_4x
sensor4_washed  = mix sensor4_sample with pbs_wash_4 for 5m

pbs_meas_4      = dispense 1 units of PBS_0_1x
sensor4_meas    = mix sensor4_washed with pbs_meas_4 for 1m

denv4Signal     = detect denv4Detection on sensor4_meas for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: DENV-4 detection QC gate
// Pass (BB11): denv4Signal > 0 -> DENV-4 detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB12): denv4Signal <= 0 -> not detected; drain.
// Both converge at BB13 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (denv4Signal > 0) {
    dispose sensor4_meas
} else {
    drain sensor4_meas
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all four IEM detection signals.
// Serotyping result is determined by which denvNSignal > 0
// branches were taken. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose denv4Signal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]

module impedanceDetection
module passageTimeDetection

manifest MCF7_Cells
manifest modMCF7_Cells
manifest FixedMCF7_Cells
manifest RBC_Cells
manifest PBS
manifest BSA_PBS
manifest PMA_500nM
manifest Formaldehyde_4pct
manifest Glycine_127mM

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Characterizing Deformability and Electrical Properties of
// Breast Cancer Cells Using a Microfluidic Device Combining
// Electrical Impedance Sensing and Mechanical Constriction.
// Zhou, Yang, Zhou, Khoo, Han, Ai.
// BioSyM / SMART Centre, MIT & SUTD.
//
// Protocol: Preparation of three MCF-7 cell populations
// (untreated, PMA-modified, formaldehyde-fixed) plus RBCs,
// followed by differential impedance measurement of undeformed
// cells (outside constriction) and deformed cells (inside
// constriction) as they are driven through an 8 um wide PDMS
// constriction at 200 mbar and 500 mbar applied pressure.
//
// DEVICE OVERVIEW:
//   - PDMS microfluidic channel with narrow constriction (~8 um
//     wide, ~20 um tall) fabricated by SU-8 soft lithography.
//   - Four pairs of coplanar gold electrodes (20 um width,
//     30 um spacing) patterned on glass substrate by lift-off.
//   - Outer electrode pairs sense undeformed cells (before/after
//     constriction); inner pairs sense deformed cells (inside).
//   - Differential impedance configuration: Z_cell-medium minus
//     Z_medium-only eliminates baseline drift and rejects
//     multiple-cell transit events automatically.
//   - Input voltage: 500 mV amplitude; HF2IS impedance analyser
//     (Zurich Instruments); frequencies 1 MHz and 2 MHz.
//   - Pressure control: Fluigent MFCS-EZ system.
//
// CELL POPULATIONS:
//   A. Untreated MCF-7  (live breast cancer cells, avg ~22 um)
//   B. modMCF-7         (PMA-treated, more deformable, avg ~22 um)
//   C. Fixed MCF-7      (formaldehyde-fixed, stiff, avg ~23 um)
//   D. RBCs             (red blood cells, highly deformable reference)
//
// MEASURED PARAMETERS per cell:
//   - Passage time   = total time in constriction system
//   - Entry time     = time to enter and fully deform into constriction
//   - Transit time   = time spent traversing inside constriction
//   - Impedance of undeformed cell (Z_undeformed, outside constriction)
//   - Impedance of deformed cell   (Z_deformed,   inside constriction)
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device priming; cell preparation;
//                              MCF-7 run at 500 mbar
//   BB2  impedancePass      -- impedanceSignal > 0: valid impedance
//                              peak detected; dispose cell droplet
//   BB3  impedanceFail      -- impedanceSignal <= 0: no valid peak
//                              (e.g. multi-cell event); drain
//   BB4  impedanceJoin      -- join: modMCF-7 branch begins
//   BB5  modPass            -- modSignal > 0: dispose modMCF-7
//   BB6  modFail            -- modSignal <= 0: drain modMCF-7
//   BB7  modJoin            -- join: fixed MCF-7 branch begins
//   BB8  fixedPass          -- fixedSignal > 0: dispose fixedMCF-7
//   BB9  fixedFail          -- fixedSignal <= 0: drain fixedMCF-7
//   BB10 fixedJoin          -- join: RBC reference branch begins
//   BB11 rbcPass            -- rbcSignal > 0: dispose RBCs
//   BB12 rbcFail            -- rbcSignal <= 0: drain RBCs
//   BB13 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime microfluidic channel with 1% BSA in PBS
//         for 20 min to block hydrophobic PDMS surfaces and
//         prevent non-specific cell adhesion to channel walls.
//         Channels filled via positive pressure at inlet.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingBSA = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
primingPBS = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingMix = mix primingBSA with primingPBS for 20m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Prepare PMA-modified MCF-7 cells (modMCF-7).
//         MCF-7 cells treated with 500 nM PMA
//         (Phorbol 12-myristate 13-acetate) for 18 hours at
//         37 C to activate PKC and increase cortical
//         deformability. After PMA treatment cells are
//         resuspended in PBS for measurement.
//         18 hours = 1080 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mcf7_for_mod    = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
pmaReagent      = dispense 1 units of PMA_500nM
modTreatmentMix = mix mcf7_for_mod with pmaReagent for 5s
heat modTreatmentMix at 37c for 1080m

modWashPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
modMCF7_Ready   = mix modTreatmentMix with modWashPBS for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Prepare formaldehyde-fixed MCF-7 cells.
//         MCF-7 cells fixed in 4% methanol-free formaldehyde
//         for 8 min at room temperature to crosslink cytoskeleton
//         and stiffen the cell. 0.127 M glycine added for 5 min
//         to quench excess formaldehyde. Fixed cells resuspended
//         in PBS for measurement.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mcf7_for_fix     = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
formaldehydeSoln = dispense 1 units of Formaldehyde_4pct
fixationMix      = mix mcf7_for_fix with formaldehydeSoln for 8m

glycineQuench    = dispense 1 units of Glycine_127mM
quenchedFixation = mix fixationMix with glycineQuench for 5m

fixWashPBS       = dispense 1 units of PBS
fixedMCF7_Ready  = mix quenchedFixation with fixWashPBS for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Load untreated MCF-7 cells (live) into primed
//         microfluidic device at 500 mbar applied pressure.
//         Cells are driven through the 8 um constriction.
//         Differential impedance is recorded continuously:
//           - Outer electrode pairs detect undeformed cell
//             impedance before/after constriction entry.
//           - Inner electrode pairs detect fully deformed
//             cell impedance inside constriction.
//         Passage time, entry time, transit time are extracted
//         from the bipolar impedance peak shapes.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts pressure-driven cell loading
//         into the microfluidic channel and constriction;
//         this is not a droplet-merging step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mcf7Live      = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
mcf7FlowMix   = mix mcf7Live with primingMix for 2s

// Differential impedance measurement at 500 mbar.
// impedanceDetection captures both Z_undeformed and Z_deformed
// peak amplitudes plus passage/entry/transit timing per cell.
impedanceSignal = detect impedanceDetection on mcf7FlowMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: MCF-7 impedance QC gate
// Pass (BB2): impedanceSignal > 0 -> valid bipolar peak pair
//             detected (single cell transit confirmed by
//             differential sign reversal); dispose cell sample.
// Fail (BB3): impedanceSignal <= 0 -> invalid signal (multi-cell
//             event or no cell detected); drain sample.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (impedanceJoin).
// ============================================================

if (impedanceSignal > 0) {
    dispose mcf7FlowMix
} else {
    drain mcf7FlowMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: impedanceJoin
// Dispose MCF-7 QC signal. Control falls into modMCF-7 branch.
// ============================================================

dispose impedanceSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Load PMA-modified MCF-7 cells (modMCF-7) into the
//         device at 500 mbar. Differential impedance measured
//         identically to STEP 4. modMCF-7 cells are expected
//         to show shorter passage times and lower impedance
//         of undeformed cells compared to untreated MCF-7,
//         reflecting increased deformability from PMA-induced
//         cortical actin remodelling.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingMix2    = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
modFlowMix     = mix modMCF7_Ready with primingMix2 for 2s

modSignal = detect impedanceDetection on modFlowMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: modMCF-7 impedance QC gate
// Pass (BB5): modSignal > 0 -> valid single-cell transit; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): modSignal <= 0 -> invalid event; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (modJoin).
// ============================================================

if (modSignal > 0) {
    dispose modFlowMix
} else {
    drain modFlowMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: modJoin
// Dispose modMCF-7 QC signal. Control falls into fixed branch.
// ============================================================

dispose modSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Load formaldehyde-fixed MCF-7 cells into the device
//         at 500 mbar (and separately at 200 mbar for Figure S4
//         comparison). Fixed cells are expected to show the
//         longest passage times of all populations, reflecting
//         maximum mechanical stiffness. Impedance of fixed cells
//         is dominated by cell membrane properties since the
//         crosslinked cytoskeleton prevents full deformation
//         in the constriction.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingMix3     = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
fixedFlowMix    = mix fixedMCF7_Ready with primingMix3 for 2s

fixedSignal = detect impedanceDetection on fixedFlowMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Fixed MCF-7 impedance QC gate
// Pass (BB8): fixedSignal > 0 -> valid single-cell transit; dispose.
// Fail (BB9): fixedSignal <= 0 -> invalid event; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (fixedJoin).
// ============================================================

if (fixedSignal > 0) {
    dispose fixedFlowMix
} else {
    drain fixedFlowMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: fixedJoin
// Dispose fixed MCF-7 QC signal. Control falls into RBC branch.
// ============================================================

dispose fixedSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Load RBCs (red blood cells) as a highly deformable
//         positive-deformability reference at 500 mbar and
//         200 mbar. RBCs are biconcave discs (~8 um diameter)
//         that readily squeeze through the 8 um constriction
//         with minimal entry resistance. Expected to show
//         shortest passage times and smallest impedance
//         signals due to low cytoplasmic conductivity and
//         absence of nucleus.
//         NOTE: passageTimeDetection module abstracts the
//         high-speed optical camera readout (Phantom v9.1,
//         Vision Research) used in parallel to validate
//         impedance-based timing measurements.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rbcSample      = dispense 1 units of RBC_Cells
primingMix4    = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
rbcFlowMix     = mix rbcSample with primingMix4 for 2s

// Impedance detection with simultaneous passage-time
// optical validation (high-speed camera @ 1000 fps).
rbcImpedance = detect impedanceDetection on rbcFlowMix for 30s
rbcSignal    = detect passageTimeDetection on rbcFlowMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: RBC impedance QC gate
// Pass (BB11): rbcSignal > 0 -> valid RBC transit confirmed by
//              both impedance peak and optical frame analysis;
//              dispose RBC sample.
// Fail (BB12): rbcSignal <= 0 -> no valid RBC detected; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB13 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rbcSignal > 0) {
    dispose rbcFlowMix
} else {
    drain rbcFlowMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal variables.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose rbcImpedance
dispose rbcSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
